e_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impulsiveIngenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3526#post3526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... this is in the Exalted forum, what's...<br /> <br /> .... ponies confirmed for 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastmen with wing mutations, or sorcery initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:43:33-08:00","id":3650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impulsiveIngenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3526#post3526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woo, ponies! Sadly, though, I too am on the no spoilers train.<br /> <br /> Wait... this is in the Exalted forum, what's...<br /> <br /> .... ponies confirmed for 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out Exigents are a lot more flexible than we knew!<br /> <br /> But, yeah, this is a continuation of a popular thread from the old forum, much like the Homestuck and Avatar threads...and like them, we DO stray on-topic by <br /> discussing how some things in FiM could equate to Exalted (there was a nice debate over how to translate Queen Chrysalis to Creation, for ex)! <br /> <br /> And I made sure to post a non-visual link to the promo, and I'm sure any others with possible spoilers will be similarly circumspect, so there's really no need to fear spoilers here!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:59:22-08:00","id":3660,"title":"","content":"Did you guys know that Hasbro officially gave the ok for the first fully fan-made episode? It's pretty damned amazing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=26BQ0HNtDmI\" data-code=\"26BQ0HNtDmI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/26BQ0HNtDmI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Check out one of the analyzing videos, such as &quot;Everything Wrong with Double Rainboom in Four Minutes&quot;, to see all of the stealth cameos hidden in the background that you missed. I guarantee, you didn't see them all!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:01:05-08:00","id":3663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3571#post3571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to know, good to know. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you guys know that Hasbro officially gave the ok for the first fully fan-made episode? It's pretty damned amazing!</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> I thought that was just yet another case of &quot;&quot;as a company we do not acknowledge that this is happening, but think it is cool that it is&quot;, like all other fan-made stuff.<br /> Where did Hasbro give it, their official blessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","user":"Vegetalss4","date":". 11-05-2013, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:26:38-08:00","id":3678,"title":"","content":"They can't, legally speaking, give Double Rainboom their blessing without doing something about it.<br /> <br /> And Double Rainboom was shit. Snowdrop, on the other hand, was phenomenal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:42:41-08:00","id":3692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vegetalss4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3663#post3663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> I thought that was just yet another case of &quot;&quot;as a company we do not acknowledge that this is happening, but think it is cool that it is&quot;, like all other fan-made stuff.<br /> Where did Hasbro give it, their official blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the guy who made it sent them a letter and asked. If they had said no, there'd be no Double Rainboom and we'd not know about it at all. I'd not marvel too much about it when the only way for us to know about it was in the case of success.<br /> <br /> It probably also helped that the episode was a school project, and I think school work has slightly less restrictions on it so it was safer to say yes without setting too much of a precedent. I'd not count on them saying yes to similar things as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Strikes me that I've not actually seen Double Rainboom. Should probably do that, just to get in the know.<br /> <br /> Snowdrop... it was well made, certainly. Animation was great. I also liked how they returned to the idea of ponies actively creating weather and similar, which was present in Winter Wrap Up and The Running of the Leaves but has since been left to the side. For me, though, it was a bit too soppy and didn't feel in spirit with the show. I'm not complaining or anything, but it's not all that for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 11-05-2013, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:58:16-08:00","id":3783,"title":"","content":"For Snowdrop, I have to agree with what Weimann said. Good animation, but had some issues with telling instead of showing, and the monologue at the end dragged on for far too long without actually saying anything new. It also felt as if it was beating me over the head with &quot;Are you sad yet!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer Button's Adventures to Snowdrop and Double Rainboom.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S2VhC1QF7ww\" data-code=\"S2VhC1QF7ww\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/S2VhC1QF7ww/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T19:11:18-08:00","id":3935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3783#post3783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I prefer Button's Adventures to Snowdrop and Double Rainboom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Button's Adventures is hilarious. It and Rainbow Dash Presents are the only fanworks I really keep up with now that the shed.mov series is done. And shed.mov was always a guilty pleasure anyway, like watching a train wreck. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:43:09-08:00","id":16142,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i2.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/501/201/272\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Tomorrow...</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:12:54-08:00","id":16190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impulsiveIngenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3526#post3526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woo, ponies! Sadly, though, I too am on the no spoilers train.<br /> <br /> Wait... this is in the Exalted forum, what's...<br /> <br /> .... ponies confirmed for 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention that, given the Shard I've been working on....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T14:29:30-08:00","id":16280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vegetalss4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=3663#post3663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> I thought that was just yet another case of &quot;&quot;as a company we do not acknowledge that this is happening, but think it is cool that it is&quot;, like all other fan-made stuff.<br /> Where did Hasbro give it, their official blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>When they didn't kill it like they did with Fighting Is Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T15:52:12-08:00","id":16315,"title":"","content":"This thread be relocated?<br /> <br /> There shall be a reckoning.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I'd like to take this opportunity to direct people to what I think is the finest fan map of Equestria yet made, and a pretty good example of map making overall.<br /> <br /> I shall be making use of it for Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2011/348/6/f/map_of_equestria_by_djinn327-d4czwjj.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2011/348/6/f/map_of_equestria_by_djinn327-d4czwjj.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2011/348/6/f/map_of_equestria_by_djinn327-d4czwjj.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2011/348/6/f/map_of_equestria_by_djinn327-d4czwjj.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:00:31-08:00","id":16586,"title":"","content":"Dammit! Knew I should have posted those Pony Charms quicker...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anywho, we're only about an hour away from Pony Hour! What are you hoping for in the new season? I think I'd most like to see Celestia succeed at being *effective* at something, otherwise I have to conclude that she's come down with a serious case of Worf's Flu...<br /> <br /> Between this and the season premier of Doctor Who, today is Geek Heaven! If only Sherlock's Third Season and Exalted Third Edition had managed to come out today, I'd be set! Well, I'd probably *explode*, but still...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:37:20-08:00","id":16609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=16586#post16586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywho, we're only about an hour away from Pony Hour! What are you hoping for in the new season?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I posted my hopes, some of them got fulfilled, and it was awful. I will do this much like I do 3e; I'll leave it in the hands of the writers and try to come at it as blank as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=16586#post16586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd most like to see Celestia succeed at being *effective* at something, otherwise I have to conclude that she's come down with a serious case of Worf's Flu...</div> </div> </div> </div>When Chrysalis defeated Celestia was probably my one instance of nerd freakout in the show. Great was my rage for a week or so. The only other thing in the pony community that's enraged me harder was Fighting is Magic getting C&amp;D'd.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, though, I'm kind of glad for the implications Celestia's defeat had. It clearly shows that needs Twilight, for one, but more importantly it shows that power (because she's clearly powerful) doesn't have to be physical, manifest, destructive power. I like that we have a god-queen who is clearly in charge for a good reason but still needs her champions to fight for her.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, this forum messes up my pony avatar something fierce. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 11-23-2013, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T07:16:11-08:00","id":16626,"title":"","content":"So, it's doing a lot right so far, Season 4 is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-23-2013, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T07:21:39-08:00","id":16629,"title":"","content":"Aww, I failed to catch a stream. I'll have to wait for YouTube. Just a few more hours.<br /> <br /> A few more <i>hours</i>! Gaaaah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T08:03:08-08:00","id":16643,"title":"","content":"I don't feel like doing a full on review, so I'll be brief. This was a remarkably mature opening for the season, beautifully animated, and appropriately dark. Discord is the episode and is done a great service in his portrayal particularly, but this episode clearly sets up the rest of the seasons themes and ideas solidly. It's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T08:10:33-08:00","id":16645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=16315#post16315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread be relocated?<br /> <br /> There shall be a reckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, now I have to actually go to other parts of these forums.<br /> This attack on the Exalted forums microcosm, Shall Not Stand!<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Well it porbably will, after all I can't think of anything I could do about it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">As for the New episode, I am still high on new episode Pony.<br /> But I think that this will be one of my favorite episodes to date.<br /> Also Twilicorn is the most Twily-like princess in the whole twily universe.<br /> Twily.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T09:55:42-08:00","id":16675,"title":"","content":"Spoilers below, as expected.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E1-2: Princess Twilight Sparkle</b><br /> <br /> Omigod omigod omigod!!!!!1!<br /> <br /> Yeah, had to get that out of the way. I am excited for this season. Not as excited as I may have been other times, but god damn it, it's ponies. I just love the fact that they're back.<br /> <br /> And the introductory episode was wonderful. I've said before that FiM isn't too good at doing the adventure type of episodes. This might be attributed to the fact that in the end, it's still a kid's show, and the type of adventure that entails isn't necessarily that impressive for someone who's watched Game of Thrones. But this might very well be the best adventure episode they've done yet. They actually did manage to establish a form of uncertainty about the outcome by kidnapping Celestia and Luna, and I could see half of season 4 being about Twilight learning the pricess trade the hard way. They didn't go that route, and I didn't really think they would either, but it wasn't entirely unrealistic. Well done on that.<br /> <br /> This episode also played excellently on tying things back to what we know, and by adding to it. I never even imagined where the Elements of Harmony came from in the first place, but the idea that they're some kind of fruit is not only utterly hilarious to me but also raises questions I'm sure will be developed in depth in fanfics. It also gave a quick refresher on why Discord is infinitely more dangerous than he lets on. I did quite like that. I wonder how many other little time bombs that's been ticking for 1000 years are spread around Equestria. One thing I was not a big fan of is how the episode dealt with Nightmare Moon; turns out Celestia defeated her in about three minutes. Again, we have the problem with rushing things in this show. In a more dedicated adventure show, how epic would the Nightmare Wars have been to delve into? Hella epic, is how. But I'm willing to flat out selectively disregard the flashbacks, to be honest. It's not likely to come up again in the show anyway.<br /> <br /> We don't get many friendship moments we haven't honestly already seen, but I like how Applejack takes the fore a lot in this episode. It feels entirely appropriate to her persona, and I'd not object towards making her the voice of reason in an even bigger way than she already is. Otherwise, amusing interactions between the mane six are fairly limited, which is kind of a bummer.<br /> <br /> One thing I noted was that Discord prided himself on having given Twilight &quot;a princess lesson&quot; towards the end. That's... wrong. Applejack gave her a princess lesson; the idea that you shouldn't put the only remaining alicorn princess at risk is entirely correct. A leader is needed. Turn out, of course, that sticking to her friends worked out in this case, but as much as they have said that not much will change between the mane six, I'm looking forward to seeing if they'll pull the royal duty card at any other points ahead.<br /> <br /> One thing that <i>did</i> change in this episode was, of course, the relinquishing of the Elements of Harmony. This is highly interesting. The status quo is broken, and suddenly there's a whole new threat to keeping Discord around. As has been seen previously in the episode, he is not to be trusted. I still think he's running a long con here. Remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> And, of course, that delicious locked box. I hope they'll return to that more throughout the season than they did in the last season with the book with Starswirl's spell in it (ie, one second flash in the first episode and then not a word about it until the last). They made it pretty clear it'd be a returning thing, though, so I have pretty high hopes.<br /> <br /> All in all, hell yes. Strong start with only a few annoyances. We're back on track. Here we go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:33:40-08:00","id":16827,"title":"","content":"Wait, it's starting <i>now</i>?!<br /> <br /> Dammit, I literally have no time for this between Eirtakon and sleeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T18:28:05-08:00","id":16891,"title":"","content":"Initial thoughts on part 1: Interesting bits of world-building, plus Discord signing &quot;Winter Wrap-Up.&quot;<br /> Initial thoughts on part 2: More world-building, more goddamn stairs in the way, and HOLY CRAP EQUESTRIA HAS ROCKODILES.<br /> <br /> The mysterious six-keyed box... I hope we get the episodes dealing with the keys distributed relatively evenly across the season, rather than having it all crammed into the season finale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":1048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","user":"Ryumaru","date":". 11-23-2013, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T21:03:44-08:00","id":16922,"title":"","content":"Is cute ponies doing cute pony things. Twilight trying to fly was super cute, and I was really intrigued by the heavy inclusion of Discord and the world building.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=16315#post16315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, I'd like to take this opportunity to direct people to what I think is the finest fan map of Equestria yet made, and a pretty good example of map making overall.<br /> <br /> I shall be making use of it for Exalted.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2011/348/6/f/map_of_equestria_by_djinn327-d4czwjj.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs71/f/20...27-d4czwjj.png</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I take offense to this map as there is no indication of donkey majority anywhere!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:34:42-08:00","id":18156,"title":"","content":"Watched the first two episodes, and I can state with confidence that <i>every aspect of this show has been ruined forever.</i><br /> <br /> More seriously: nah, it was fine. Standard two-part saving-the-world episode to kick off the season, as is the norm. Darker than I'd prefer, to be honest - I like gritty-dark-mature themes to stay far away from this show (a big part of why I don't involve myself in much fanmade content; the popularity of Fallout Equestria is a prime example), and the whole Twilight-needs-to-seclude-herself-in-safety moment strayed too close for my liking. Given that sending her back to Ponyville turned out to be a bad idea, I don't think I need to worry about the writers getting all serious-business, but who knows. Giving up the Elements and thereby losing the trump card vs. Discord had similar potential, but I have no doubt that whatever's hidden in that box will prove an appropriate replacement if he goes all villainous again.<br /> <br /> Speaking of that box, hopefully it will also provide some interesting character-study-ish episodes centered around each of the main six characters. (Maybe all of them will turn into alicorn princesses as they learn their personal lesson. I think that might be worth it just to see how pissed off people would get. :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 11-26-2013, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T23:00:38-08:00","id":18198,"title":"","content":"Special double post: finally took the opportunity to watch Equestria Girls. Definitely not bad. I mean, the message about social divisions was a little cliche to me, but it's a kids' show, it doesn't need to be groundbreaking.<br /> <br /> The last fifteen minutes or so really caught me off guard, though. After an hour of mundane high school life and simple messages about kindness and humanity, I was not expecting things to get all <i>Buffy the Vampire Slayer</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T09:13:15-08:00","id":18446,"title":"","content":"Pilgrim approves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:42:42-08:00","id":18631,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't take Discord's &quot;princess lesson&quot; as more than the excuse it blatantly was. I'm really liking that his motives are pretty ambigous so far...that's better writing than I've come to expect from the last season.<br /> <br /> What's in the box?! My best theories:<br /> <br /> 1) Flash Sentry's head.<br /> <br /> 2) New Elements<br /> <br /> 3) One big, new Element.<br /> <br /> 4) Princess Skyla (who takes the role of the Elements)<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, it will most likely be revealed at the Equestrian Games, which the season is apparently building up to. I was a little disappointed that there wasn't a real villain behind this ep, per se, but apparently new ones are coming. I'm guessing the Pony of Shadows turns out to be something innocuous, like the groundskeeper or something...<br /> <br /> Seeing the canonical fall of Discord and Nightmare Moon, while cool, makes me suddenly realize why some folks think giving a close look at the First Age of Exalted might be a bad idea...Suddenly, a lot of fanfics, extant and potential, just died a lasting death. Oh well, that's what AU continuity is for!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T03:22:17-08:00","id":19069,"title":"","content":"After a long hiatus from the sketchpad, I've sketched up another 3e signature Solar pony: Prince Diamond!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://fc07.deviantart.net/fs71/i/2013/331/a/6/exalted_ponies___prince_diamond_by_hushnowquietnow-d6vsxhc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Anybody want me to repost the others here?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's four out of five done, only Perfect Soul remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T03:27:22-08:00","id":19638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=18631#post18631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing the canonical fall of Discord and Nightmare Moon, while cool, makes me suddenly realize why some folks think giving a close look at the First Age of Exalted might be a bad idea...Suddenly, a lot of fanfics, extant and potential, just died a lasting death. Oh well, that's what AU continuity is for!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a pretty big problem for me. Not that I read much fan material, but I still think that at this time, the material produced in the fandom is more interesting than what's in the show from a dramatical standpoint. Thus, I'm not too keen on pronouncing too much canon, while I do like hints and implications that can then be built on. For example, the Tree of Elements. What's up with that? I honestly hope we'll never know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't think these two episodes destroyed too much, though. The idea that Luna raised the moon, became Nightmare Moon, was battled by Celestia and banished to the moon in the time span of three minutes seems like a medium conceit to me and shouldn't be taken too seriously, while the battle against Discord was literally &quot;Hey Discord! We'll defeat you now, k?&quot; and could have been the end of any amount of struggle beforehand.<br /> <br /> What I think was most interesting is the structure in which Celestial stores the Elements. That's the same structure that's in Nightmare Moon's castle in pilot episode. Might this mean Canterlot wasn't built at the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T15:38:25-08:00","id":20406,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, finally caught it (had to watch Equestria Girls first; basic verdict, I did not hate it). A more in-depth recap might be forthcoming, but for now, my thoughts come down to two factors:<br /> <br /> * Best season opener since the start. Probably one of the best episodes yet. The pacing was good, the stakes felt really high and genuine (and the fact that they were tailored to each pony race was a very nice touch), and though it lacked a specific antagonist*, I think it was actually kind of stronger for it, in being able to let the force itself be threatening in its unremitting facelessness (certainly the monster plants feel like the most genuinely dangerous things yet), as a realisation of the dangerous potential the Everfree Forest has always seemed to have (even if the thing itself wasn't strictly of it). Also liked the sense of characterisation in it, Twilight's struggling with duty and the others struggling with her having to engage with that. Discord's return was also a good use of him, this kind of trickster ally pushing and prodding them. The depictions of the background mythology of the setting were also extremely well realised (little touches I liked included Discord's time having wattle huts for the ponies and Luna being all scuffed up). And I like the implications of some genuine kind of sacrifice being entailed in the resolution.<br /> * This is technically kind of a subset of the other point, but it stood out enough to me to warrant saying separately; the visual composition and direction of this episode was phenomenal. Framing, contrast, motion, this is definitely the best looking episode yet. It really helped with my immersion. I'd understand if this was the kind of big budget thing they can only have at the start, but I really hope some of it can carry through into the rest of the season.<br /> <br /> All in all, full marks. Definitely has me stoked for what's to come, after a shaky prior season.<br /> <br /> * Depending on how much you buy Discord's reform, mind. There's some interesting ambiguity there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T18:30:53-08:00","id":20451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=16922#post16922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take offense to this map as there is no indication of donkey majority anywhere!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, donkeys are still Equines, and they seem to live in more or less the same society as the ponies (whereas cattle and bison, while both Bovines, probably live kind of differently).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T10:10:17-08:00","id":20676,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E3: Castle Mane-ia</b><br /> <br /> What is a pony? A miserable pile of friendsh- yeah let's not do that.<br /> <br /> So in this episode, the mane six <i>minus one conspicuously absent</i> <i>pony</i> spends the night in the Castle of the Two Sisters (which I don't think has been ever named before, has it?) and inadvertently scare the living crap out each other. The plot is pretty standard but it's done pretty well I think, particularly in the end when they all freak out together; I laughed harder than I should have when Applejack stomped on the pillar Fluttershy thought Angel was under. In some way, everyone's personalities come to their right in a really subtle and natural way here, and it was nice to watch. Although... did anyone seriously believe that the Pony of Shadow was not Pinkie Pie? I mean, all the other five gathered at a place and one spooky, unidentified one? I guess the kids might find it thrilling, though.<br /> <br /> Aside from the main plot, this episode had some excellent call-backs. I asked in a post above about the old castle, and here we get an episode about it right form the start. And boy oh boy is this episode <i>brimming</i> with fandom material to explore. Celestia's journal and the Organ to the Outside [1] just as examples, and also the whole situation: is this where they lived before they were regents of Equestria, possibly before they defeated Discord? Is there a reason they lived in the Everfree Forest? Come to think of it, just what is up with that forest anyway? It's creepy and dangerous and <i>clearly</i> magical, and it is the origin of the Elements of Harmony. So much potential about that place just in these three episodes. Not tomention, of course, the shadow with the glowy eyes at the end. Will the be returning, or was it was an ominous OR WAS IT?! moment?<br /> <br /> Speaking of returning, I'm really happy they came back to the locked box right away, and that they used it to fuel the plot of the episode without the episode actually being about it. This is good storytelling; begin with something known and then expand it into something unknown. It's also something FiM has been less than excellent at doing the last few seasons. It's only been 3 of 26 episodes, but I'm loving how it's looking so far.<br /> <br /> A few complaints would be these: I get that it's not the point of the episode, but remember back when the Everfree Forest was a place you just did not go? Ever? This is the second time in three episodes, and this time it was just a Sunday stroll to get to the castle, it seems. I realise that last time they tried, Nightmare Moon was actively messing with them, but even the last episode it was a matter of sending Twilight home <i>in case they all died</i>. The clash bothered me. Also, I have to say, I kind of thought Pinkie was just a <i>bit</i> overdone. She works best when she's not explained very much, and the whole justification behind her being there went on just long enough to make me actually think about it, and then it just didn't hold up. But I did love how she rang the school bell.<br /> <br /> All in all, a few so-so spots, but absolutely a worthy follow-up to that excellent season intro. I heartily approve.<br /> <br /> [1] Note to self: Once Exalted 3e hits, build this Manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 11-30-2013, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T13:00:13-08:00","id":20743,"title":"","content":"Well the forest this time has the elements back in the tree so maybe that's having a positive effect on the forest?<br /> <br /> Also.<br /> <br /> Continuity error!<br /> <br /> Rarity sees 2 big blue tapestries correct? The one with Lune rapmant that Fluttershy triggers the secret spinning wall. Then the one in the throne room above Luna's old seat.<br /> <br /> Rarity is fiddling with the tapestry in the throne room when she gets flipped through the trap door, tearing THAT tapestry.<br /> <br /> But later when running like mad the tapestry she got covered in later was the one with Luna rampant, the one with the spinning wall Fluttershy triggered.<br /> <br /> The scene at the end though has her repairing the tapestry she got covered in. That means she's sewing part of the throne room tapestry to the Luna rampant tapestry!<br /> <br /> Yes my full time job is QA. I am a professional complainer. Literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T13:15:34-08:00","id":20751,"title":"","content":"Huh, I never noticed that. Then again, that's par for the course. :P<br /> <br /> What I did notice in relation to that, though, was that when Rarity was sewing the tapestry, they actually bothered to animate the progress each stitch had. Any other comic would have just put the motion on loop, but if you look closely you can see new stitches being added. I'm impressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T14:32:36-08:00","id":20796,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, attention to quality where it matters is what the series does well.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I'm not one for analysing the series much, I just know that when an episode ends there's usually a silly grin or smirk on my face. Which is all that matters.<br /> <br /> I do kind of wish that Rarity takes some of the tapestries with her though...or perhaps they get Big Mac/Applejack/Applebloom in there to fix the place up proper like. Applebloom would get it done nice and quick, if the treehouse transformation is anything to go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T15:11:37-08:00","id":20815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=20796#post20796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do kind of wish that Rarity takes some of the tapestries with her though...or perhaps they get Big Mac/Applejack/Applebloom in there to fix the place up proper like. Applebloom would get it done nice and quick, if the treehouse transformation is anything to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm betting they'll fix it up to be Twilight's new home. I mean, why live in a tree library when you can live in a Friendship Palace Playset?<br /> <br /> This ep was totes adorbs. The beekeeper suits, the amazing variety of scared faces... I was squeeing all the time from it! I am a very manly man, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T04:46:12-08:00","id":21116,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the idea that the ancient &quot;traps&quot; were basically there as a form of entertainment.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Princess, why would you want to get flipped and tosses and barred inside your own castle?&quot;<br /> &quot;It was the style at the time.&quot;<br /> &quot;And the... weird spiked armour-&quot;<br /> &quot;Style!&quot;<br /> <br /> I was also heartily amused by the thing with Pinkie Pie.<br /> <br /> Pinkie Pie: Can I play the piano anymore?<br /> Twilight Sparkle: Of course you can.<br /> Pinkie Pie: Well I couldn't before!<br /> <br /> And having seen some ancient tapestries myself, I can really appreciate Rarity's desire to restore some.<br /> <br /> I'm amused by the idea of her being drawn more to Luna's ones.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, as &quot;night in a scary house&quot; episodes go, this was a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T23:57:05-08:00","id":21474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=18631#post18631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't take Discord's &quot;princess lesson&quot; as more than the excuse it blatantly was. I'm really liking that his motives are pretty ambigous so far...that's better writing than I've come to expect from the last season.</div> </div> </div> </div>I somewhat agree. Discord is willing to push the limits of his friendship (simply because it's entertaining for him and he is after all, the embodiment of chaos) but is not willing to go over the edge. He might not care about the rest of the 5, but he does care enough about fluttershy to pull the punches.<br /> <br /> I personally think he enjoys toying with Twilight more than anything just to deal with his boredom. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:27:46-08:00","id":25124,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E4: Daring Don't</b><br /> <br /> I have to hand it to them. Of all the things they could have done with Daring Do, I didn't expect this. In fact, up until that most dramatic plot twist, the story proceeded almost exactly as the first minute had lead me to believe it would. And then it didn't.<br /> <br /> In fact, the whole episode is kind of divided into two parts for me. The first one is the part that deals with the concept of fandom, of how your relationship to your favoured author looks in relation to how <i>you feel like</i> it looks and how things that are actually rather minor can seem huge. This part works <i>really well</i>. This is a subject that I think many people deal with today. A great abundance of people are fans of something, and will know just how it can feel when something you've been waiting for sometimes <i>years</i> get delayed another two months (on an <i>entirely unrelated</i> unrelated note, I think Exalted 3e was originally announced for this time of year, <i>last year</i>, but I have <i>no idea</i> what made me think of <i>that</i>). And it's most assuredly a nod towards the brony fandom as well. Rainbow Dash and to some extent Twilight spends the whole first part of the episode acting like typical internet fangirls. All in all, this subject matter is an excellent foundation for an interesting episode with a relevant moral.<br /> <br /> And then... they just don't do that? I mean, I guess they do to some extent as laid out above, but why exactly did they feel the need to make an adventure episode out of this half-way through? The fact that Daring Do is non-fiction doesn't even bother me; it's not what I'd have done but it's not a big deal anyway (Also, A. K. Yearling? Best pony name.). I'm not sure that in the end, we even get an answer for what is delaying the book, or if this adventure actually helped any. I don't really care about that, either. But I felt like they had something in their hands and just didn't recognize it. They had a good idea and just didn't think it would carry, so they threw in some adventure at the end. Maybe I'll feel differently when I've rewatched it, but right now I'm feeling a bit teased, as it were.<br /> <br /> Edit: For all that though, there are some good jokes there. I loved Pinkie Pie's paint, and I predict this is the only episode where you'll be able to see Rainbow Dash punching herself repeatedly in the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 12-07-2013, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T09:38:10-08:00","id":25174,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah. Third episode, good. This episode? Enjoyable, but piss once they played it straight. Should have gone with the fandom exploration.<br /> <br /> Or at least made the joke it was all a fanfic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:48:39-08:00","id":25329,"title":"","content":"So, my question is: why is Daring Do refusing help from the ELEMENTS OF HARMONY? Y'know, the six ponies who've saved Equestria... I think four times now? I mean, yeah, there's the trust thing, but you'd think national heroes would be considered trustworthy. And even if she lives in isolation like that you'd think she'd have heard about them by now.<br /> <br /> Still, my favorite line is Twilight's &quot;That's NOT a plan!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T15:07:20-08:00","id":25362,"title":"","content":"My favourite was Rainbow Dash punching herself. Repeatedly. In the face.<br /> <br /> That is a good question, though. It's really remarkable how unknown the Elements of Harmony are in Equestria. It doesn't help that there's no good way of making out what kind of magic and/or technology is available. In our hyper-medialised society, it's easy to forget how slow and selectively information can get spread without the proper channels. I don't think we've ever seen a TV, have we? But we have seen papers, trains and other things at least, so they have some communication. It's hard to judge how much the common pony would know about their royalty, or hell, even about the threats themselves. How many outside of Canterlot even knew that Nightmare Moon was back? That's actually a valid question. I've no answer, though.<br /> <br /> Another good question is how none of the ponies knew about this monster guy who's name I can't be bothered to attempt writing when he apparently lived within walking distance. The first Daring Do books made it out like this was some land far away, but (just like the last episode with Everfree) it seems to be easy for them all to get over there on hoof. Not even wings, since at least two of the ponies can't fly (I guess Pinkie Pie can't either, but that never stopped her before). It bothers me, but I'm coming to terms with my suspension of disbelief just having to extend to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T15:25:10-08:00","id":25384,"title":"","content":"My favorite moment was the rapid-fire fangirl argument between Twilight and Rainbow Dash. It sounded like something I would hear on these forums. I liked this episode, because I like Rainbow Dash being silly in general and because adventure episodes are frequently fun. Also because self-esteem problems are a thing for me and I gravitate toward media that toys with those themes. As a total sidenote: in last week's episode, I really should have been able to figure out that Pinkie Pie was the Mare of Shadows. Felt dumb as hell after the big reveal. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:00:26-08:00","id":25502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=25124#post25124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S4E4: Daring Don't</b><br /> And then... they just don't do that? I mean, I guess they do to some extent as laid out above, but why exactly did they feel the need to make an adventure episode out of this half-way through? The fact that Daring Do is non-fiction doesn't even bother me; it's not what I'd have done but it's not a big deal anyway (Also, A. K. Yearling? Best pony name.). I'm not sure that in the end, we even get an answer for what is delaying the book, or if this adventure actually helped any. I don't really care about that, either. But I felt like they had something in their hands and just didn't recognize it. They had a good idea and just didn't think it would carry, so they threw in some adventure at the end. Maybe I'll feel differently when I've rewatched it, but right now I'm feeling a bit teased, as it were.<br /> <br /> Edit: For all that though, there are some good jokes there. I loved Pinkie Pie's paint, and I predict this is the only episode where you'll be able to see Rainbow Dash punching herself repeatedly in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain it was implied that the book was delayed because the adventure it was describing was still ongoing. When the book finally <i>was</i> completed, RD's help netted her a place on the cover.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know how long they were traveling for, or how far. IIRC, they bounced off a few cities before reaching A.K. Yearling's house.<br /> <br /> Also also, I'm kind of curious now how many other ponies <i>also </i>save Equestria/the world on a semiregular basis. Maybe this is part of the reason that the mane 6 doesn't get the levels of attention that we expect they would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T04:21:02-08:00","id":25733,"title":"","content":"Well this episode was tons of fun. Started me recording my thoughts as it went through again.<br /> <br /> Here they are, unedited:<br /> <br /> i thought rainbow was excited for the games<br /> can pegasi do that tail cyclone thing<br /> heh, birds around the head<br /> rarity loves her giant hats<br /> ha exalted development joke<br /> map visual gag is fun<br /> books and thugs, it's all adventure game innit<br /> belloq pony<br /> more in over your heads than nightmare moon? or discord? or the changelings? sombra? the invasion of the everfree forest?<br /> it's fun to see rainbow dash with a hero<br /> i like the idea of a jaded middle aged pony adventurer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> wait, so is all that stuff twilight knows about ak yearling real, or a cover, or what<br /> heh fagin pony<br /> hmm, wonder if this'll turn out to not be real... do ponies have movies? there was that bit in the bad seed song...<br /> heh, ring pun<br /> awww and he turned it around<br /> i kind of wish twilight would go the whole hog and explicitly say &quot;we've been on all kinds of crazy adventures you foo&quot;<br /> noooooo, not sweltering heat! :O<br /> heh, applejack can't pronounce names<br /> &quot;use the spears! use the spears as spears!&quot;<br /> heh wilhelm scream<br /> nooo, my cultural heritage site!<br /> aw yeah, they're doing a diary now.<br /> aw that's nice, she gets to be in the book<br /> so was daring do taking so long because she hadn't had the full adventure to write about yet? Maybe that's Holden and John's problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:03:41-08:00","id":25756,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest, while I enjoyed the first act, and it was certainly funny, I was kind of dreading the idea that we'd have to spend ten to fifteen minutes watching Rainbow Dash be an obnoxiously intrusive and overbearing fan (while the rest of the cast just kind of stands around and comments on how inappropriate she's being, I guess) and then she learns a lesson. Like, that's the kind of episode that I'll be intermittently pausing until I think it'll have my attention again.<br /> <br /> I love this show, but it's at its weakest when the characters act like idiots.<br /> <br /> The moment where the novelist opens the catch on the secret book and it's all Lucasarts adventure game, that was the moment when it really caught my attention, creative and unexpected and letting the characters act in more reasonable and enjoyable to watch ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T08:05:42-08:00","id":25793,"title":"","content":"Gentlemen, BEHOLD!<br /> <br /> Ponies: The Anthology Threeeeeeeeee!!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPW9ki-IfZ8&amp;feature=player_embedded\" data-code=\"sPW9ki-IfZ8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sPW9ki-IfZ8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T11:00:12-08:00","id":29997,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E5: Flight to the Finish</b><br /> <br /> I've said before that I'm typically not well predisposed towards CMC episodes. The dynamic in them hasn't changed in ages. They're usually Those Wacky Kids type of things, Diamond Tiara and Silver Spoon are designated bad fillies and whatever happens at the end will be forgotten by the next episode. I'll admit, Babs Seed did make a return once, but that's about it I think. It seems that they are working on producing more continuity in the show this season, which I cannot praise them enough for, so there's a good chance they'll be showing the CMC as flag-carriers in an upcoming Equestria Games episode. This is, of course, great.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, this CMC episode isn't that different in structure from others of its ilk. In fact, the episode kind of pokes fun at the sameness at some points, like in the following exchange:<br /> <br /> <b>Diamond Tiara:</b> &quot;Did you see that?! I can't believe I'm saying this, but they could win!&quot;<br /> <b>Silver Spoon:</b> &quot;But how do we stop them? We already called them blankflanks!&quot;<br /> <br /> The little metaness is actually pretty amusing, and it bodes well for the new writer who did this episode. Appearently, Ed Valentine is a newcomer to FiM, but is well merited with shows like Sesame Street, Fairly Oddparents, and Ultimate Spider-Man under his belt (I got this from the comments at EQD, though, so bit of a source warning there). I am still a little surprised they let a new hand tackle this episode, though, since the fact that you can write for one show doesn't have to imply you can write for another. I think he pulled it off, though, and to great effect, for which I'm grateful.<br /> <br /> Because yeah, this isn't quite just another CMC episode. This episode addresses one of the oldest issues about Scootaloo; the fact that she can't fly. I'll admit, I actually hoped for a moment that she would actually fly at the end and bring some god damn progression into the CMC, but no such luck. Also, in retrospect, not much is actually said about it. We're not given a reason for why she's landbound, nor any real sense of her being close to flying. Still, the fact that it's getting addressed is actually quite a big deal for me. It's got to be a pretty big burden for a pegasus to not only not have her Cutie Mark but also to not be able to fly. She's an outsider in two ways, and even with friends like the CMC, that hurts. That aspect was definitely the strongest part of the episode for me.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Rainbow Dash really came into her role as leader. She's so good with that. Earlier, Rainbow Dash was on the bottom of my Favourite Mane Six list, but she has climbed significantly. In fact, recent developments might have to lead me to reconsider the positions on that list fundamentally.<br /> <br /> The song was meh. Not cringeworthy, but a little... I don't know? Generic? Didn't do much very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 12-14-2013, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T11:40:40-08:00","id":30015,"title":"","content":"Regarding the flying getting addressed, it was also explicitly stated that she <i>should</i> be able to fly by now. Of course, when you can outrace a train...<br /> <br /> Also, RD's expression when the CMC started talking about getting their cutie marks in flag carrying was great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:56:56-08:00","id":30065,"title":"","content":"To a degree I'd actually wonder if it would be good to see her learn later that she <i>can't</i> fly. Kind of a disability angle or perhaps a lesson in how to handle failure, and not the silly comedic failure of Oh NOEZ Cutie Mark Crusader Detectives! But more...you dedicated yourself to becoming a doctor and worked REALLY REALLY hard at it but...didn't get in to medical school kind of failure.<br /> <br /> Or not. No idea what would be better for the series overall.<br /> <br /> I also find myself looking at the tabs in my browser and shaking my head. Tab 1: My Little Pony Season 4 Ep. 5, Tab 2: MTV Unplugged Nirvana Full Show.<br /> <br /> Juxtaposition ftw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T13:21:19-08:00","id":30077,"title":"","content":"The disability angle was actually what Faust had in mind for Scootaloo at first, so that was definitely in the cards. I don't think they'll go much more into that, though. But I'm kind of wondering about Sweetie Belle's magic as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T13:52:57-08:00","id":30091,"title":"","content":"For Sweetie Belle's magic, I just think back to what we saw of Twilight's magical ability pre-rainboom/cutie mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:31:30-08:00","id":30164,"title":"","content":"<br /> lot of rainbow dash so far...<br /> i like miss harshwhinny; her demeanor is stern, but i find her encouragement of the kids sincere. she even cracks a smile occasionally. she's just trying to reign in rainbow dash, and even that's less anti fun and more &quot;this isn't about you it's about them&quot;<br /> huh, this should have been the song they did at the talent show<br /> Hah, as themes go, diversity can't win out over privilige!<br /> &quot;Blank flanks, blank flanks.&quot; &quot;Jeez, change the darn record, that got old in season 1.&quot;<br /> I like the streamers.<br /> &quot;What do we do? We used up childish name calling, and that's all we know!&quot;<br /> So, I guess they're finally addressing the idea that it's kind of weird that Scootaloo can't fly. This is probably the meanest Diamond and Silver have been yet.<br /> Poor rainbow dash, doesn't have the slightest idea how to be profesionally restrained while still sincere and encouraging.<br /> Awww no, not the group!<br /> &quot;Why have I never realised how awful those two are before?&quot;<br /> Nooo, not the scooter!<br /> Awwww, those bastards teasing us at the end.<br /> <br /> Just gonna say, this is probably the best Cutie Mark Crusader episode yet, just because it lets concerns about cutie marks fall into the background and just be about the girls, as well as their relationship.<br /> <br /> Also nice to see Rainbow Dash still living up to that big sister role for Scootaloo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:42:36-08:00","id":30167,"title":"","content":"I actually kind of feel like the fact that nobody apparently makes a big deal out of it (and Rainbow Dash even seems to acknowledge the possibility that Scootaloo might never fly, although that might just be rhetorical) to be an indication that, while probably uncommon, it's not exactly the most concerning thing in the world.<br /> <br /> I mean, Scootaloo herself never seemed to have a problem with the fact that she can't fly, and even within the context of this episode they mostly hit at the idea that it makes her a bad representation for a pegasus in a routine depicting pony diversity rather than it being a quality that undermines her general aspirations, such as they are (although perhaps her level of fixation, and her question at the end, suggest that she does have a kind of niggling little insecurity behind it).<br /> <br /> Maybe she's just a late bloomer; Fluttershy seemed hardly capable of flight at a point when she was possibly a bit older than Rainbow Dash, although maybe that was just a confidence issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:01:17-08:00","id":30451,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we don't know what's up with her. Maybe she's going to grow into it, maybe it's a disability. I still wonder how easy it'd be for her if her flightlessness progresses into her adult life. She would be an outsider, no matter how many friends she had.<br /> <br /> On another note, I was actually a bit surprised to learn that Ponyville is particularly pluralistic in terms of pony races. Most of the other places we've seen also seem to sport a mix of races. Then again, the other place we've seen the most of is Canterlot, and that's the capitol, so you're bound to get an urban mix there. Unless I'm mistaken, all the crystal ponies were earth ponies of a kind, and I think everypony in Appleoosa were as well. And naturally, only pegasi can live in cloud cities. I don't know if this indicates widespread segregation or not, though; it could be that we just haven't seen enough samples. And in no place yet have all the ponies been unicorns, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:41:16-08:00","id":30501,"title":"","content":"I'd think segregation is the wrong term, since that implies institutional enforcement. It might just be a matter of trends, possibly deriving from certain cultural differences deriving from difference in focus and aptitude.<br /> <br /> Something like unicorns having a higher tendency to be urbanised, considering the academic and manufacturing matters suggested by magic, while earth ponies might be more rural considering not just their proclivity for farming, but also how the general ecology needs to be directly managed.<br /> <br /> It could be different in major cities (although Canterlot still seems to trend towards a predominance of unicorns in high society), but I could see Ponyville as unusual for having those characteristics in such a small town (albeit one that seems to have been a bit of a trade hub, for capitalising on a unique resource and possibly proximity to Canterlot). Or possibly even cities might trend towards different pony tribes kind of coming up and living separately (like, there won't be earth ponies in magic school), while Ponyville seems to have people mixed as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Heck, it even has an earth pony couple with unicorn and pegasus children; that's got to be kind of weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-15-2013, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:20:40-08:00","id":31165,"title":"","content":"In a way I wanted to see Scootaloo fly at the end of the episode too, but I'm also glad they didn't go that direction. The moral of the story was too good to just shove in a happy ending for the sake of happy endings. &quot;You might end up flying, you might not. So what? You're awesome for other reasons anyway.&quot; Imagine what a poke in the eye it would be for a youngster with a disability watching if she starting flying around in the end because she &quot;tried harder this time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T15:57:29-08:00","id":34647,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E6 - Power Ponies</b><br /> <br /> Super heroes. Why did it have to be super heroes?<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll actually admit. The episode is surprisingly good. They don't do the stereotype with saving babies and stuff, like The Mysterious Mare-Do-Well did. For that, I'm eternally thankful. For a show that starts with them all getting sucked into a comic book, it was pretty solidly done. The new villain was pretty well-made, and it helped that I really enjoy people with prehensile hair like that. The Power Pony alter-egos were funny commentaries on the characters, and I won't go into all the subtleties right now but the fact that there <i>were</i> subtleties is very encouraging. Oh, and Rarity had best power.<br /> <br /> But. Super heroes?! I'm just... I realise many people may enjoy super hero comics, but to me, the super hero played straight is <i>stupid</i>. The costumes, the side-kick, the whole premise of their existence... I can't take it. I don't read super hero comics, and I would frankly appreciate if they stayed the heck away from the shows I watch that allegedly are not super hero shows. I am at least grateful that this time, they had the good taste of putting the super heroes in a very literal own universe, and not in the real Equestria... y'know, like The Mysterious Mare-Do-Well.<br /> <br /> I didn't hate this episode, in fact it was better than I had expected for what it was. I just question the justification for its existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T16:49:08-08:00","id":34662,"title":"","content":"Well, this was rather a silly episode.<br /> <br /> But undeniably a very fun one.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just seeing them all play out the superpowers they wound up with was a nice change of pace (I especially like Rainbow Dash going a little bit mad with power).<br /> <br /> And I liked the animation on the Maneiac; all that twitching and lounging and getting into personal space. The voice acting was pretty good for her too.<br /> <br /> Although, is that seriously the explanation they're going with for it; there's just some asshole in Canterlot distributing magical comic books?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T07:36:41-08:00","id":34938,"title":"","content":"I waited all episode to see Fluttershy Hulk out. I was not disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:59:25-08:00","id":35961,"title":"","content":"I'm actually a big fan of superheroes in general, so I had a ton of fun this episode. It oozed Golden Age DC charm, though none of the ponies had ridiculous weaknesses to their powers. If they had the time to explore that, I'd imagine Rarity's weakness would have been tackiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:44:12-08:00","id":36240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=34662#post34662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, is that seriously the explanation they're going with for it; there's just some asshole in Canterlot distributing magical comic books?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly?<br /> <br /> If someone could use magic to make stories that literally sucked you in and let you be the characters (with safety magic too!) do you not think there'd be a market for that?<br /> <br /> Be Superman for a day! Ever wondered what it's like to be a Roman Emperor?!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T14:01:17-08:00","id":36543,"title":"","content":"I just recalled, part of this episode's premise was that the group is reconstructing the old castle.<br /> <br /> Is that something that they brought up before now, or is this the first it was mentioned?<br /> <br /> I'd wonder why... the last episode seemed to present that the library was not especially useful to their quest (although Twilight was certainly enamoured of it)...<br /> <br /> Maybe they've just been given permission for Twilight to establish a seat of power in closer proximity to her friends.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T20:36:46-08:00","id":37133,"title":"","content":"Guys, you gotta help me. What is the joke in the name &quot;Saddle Rager?&quot; This is killing me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:42:51-08:00","id":39506,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E7 - Bats!</b><br /> <br /> I didn't get around this until today. I blame Christmas.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I really liked this episode. On the other hand, I don't have that much to say about it. I feel like this is kind of an adventure episode done right. Previously, I've commented that the big epic adventures that tend to begin and end season often feel rushed and half-baked to me. This one didn't. It was a daring premise with logical (in a loose sense of the word) progression and with a personal stake in the matter for Fluttershy. I even think the moral at the end was very important, and it did a good job of showing how considering multiple perspectives are important. Solid episode, not much more to say, just great fun.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Flutterbat is so becoming a meme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T05:04:06-08:00","id":40463,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I liked the episode and didn't stagger my watching of it or anything, it just doesn't have much to it <i>besides</i> being entertaining.<br /> <br /> Even in its musical number, fun to listen to, certainly a nice kind of melodious difference, kind of insubstantial.<br /> <br /> I do like the joke in the distinction between fruit bats that are made of fruit and fruit bats that eat fruit (and are thus vampires?) probably a bit more than it deserves.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, yet another instance in which people don't really question Twilight's explanations.<br /> <br /> &quot;It took the vampire fruit bats' desire to be vampire fruit bats and transferred that desire into Fluttershy.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, but why can she change shape?&quot;<br /> &quot;Uhmmm... because Pinkie Sense?&quot;<br /> &quot;Good enough for me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T13:25:02-08:00","id":42447,"title":"","content":"No one has mentioned this yet? Build A Bear Workshop has had Pinkie Pie &amp; Rainbow Dash for awhile, but they just now got Fluttershy! (Best pony, yay!) And they have accessories for what she wore at the Grand Galloping Gala!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>First Age Spray may cause temporary insanity, limit breaks or usurptions. Do not use First Age Spray on children. If Shogunate persists, please see your doctor. - Megapope<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://farm4.staticflickr.com/3923/14658615863_c919f4c13c_s.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1099-noshpan","name":"noshpan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1099_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T00:34:11-08:00","id":42751,"title":"","content":"Newest episode, a Rarity episode.<br /> <br /> Not <i>bad</i> but it really felt like it was hammering home the Generosity thing a bit much...it felt disingenuous like she was being nice to people so other people could see her being nice rather than just because she's generous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:58:15-08:00","id":42948,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E8 - Rarity Takes Manehattan</b><br /> <br /> ...then she takes Berlin. Anyone? No? Okay.<br /> <br /> Even if few and far between, Rarity episodes are usually really good. I find that she is the pony who best carries her own episodes, the one who can do best without the support of the ensemble. Of course, this time she did have the rest of the mane six around, but that didn't stop her from putting her own personal spin on it.<br /> <br /> I will have to disagree with Scutarii about how Rarity's character felt. While the song was a bit in-your-face about it, I found the overall impression to be quite natural. It's just these little almost subconscious acts that I think best drives home how the mane six examplifies their Element. I also, in fact, quite liked her breakdown in the middle. It didn't feel out of place at all, and it helped making her feel real to me. The best part was that they didn't make excuses about it, either. It'd have been so easy to go &quot;no, no, it was all right&quot;, but Applejack's &quot;Yeah, you were pretty rotten&quot; makes it clear that it wasn't okay, but that they'll overlook it. Much better handled. In fact, I found that Rainbow Dash and Twilight also were really well-written this time. It strikes me that I may have to grossly rearrange my Best Pony List.<br /> <br /> And that rainbow thread. I absolutely love how they drop little hints that I've no idea what they mean like that. They might mean nothing, though I don't think so. They might even drop a few fake ones, just to shake us up. Sooo much stronger continuity in this season.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I loved this episode. One of the strongest yet the season (and that's in a season which has started out particularly strong), and among the upper tiers ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 01-05-2014, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:08:07-08:00","id":42952,"title":"","content":"The girls get to go to a long sold-out musical?<br /> <br /> I instantly hate this episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:51:05-08:00","id":43552,"title":"","content":"I re-watched it,and it just strikes me again how great the break-down scene is, not least because it has some great lines. &quot;Congratu-pony-lations, fillies!<i> Isn't friendship magic?!&quot; </i>&gt;:O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:49:38-08:00","id":43575,"title":"","content":"Anybody here play MLPCCG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:20:13-08:00","id":43594,"title":"","content":"I'm currently spending all (literally <i>all</i>) my time with the Hearthstone beta right now, so I'm not getting into any other CCGs. I'm not a CCG person to start with, either. I've heard some about it, though. It might be good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T23:04:21-08:00","id":43974,"title":"","content":"I've been working on putting together a Twilight/Pinkie deck, but I have no idea how well it will actually work in practice. I'm going to be going to a tournament at a semilocal game shop this Thursday though, so wish me luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T12:19:18-08:00","id":47003,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E9 - Pinkie Apple Pie</b><br /> <br /> First of all, this song was <i>lovely</i>. I just wanted to get that out of the way. Easily the best song this season. I don't know if it's because I heard it before (it was spoiled at ComicCon, I think), but it's brilliant. I'm getting Smile Smile Smile vibes, actually.<br /> <br /> Second, <i>my god the jokes</i>. This thing is <i>packed</i>. Not just Pinkie Pie being random; actually, she's responsible for surprisingly few of them. Instead, the Apples are at their best. I don't think I've ever seen so much characterisation put into them as a family before, and in some respects in them as individuals as well. And they do it by being gut-bustingly funny as well! I just about lost it with the map: &quot;M to the A to the yeah-that's-right P! Ain't no other pony find the map like me! I'm Apple- uh oh.&quot; I swear, they're spoiling us.<br /> <br /> Third, the story. Once again, the Element of Honesty isn't very good at keeping up false appearances (the curious thing was that she was the one suggesting it in the first place; strange, that). The story and moral is nice, but what's more important to me is that the conveyance of it was really smooth throughout the entire episode. At no point (other than the end, I guess) did it really write us on the nose with it, which there is a tendency towards in some episodes. Very well written. Who did it? Natasha Levinger? Okay! I'll keep an eye out for her!<br /> <br /> Also, was it just me who taken for a complete spin when the episode was actually completely backwards to what you had imagined? I thought for sure it'd be &quot;I'm related to Pinkie Pie? <i>Oh my god no!</i>&quot; on Applejack's part, and Pinkie insisting on pushing herself in where she wasn't welcome. I was incredibly pleasantly surprised, and man did I just realise the sheer amount of fanfiction this will spawn. I scarcely dare imagine it.<br /> <br /> Last epsiode was the best episode in the season by then, but this one beats it outright, and quite solidly too. I thoroughly <i>enjoyed</i> myself. This is how it's done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 01-18-2014, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T15:09:00-08:00","id":47090,"title":"","content":"Excellent episode. Silly grin on my face throughout. No stand out lines - &quot;Isn't friendship <i>maaagic</i>&quot; is still the best of this season - but Pinkie just brings the upbeat and quirkiness so that everyone else does the real comedic work and she's the spice that makes it all come together.<br /> <br /> This Pinkie I think works well because she bring excitement and enthusiasm to everything, rather than being hyperactive and potentially annoying.<br /> <br /> Kind of like how there are the fans of stuff who annoy you by going on and on and then the fans who have infectious enthusiasm. Pinkie's the infectious sort here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:49:45-08:00","id":52672,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E10 - Rainbow Falls</b><br /> <br /> Epsiode 10 already? Man, that went fast. Good luck there are still 16 left, and not 3 like last time. Ho-hum.<br /> <br /> Have I said how happy I am about the recurring continuity between the episodes yet? I know I have. But I'll do it again. <i>I'm really, really happy.</i><br /> <br /> This episode was a pretty standard Rainbow Dash episode, but that's not a bad thing. Rainbow has developed incredibly since season 1. She used to be my least favourite pony, and now she's not. So that's something I guess. Putting Rainbow's Loyalty against her aspirations is an obvious but effective way of creating meaningful conflict in an episode, and it does more often than not make Rainbow herself an interesting and flawed character in them.<br /> <br /> At times, though, I could feel like it became a little bit like the Club for Rainbow Dash Admiration. Scootaloo would have fit right in there. It was &quot;Man, Rainbow Dash is such a good flier.&quot; &quot;Yes I am.&quot; &quot;Yes you are.&quot; It just got a bit thick at times. Meanwhile, Twilight was rather low-key the whole time (growing into her princess-role of never actually doing anything herself, maybe?). And furthermore, I don't usually actually think Pinkie is annoying, but this time? She was annoying.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed myself, though. Basing an episode on the obvious Rainbow dynamic hasn't grown old, like I'd argue that for example Fluttershy's go-to plot has. It was cool to see the gryffon team, Bulge Biceps got a name, and well, Derpy returned. It's all good, no more, no less.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh yeah, and even more continuity with the odd rainbow light, just like with Rarity's spool of thread two episodes ago. How could I forget that? It's notable that in both cases, the rainbow light appeared twice: one where both Rarity and Rainbow Dash came to their senses, in a manner of speaking, and one at the very end, where something they obtained glimmered prismatically, seemingly without them noticing. It's not very hard to guess that these items will be instrumental in opening the locked box Twilight got in the first episode. Just one more of those connection-weaving things. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 01-19-2014, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:08:43-08:00","id":53057,"title":"","content":"The frequent gushing about RD being amazing grated a bit, but at this point it's probably deserved so I'll let that one slide.<br /> <br /> I was pleased to see Fluttershy has remembered her character development, she's a willing participant in a <i>flying</i> event!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:16:16-08:00","id":53059,"title":"","content":"Y'know, thinking about it, I think Bulk Biceps has the same issue with flight that Scootaloo does - they both have to exert tons of extra effort to fly, and they're both buzzing rather than flapping. Not sure if it means anything, but it's food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:01:44-08:00","id":53278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=53059#post53059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, thinking about it, I think Bulk Biceps has the same issue with flight that Scootaloo does - they both have to exert tons of extra effort to fly, and they're both buzzing rather than flapping. Not sure if it means anything, but it's food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since it seems unlikely that Scotaloo can manage to develop all those muscles to partially compensate underdeveloped wings, I guess they need to find a pony with a rocket cutiemark to make her a flying scooter XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T03:10:44-08:00","id":55355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=47003#post47003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, <i>my god the jokes</i>. This thing is <i>packed</i>. Not just Pinkie Pie being random; actually, she's responsible for surprisingly few of them. Instead, the Apples are at their best. I don't think I've ever seen so much characterisation put into them as a family before, and in some respects in them as individuals as well. And they do it by being gut-bustingly funny as well! I just about lost it with the map: &quot;M to the A to the yeah-that's-right P! Ain't no other pony find the map like me! I'm Apple- uh oh.&quot; I swear, they're spoiling us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I favoured the stuff with the bird myself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T12:23:40-08:00","id":57565,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E11 - Three's a Crowd</b><br /> <br /> This episode took me by surprise. I don't do spoilers, so from the intro, I had somehow expected Twilight's day with Cadance to get interrupted by Fluttershy's animal stuff. Which essentially made me write this off as liable to be the first genuinely bad episode for the season. And then there was Discord and everything was awesome all the time.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, at first I was sceptical to the idea of Discord getting &quot;reformed&quot; by Fluttershy, but I've since been proven wrong. He works <i>so much better</i> as a wolf in sheep's clothing. Even at the end here, I don't know if the reason he was disappointed because his plan to prevent Twilight and Cadance to bond hadn't turned out as he had hoped, or if it was just his nature making him put off when people got along. I personally think he's running a long-con here, but I'm not sure, and <i>that's fantastic</i>.<br /> <br /> In excess of Discord, this episode had a lot of other things to offer as well. World-building, a new monster (<a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2014/01/tatzlwurm-name-of-new-wurm-creature.html\" target=\"_blank\">apparently called a Tatzlwurm by word of god</a>), an awesome princess laser fight and not to mention that I genuinely like Cadance. Other notable things were: Crystal Empire train is swaggest train ever. First sighting of a crystal pegasus in Cadance escort, so far they've all been earth ponies. Was it just me, or was the other guard to escort Cadance Flash Sentry, from Equestria Girls? For some reason, I didn't think Cadance would have been the girl to appreciate a Starswirl con, but hey, I'll take it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and just that little other detail of <i>Discord singing!!!</i> Genuinely great, seriously one of the best songs this season, second only to Apples Forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T01:44:43-08:00","id":58585,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who saw Discord's sudden eruption in green spots as a very Looney Toons moment?<br /> <br /> I also like how the crystal train makes an awful scraping noise. And some of the background details of what Discord sneezed on was doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T06:01:08-08:00","id":58654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=58585#post58585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like how the crystal train makes an awful scraping noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The subway trains in Boston make the same sound, but louder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T14:42:30-08:00","id":63126,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E12 - Pinkie Pride</b><br /> <br /> <b>Applejack:</b> She actually <i>has</i> a goof-off rulebook?<br /> <b>Spike:</b> Are you kidding? Twilight can find a rulebook for everything!<br /> <br /> ...can haz Exalted 3e plz? :O<br /> <br /> Right, let's get straight to the big thing. Weird Al Yankovic. This has been something that's been talked about for a long time, and I've always had this attitude of &quot;whatever&quot; towards it. Weird Al occupies a strange place in my heart, somehow straddling the line between being really good and just too silly. Many of his songs play too much on American culture that I just don't understand, and many of his lyrics are not quite there for me. But equally many are, so... well, when talk about him appearing in FiM came up, I could take it or leave it. It wasn't anything I was looking forward to in particular.<br /> <br /> And now, when it happened? Well, I'll say that Weird Al's performance as Cheese Sandwich was rock solid. One of my concerns with taking him in was that they'd do it just for the sake of it; as good as he is at singing, maybe problems with his voice acting would get overlooked because of the glamour of his stardom. That was emphatically not the case. He'd fit right in, right the hell in with all the others as a regular if he wanted to. And while Cheese Sandwich was clearly designed around Weird Al's persona to a great extent, it didn't feel constructed... okay, it did feel constructed, but not shoehorned in or violently out of place.<br /> <br /> The songs were also good, if not beating Apples to the Core and Discord's song last episode in this season. With Pinkie and Weird Al, I'd expect no less than a semi-musical. However, unfortunately the spoken manuscript does not boast the same quality as the sung one, and is easily the episode's weakest link. The focus has clearly been on Cheese Sandwich's lines, which is understandable, but the rest feels uninspired with many repetitions, unnatural phrasing and stating of the obvious. Compare this to Rarity Takes Manehattan, for example: no contest at all.<br /> <br /> I realised about half-way through that this episode would contain Pinkie's &quot;rainbow moment&quot;, and I suppose it makes sense. The conflict was neatly resolved with a reasonable moral, but there were such extremes; first Pinkie quitting, then her issuing a challenge in the city square and then, after forfeiting, packing to leave the town? It's a bit too, well, cartooony for what I've come to expect if FiM. And Weird Al certainly carried the plot; often, the aforementioned issues felt like they were covered up by waving Cheese Sandwich around for distraction.<br /> <br /> So in the end, did I like the episode? Yes. Season four has yet to have a genuinely bad episode. But it was a gimmick episode, one I can only really praise for efficient use of the guest star against an appropriate permanent cast member.<br /> <br /> I could still take or leave Weird Al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-01-2014, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T14:48:03-08:00","id":63128,"title":"","content":"Not that I dsagree with you on this episode, but really? Season four has yet to have genuinely bad episodes? Do Power Ponies or Daring Don't mean nothing to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:22:58-08:00","id":63150,"title":"","content":"Power Ponies is the weakest one in the season, certainly, and I'll agree that it didn't add much. But I can't shake the feeling that the lack of lustre comes from comparisons with the others. It feels like inconsequential filler in season four, because season four actually has continuity. In season three, it would have looked much better. I did like the villain's design, as Evil (tm) as she was. Maybe I'm also just so happy that they decided to shut the super hero crap away in a whole different dimension, the portal to which is visibly seen to vanish in the last frame, that I don't bother to issue further objections.<br /> <br /> Daring Don't was really <i>really</i> good the first half, and the second half would have been better if I didn't feel so let down by them not running with a theme that I felt was <i>so obviously right there oh my god how could they not have seen it</i>- *cough* However, many seems to have enjoyed the twist, and I'm not sure I can honestly call it bad. The execution of what they did chose to do isn't actaully bad, and the first part of the episode is so strong that I can kind of make do with what I got there. A disappointment, but FiM has given me way worse.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'll stand by my statement that none of the episodes have been genuinely bad. Some worse than other, but none without some substantial redeeming factor. Which cannot be said for several others in previous seasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T00:03:01-08:00","id":63324,"title":"","content":"Did not enjoy this one and, while there are multiple niggles, the main reason is the name. Cheese Sandwich sounds...dumb. And every time his name was mentioned it grated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T05:25:41-08:00","id":63390,"title":"","content":"Also, Pinkie is Best Pony (or is it AJ...), this is a Pinkie episode...but it's shared with the guest celebrity and so she is sidelined a bit to let him do his thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T05:55:40-08:00","id":63401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=63324#post63324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did not enjoy this one and, while there are multiple niggles, the main reason is the name. <b>Cheese</b> Sandwich sounds...dumb. And every time his name was mentioned it <b>grated</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huehuehuehue.<br /> <br /> But yeah, that's actually a pretty good representation of what bothers me with Weird Al. Some of his stuff is just... juvenile? And that works some times, but others it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T08:10:07-08:00","id":63436,"title":"","content":"I'm glad someone found that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T00:08:31-08:00","id":68283,"title":"","content":"FINALLY catching up!<br /> <br /> Re: Three's a Crowd - not bad, certainly. Rainbow Dash going &quot;not it&quot; and taking off like lightning was pretty entertaining, for sure. Discord... I liked him better as an outright villain and malevolent force of nature, but here he's still pretty entertaining. The musical number was pretty fantastic. And, as an added bonus, I got some ideas for more Discord Charms, which is always happy. If I build them right, his Charm Trees are going to be <i>incredibly</i> fun.<br /> <br /> Re: Pinkie Pride - Loved it. Absolutely loved it. Cheese Sandwich was highly entertaining, though I will admit I'm being swayed by the repeated references to Westerns, which were easily my favorite part of the episode. Cheese channeling Clint Eastwood's Man With No Name was great, but the icing on top was name-dropping High Noon and then almost immediately referencing 3:10 To Yuma right after. The songs were pretty great, too, and I also loved all the callback jokes, particularly Cheese Sandwich &quot;stealing&quot; Pinkie's Smile song and the ensuing gag. The one bit that was weird was the live-action footage, but given how outright bizarre the focus ponies are in this episode, I'll let it slide. Plus, it was in the same vein as the felt-animated bit in the episode &quot;Smile&quot; originates from, so it's not too bad.<br /> <br /> Re: Simple Ways - I'm not done with it yet, but... um, the animators <i>do </i>know how some people will react to those tunnel-vision shots of Applejack, right? It'll be the wet mane trend all over again. Also Trenderhoof is coming across as a bit... smug. Nah, that's not quite the right word. Superior, that's it. I get the feeling we're getting set up for another Blueblood here. Also, seriously? Another crush episode? Though I admit Spike's glance at the screen was pretty well-timed. Snarky Dragon Mode is fully engaged in this one.<br /> <br /> ... pointing at Derpy and saying &quot;unappreciated.&quot; Yeah this colt's going down hard later, I'm sure.<br /> <br /> Oh God. Rarity attempting a Southern accent is... a mix of painful and funny.<br /> <br /> ... OH GOD NO NOT YOU TOO APPLEJACK.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what was most painful in this episode. Rarity's attempt at a Southern accent, Applejack's attempt at a high-class accent, or this being a bloody love triangle episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T00:39:22-08:00","id":68286,"title":"","content":"I thought this most recent episode was great, Rarity in tears was fabulous overacting, AJ bemused and annoyed throughout.<br /> <br /> Enjoyed this one a lot more than Pinkie Pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:42:34-08:00","id":69149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=68283#post68283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what was most painful in this episode. Rarity's attempt at a Southern accent, Applejack's attempt at a high-class accent, or this being a bloody love triangle episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think AJ's accent was better than Rarity's, but then, AJ did spend some time with the Oranges...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:44:55-08:00","id":69906,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, just catching up on the last couple of episodes.<br /> <br /> I'll comment on the Weird Al one later, but for now, first impression of Simple Ways, at about six minutes in:<br /> <br /> Just when you thought Rarity couldn't get any better, she becomes adorably shy.<br /> <br /> Awesome.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:50:15-08:00","id":69909,"title":"","content":"Second impression: I guess they had to get around to depicting a measure of romantic attentions sooner or later.<br /> <br /> Thank God it's hilarious.<br /> <br /> I think I'll do my usual writing them as they go thing now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T11:08:58-08:00","id":69918,"title":"","content":"best snarky spike moment ever<br /> well, at least she knocked down <i>a</i> apple<br /> confused and concerned big mac is the greatest<br /> rarity is doing an applejack impression. rarity! is doing! an applejack impression!<br /> spike with hat and banjo!<br /> huh, that new mane style actually looks pretty good on her<br /> though the hat and overalls are a bit much. applejack and fluttershy are saying what we're all thinking<br /> oh don't tell me, my heart won't be able to take it<br /> aaaaaand applejack really pulls off <i>her</i> alteration well too. looks like that stint in manehatten didn't go to waste after all.<br /> oh rarity; i knew you would break first.<br /> that trenderhoof is a pretty swell guy<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:54:44-08:00","id":70145,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E13 - Simple Ways</b><br /> <br /> Oh my, I'm a bit late on this one, amn't I? I didn't have opportunity to watch it earlier, but now I have, and I absolutely <i>adore</i> it.<br /> <br /> There are the obvious things. Rarity going country is just too much to bear. Applejack acting all posh is a close second. I mean, the episode is sold with that alone, particularly given Tabitha St Germain habit of absolutely killing Rarity's deliveries. I do think she's the best voice actor working on FiM at the moment, I really do.<br /> <br /> However, the episode also treats the characters, and what's more, even the whole <i>situation,</i> really well. This is highly surprising, particularly given an episode which deals with... well, I'd hesitate to call it love, but infatuation at least. I can't point at any specific points which makes me feel this way (or rather, I can, but listing them would be long and hard), but the whole set-up feels reasonable and there are so many details and off-hand comments which really conveys multitudes of meaning. Take Spike's sarcastic look, for example; he's probably the one feeling the closest thing to love out of all of the involved parties. And Applejack's half-mumbled &quot;maybe you two should try it sometime&quot; makes it abundantly clear what her position on the whole thing is.<br /> <br /> I'll have to watch it again, and I will... tomorrow. I'm kind of getting tired of saying it, but this season just keeps delivering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T22:59:04-08:00","id":71063,"title":"","content":"Fellow Disciple of Celestia checking-in here! I'm from the old WW forums and decided it was time I introduced myself.<br /> <br /> Rarity is getting so much good material this season. Better late than never!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2265-retrokinesis","name":"Retrokinesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2265_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0