posted by <strong>Retrokinesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=71063#post71063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fellow Disciple of Celestia checking-in here! I'm from the old WW forums and decided it was time I introduced myself.<br /> <br /> Rarity is getting so much good material this season. Better late than never!</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you found your way here! Welcome (back)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:25:12-08:00","id":71566,"title":"","content":"That song is nowhere near as catchy as &quot;Helping Twilight Win the Crown&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T17:07:26-08:00","id":71723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=71556#post71556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rainbow Rocks, hmm?...<br /> <br /> *Looks at other pony-related resources for community reactions*<br /> <br /> Yep, significant backlash everywhere. I am now taking bets that everything turns out better than expected, same as the last few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno-the last one barely squeaked by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T16:00:16-08:00","id":72860,"title":"","content":"Rather liked the most recent one and particularly Pinkie's wonderful crazed eyes at the end of her first assault on Fluttershy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T06:46:28-08:00","id":73157,"title":"","content":"I've not seen the Rainbow Rocks clip you're talking about, but I take great satisfaction in that the movies aren't canon. I can just see them as something entirely disconnected. Looking at it that way, Equestria Girls actually had a few interesting aspects in that the mane six were actively unfriendly from the start. I kind of liked that. This one... I'm not sure if it'll catch my attention, but I'm not opposed to its existence. I'll not comment until I've seen it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of comments...<br /> <br /> <b>S4E14 - Filli Vanilli</b><br /> <br /> <b>Zecora:</b> I can cure this pony that is hoarse.<br /> <br /> I died.<br /> <br /> Right, this one is... split for me. On the one hand, the episode itself touched themes I can totally relate to. Not all people handle attention well, even if that attention is positive. That's something we in the western world, with out celebrity culture, sometimes may forget. I can look at some people I follow on YouTube, for example, for real life examples. In fact, Pinkie kind of took on the role of the &quot;well-meaning critic&quot; in this episode, and I thought it came out wonderfully.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, fact is, we know that Fluttershy has been on stage before. Hearthswarming Eve, anyone? She didn't sing, but she sure performed. That just gnaws in the back of my head all throughout this episode, and I can't really overlook it.<br /> <br /> But I still liked the episode, and I'm not going to let a continuity error ruin it, particularly not in a show that's traditionally been rather loose with continuity anyway. The animation, the little jokes, the song - let's not forget about the song, it was great - it was as good as I've come to expect of season 4.<br /> <br /> Edit: Only thing I didn't get was the title? What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:17:04-08:00","id":73276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73157#post73157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S4E14 - Filli Vanilli</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Only thing I didn't get was the title? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to see the episode, but I assume the title is a pun on 80s/90s R&amp;B group Milli Vanilli","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T21:44:42-08:00","id":73545,"title":"","content":"In the Interest of All Things Pony:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.fimfiction.net/story/36641/My-Little-Exalt\" target=\"_blank\">My Little Exalt</a> (Pony Exalted Fanfiction set in Exalted. Pinkie Pie is...well, more than we ever knew <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.mlprim.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My Little Pony: Roleplaying is Magic</a> (S1, S2, &amp; S3) -- S3 is the newest &quot;version&quot; &amp; the most complete. It's not too bad either.<br /> <br /> Enjoy and have fun with all things Pony.<br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Yes...I am a Brony...just don't tell my Wife...)</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T11:50:25-08:00","id":73815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73545#post73545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Interest of All Things Pony:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.fimfiction.net/story/36641/My-Little-Exalt\" target=\"_blank\">My Little Exalt</a> (Pony Exalted Fanfiction set in Exalted. Pinkie Pie is...well, more than we ever knew <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.mlprim.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My Little Pony: Roleplaying is Magic</a> (S1, S2, &amp; S3) -- S3 is the newest &quot;version&quot; &amp; the most complete. It's not too bad either.<br /> <br /> Enjoy and have fun with all things Pony.<br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Yes...I am a Brony...just don't tell my Wife...)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>On the subject of fanfics, I'd like to re-rec <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2011/07/story-of-time-before.html\" target=\"_blank\">Of The Time Before</a>. I just wish it was available in a non-google docs form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T12:12:21-08:00","id":73830,"title":"","content":"Actually, I rather disdain RiM. I'll explain more later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T13:32:47-08:00","id":73856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73830#post73830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I rather disdain RiM. I'll explain more later.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Shrug) It's something to get my Daughter into RPGs (She is into My Little Ponies...). We're slowly transitioning into other RPGs...including Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T13:53:19-08:00","id":73868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73157#post73157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pinkie kind of took on the role of the &quot;well-meaning critic&quot; in this episode, and I thought it came out wonderfully.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... I think I'm going to have to disagree with you on that. Pinkie... did not come across as well-meaning at all. She reduced Fluttershy to <i>tears</i>. <i>Twice</i>. Clearly her friend was very upset by what she was saying, and it seems rather out-of-character, to me at least, that Pinkie wouldn't get that. She's not a dumb &quot;lol I'm so random&quot; character. She, y'know, cares about her friends, and not once did she apologize.<br /> <br /> I will admit, though, that I found the bit where Rarity bopped her on the nose with a rolled-up newspaper pretty funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T13:55:54-08:00","id":73871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73856#post73856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Shrug) It's something to get my Daughter into RPGs (She is into My Little Ponies...). We're slowly transitioning into other RPGs...including Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd... be careful about that, depending on how old your daughter is. Exalted is not exactly something I'd say is aimed for a young audience.<br /> <br /> Now, I <i>did </i>find a little project where someone actually wrote an RPG <i>of</i> My Little Pony, which may be more the speed you're looking for. It was pretty rules-light and was designed with the tone of the show in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:43:08-08:00","id":73895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73871#post73871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd... be careful about that, depending on how old your daughter is. Exalted is not exactly something I'd say is aimed for a young audience.<br /> <br /> Now, I <i>did </i>find a little project where someone actually wrote an RPG <i>of</i> My Little Pony, which may be more the speed you're looking for. It was pretty rules-light and was designed with the tone of the show in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries here, I've been GMing/STing for nearly 40 years and I do know how not to bring things in that a young person, like my daughter, should not be involved in. I ST to a person's maturity level <i>(Which does not always equate to a persons age...)</i>.<br /> <br /> And as far as &quot;Theme&quot; and &quot;Subject Matter&quot; goes...that is in the hands of the ST and other people in the Group. I for one can keep it appropriate to the age/maturity level, and the only other person in the group is my Wife. We set down with her and we all looked thru the various RPGs we have <i>(We have 10 huge group of bookshelves: 4' x 8')</i> -- She decided she liked Exalted, for various reasons. As a 9-year old, the reasons were pretty reasonable and mature. Some of them were too restrictive on her imagination, while other's just didn't appeal to her story <i>(she had a character in mind),</i> and other's were just...&quot;weird&quot; with how the rules worked in the system <i>(too her at least...surprisingly, she's actually picking up on a lot of Exalted...go figure...)</i>. I set down with her, she created a character that fit her concept, and we've been playing about 2-3 times a month over the last 6 months.<br /> <br /> It's &quot;Exalted Morality Lite&quot; when we play with her, but we're all having a blast, and she's having a lot of fun. She's drawing and writing about her character -- and not losing &quot;touch with reality&quot; either. And the good thing is, it is not interfering with her School <i>(We home school...so we know it is not interfering...and we are using it in homeschooling too...we use everything in homeschooling. We are very Evil Parents that way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i>. We <b>don't</b> include &quot;Adult Themes&quot; with out kids...we <b>don't</b> let them watch Adult Themed shows, or Violent Shows with them, heck, we even pause Adult type commercials when they are around <i>(&quot;Erectile Dysfunction&quot; &amp; &quot;Condom Commercials&quot;)</i> -- we don't keep them in the dark...just they are 9 &amp; 6, and should be kids for a while longer. <i>(My son covers his eyes when two people kiss...but he's six...so don't let him fool you, he's actually a flirt...)</i><br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you for your concern Ryumaru. It is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the project your talking about...I would be very interested in it. I'm always interested in new RPGs...and if it's My Little Pony...my Daughter would be very interested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Peace...<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T15:02:50-08:00","id":73900,"title":"","content":"Well, glad to be of help! The RPG I mentioned is<a href=\"http://akuoreo.deviantart.com/art/Pony-RPG-First-Draft-289542812\" target=\"_blank\"> here.</a> Very easy to understand and simple to run, at least on my first parsing of it. It is partly a point-build system, though, so it might be a little wonky to run for a 9-year-old. On the other hand, it might be good for practicing math skills!<br /> <br /> If your daughter really does like Exalted and MLP, she might also be interested in the Shard I'm writing, though I should mention that I'm writing it with, basically, the membership of this forum as the target audience. I'm not quite finished, mostly because I'm still working on the Infernal Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T15:44:43-08:00","id":73921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73900#post73900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, glad to be of help! The RPG I mentioned is<a href=\"http://akuoreo.deviantart.com/art/Pony-RPG-First-Draft-289542812\" target=\"_blank\"> here.</a> Very easy to understand and simple to run, at least on my first parsing of it. It is partly a point-build system, though, so it might be a little wonky to run for a 9-year-old. On the other hand, it might be good for practicing math skills!<br /> <br /> If your daughter really does like Exalted and MLP, she might also be interested in the Shard I'm writing, though I should mention that I'm writing it with, basically, the membership of this forum as the target audience. I'm not quite finished, mostly because I'm still working on the Infernal Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall give Ponies: The RPG a look. Right now though my Daughter is on a quest to bring peace to all Creation! A suitable quest for an Eclipse...and fully self imposed on her part (There are plenty of Side Quests...). She's already made an enemy <i>(A Death Knight that hurt a &quot;Poor Bunny,&quot; whom she promptly made broke down in tears -- god she can roll dice -- and then thru charms &amp; her ability has him &quot;helping all Bunnies in the world...&quot; Good for an evening of laughs.)</i> So now the Death Knight, Shadows of the Night Fields, is after her in the company of a hoard of Rabbits...as &quot;followers.&quot; Yes...tongue in cheek...and a little &quot;Zena &amp; Hercules:...but fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T03:03:55-08:00","id":75501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73276#post73276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have yet to see the episode, but I assume the title is a pun on 80s/90s R&amp;B group Milli Vanilli</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand and clarify on this, Milli Vanilli was a group that had a brief stint of popularity which quickly collapsed after a very public demonstration of lip synching, and subsequent revelation that they were not even the ones who had recorded the album vocals.<br /> <br /> On that note, ponies appear to be surprisingly cool with lip synching.<br /> <br /> I just love Rarity and Big Mac in their cute little acapella jumpers as well (and the whole idea of Mac being the baritone vocalist for an acapella group), and Fluttershy getting increasingly into her performing is probably the most adorable she's ever been.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a strange thread of continuity in these last few episodes, in the form of Pinkie Pie expressing significant interest in taking part in some public event and then being basically cool when it goes to somebody else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T13:09:10-08:00","id":75832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=75501#post75501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To expand and clarify on this, Milli Vanilli was a group that had a brief stint of popularity which quickly collapsed after a very public demonstration of lip synching, and subsequent revelation that they were not even the ones who had recorded the album vocals.<br /> <br /> On that note, ponies appear to be surprisingly cool with lip synching.<br /> <br /> I just love Rarity and Big Mac in their cute little acapella jumpers as well (and the whole idea of Mac being the baritone vocalist for an acapella group), and Fluttershy getting increasingly into her performing is probably the most adorable she's ever been.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a strange thread of continuity in these last few episodes, in the form of Pinkie Pie expressing significant interest in taking part in some public event and then being basically cool when it goes to somebody else.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair she did win the turkey competition which was a public event...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:37:15-08:00","id":76692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=75832#post75832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair she did win the turkey competition which was a public event...</div> </div> </div> </div>That one was funny.<br /> <br /> We have a My Little Pony Episode every day at lunch (I think we have 40+ recorded...and are recording the new ones). My kids insistence (I don't resist......it's for the kids afterall <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:21:09-08:00","id":77262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=73868#post73868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm... I think I'm going to have to disagree with you on that. Pinkie... did not come across as well-meaning at all. She reduced Fluttershy to <i>tears</i>. <i>Twice</i>. Clearly her friend was very upset by what she was saying, and it seems rather out-of-character, to me at least, that Pinkie wouldn't get that. She's not a dumb &quot;lol I'm so random&quot; character. She, y'know, cares about her friends, and not once did she apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give you that. I guess I saw her as the YoutTube comments, kind of. She represented the unreflected attention famous people may be subject to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:56:55-08:00","id":77282,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E15 - Twilight Time</b><br /> <br /> I see Twilight is starting to make a name for herself. I mean, she's only the 1000-year queen's chosen prot\u00e9g\u00e9, the literally ascended newest princess and saviour of the world like three times already (I don't count Chrysalis, because Canterlot isn't really the world), so I suppose a bunch of school kids thinking she's cool is a reasonable celebrity level, right? In all honestly, it's nice to see it at least slightly recognized.<br /> <br /> What's even nicer, though, is seeing Twilight working. Yeah, I know, it's like she's a librarian or something. Huh, now when I think about it, has that ever been established in the show that it's a public library, or is that just something I picked up from the fanbase? Nevertheless, the role as teacher fits her amazingly well (I see she's taking cues from her own teacher), and I feel it does good for her character.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I guess the CMC was in it too. As always, I find them rather flat. There was something to be said about showing the procedure of how social status develops, though. And how benefits beget obligation, and you either got to be able to deliver or be cynical enough to ignore it. Useful subject, actually.<br /> <br /> Somehow I'm not surprised it's Sweetie Belle spearheading the episode, she must have taken some influence from Rarity. And, can I say, Pip's British accent? Is awesome.<br /> <br /> I'll not call is super, but it's solid. It was logical and I liked Twilight's character. Overall, highly acceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T04:55:10-08:00","id":77591,"title":"","content":"First episode of the season that I didn't want to watch all the way through. Didn't leave the episode with a silly grin on my face (which is the only criteria I use for deciding if it's a good episode) so...meh. First miss of the season for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:41:16-08:00","id":79468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=77282#post77282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweetie Belle spearheading</div> </div> </div> </div>Ba-dum Tish!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:33:38-08:00","id":79700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=77591#post77591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First episode of the season that I didn't want to watch all the way through. Didn't leave the episode with a silly grin on my face (which is the only criteria I use for deciding if it's a good episode) so...meh. First miss of the season for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally see that. The overall feeling was just all there this time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=79468#post79468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ba-dum Tish!</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems I'm funnier than I think. :P Sorry, you'll have to explain that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T18:07:59-08:00","id":79795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=79700#post79700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally see that. The overall feeling was just all there this time.<br /> <br /> It seems I'm funnier than I think. :P Sorry, you'll have to explain that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spearheading. Sweetie Belle is a unicorn. See it now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T06:56:31-08:00","id":82085,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's talk about Fighting is Magic.<br /> <br /> Short recap in case someone doesn't know. Fighting is Magic was a fan-made 2d fighting game developed by underground developers Mane6, containing, well, the mane six beating the snot out of each other. The project was inspired by a couple of joke photoshop pictures, then went on to become a concept and eventually there emerged a full-fledged fighting game made in FighterMaker. It was a pretty big deal in the fandom a year and a half ago, having received endorsement from people like Lauren Faust and others working on the show. Unfortunately, it wasn't endorsed by Hasbro, who sent a C&amp;D letter to Mane6 just a couple months before the projected release date. Cue outrage, upheaval and, most importantly, one dead game. After regrouping and acquiring the help of Faust herself, Mane6 decided to reforge their game in a non-pony form. They are currently working on that, and posted earlier this year they'll have a Kickstarter soon.<br /> <br /> Why am I bringing this up now? Well, currently on EqD, there's a news post containing a &quot;tribute version&quot; of the original, pony-based Fighting is Magic. It's made by an unknown group who's kept it on the low-down until completion (and EqD is currently getting some flak for blowing that cover, though I wonder how they had imagined distribution to work otherwise), and is based on leaked files from a Fighting is Magic alpha test, containing new work to fill in the content holes. This is likely the closest we're going to get to a pony fighting game.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, don't get me wrong: I raged along with the best of them over the C&amp;D. I swear, I was honestly emotionally upset about it and it took me months to actually get over. In my opinion, it's the worst controversy in brony history, nevermind alicorn Twilight or Equestria Girls. But on the other hand, is this really smart? I have two argument for why it might have been better to just let it die.<br /> <br /> 1) It might annoy Hasbro again. I'm not a lawyer, but I'm afraid they might come to Mane6, tell them they're not doing enough to keep their project dead and sue their asses. And it seems they too are worried about that, given <a href=\"http://www.mane6.com/2014/02/friendly-reminder/\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a> from yesterday. From where I stand, I don't even see Hasbro having to be 100% correct in their charges, since Mane6 just won't have the means to dispute it. It seems to put unnecessary spotlight on Mane6 for a marginal profit.<br /> <br /> 2) Let's not forget that Mane6 is actually developing a game for us. Much as they hated the C&amp;D, they've said that it will be better in every way (and odds are it will, as they've upgraded from FighterMaker to the Z Engine used for Skullgirls), except the simple fact that it won't contain ponies. I feel like it's unhelpful to remind Mane6 that many of the fans will take a technically worse game as long as it contain ponies. It seems like it's a dick move.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, though, I never thought I'd get to hear the RC88's background music on top of an actual fight. I can't say I'm not happy about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-01-2014, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:50:15-08:00","id":82245,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E16 - It Ain't Easy Being Breezy</b><br /> <br /> This episode was written by Natasha Levinger, the new writer who also gave us Pinkie Apple Pie earlier this season. That episode had the highest joke and reference saturation out of any episode yet, and was also one of my favourites this season. Can this one stand up to it?<br /> <br /> Yes. Yes, it can. But it also has problems.<br /> <br /> First, the good things. God DAMN those things are cute! And, more importantly, they add to the scope of the pony world. World building helps the show feel fresh, at least when it's credibly done, and by the standards of this show, it certainly qualifies for well-written. Also, the episode has an element of Equestria-specific culture and biology, which I adore. Things like Hearts and Hooves Day and Hearth's Warming is derived from our real world customs, but the Winter Wrap Up and Running of the Leaves spring from the fact that the ponies have to manipulate the nature around them on their own. This little fact seems to have slipped by the wayside, and I'm sort of thinking that's due to Faust leaving the show, but I'm always happy when we get some sort of quirky natural phenomenon at least. Admittedly, it's a bit strange that the Breezies would have plants which they have to <i>go to another world</i> to get pollen for, that really makes no ecological sense <i>but fuck it, it's magic!</i><br /> <br /> What are the problems? Well... I never felt the conflict was credible. Right, Fluttershy is a nice host. That's really not enough to make anyone willing to risk a whole year stranded in another world. Sure, take a break, catch your breath, but they should be more eager to go on home. This in turn gives the &quot;rainbow lesson&quot; with Sea Breeze the same kind of problem; okay, he was strong-worded, but for the rest of them to just obstinately refuse? I don't buy it. And speaking of the rainbow lesson, we once more see that Fluttershy is the same one-trick pony as always. No other pony is as type-cast as her. It's always overcoming shyness, one way or the other. Admittedly, this time it's comparatively well done, but still. All the other ponies have at least a couple of typical perspectives. For Fluttershy, it's really only the one.<br /> <br /> All in all, the episode is good. I wager the fanbase will be split on the issue, but I quite like the style that Levinger is showing in her two episodes so far. I can tell a marked difference between her and others' work. Her language and dialogue is snappier and less forced than in some episodes. She dares to go new places, bring up new ideas. I'm a fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T16:02:27-08:00","id":82380,"title":"","content":"So, update on the whole Fighting is Magic thing.<br /> <br /> Having played it a little, and having read other reacting to it, I can conclusively say the story mode AI is OP. I haven't managed to get past the first level yet, and I'm not saying I'm good at fighting games, but it's the <i>first level</i>. I suppose the people who made it are into fighting games, and so they set the difficulty to what they thought was reasonable, which is just bullshit for the average brony. I've seen it described as <i>Fighting is Magic: Don't Touch Me You Filthy Casual!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T06:45:46-08:00","id":82605,"title":"","content":"I like the whole 'ponies run nature' thing too. But these Breezies seem....utterly hopeless on their own and completely dependent on the good will of others. Which is fine; but I'm the kind of person who can't see much point in the huge efforts people go to save the panda when they're evolved to give themselves almost no fighting chance on their own.<br /> <br /> Sea Breeze didn't seem like he was in the wrong either despite having to apologise to all the other Breezies at the end for 'being mean'. When as far as I could see he wanted to get home back to his family etc., the opportunity to do that was extremely narrow and everyone else was outright unwilling to even try. Getting desperate and rude to people who are essentially preventing you from escaping a highly lethal prison dimension...yeah. Not seeing how he's in the wrong.<br /> <br /> Only thing I got from that was pretend to be nice to make people do things for you. Emotional manipulation FTW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T17:28:38-08:00","id":82853,"title":"","content":"I definitely enjoyed the brief joke where Time Turner (Pony Tennant) was seen wearing 3D glasses.<br /> <br /> I think the moral of this episode got a little muddled, but I think the intended message was &quot;sometimes you have to be harsh to be kind.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T18:30:32-08:00","id":82876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=82853#post82853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely enjoyed the brief joke where Time Turner (Pony Tennant) was seen wearing 3D glasses.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was also accompanied by Roseluck","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T19:54:58-08:00","id":82920,"title":"","content":"Who is still a better companion than Rose fucking Tyler.<br /> <br /> And she doesn't even <i>say anything</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:18:09-08:00","id":83677,"title":"","content":"This will likely be an unpopular opinion, but...fuck this episode, for real.<br /> <br /> I've talked about this before in other venues - the idea of &quot;tough love&quot; is something which never fails to set me off. It's the justification every bitter cynical asshole on the planet uses to justify his/her assholery - the idea that kindness is weak, and harshness is strong, and <i>true</i> kindness comes not from treating people how they'd like to be treated, but pushing them into doing what <i>you</i> feel is best. It's one of the most toxic mindsets I commonly see in people.<br /> <br /> And what did they do? They made an episode of a children's show dedicated to reinforcing those poisonous ideas. IMO, this episode should be filed alongside &quot;Feeling Pinkie Keen&quot; as one of the only MLP episodes to contain an actively harmful lesson.<br /> <br /> And TBH, it just kinda reeks of pandering to me. It's the sort of lesson that plays well to the demographics most prevalent among bronies, not little girls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 03-03-2014, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:22:37-08:00","id":83719,"title":"","content":"It was a boring episode and not that great, but I'm here cause of Cielle, not the episode(PS, yes, I'm still a pony fan).<br /> <br /> The episode garbles it's message, but it's not exactly tough love as you describe it. There are situations where you need to motivate people to do what's good for them-provided you actually understand the entire scenario. A small example is that inevitably every parent is going to have to say no to something in regards to their kids. It's not that harshness wins out-the episode points that out with Sea(Seed?) Breeze. It's that kindness is NOT a weakness, that it DOES NOT make you a pleaser and a push-over. It's ultimately about firmness in action when acting out of understanding and concern. You'll notice that in the episode, what really set Fluttershy into motion was the realization that the Breezies couldn't live in Equestria without being completely dependent on someone like her-and I'm of the opinion that a life of dependency is a not much of a life at all, feel free to disagree. She showed kindness by doing what she could to motivate them through a rough transition rather than just letting them avoid it-and if there's any redeeming of the toy bait, it's that she did so by making the journey with them at the risk of losing her own home, which is a good show of <i>firm</i> love.<br /> <br /> I understand why the episode rubs you the wrong way, but I think more of it comes from the convoluted way they did it rather than the actual message. I dunno, feel free to disagree with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:45:43-08:00","id":86818,"title":"","content":"<i>Somepony to Watch Over Me</i>:<br /> In which we are reminded of two important facts: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Equestria is a deathworld.</li> <li>The ponies are used to this.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:55:59-08:00","id":86827,"title":"","content":"Somepony to Watch Over Me. In which they continue to show that they understand that Applejack is perhaps the most adult one in the group, and proceed to do all the wrong things with that fact.<br /> <br /> My sympathies to everyone who has this episode matter to them, because your home life sucks, and my sympathies to the other 90% of you, because this episode offers you nothing but damn annoying caricature of not only real life scenarios, but also one of the best characters on the show. This episode is just about worthless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:35:30-08:00","id":86976,"title":"","content":"How so? For quite a while now, I've been of the opinion that AJ's special talent is along the lines of &quot;being there for her family (and friends)&quot;, and as we've seen in previous episodes as well, when she feels she's in danger of failing that, her talent seems to go into overdrive, and she overdoes whatever it was she was trying to do to help out.<br /> <br /> I won't disagree that the way the moral is achieved could set a rather dangerous example, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T15:32:26-08:00","id":87042,"title":"","content":"And we're back on form.<br /> <br /> As I explained before, silly grin on my face is all that is required for an episode to be good in my books and this delivered.<br /> <br /> From my point of view I was the older sibling so certainly don't get ABloom's side of it and I never really looked after my younger brother so...no comment really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:20:01-08:00","id":87069,"title":"","content":"Henry Wong from Digimon Tamers. I'll get back to this in a second, but start googling or remembering.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: as I said, DHX knows that Applejack is one of the two most grown up characters in their roster, quite possibly the most adult period. This is a good thing to know, it's critical to handling a character like Applejack. The concerns she deals with aren't necessarily the sort of things other should deal with respectively, and in fact much of it comes back around the issues of control, wisdom, and motivation-Applejack knows what to do, but not necessarily for the right reasons, in the right way, or in the right amount. THe fact that DHX gets this is, again, good.<br /> <br /> What is not good is how much of a caricature they make her since Apple Family Reunion. Which, admittedly, isn't that long of a time, but it drives me nuts.<br /> <br /> Simply put, Applejack doesn't feel like a person in these episodes, nor an archetype-she feels like a stereotype, and one of such extremity that if you actively <i>can </i>relate to putting up with er her overbearance, god fucking god almighty do you need to get out of that house-I have met people like that, and they are not good for you and most importantly will not change without a major provocation. The simple fact is that while Applejack <i>is</i> overprotective of her sister, it's never been as bad as it was here today, after <i>god knows what else she lets her sister get up to</i>. THe Everfree forest? Sure. Some of the things going on in Ponyville? Sure. But NOT THE FUCKING FARM AND HOUSE. YOU LET APPLEBLOOM RUN AROUND DANGEROUS TOOLS ALL THE TIME THERE BECAUSE SHE FUCKING UNDERSTANDS THEM AND YOU KNOW SHE KNOWS THAT.<br /> <br /> It's not like it's out of left field, but <i>it is way too fucking much compared to what we've seen</i>.<br /> <br /> So, Henry Wong. Remember him? Good. Because these characters are just about identical in so many ways,it's not even funny. Henry is a pacifist after having hurt some kids in an effort to be the model of a strong older brother, and when he gets Terriermon from a near death battle after that point in his life, we have a scenario much like this one-Henry is Applejack, overly concerned for the safety of what he regards his younger brother, and Terriermon as Applebloom, an individual more capable of himself than the 'older' one believes, but maybe not as much as they think.<br /> <br /> There are differences in the shows style, namely the time they took on this issue, but there's a classic example of how this episode could have gone. Namely, without the overbearing one being portrayed as a god-damned idiot, but as an intelligent person who has their reasons to worry.<br /> <br /> MLP Can do that. MLP <i>has</i> done that. So why they fail to here just-ergh, it drives me nuts. Applejack's episodes always kind of get the short stick in the end, and alongside some other episodes since Season 3, I really don't think they care anymore to try. Yes, this was an Applejack issue, but that wasn't Applejack having the issue. That was farce in her stead having the issue.<br /> <br /> Applejack deserves the same respect as Henry Wong, and god don't I sound pretentious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:10:20-07:00","id":87588,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E17 - Somepony to Watch Over Me</b><br /> <br /> <b>Applebloom:</b> Hey! Who put a pillow on the rake?!<br /> <br /> This episode turned out to be my first straight-up miss in season 4.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, they do pretty well with what they get, and some of the jokes did make me chuckle. Also, the adventure part at the end was actually kind of enjoyable this time around. The monster was a cute little twist on the concept of overbearing relatives, too. It tied in neatly.<br /> <br /> However, as Arcane put it, Applejack got replaced by some kind of stereotype cardboard cut-out who exhibits traits she has never shown before in the environment she should be most at home in. I'm not sure I agree she's been so mono-focused since the Reunion, but it's certainly showing here. Moreover, even with the gags, the whole script this time seems to consist of the same thing being said over and over and over again for a good third of the time. And in the end, the fact that she had to go through a fire swamp and fight three-headed chimerae to be trusted around her own farm was just a small bit overkill.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no. I'm not buying it. Next, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T14:33:35-07:00","id":92473,"title":"","content":"Throwing it out there.<br /> <br /> I like Maud. She's a lot like me - introverted, quiet and literal.<br /> <br /> Same reason I like Pinkie actually. She's the exact opposite of me, a bit of aspirational personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T15:33:48-07:00","id":92496,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on &quot;Somepony to Watch Over Me&quot; can be summarized by one sentence: &quot;Curse of the Mother Hen: The Episode.&quot; All negative implications therein.<br /> <br /> ... okay, okay, I do want to go into more detail. This episode is not my favorite. It bothers me that Applejack - &quot;the loyalest and <b>most dependable</b> of ponies&quot; - goes flipping psychotic over this. As someone else already pointed out, she's the most mature of the main cast, and it feels bloody out of character for her to be acting the way she does in this episode. I feel like it maybe would have been more appropriate for Rarity and Sweetie Belle to have been the focus.<br /> <br /> Oh well. At least there was a nice reference to The Princess Bride.<br /> <br /> Now, as for &quot;Maud Pie.&quot; My initial impression of Maud is that she reminds me a bit of Raven from Teen Titans. Although, I admit, the &quot;sedimental&quot; pun was pretty good. And the &quot;igneous&quot; one.<br /> <br /> I do like how they acknowledge that Pinkie was maybe trying a bit too hard on this episode, And how it seems to have a message about how people need to take their time when it comes to bonding with others, and take things at their own pace. Also that not everyone shows their enthusiasm the same way others do.<br /> <br /> The highlight of the episode was a tie between Dash's constant confusion and Maud being a frigging superhero when dealing with rocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:41:36-07:00","id":93574,"title":"","content":"I get the most distinct impression of Maud Pie being high-functioning autistic.<br /> <br /> She is now my favourite character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T00:03:51-07:00","id":96758,"title":"","content":"Luna!<br /> <br /> I think Sweetie Belle may have been in the episode as well. Not sure about that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T18:22:47-07:00","id":97159,"title":"","content":"Sweetie Belle!<br /> <br /> I think Luna may have been in the episode as well, but who cares.<br /> <br /> Okay enough mixed sarcasm/seriousness, review time!<br /> <br /> I really liked this episode.<br /> <br /> And that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:22:40-07:00","id":97396,"title":"","content":"This is a thing a lot of people with siblings ave told me about, stories written about it etc. The whole one sibling shines brightly while the other is overshadowed thing.<br /> <br /> I...don't get it. I had an older brother. We were really different people.<br /> <br /> I was all SCIENCE! HISTORY! FANTASY! while he was SPORT! HANGING OUT! BEER! so we...never really competed for the same kinds of attention.<br /> <br /> It was fun and cute as an episode, but the emtional bit and moral lesson and so forth is all academic from my point of view. Someone else telling me about how they feel rather than it resonating with anything I've experienced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:31:38-07:00","id":97400,"title":"","content":"&quot;Princess Luna, how do you know all this stuff about my sister?&quot;<br /> &quot;Voice actor ESP.&quot;<br /> &quot;Huh?&quot;<br /> &quot;Nothing. Now quickly, help me save your sister by fixing up this jam.&quot;<br /> &quot;Aren't we supposed to be repairing the headdress?&quot;<br /> &quot;That's what I said, now move it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked this episode; I enjoy the dynamic between Rarity and Sweetie Belle, I like this track they've been on lately with Sweetie Belle wanting a bit more general attention, and the format in the latter half was pleasantly bizarre, possibly even a bit experimental. At the very least, I like how it gave more development to the whole &quot;Luna as guardian of dreams&quot; thing than before, and it was nicely paced in doing so; this was a good, evenly structured episode. That and the idea of Luna sympathizing with somebody who feels overshadowed by their sister.<br /> <br /> I also got a kick out of Sapphire Shores' little &quot;[dolphins] swim with me in my dreams&quot; line, it ties the concept nicely together with the resolution. Also, seeing Shores in general return was enjoyable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:12:07-07:00","id":97652,"title":"","content":"There was this portion of my life where I would try and make friends with someone, and then my brother would come and introduce himself and before long they were <i>his</i> friends, not mine. This was triply frustrating because he often didn't even like them all that much and didn't have a need for them,where I felt like I could barely connect to people and had to work hard to get any form of social interaction.<br /> <br /> This episode resonates with me, you might imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T13:45:20-07:00","id":98625,"title":"","content":"Hmm...hopefully Maud won't ever know in detail about the past adventures of the main characters, or Rarity could find herself in trouble...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LNbwTnomKyM\" data-code=\"LNbwTnomKyM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LNbwTnomKyM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> On the other hand they might share a liking for gemstones and other shiny rocks, so they could reconcile XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T13:45:22-07:00","id":100857,"title":"","content":"So, anyone especially interested in talking about the most recent episode?<br /> <br /> What really struck me about Sweetie Belle's actions is that it's not often we see the ponies outright act maliciously toward each other. Sure, they don't always get along: the CMCs sometimes get carried away and don't realize how their actions affect others, for example, and I recall Rarity and Applejack butting heads sometimes because of their different sensibilities. But the only times I can remember a pony just doing something outright cruel are (a) Fluttershy's periods of berserker rage under Discord and Iron Will, or (b) Silver Spoon &amp; Diamond Tiara, who are meant to be terrible people anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:06:24-07:00","id":102123,"title":"","content":"Oh shit, it's been three weeks since I last watched pony? I tell you, the end of this semester may turn out to be the end of me. I actually still don't really have time to watch MLP, but hell, let's watch MLP.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E18 - Maud Pie</b><br /> <br /> This one was okay. Maud was pretty cool a character, but after a while the episode started repeating, just like the previous one. I also thought the moral could have stopped when she left Ponyville. The message that not every friend will like your other friends, and that neither of them will be less of your friend for that, seemed pretty important to me. I'm not sure the idea of bonding over their simultaneous friendship is necessarily a healthy thing to do. Better than Somepony to Watch Over Me, but not by all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:41:38-07:00","id":102133,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E19 - For Whom the Sweetie Belle Toils</b><br /> <br /> And we are back to form! I quite liked this episode. For one, I can totally relate to Sweetie Belle, as I've felt that kind of rage as well; that unreasonable, illogical (and mostly in my case, though not in Sweetie Belle's, undirected) anger when some detail just doesn't work out like you plan. I've been there, and it's aggravating.<br /> <br /> Also, LUNA! The influence from A Christmas Carol was excellent. I always like when she shows up, but it's best kept rare. We've seen her twice as some sort of helping dream spirit, walking the line between the real and the ethereal, and while I lament that she's not made more of a character, I also don't think she'd be good as a main focus of an episode. That's also, I recon, why Celestia is kept mostly off camera; retaining the mystery and grandeur befitting millennia-old entities requires not, y'know, showing to much of them. But I do think the Royal Canterlot Voice could stand making a return.<br /> <br /> Yeah, really good. Absolutely a fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T16:37:26-07:00","id":102241,"title":"","content":"You have done well to reclaim my affections for Applejack, show.<br /> <br /> Also, excellent use of your Granny Smith and Flim Flam Brothers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:23:26-07:00","id":102310,"title":"","content":"Probably Applejack's second best episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:16:03-07:00","id":106780,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, not sure I like the real world implications of this newest episode.<br /> <br /> 'Everyone is different and learns differently!'<br /> <br /> Yes. And?<br /> <br /> When you can get a school to have tailored teaching methods for each student it might mean something. But I've never been in a class where they'll teach a lesson with interpretive dance and then again with actors and then again with...<br /> <br /> And, you know what? I worked hard at school. It offends my sensibilities that apparently it's so easy to learn stuff you can just do it flying around aimlessly talking to someone.<br /> <br /> 'You know how you worked hard to achieve something? Yeah, screw that, it's piss easy for them over there, they learned the stuff you worked hard for while doing other stuff they're also awesome at!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T10:07:15-07:00","id":106955,"title":"","content":"Being a former education major, I took this episode differently.<br /> <br /> Namely, I read it as as big, magnificent declaration of &quot;FUCK YOU, AMERICAN EDUCATION SYSTEM!&quot;. Which I always approve of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:49:27-07:00","id":107119,"title":"","content":"Leap of Faith thoughts:<ul><li>Nice to see a little visual pun involving Dr. Whooves.</li> <li>Ah, the Flim Flams have graduated to being actual Snake Oil salesponies.</li> <li>I REALLY wish Big Macintosh would actually have lines....</li> <li>*snrk* Granny Smith tested, Applejack approved.</li> </ul><br /> Testing, Testing, 1 2 3 thoughts:<ul><li>Twilight uses her new wings. For once.</li> <li>Acknowledgement of singing about freaking out. Heh.</li> <li>Twilight's &quot;not amused&quot; face is wonderful.</li> <li>You'd think Twilight's enthusiasm for learning would have led her to be a better lecturer.</li> <li>Oh hai Owlowicious.</li> <li>&quot;General Firefly.&quot; I see what they did there.</li> <li>... okay, really? You'd think Twilight being so passionate about education would mean she would know more about actually educating.</li> <li>Angel as Celestia and Opal as Luna is gold.</li> <li>SO MUCH 90'S IN THIS SONG</li> <li>IT IS PAINFUL</li> <li>I agree with Dash: &quot;IT'S TOO MUCH FOR MY EYES!&quot;</li> <li>Rarity also has a wonderful &quot;not amused&quot; face.</li> <li>Hm. Pinkie's rapping has, in a roundabout way, given me a Charm idea...*</li> <li>On that note, Dash has been pouring XP into Awareness Charms. Caste Abilities, yo.</li> <li>Nice voice actor joke having Rarity be Luna.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So, on top of this one being a big fat &quot;Fuck You&quot; to the American education system, it does encourage the viewers to acknowledge that they might learn differently than the next person. That's a good thing. I wish that they hadn't shown Rainbow Dash getting a 100% on the test - even if you study hard and learn well, you might miss a question or two due to other factors. I mean, there wouldn't be much difference between her having 100% and having, say, 93%. Both are still passing grades. Even an 86% would have been good.<br /> <br /> *Rough draft:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Perfected (Ability) Focus</b><br /> <b>Mins:</b> (Ability) 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Cost:</b> --<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Relevant Infinite (Ability) Mastery<br /> This Charm allows the Solar Exalt to take any number of Specialties in the chosen Ability. However, she may still only benefit from three dice on any one roll, and the XP cost of gaining Specialties in any other Ability is increased to 6 XP. Additionally, the training time is increased by an extra week.<br /> <br /> The idea came from how Pinkie seems to do <i>everything</i> (or almost everything) via Performance. Therefore, she must have some way of having multiple multiples of Specialties in the Ability. The only problem with this theory is that she matches Sidereals more so than Solars....</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":1048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","user":"Ryumaru","date":". 04-06-2014, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T16:16:38-07:00","id":107129,"title":"","content":"On Twilight as educator,well, two things. 1)She's enthusiastic about learning, not really about teaching. Twilight Time worked because the activities were things to do, but when it comes to a thing like history her time as a student takes the lead. 2) There's an irony in that from a certain point of view, Twilight's the antagonist of the episode-she's the one pushing this and perpetually making an issue of it(one wonders if Rainbow would have just done what worked for her without prompting, doubtful, but still)). But more to the point, the reason she's an ineffective teacher is because <i>she's the primary teaching method of the education system</i>. She is 'Merica here, albeit she learns her lesson. THe others are some of the other failed systems we've tried over the years(in the sense that we're doing things differently but still insist the student learn <i>this</i> way), but Twilight is the educational hegemony killing students across the nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T07:17:18-07:00","id":107428,"title":"","content":"This may well be my new favourite. It's got the usual fun dynamic between Twilight and Rainbow Dash (also developing Twilight's talent for education, as well as further referencing her difficulty with flight), that good old fashioned &quot;all the ponies bickering&quot; thing, some nice but unobtrusive world building (of the sort I like that references the idea of styles and systems changing over time), and a whole plethora of absolutely hilarious visuals (particular standouts being the animals acting out the history of Equestria, and all those ponies waving flashcards at the end). Good props to the team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:45:56-07:00","id":108226,"title":"","content":"Pony? Pony.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E20 - </b><b>Leap of Faith</b><br /> <br /> Oh shit son, this one rocked! Applejack episodes have been up-and-down recently, but I absolutely loved the sheer amount of stuff they put into this one. In talking about the placebo effect (but not using that word, of course), it touches on issues of scientific morality and the price of honesty. And what makes that so effective is that we get to see Applejack, the Element of Truth, deal with that dilemma while it affects those she cares about the most. The production really brought home how she felt at times.<br /> <br /> And I'm so glad to see Flim and Flam again, this time as actual snake oil salesmen. They also played quite well the subversive part, seeming to have a point at the start but then showing what the conclusion of that line of reasoning becomes. Awesome to see them come back!<br /> <br /> One thing though, that made me kind of flinch. I realise that it's a cartoon and screw physics, but seriously, catching Granny Smith in a lasso like that? I had to pause for a minute. NO give in that rope would have made her not lose her hind legs.<br /> <br /> But yeah, super strong episode. I can't believe I keep saying this. Season 4 is shaping up to be the best one yet.<br /> <br /> And from the posts here, I think the next epsiode will be interesting as well, given that I'm currently studying to become a teacher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T20:57:07-07:00","id":114521,"title":"","content":"Old news, I'm sure, but looks like there's a sequel to the Equestria Girls movie coming soon (that was fast!). Interesting promos they've been offering:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qh7j1qUaGOc\" data-code=\"qh7j1qUaGOc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qh7j1qUaGOc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fg46129oPIs&amp;src_vid=BniijKHywXM&amp;feature=iv &amp;annotation_id=annotation_398090\" data-code=\"Fg46129oPIs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Fg46129oPIs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BniijKHywXM\" data-code=\"BniijKHywXM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BniijKHywXM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Immediate observations: I note that there's no sign of Twilight, which could be good or bad. Does the movie start in the human world, then Twilight shows up midway through? Do the characters find the human Twilight hinted at in the first movie? Or is she just not in this one at all? Either way, it seems there may be even less Pony in this one than there was in the first...<br /> <br /> Also, I haven't seen Sunset Shimmer, which would be a bit harder to explain. Did she go back to Equestria? I hope they don't just lazily write her off as having &quot;moved away&quot;, as that would cheat us of her character dev, and...she really has no where to move *to*. I'd rather see her return to Equestria and show up in the next season...<br /> <br /> It seems that Trixie is gonna be the main antagonist this time around! More Trixie is always welcome, even if it's humanized. If there is a Pony connection in the plot, maybe we'll even get to see original Trix in Equestria!<br /> <br /> Aside from that, this movie reminds me, yet again, of how most cartoons are made by guys much older than their target audience. Ever notice how, whenever cartoons have popular music characters, it's always &quot;rock stars&quot;, who are almost always done up as Kiss parodies? Do kids today actually listen to &quot;rock music&quot;? Can any of the groups kids listen to today even be correctly classified as &quot;rock&quot;? What was the last kid's cartoon you saw that had a musician character perform something that actually seemed like something kids would really listen to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:20:54-07:00","id":116148,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, newest episode, our first sight of an unambiguously physically disabled pony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T14:01:32-07:00","id":116676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=116148#post116148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, newest episode, our first sight of an unambiguously physically disabled pony?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the result of collaboration between the Make A Wish Foundation and Hasbro! That guy was voiced by a patient with <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spinal Muscular Atrophy type III. I found that nifty.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:25:35-07:00","id":117127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=116676#post116676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the result of collaboration between the Make A Wish Foundation and Hasbro! That guy was voiced by a patient with <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spinal Muscular Atrophy type III. I found that nifty.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That explains why he looked so much like somebody's OC. That's really cool of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T06:34:22-07:00","id":119695,"title":"","content":"This may sound weird, but I honestly didn't realize that he WAS handicapped, until I read some comments about it and rewatched! I don't recall what I DID think, but I think I thought that he was pulling something (like, it was a fancy cart); maybe it was because we'd seen wheelchairs before, and they didn't look anything like that! This design works much better for the equine form, tho. And yeah, his design was pretty over-the-top &quot;cool&quot;, so maybe that was distracting me, too. Also nice that they let him be a bit of a jerk!<br /> <br /> Given he's a pegasus, I imagine he flies most of the time, but needs the support when he must spend time on the ground, such as at a stall or in line. It'd probably make sense for it to be made of extremely lightweight materials and be easily collapsible so that he can take off quickly if need be...<br /> <br /> Overall, I thought that was a good ensemble ep, tho the Rarity-Applejack plot was a little weak, but at least they didn't forget about Rarity representing &quot;generosity&quot;. Rainbow trades Fluttershy away...so, slavery/indentured servitude is legal in Equestria?! Someone could trade their child away, so long as both traders agree it's fair?? Also, I don't always look for that sort of thing, but the shipping is strong with this one; certain fans must have had a field day!<br /> <br /> One thing I really appreciated; I consider it a mark of lower standards in children's tv that mandates that the heroes must always &quot;win&quot;. Sadly, the otherwise great early Harry Potter movies were afflicted with this, where we must see House Griffindor win against Slytherin at some contest every film (even if Dumbledore has to blatantly cheat to make it so!). And this season of Pony was slipping into that mode, with Rainbow implausible getting such a high score on her test, and even little stuff like the Mane Six finding something to connect with Maud Pie over. Remember the end of Season one, where NO ONE got what they really wanted (well, except for Celestia, I guess)? <br /> <br /> So it's nice to see that we can still get an episode approaching that here, with the ponies at least not getting what they were after, even tho they end up with some pretty cool stuff nonetheless...<br /> <br /> Also, is it me, or did the Scary Beasts Trader resemble a ponified Kratos?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T10:38:01-07:00","id":119821,"title":"","content":"Did...Spike just find (and then EAT) the Broken-Winged Crane??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T06:47:34-07:00","id":120911,"title":"","content":"Heh, Owlicious is the best. &quot;Oh man, I don't like the look of this! This a bad scene man!&quot;<br /> <br /> Stuff messing with unicorn horns is always creepy.<br /> <br /> I like the design and personality on that puppeteer; it's fun to have a character who finally directly calls out the impractical ostentatiousness of one of Rarity's designs.<br /> <br /> So, wait, they make a big deal out of this fair, and it happens off-screen?<br /> <br /> That book is evil I tells ya! Evil! EVVIIIIIIIL!<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(&quot;Levi, you say that about all the books.&quot; I just want attention.)</span><br /> <br /> Lost robin is hilarious<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LHpdgHTINik\" data-code=\"LHpdgHTINik\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LHpdgHTINik/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That child's face falling at the sight of hors.... food that is no longer treats is a nice bit of animation.<br /> <br /> Heh, Spike is Rarity's Lunar mate; solving her problems by eating them.<br /> <br /> Was... was that a Saved by the Bell reference?<br /> <br /> .... it kind of works.<br /> <br /> I had to relisten to it a couple of times to realise that Twilight said <i>dark</i> magic instead of derp magic.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining that green mist going off to possess Derpy Hooves, who goes around turning everything into muffins (stupid internet memes).<br /> <br /> Speaking of internet, oh no, Spike turned into That Guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T15:36:12-07:00","id":124814,"title":"","content":"Good overall, but shame it ended in a single episode. I'd kind of hoped they'd find some way of merging the EqGames with the keys and crystal box thingy.<br /> <br /> Spike gains new powers because once again we see it's entirely possible to effortlessly become amazing at stuff. Sure <i>others</i> have to work hard to be good or, hell, even compete (the opening scene on the train) but some people just pull off amazing feats of stuff with no practice or anything at all. I know, I know, children's thing, message of 'everyone is special at something' yadda yadda. I'd rather see a message of 'if you work hard at something you can accomplish a lot' (not accomplish anything as that's just as disingenuous as the whole 'naturally special' angle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T10:32:40-07:00","id":127573,"title":"","content":"I liked the episode, although I'm not quite so sure it was appropriately named. I do feel that it's in keeping with how they've usually been doing this Equestria Games stuff, where it's important mostly for the dramas it generates in the characters' lives rather than just depicting the sporting events themselves. Indeed, if that had been the focus, I imagine I'd have been irritated; I recall other shows I've seen that veered off into the tension of contests with little narrative or genre relevance.<br /> <br /> But yes, episode itself: I don't have many words at the moment, but can say that I liked the depiction of Spike feeling pressured by attention, and little nods to various equines. Also how Twilight informed Spike of what she'd done to the torch basically straight away, rather than letting the plot hinge on a dumb lie.<br /> <br /> Also that touch with the thing to turn off unicorn powers; I'm kind of ashamed to admit that it I didn't see it for foreshadowing, just as a nice little element building out of Twilight's interference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=124814#post124814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spike gains new powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T14:45:17-07:00","id":127742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=127573#post127573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have we ever seen Spike be able to pull off a massive sustained burst of fire before? Enough to melt a huge frozen cloud in seconds?<br /> <br /> Perhaps difference in scale rather than kind, but I'd call fire breath to deliver letters, singeing stuff and melting vast ice clouds three different powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T07:52:47-07:00","id":128237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=127742#post127742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have we ever seen Spike be able to pull off a massive sustained burst of fire before? Enough to melt a huge frozen cloud in seconds?<br /> <br /> Perhaps difference in scale rather than kind, but I'd call fire breath to deliver letters, singeing stuff and melting vast ice clouds three different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call it the difference between a person who never lifted anything heavier than a melon and a person who's able to shit a concrete beam enough so that their child can be pulled out from under it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:04:03-07:00","id":128543,"title":"","content":"Whew. Weren't those a couple of intense weeks. Now when I have time to do anything else than study every waking minute of the day, time to catch up on some pony. I can't believe I've missed three more episodes since last time. Just some short comments on each this time.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E21 - </b><b>Testing Testing 1, 2, 3</b><br /> <br /> To summarize the epsiode, I liked it a lot. I could see what you meant by this episode giving a boot to the educational system, and I don't think it's just the American one, either; most school systems would use Twilight's methods as the base. And yeah, it's true that some people learn differently. Still, I can't help but feel that while they may have had to approach this episode this way to make it fit the show format (which it did, and it was great; 90s Pinkie in tha house, yo), I don't think the episode got to the bottom on the analogy it was making. And it certianly failed to problematize the representation of education that it gave, but hey, that's not its job either, so I'll let that slide.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E22 - Trade Ya!</b><br /> <br /> This one was a bit hit-and-miss. The kind of comedy of complications that Rainbow Dash had usually doesn't appeal to me, and it was the weakest part of the episode up until the end. I did like Applejack's and Rarity's passive-aggressive feud though, and Pinkie had some great moments. I'll have to admit, Fluttershy had some sweet moments in here as well, which surprised me: I usually think she's among the weakest of the mane six. Towards the end, it kind of escalated a bit with Rainbow Dash selling Fluttershy into slavery, but at least something happened. I liked how an otherwise lightweight episode got at least a little dramatic, if in a very silly way, and how Twilight got to follow through on her duty. It was an okay episode.<br /> <br /> <b>S4E23</b><b> - Inspiration Manifestation</b><br /> <br /> I love the sounds Rarity makes! And the portly stallion's voice acting is great as well. I'm not too keen on the premise; Rarity was never one to forgo the function of a dress for its design, or rather, she made them work together. I don't see why she's so distraught at the the critique when the puppetry wagon clearly doesn't live up to functional standards. The rest of the episode is frankly a bit too magical for me to take any lesson from very strongly. I suppose there are questions of consent and hard-lining an ideal, but for me, it mostly comes across as a much better variety of the super hero theme. Bit of a cop-out at the end, though, with the memory loss. By the way, wasn't there a comic about Rarity getting corrupted a bit ago? Seems to be a thing. :P<br /> <br /> <b>S4E24 - Equestria Games</b><br /> <br /> Okay, on the one hand, that was a HILARIOUS episode. As I said above, I don't really like the comedy of complications and people embarrassing themselves, but damn it, it was too well paced not to be freaking awesome. Most of Spike's jokes were exactly spot on, and that anthem... I cried with laughter. Top notch. On the other hand, it was really inconsistent and sometimes downright dumb. At the end, there were <b>four princesses</b> present, but heaven forbid they actually do anything? Even the competitors are faster to react than the security squad. I realise it's a dumb complaint given the obvious slapstick comedy style of the episode, but sometimes I just lose it over how damn useless the godkings are. Pretty neat lesson at the end, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T16:42:10-07:00","id":128617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=128543#post128543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end, there were <b>four princesses</b> present, but heaven forbid they actually do anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they had their magic blocked as well? I mean, I assumed that the magic block thing was something that Twilight had added in the first place to keep herself from interfering anymore.<br /> <br /> I suppose they can still fly...?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T01:52:16-07:00","id":128826,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, the fact that Twilight could interfere at the torch lighting ceremony is what made me assume princesses were exempt from the magic-blocking. Even if they don't, I'd still assume there were security unicorns who could take charge, or in fact any kind of security team that didn't require competitors like Rainbow Dash and Fluttershy to intervene.<br /> <br /> I've no illusions that I'll be able to adequately explain this to myself. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T00:54:21-07:00","id":129706,"title":"","content":"I thought they put magic security up for the competitive events and didn't bother for the opening ceremonies. To stop cheating from the crowd during the sports. No need to block magic during the ceremonies because no medals could be affected by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T08:09:13-07:00","id":129898,"title":"","content":"I'm just saying it now, completely with bias: Best. Season Finale. <i>Ever</i>.<br /> <br /> Not only was it a hell of a spectacle, but I actually really liked a lot of the ideas and character growth that happened, and the best part is that the growth I'm talking about has been building for the entire season(or at least since the Discord tries to screw with Twilight and Cadence episode), not just in this one shot. It was simple, but really well done given the time frame they had.<br /> <br /> And you know, despite the rocky start(a lot of the early episodes were bad, and I nearly stopped watching), Season 4 has had a lot of powerhouse episodes, and in the end and on the whole it's as good if not better than Season 2. Still not as good as Season 1 in my opinion, but I really started feeling the show's spirit burning again by the end.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, the finale is really damn spectacular.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Tirek is now best villain. He kind of always was, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:40:20-07:00","id":130524,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll have to watch this tomorrow. I've been noticing generally good reactions, though, so that's promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T23:58:22-07:00","id":131745,"title":"","content":"Generally impressed. Shame we didn't get more of the other Mane 6. I also felt AJ got short changed on the new outfits at the end.<br /> <br /> Thought the light show duel with the bad guy was good. I thought Discord could have had longer to do his turn: Meet bad guy, become tempted, run away. Meet bad guy again, repeat of offer, make turn.<br /> <br /> Fluttershy's key transformation was a nice bit of animation. The raising of the Sun was good and got a a bit of a laugh.<br /> <br /> Overall I liked it a lot.<br /> <br /> Except.<br /> <br /> Princess of Friendship. Guh...such a silly title...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T17:14:53-07:00","id":135892,"title":"","content":"<b>S4E25-26 - Twilight's Kingdom</b><br /> <br /> So I came into this wondering just how exaggerated the reactions to this episode was. I found they weren't. I can only concur, best season ending. Hell, even the things I could complain about aren't actually <i>bad</i>. Not only does it (as we knew) pick up the thread with the locked box and the Keys of Harmony (which I've decided they are called), but it also ties into many previously planted plotlines. Discord's redemption, for example, which I only now feel is actually worth putting some score into. The fact that Twilight is a princess without any actual authority over anything. And, perhaps most importantly, the fact that the show did not return to the <i>status quo</i> and returned the Elements of Harmony. They seem to be actually gone now? And I find myself thinking this was the best thing they could have done. Move forward, keep developing. That's what make shows stick around.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think I lied. The best thing about this episode is that it does what it proclaims to do. It shows that this show dares believing that little girls actually likes watching a female character beat the shit out of giant monsters. That makes them more progressive than the majority of the gaming industry, and I really, honestly believe it's the right call. I've not seen any demographics lately, but for all the space we bronies take up, I still think the show's biggest audience is the &quot;intended&quot; one. And <i>that</i> is what will make this show stick around.<br /> <br /> Seriously. It better be, or Hasbro will pull it. Can't mess with them.<br /> <br /> Did I have some complaints? Well, there's only one real one, and it has to do with the Twilight's combat scene with Tirek. First, let me preface: I freaking loved that combat scene! As an Exalted fan, do you know how long I've waited to see some disgustingly overpowered equine godqueens unleash their full fury? They are both so freaking powerful that they can't even hurt each other, it's beautiful. But therein lies the problem, too. That fight was never going to solve anything. As much as I loved it, I knew it would end in a draw, because one-on-one violence can't win the day in Friendship is Magic. I felt like it was easily the weakest part of the episode. Which admittedly isn't saying much, given the rest.<br /> <br /> Eh, I guess it's not really a complaint, but I feel inordinately sad about Twilight's tree-library. I guess I'm supposed to, but damn, that place was iconic. And all the boooks!<br /> <br /> Right, I don't have any other ways of saying &quot;everything was awesome&quot;, so I'm just going to go right on into...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Some collected thoughts on season 4</b><br /> <br /> You all know I love this season by now, so I won't go on about why I love it again. Instead, I will relate my perspective on what I think this season represents for the development of the show. And it is this: this season has been important because it shows we don't need Lauren Faust.<br /> <br /> Before you collectively lynch me, give me a moment to explain.<br /> <br /> In the history of My Little Pony, it makes sense to talk about a Faust and post-Faust era. In season one, Lauren Faust laid the ground foundations of what FiM was, the core tenets and the tone for the entire show. I don't believe FiM would have come about without her, and we must recognise that. She was directly involved in the first season, and on-and-off in the second season, and those season are also widely beloved.<br /> <br /> Much as Faust is to thank for the event of FiM, fact is that she won't be coming back. Season three had to prove that Faust's absence would not have detrimental effects on the quality of the show, and I think it's not controversial to say that it failed. By the end of season three, I had at least to some extent prepared myself for the start of decline. The golden days behind us, we'd see the show falter and lessen until some executive at Hasbro decided Gen 5 was in order. It would all be Equestria Girls from here on out, oh yes.<br /> <br /> And then season four came along and showed us that not only can FiM manage without Faust, it can actually make many parts better. For example, I honestly suspect we'd never have seen a season-long subplot if Faust had still been on the team. Even in season three, note how they tried to do it but rather failed; it's unlikely to be a coincidence that they attempted it the moment Faust was gone. But conspiracy theories aside, season 4 has been a cavalcade of success, with a few blemishes but hey, that's how it goes. We've seen that the crew can carry our beloved series into the post-Faust world not only in name only but also in spirit and execution. That is the significance of season 4, and it's damn significant.<br /> <br /> Glory days ahead, bronies. Glory days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 05-13-2014, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:22:47-07:00","id":136343,"title":"","content":"I still think it's a mixed bag, because fucking ass did this season have some stinkers, particularly up front, and even though i love the season finale, It is <i>riddled</i> with issues(but in this case, I think those issues actually don't matter, not that I'm sweeping them aside and ignoring them, but because they somehow don't act as problems while being problems). But when it kicks ass, it kicks ass. Some of the strongest episodes in this style of narrative are in Season 4, rather than 3 or 2. Do I think Faust had a better idea overall? Yes, but I came to terms with her being gone shortly after becoming a brony(althought Season 3 and the a lot of the first episodes of Season 4 made me look back more than wistfully).<br /> <br /> My point is that, while my journey is different from Wei's(and sooner or later I should properly review the episodes), I have to agree-I am now convinced the team can fully stand on their own and play their game competently.<br /> <br /> The only problem left is if Hasbro is going to force it into being a an undying cashcow or trust the writers to know when it's done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T17:38:55-07:00","id":140056,"title":"","content":"So. I only just got around to watching the last couple of episodes.<br /> <br /> Hands down, best season finale of the show. Greatly exceeds the expectations set by the season opener. In the upper tier of episodes in the entire show. Personally, I honestly find it to be one of the best <i>things</i> that I have seen; it actually managed to truly move me.<br /> <br /> I was actually ready to start with my usual thing for recording thoughts as they come to me, but the episode managed to draw me in enough early on that I actually didn't want to stagger my way through it. I'll be rewatching it for the sake of doing that thing.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'll just say: excellent villain, excellent plot and pacing, some really genuine stakes, an amazing way to actually make stuff that has come before it all come together, and ends on a note that would be excellent in its own right, but certainly leaves me eagerly awaiting what's going to be coming next.<br /> <br /> Well done show, well done; all is forgiven for season 3. No, more than that; I feel as though <i>I</i> owe <i>you</i> something.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T19:20:37-07:00","id":140153,"title":"","content":"So...any thoughts on the Rainbow Pony designs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru