attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T15:42:17-07:00","id":140963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=140471#post140471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have pictures of them? They only flashed into view for a few seconds on screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you are:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc07.deviantart.net/fs71/i/2014/036/6/3/rainbow_power_ponies_by_benybing-d75aoar.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"http://benybing.deviantart.com/art/Rainbow-Power-Ponies-432159363\" target=\"_blank\">http://benybing.deviantart.com/art/R...nies-432159363</a><br /> <br /> Though Rainbow Dash's was tweaked to include some sort of speedy...afro...thing:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://news.everfree.net/files/2014/01/rainbow_power_rd_by_wolfyomega-d712wvs.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"http://wolfyomega.deviantart.com/art/Rainbow-Power-RD-425078776\" target=\"_blank\">http://wolfyomega.deviantart.com/art...r-RD-425078776</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T00:30:17-07:00","id":141302,"title":"","content":"I feel that AJ got a bit shortchanged, not a lot changed with hers and what did change blends quite well with what she used to look like without them appearing like accentuating highlights.<br /> <br /> Pinkie is the big winner here, her darker pink on pink original colour scheme is getting a big change here and she looks more dynamic and visually interesting so I like hers the most.<br /> <br /> &quot;I really like her...mane?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T01:27:30-07:00","id":141356,"title":"","content":"I'll agree Pinkie is among the better ones, but I like Fluttershy a lot as well. The new streams of colour in her mane does a lot to improve an otherwise boring look. The others also get such streams, but I don't feel they had the same problem to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T06:42:28-07:00","id":141511,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about Tirek, and how he really is firing on all cylinders as a villain. For one thing, it's great that they introduce him early and then have a double length episode to develop him; I wouldn't exactly call him a complex character, but between the way that he's able to manipulate Discord (with the sense of, if not a history, than a familiarity of reputation), his vengeful attitude towards the Princesses, and his persistent references to his brother that demonstrate a lingering bitterness over that whole deal, he's got a good deal of nuance when it would be so easy to just leave him as a generic villain. That thing with the brother in particular... he keeps being brought up, to the point where you'd think it might be setting up his presence, but instead it just serves as a way to characterise the antagonist (as well as inform his motivations and factors that make for his eventual downfall.<br /> <br /> Also, he fucks around with unicorn horns and cutie marks, which I've always thought was the easiest way to show something off as severely messed up with ponies.<br /> <br /> His voice is great too, initially quite creepy and unnerving but also growing suitably powerful sounding as he grows stronger. And he's got a great design, the whole bull-baboon centaur thing, and the particulars of how he grows out, all warped and stretching and his horns curving out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:12:48-07:00","id":144845,"title":"","content":"I liked Tirek too. As you say, he'd going all out. Admittedly, he's also probably the most formulaic bad guy since Nightmare Moon, but that doesn't make him bad. Sombra had a much better premise, but didn't turn out a tenth as good.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking of something else during this season, namely the songs. I don't know about you, but I kind of feel they've been so-so. The only one that really gripped me was Apples to the Core. The only possible contender is Twilight's song in the last episode, but I don't really know. I'm missing the Smile, Smile, Smiles and Winter Wrap Ups this season, the iconic earworms. And I'm still waiting for Ingram to top This Day Aria, which I hold to be the best song in the series, but it's starting to look like he won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:18:58-07:00","id":144849,"title":"","content":"Smile Smile Smile is obviously the best.<br /> <br /> No. Imma let you finish but Smile Smile Smile shoulda been top of your list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:34:49-07:00","id":144864,"title":"","content":"Smile, Smile, Smile is certainly on place two or three. The #1 has to go the This Day Aria, though. It's not only super-high quality, it's also clever. Like, the fact that the musical term for the way Chrysalis sings the end of her verses is a &quot;deceptive cadance&quot;? I'm too much of a nerd to not fall for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T00:12:56-07:00","id":145364,"title":"","content":"That's actually one reason I dislike that song. The discordant/dissonant/whatever the correct musical term is for the vocals makes me immediately start thinking of the song in technical terms, using techniques and the like while Smile Smile Smile is essentially everything you'd expect it to be meaning it's fun and silly and doesn't make me think about the 'mechanics' that went into the song. See also the song in Frozen by the younger princess at the beginning about not being able to leave the palace.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Discord and dissnonance and the like always makes me think of grunge :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:10:49-07:00","id":145952,"title":"","content":"Songs: Agreed that the &quot;This Day&quot; Aria was the high point of the series so far. My runner up is Discords' song, which narrowly beats out Ying-Yang, I mean, Flim-Flam Brothers' songs...Hm, guess I have a thing for Villain Songs! Most of the other songs I can honestly take or leave...Celestia's song to proto-Alicorn Twilight was pretty nice, tho!<br /> <br /> Power-Up Rainbow Designs: Ugh, no thanks. Both ugly AND catering to what corporate execs *think* little girls like. It might be telling that the animators gave them so little screen time...I do find it funny that, in the group picture, only Fluttershy seems to have the taste to look suitably embarrassed by the whole thing...<br /> <br /> Season as a whole: Vast improvement over the last one, this should be a good sign for great things ahead! Still not sure if I liked it as much as Season 2, tho. Must rewatch that one soon...<br /> <br /> Hm, remember how the first few eps of this season kept ending with &quot;or IS it??&quot; teasers? Given how Tirek looked when we first see him, I wonder if we now know the true identity of the &quot;Pony of Shadows&quot;...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:27:26-07:00","id":145976,"title":"","content":"The Equestrian Games: This actually disappointed me a bit. After all that build up, and we don't even get to really SEE them?! I get that the character development was more important, but if you compare this to, say, the Grand Galloping Gala, it feels like we got to know that event much more. At least they didn't entirely commit the &quot;kid's entertainment&quot; sin I mentioned before by having Ponyville's team (which, let's face, was RD carrying everypony else) sweep the gold. <br /> <br /> I almost didn't mind the above, tho, because what was going on with Spike was just So. Damn. Funny! I can't recall when this show has made me LOL so long or hard as Spike's anthem...Daaamn, that was painful!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Didn't mind Spike finding it within himself to melt the ice-cloud (why did they have to use magic ice arrows again?), but...judging from where the melted water rained down, it, um...wouldn't have hurt anypony anyway, since apparently the pegasi had already moved it over the empty field. Whatever, let the little guy have his day! Even tho this was almost the same lesson as from the Superhero story earlier on ...(also, even if the Princesses had their magic sealed, they still should have been physically strong enough to shift it by themselves...Well, I still did like their different reactions to Spike's initial problem, esp Luna!) <br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I had had a strong feeling that the villain was going to interrupt the games, which would have given us a three-part ending. Didn't happen, but we really got enough of him anyway. When I saw all the speculation that it would be Tirek, I watched his original ep on Youtube, just in case. Shame he didn't mutate any ponies into reptilian beasts this time around! Nice shout out to Scorpan, tho (and Starswirl)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:48:16-07:00","id":145997,"title":"","content":"I can't add much to what's already been praised about the finale, so I'll just add that I agree. Only two things really bothered me: The emotional dilemma Twilight is going through in the beginning, is virtually *exactly* what Spike was going through just last episode! She can't take her own advice? <br /> <br /> Also, I agree with Tirek's disbelief, what exactly WAS Celestia's plan? Just to hide all of their power and...what, wait? I think they would have had better odds of taking him on as four Alicorns, than one with the power all them all. <br /> <br /> OTOH(oof), putting things together from the past gives us some interesting possibilities: Tirek escaped when Cerberus left Tartarus back in season 2 (we still don't know why Cerberus did this). No prison worth the name will let a security breach go without a roll-call of prisoners to see if any are missing, so they should have noticed he was gone soon after. Why does Celestia have Discord released in S3? Because she foresaw a time when his magic would be useful! IOW, Celestia saw this coming and was playing a very long game, indeed! She's spent all this time waiting for Tirek to regain enough power to appear on Discord's magic radar, knowing that he was out there creeping around like Cell (or Voldemort, if you prefer), helpless until he did! I wouldn't be surprised if the nightmare vision that woke her up was part of a spell she cast to alert her when something like this happened... (of course, Discord can respond far faster to such things than she could)<br /> <br /> Also, we learn of a new, separate Pony nation, Maretonia, as well as seeing the Saddle Arabians again! I wonder if they have Princesses of their own, even if they aren't Alicorns...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:23:04-07:00","id":148133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&amp;v=vL4q7BBzanI\" data-code=\"vL4q7BBzanI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vL4q7BBzanI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Weird shadowy tentacle powers?<br /> <br /> Trapping someone in a bizarre Oubliette realm?<br /> <br /> Totally a Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:38:47-07:00","id":149667,"title":"","content":"So I finally got a chance to catch Fall of the Crystal Empire. Here be spoilers: take ten minutes to watch the video in Scutarii's post.<br /> <br /> First impression: fuck yeah! This is wonderfully animated. A whole ten minute long combat scene with dramaturgy, choreography and voice acting on that level must be acknowledged. The technical fidelity alone makes it entirely worth watching, and well, I won't pretend I don't enjoy ponies kicking the shit out of each other.<br /> <br /> That said, I know the video has had a mixed reaction, and I must say I can understand it. The video plays fast and loose with one of the few pieces of actual canon we can derive from the show about the war against Sombra, namely that he was banished by Celestia and Luna together. In the video, Luna is clearly doing most of the work, and while I personally think they've made a good product, I do admit, I can understand if people get a little feeling of &quot;with all that freedom, you had to change the one thing we actually knew?&quot; I've also seen some accusations of pandering to the crowd by letting the more popular sister take front stage. I'm not so sure about that one; I think the interaction between Sombra and Luna was the best part of the video, and if that was pandering, then I'd like some more, please.<br /> <br /> Silly Filly Studios were the group who brought us Snowdrop earlier, and of course, there are more things that differ that story from this one than unites them (but notably, they both relate stories of the distant past and describe some pivotal moment in Equestria's history). The biggest difference, though, is that despite Snowdrop being a bit soppy in a way the show has never been, it could be mistaken for an episode. Fall of the Crystal Empire... can't. At all. I think that's the biggest thing that makes it less well-received than Snowdrop. Snowdrop was a fan-made episode of MLP:FiM. Fall of the Crystal Empire is just a fan-made video. And we have lots of those already.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I did like it. Really solid video. Unlikely to achieve the acclaim of Snowdrop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:59:34-07:00","id":149683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=144864#post144864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smile, Smile, Smile is certainly on place two or three. The #1 has to go the This Day Aria, though. It's not only super-high quality, it's also clever. Like, the fact that the musical term for the way Chrysalis sings the end of her verses is a &quot;deceptive cadance&quot;? I'm too much of a nerd to not fall for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hey just noticed this.<br /> <br /> This Day Aria is cool. It's got a lot of clever touches to it and a nigh on perfect delivery.<br /> <br /> But Smile Smile Smile <i>is Friendship is Magic</i>. It is <i>everything </i>this show embodies. It is more so the theme of the show than the actual theme song.<br /> <br /> Point to Smile.<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, the Crystal Empire thing was fun. But yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T13:22:32-07:00","id":149692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=149683#post149683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, hey just noticed this.<br /> <br /> This Day Aria is cool. It's got a lot of clever touches to it and a nigh on perfect delivery.<br /> <br /> But Smile Smile Smile <i>is Friendship is Magic</i>. It is <i>everything </i>this show embodies. It is more so the theme of the show than the actual theme song.<br /> <br /> Point to Smile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Sure, FiM makes me smile, in many ways. From the comedy, and the cuteness, and the sheer quality. But if FiM was first and foremost about making people smile, it'd not have gotten the following it did. Call me politicising or pretentious, but I firmly believe that the point of FiM, the reason it gets so much attention and has such a following, is that it challenges norms. Primarily, it challenges the ideas surrounding young girls and their taste, but with the brony phenomenon it has also come to represent a rather non-standard stance of what is male and manly. <i>That</i> is FiM to me.<br /> <br /> But, y'know, Smile is good. Not sayin' it ain't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=149683#post149683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, the Crystal Empire thing was fun. But yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that about sums it up, doesn't it? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T15:12:16-07:00","id":156928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=148133#post148133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird shadowy tentacle powers?<br /> <br /> Trapping someone in a bizarre Oubliette realm?<br /> <br /> Totally a Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I would have said Ebon Dragon...ESP with the &quot;mindscrew&quot; elements (can Obtenabration even do that?). Sombra is a pretty good idea of what an Infernal Exalt who favors Malfeas and the Ebon Dragon might turn out like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T15:16:21-07:00","id":156932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=149692#post149692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Sure, FiM makes me smile, in many ways. From the comedy, and the cuteness, and the sheer quality. But if FiM was first and foremost about making people smile, it'd not have gotten the following it did. Call me politicising or pretentious, but I firmly believe that the point of FiM, the reason it gets so much attention and has such a following, is that it challenges norms. Primarily, it challenges the ideas surrounding young girls and their taste, but with the brony phenomenon it has also come to represent a rather non-standard stance of what is male and manly. <i>That</i> is FiM to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly those last points. If I were tasked to convince a non-fan what all the fuss is about through the songs, &quot;Smile&quot; is probably the LAST thing I would expose them to, as it could only cement most non-fans' preconceived notions about what MLP is. Once you're a fan, it's great, but anyone else would just roll their eyes and write the show off as sweet and insipid. Show them the Aria, otoh, and you'll probably get a much more impressed reaction...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:49:28-07:00","id":157137,"title":"","content":"Coming into A Canterlot Wedding unspoiled, if it hadn't already happened, that song will make you truly realise that this show is something new compared to its predecessors. I mean, for all I knew, Cadance was actually a manipulative bitch, or maybe straight-up insane. And then, when you meet the real Cadance, you start thinking about evil twins or something. And then they <i>sing about it!</i> In a way that, in all but length, can compete with Disney on their best day. Again, this is <i>My Little freaking Pony!</i><br /> <br /> Smile or Winter Wrap-Up are very indicative of certain aspects of the show which are indeed present. But like Omega said, Aria displays the parts where the show actually is being progressive. And that part is vital to the show's identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T21:53:33-07:00","id":167559,"title":"","content":"So, I finally got into reading the comic book, not from the beginning, but with the latest storyline. This is some really clever stuff, definitely written for an older, more mature audience but without getting &quot;grim and dark&quot;. Frankly, I think the comic may well spoil me for the show!<br /> <br /> The current storyline involves the Mane Six discovering the Mirror Universe, where Equestria is ruled by Good King Sombra...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static1.e621.net/data/sample/27/43/2743002c0d45e41cf646cd05ff45f82f.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...And <a href=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2014/5/20/631566__safe_derpy+hooves_trixie_edit_queen+chrysalis_glasses_alicorn_idw_race+swap_spoiler-colon-comic.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>these</i> guys are (apparently) the Elements of Harmony...</a><br /> <br /> The backstory to this setup also involves Princess Celestia and Starswirl the Bearded, and their cosmic adventures visiting other worlds:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/wyghlHq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Starswirl is hilarious, btw!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2014/5/24/635313__safe_shipping_princess+celestia_straight_idw_king+sombra_spoiler-colon-comic_star+swirl+the+bearded_celestibra.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In the present, after narrowly escaping, Celestia <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/n8kuNkW.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">dispatches the Mane Six (er, Seven!)</a> to help Sombra out, much to Luna's chagrin...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.adventuresinpoortaste.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/my-little-pony-friendship-is-magic-18-luna.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> While there, Twilight has to confront the decision of which path her future will take, while learning a secret about Celestia that her mentor fears will change how Twilight sees her forever...<br /> <br /> Plus, <a href=\"https://derpicdn.net/media/W1siZiIsIjIwMTMvMDMvMTUvMDJfMTFfMjlfODk4XzI3MDg2NV9fVU5PUFRfX3NhZmVfZG9jdG9yX3dob292ZXNfaWR3X2ZvcmVzaGFkb3dpbmdfNTEzNzgwZGZhNGM3MmRhOWEzMDAwMzk0LmpwZyJdXQ/270865__safe_doctor-whooves_idw_foreshadowing_fringe_513780dfa4c72da9a3000394.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a> keeps popping up in the background to observe important events during various storylines! No word on him yet, but I'm pretty sure he's a reference to Fringe, of all things!<br /> <br /> Looking forward to seeing how this storyline finishes up...<a href=\"http://i390.photobucket.com/albums/oo345/stryke81/MLP/579567__safe_princessluna_princesscelestia_comic_idw_cover_selfponidox_artist-colon-andypriceart_dualpersona_mirroruniverse.jpg~original\" target=\"_blank\">next issue looks like a real doozy!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 06-13-2014, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T01:20:57-07:00","id":167675,"title":"","content":"The comic is something I've heard about but never gotten into. Maybe I should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T03:15:31-07:00","id":167710,"title":"","content":"Where would one find it if one were to go looking?<br /> <br /> Does it have a sensible start point or is it like other comics where volume 7 of random storyline is a crossover start point for three other unrelated comics and it turns into a fractal spreadsheet nightmare trying to work out where to start?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, just noticed it. Evil world Derpy has glasses. No idea why that's so funny to me but it just is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T05:34:42-07:00","id":167783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=167710#post167710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would one find it if one were to go looking?<br /> <br /> Does it have a sensible start point or is it like other comics where volume 7 of random storyline is a crossover start point for three other unrelated comics and it turns into a fractal spreadsheet nightmare trying to work out where to start?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, just noticed it. Evil world Derpy has glasses. No idea why that's so funny to me but it just is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each volume is a standalone story, so no worries on that front. Though there are a ton of background references and cameos. See if you can spot the pony versions of the Sailor Senshi, they're all there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T07:23:39-07:00","id":167896,"title":"","content":"I've been enjoying the comics, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T22:36:22-07:00","id":169490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=167710#post167710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would one find it if one were to go looking?<br /> <br /> Does it have a sensible start point or is it like other comics where volume 7 of random storyline is a crossover start point for three other unrelated comics and it turns into a fractal spreadsheet nightmare trying to work out where to start?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, just noticed it. Evil world Derpy has glasses. No idea why that's so funny to me but it just is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be picked up at any comic book store; in fact, they worked out a deal where specific stores get specific covers. I had to go a little out of my way to visit one store, which actually had a cool Dr. Whooves/Derpy cover, but they were asking $17 for it! Buck that noise...A friend of mine later told me that it's illegal for stores to do that, but that ain't stopping them, if true...<br /> <br /> I like &quot;Scholar Derpy&quot;! Interesting to note that the Mirror Doctor doesn't seem to be &quot;evil&quot;, just another incarnation...That's King Sombra in the mirror, in case you missed it. I *really* want to know what's going on with Mirror Cadence and Shining Armor, there! Also interesting to see that both Spikes seem the same...<br /> <br /> <br /> A previous issue that I liked was a special about Luna:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-yC-NFLFyJ2w/UrXXjMnWjdI/AAAAAAAAJsc/sjRU2pMcUlo/s1600/mlpmicro10a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Luna takes over Celestia's duties for the daytime. Some of which involve watching the &quot;common folk&quot;...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140312044121/mlp/images/c/c9/Micro-Series_issue_10_page_4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...and hearing court cases...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/5/55582/3546501-princess+luna+comic+28.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...socializing with the Elite...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/2013/12/18/500320/medium.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> (Which leads to her an Fancy Pants forcing pony tourists to the royal castle to play out their <a href=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2013/12/18/500368__safe_princess+luna_idw_spoiler-colon-comic_fancypants_lot+of+ponies+without+name.png\" target=\"_blank\">game of</a> <a href=\"http://www.roundstable.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/lunaprotests-690x525.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">live chess!</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.roundstable.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/lunacomicsnip-690x419.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Meanwhile, Celestia enjoys her impromptu vacation...</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T14:54:22-07:00","id":183245,"title":"","content":"I cracked...and bought all 4 anthologies on comixology.<br /> <br /> And after reading I regret <b>nothing!</b><br /> <br /> I love the little touches in the background and Shining Armour caused DJ-Pon3 to get her cutie mark!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:59:15-07:00","id":183849,"title":"","content":"It's good, isn't it? Like I said, the only downside is that it's so good, it may ruin the cartoon for you!<br /> <br /> I didn't think of looking online...how much is it there?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T09:04:30-07:00","id":183851,"title":"","content":"Looks a fairly complete set, though I don't see the cover with Luna hyped up on coffee which I'm interested in reading.<br /> <br /> Edit: and of course it would probably help if I gave you a link (I literally had it copied ot my clipboard, just didn't ctrl+v into the post!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.comixology.co.uk/search?search=my+little+pony\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.comixology.co.uk/search?search=my+little+pony\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.comixology.co.uk/search?search=my+little+pony\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.comixology.co.uk/search?search=my+little+pony </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 06-29-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:04:42-07:00","id":185933,"title":"","content":"More comicy goodness: The Fall of Sunset Shimmer!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i0.wp.com/www.webstoodstupid.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-p4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-7.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-9.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 07-01-2014, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T11:43:29-07:00","id":186439,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, perhaps something to flesh her character out a bit, Sunset was a potentially interesting character but ended up as generic villain by the end of the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T14:52:27-07:00","id":187432,"title":"","content":"Imma let you finish, but Sunset Shimmer was a better villain than Trixie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T21:13:00-07:00","id":187663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=187432#post187432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imma let you finish, but Sunset Shimmer was a better villain than Trixie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but...Trixie was never *really* a villain. In her first appearance, she's barely even an antagonist (that's really the Ursa), and in her second, she's as much a victim as anyone else, and the main conflict is getting the Alicorn Amulet off her to save her as much as anyone else. <br /> <br /> Sunset, on the other hoof, was out for power and domination from the start, whether dominating a high school or invading Equestria, and no magic was forcing her to do any of that! Which is why her heel-face turn at the end just doesn't really work for me. True, the Elements restored Luna, but indications are that Luna was changed as much as Amulet Trixie was, and Twilight &quot;cured&quot; her (she says as much to Twilight, in fact). But from what we could see, Shimmer was pretty much rotten to the core all by herself, so unless the Elements actually *forced* her to become &quot;good&quot;...I don't see her conversion as being real or lasting.<br /> <br /> Besides, if it really was, then I would think she would want to return home, to face Celestia and truly apologize...<br /> <br /> I hope she's in the new movie. Even if we have to swallow an implausible conversion, it'd still be interesting to see how she's filling Twilight's shoes in their Mane Six! I thought that Trixie was going to be the antagonist, but it looks like it's a new character (who may not even have a pony analog (that we get to see)) Dazzle Adagio. Hope Trixie still gets plenty of screen time, tho!<br /> <br /> While we're on the subject, FANFIC REC TIME! <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.fimfiction.net/story/129734/matters-of-principle\" target=\"_blank\">Matters of Principle</a> is about Principal Celestia's day dealing with the aftermath of the events of the movie, and gives great insight into why she did the things she did in it. It's very short, complete in one chapter and makes a SCARY amount of sense!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T21:59:54-07:00","id":187719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=187663#post187663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> True, but...Trixie was never *really* a villain. In her first appearance, she's barely even an antagonist (that's really the Ursa), and in her second, she's as much a victim as anyone else, and the main conflict is getting the Alicorn Amulet off her to save her as much as anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div> With a slight change in perspective, the real antagonist of Trixie's first episode is the Mane Six. Trixie's a traveling stage magician doing a show, playing up the whole powerful-mystic image for the crowd, and suddenly a group of hecklers arrive to spoil the act. All poor Trixie wanted was to put on a good show, dazzle her audience! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:41:31-07:00","id":188040,"title":"","content":"I kind of <i>hate</i> that explanation.(even if I get the idea you are joking about, I'm sorry, this comes up often enough it bugs me)<br /> <br /> First off, let's get a small thing out of the way. Even though it came up later, Trixie was always going to pull the bullshit with the Ursa story. Trixie wasn't going to ever have a problem with having people thinking she did something clearly hadn't done because it makes her feel good, makes her feel as big as her stories. She <i>is </i>as boastful as Rarity says she is, and her goal is not to entertain, but inflate her own ego.<br /> <br /> Second, and the bigger point, you are doing a magic show <i>in a world with every day magic</i>. Nothing wrong with that okay, it is okay to have talents and to show them off-but it's important you realize and handle it in a such a way that it inspires people to rise, not diminishes them. Trixie's show is a mixture of a strongman running around and showing off how strong he is and laughing at audience members who haven't worked out nearly as much as he has(what work Trixie did put in)....and running around, flapping their dick around and pointing out how much bigger it is than others(Trixie's raw talent ala Cutie Mark, which I genuinely believe has to do with magic and not the stage magic).<br /> <br /> It's not fair to think of it like we think of magic shows here in life-here, of course stage magic is fake, it's all illusion, so telling stories to get us into the lie is more acceptable. In Equestria, it's more like a talent show, a display of common abilities that are taken farther than most people do, and that requires a tact Trixie from the word go is never interested in.<br /> <br /> As for Trixie and Sunset...<br /> <br /> 1)Trixie is totally a villain. She might not have been the main antagonist of her first episode, but she <i>is</i> being arrogant and prideful and spiteful for really bad reasons, and a general pain in the side. THe traits she has there grow on their own and evolve her into the main antagonist of the second one. Yes, Twilight knows that Trixie is being pushed by the Amulet to do worse and worse things(although in my headcanon that's actually bullshit and more a matter of power corrupts), but Trixie puts the damn thing on with intent of fucking up Twilight and Ponyville to begin with anyways(And even after she takes it off she tries to shoot Rainbow with lightning with the intent of torture). Once she's humbled and given time to think on it, she realizes she's a jerk and makes up for it, but she started off a complete and total jackass and let that escalate and eclipse her other aspects. In fact, she and Sunset start off at the same place, it's just that Trixie doesn't put in the work.<br /> <br /> 2)Sunset's redemption is true to me, and I don't see her as being rotten to the core. I've been her in ways, resenting being in classes that were way below my intellect and wanting to go and do something new and interesting and exciting. I get wanting more, I get demanding more, I get knowing I'm meant for better things. I also get looking down on others because they aren't as smart as you-I think a lot of people can.If you've ever once just ignored people around you because they weren't as smart as you, you know it. It doesn't start out as hateful, it becomes like that after years of putting up with it, and maybe pushed more if there's rebuttal thrown at a person for being smart(and yeah, I got trouble from others for being smart). [In fact, it's interesting to think about this with Sunset, since although ponies don't exactly work this way, people do-there's a greater stigma against girls acting and looking smart than there are with guys, and Sunset is clearly an excellent female student who has stopped giving a crap about others-coincidence?] THe Elements took her back to a time we still haven't seen and put things in perspective, so when she says she didn't know another way, I kind of believe her.<br /> <br /> All this is moot: what I'm trying to say is that Sunset was more interesting to me than Trixie ever was, so I'm just saying that I have the inverse reaction the fanbase does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:17:30-07:00","id":203563,"title":"","content":"Just got to reading the comics, only the micro series for now, but they are indeed <i>very </i>good so far. Luna's in particular was hilarious. If the series holds up to that standard (and from what I heard of the plot lines and seen of the art, I believe it does) I just might end up liking it better then the cartoon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:05:11-07:00","id":203585,"title":"","content":"I've yet to read a comic I didn't like. Some were flatter than others(Applejacks individual story), but even at their worst they are at least on par with the TV show. Quite often, they find ways to surpass them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:36:30-07:00","id":203631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=203563#post203563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got to reading the comics, only the micro series for now, but they are indeed <i>very </i>good so far. Luna's in particular was hilarious. If the series holds up to that standard (and from what I heard of the plot lines and seen of the art, I believe it does) I just might end up liking it better then the cartoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly like the Shining Armour x Cadance (Why isn't it Cadence! That's so jarring to me every time I read it! Gah) one and the Big Mac trying to get some nails issues. The art style I think is better in those than the others and they seemed to have a lot more little cameos and gags in the backdrop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:48:56-07:00","id":205477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=185933#post185933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More comicy goodness: The Fall of Sunset Shimmer!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i0.wp.com/www.webstoodstupid.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-p4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-7.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2013/10/My-Little-Pony-Annual-2013-Comic-Equestria-Girls-9.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Speak of Equestria Girls, has anyone figured out the timey-wimey stuff therein? Considering Sunset was there for what appeared to be three, almost four, years, and she was gone on the Equestria side for what must be around Ten years(the fact passing through the portal apparently changes your biological age doesn't help much...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T18:09:10-07:00","id":205508,"title":"","content":"Probably. THere's all sorts of reviewers in the community who do that sort thing. If EqD doesn't have a particular mention, some digging on Youtube probably will yield results.<br /> <br /> I had it figured out once, but that was ages ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T18:21:32-07:00","id":255716,"title":"","content":"So, Rainbow Rocks stuff is out. Sunset is now Woobie, Celestia continues to be worst principal, and our villains are evil divas/sirens/flutter-ponies. Discus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T21:24:49-07:00","id":255813,"title":"","content":"I think I'll actually take the hour drive to see it in theaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T03:22:19-07:00","id":255949,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I won't. I have to figure out how to watch it. Wonder if it'll get onto Swedish iTunes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T13:25:59-07:00","id":256212,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I'm kind of worried about Twilight showing up. I like her, keep in mind, but I'm worried that Sunset might not get a real chance to shine(not helped by the fact she's not in the band). And is Worst Principal TRYING to get Sunset hurt?! Yes, remind the students why they hate her when they're already hostile. If this had a higher rating, she'd probably be afraid for her life! Maybe I'm blowing this out of proportion, but it still bugs me. <br /> <br /> Also, I want Prime!Megatron and Sunset to sit down and have a talk. Just 'cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T14:46:18-07:00","id":256262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=255949#post255949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I won't. I have to figure out how to watch it. Wonder if it'll get onto Swedish iTunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit the motives have more to do with the fact that it involves driving and getting out of my shit town for a bit.<br /> <br /> ...but I think that there's enough of style of 'twist'(applied loosely here) from the first film to make this passable. I'm not sure if I can properly explain what makes me feel mildly hopeful about the experience, but I think there will be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T15:37:49-07:00","id":256309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=256262#post256262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit the motives have more to do with the fact that it involves driving and getting out of my shit town for a bit.<br /> <br /> ...but I think that there's enough of style of 'twist'(applied loosely here) from the first film to make this passable. I'm not sure if I can properly explain what makes me feel mildly hopeful about the experience, but I think there will be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, and I'd be glad if it was. I'm going into this expecting nothing but the subpar, myself. I have a feeling that if I like it at all, it will be the little jokes and quirky moments that do it, and precious little else.<br /> <br /> And, y'know, that might be enough, sure. It's enough in some episodes of the main show, so I'm not judging. I'm all for giving everything a chance. But I'm also not going to disregard my experience from the last movie, which was that it was a pleasant distraction with some characters that stuck in the community, but it carried very little of what in my opinion makes either the show or the community stand out among other franchises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:11:54-07:00","id":256373,"title":"","content":"I was watching &quot;Battle of the Bands&quot; a second time, and I noticed something. In the background of one moment, we see Vinyl, headphones on and outright ignoring the big musical number. Vinyl, who we don't see acting under the Dazzlings' spell. Vinyl, who had a short just like the Humane Six, and who apparently plays a role in the prequel book. I have a feeling a certain well-know background Pon3 is going to have a impact on the plot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T20:23:38-07:00","id":257812,"title":"","content":"So did a new season start or something? I haven't really been keeping up but suddenly the Pony subreddit is full of Twilight eating pretzels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T21:03:43-07:00","id":257831,"title":"","content":"Nope, no new season yet in a while. The new hotness is Equestria Girls: Rainbow Rocks. You know that movie where Twilight turned into a human? Yeah, it got a follow-up and now they're playing music. I've not seen it yet, but there's a pretty good chance the pretzels are from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:59:48-07:00","id":267440,"title":"","content":"So, Rainbow Rocks just hit theaters yesterday. What do those who saw it think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T09:11:51-07:00","id":267443,"title":"","content":"I have a lot to say about it. I'll give what I said last night and then try for a more detailed review later.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So, Rainbows Rocks is, in some ways, smarter than its' predecessor, having some of its' ideas line up remarkably well under the surface, better than the subtle thematics at work of Equestria Girls, as well as some of the genius of the characters and/or conflicts(at the very least, there's less gymnastics to see why things happen). It pays for this in a bad way though: It's boring and unengaging, uneven in it's surface focus, and pays too little too late. It's worth a watch(stay to the end of the credits), but I can't call it good, or even fun enough for multiple viewings.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">EDIT: THe biggest problem with this film, though not the only one, can be summed up with one word: passivity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">EDIT: While I'm still planning on reviewing first, a way of seeing it again has occurred, so a second viewing might change my opinion.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-28-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T11:38:03-07:00","id":267545,"title":"","content":"So, before going into Rainbow Rocks, I'm gonna quickly get out my thoughts on the last movie for contrast.<br /> <br /> Equestria Girls was a big, kinda dumb film that was a ton of fun that actually had some good cleverness underneath, although that doesn't stop it from being kinda dumb. I like Sunset Shimmer the way most people like Trixie, finding that some of her sillier or bad decisions to actually be the product of her working with bad circumstances with intelligent reasoning , playing the sure game out of the lot. I thought the secondary theme of the magic of friendship being everywhere and the possibility of Equestria's idealized world being a possibility was clever addressed in world that bridged the audience's reality with the world of the show that capitalized on an iconic time and place that not only served as microcosm for the grand theme but also as the root of the problem. The dull and boring high school tropes are still superficially derivitative, but have life cast into them as it become a game between two arcane chessmasters for the soul of a people, which in a way comments on the power of the show. It's still dumb in a lot of ways(those photos), but with constant challenges and a great sense of fun(admit it, you rocked out to Helping Twilight Win the Crown), the first movie is watchable despite its' flaws.<br /> <br /> So, Rainbow Rocks. Where to begin.<br /> <br /> Well, with the protagonist...Sunset Shimmer.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Sunset should be the protagonist, and the film knows this. It introduces her conflict quickly and solidly in the first few scenes as we find her still dealing with the fallout of the last movie. She wonders how she can ever move beyond what she's done and earn acceptance from the people she hurt, and as such deals with self doubt, not feeling it's her place to solve things, answer questions, or ask to be involved with things she really wants to, despite being more than capable. This was really good stuff, and the movie could have had a great arc on this. It was all set to!<br /> <br /> And then Twilight showed up.<br /> <br /> The movie knows Sunset is the central protagonist, but it doesn't know how to handle an audience that is used to Twilight as the hero. As such, it tries to lay it out as a story of two concurrent problems, Sunset dealing with her baggage and Twilight finding herself not up to the task of creating a counterspell to defeat the sirens(more on them later). The problem is that Twilight's problem isn't active enough to invest in(more on this later), and it takes time away from Sunset's struggle, making the exploration and resolution weaker. Her entire arc doesn't create an impact because not enough happens.<br /> <br /> Speaking of things not happening, the main problem the Mane Seven deal with is both brilliant and boring. I mean that about the brilliance, by the way. The Dazzlings' plan goes off flawlessly, and it should: the opening argument in Battle is persuasive, and when pushed with magic it's no surprise things get ugly quick. When the Mane Six try to blast them with the magic of friendship and it fails(speaking of, I'm glad the sirens didn't even worry, knowing that without some sort of item it would never go off), it barely takes a twist to turn it and make the riled up school turn on them. From there, the Dazzlings don't have to do jack-the school's antagonism would fuel the pre-existing clash of personalities in the group and from there they'd fall apart on their own. With Twilight locking up in her own inability and Sunset not confident enough to step up, all that's left to do is eat up and keep the engine going.<br /> <br /> But as smart as that is, it's boring. You have one large chunk of the same things happening again and again without much variation. The arguments between the Mane Six never go beyond each one problem for each pairing, never adding new small problems to increase a sense of dynamics or real mounting conflict within the group. They also don't try other things, like trying to steal the obviously important necklaces by following the sirens, or some other approaches to beating or subverting the baddies. They just keep stalling while Twilight flops with the spell and the Dazzlings grip the school more and more.<br /> <br /> Say what you will about the first movie and it constantly solving problems shortly after they're brought up, at least things happened that fueled a sense of conflict and activity.<br /> <br /> The Dazzlings themselves are, in theory, really good antagonists. They act as a foil for Sunset as mighty creatures that have fallen as a result of their cruelty and are now seeking a return to grace, with Sunset seeking a acceptance and a new way of life while the Dazzlings seek to restore what they had in the past. They also serve as a foil for the Mane Six and picture of what's to come if the heroes continue like they are, with each third sharing traits with theMane Six sans Twilight and portraying a group that sticks together for the same goal but more or less despise each other, a dead ringer for where the Rainbooms were headed under Rainbow's lead. They(well, okay, Adagio) are really intelligent as discussed, with a plan that let's them achieve what Discord had to cheat at-absolute disharmony between the main characters. They also sound really good.<br /> <br /> But since all they have to do is sit back and relax, they never engage or feel like a threat, and we're stuck with their mostly bad traits dominating our minds- they feel annoying and lackluster. This sort of thing can work-the witches of Hocus Pocus and the Dazzlings are basically alike, but the witches all do something and they all contribute. The Dazzlings don't really do anything, so it's just empty.<br /> <br /> I'll clarify and wrap up my thoughts later. For now, I'm tired of tapping on my phone and I got most of it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-28-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:52:20-07:00","id":271325,"title":"","content":"Hey guys so I finally returned to the forum. Some of you might recall I used to do Professor Penn review series. <br /> Which you can check here <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KaCPjnF9Q7g&amp;list=PL5EC00CD0C772F4AC\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KaCP...C00CD0C772F4AC</a><br /> <br /> I got a new microphone and was considering doing it again. Though after Hasbro threw a fit and got all the episodes pulled, thus even with them back I dont think ad revenue is an option, I was considering running a patreon to justify the work. Sadly I'm in a financial position that I cant put that much time into something with 0% percent chance of making ANY money. Same with my artist who is done giving me free art (not that I blame her). Trust me it is time consuming since I want it to be more than just a simple podcast, I work to have some actual production value to it.<br /> <br /> Since this is where I did alot of my discussion on it originally (ok it was the old forum but still) I thought I'd bring it up here again. Now it wouldn't be much, maybe like 20 bucks per episode. Thinking if ANY money is donating I'll atleast do audio reviews of new episodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T20:35:45-07:00","id":271353,"title":"","content":"Hey there, and welcome back! I liked your reviews back when you made them, and it'd be cool to see them come back.<br /> <br /> That said, I just want to point out that even if you don't monetize your Youtube video, having a Patreon for them is still making money off of them. Hasbro has a tendency to not be too happy about that, no matter how it happens. It's a risky thing, particularly as you can't really have a Patreon on the low-down; that'd defeat the point. I don't want to be too negative about it, but do consider the risks. Once you bring money into it, in any capacity, it becomes a whole new game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T20:49:51-07:00","id":271362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=271353#post271353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there, and welcome back! I liked your reviews back when you made them, and it'd be cool to see them come back.<br /> <br /> That said, I just want to point out that even if you don't monetize your Youtube video, having a Patreon for them is still making money off of them. Hasbro has a tendency to not be too happy about that, no matter how it happens. It's a risky thing, particularly as you can't really have a Patreon on the low-down; that'd defeat the point. I don't want to be too negative about it, but do consider the risks. Once you bring money into it, in any capacity, it becomes a whole new game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not really a concern for me. They have no real claim on it since its covered under fair use, but with how youtube works companies can just take down stuff with only a thinly veiled justification. To be fair they also aren't as bad as they used to be. Besides there are already lots of pony based Patreon stuff in much more legal danger than my show would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T21:02:24-07:00","id":271364,"title":"","content":"You'd be the one to know, I suppose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you're doing it, I'm sure I can drop a few bucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:48:57-07:00","id":274151,"title":"","content":"Has anyone posted this yet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qRC4Vk6kisY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qRC4Vk6kisY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"