rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T10:33:38-07:00","id":278927,"title":"","content":"I have nothing to do with MLP fandom (not even have any opinion about anything related to the franchise), but I'm just dropping by to tell you that in one exorcist site there was a confession of mother that faced her the insidious threat of Satanic My Little Pony toys.<br /> <br /> The mother in question was worried that her 4 year old daughter plays with MLP toys for two hours per day. She came to conclusion that it is unnatural, and burned the toys. Inexplicably for her, the child fell into bouts of &quot;infernal wrath&quot; and depression. <br /> <br /> Of course a brave exorcist explained that all the toys were crafted by insidious corporation controlled by forces of evil and corruption and she already caught evil spirits infesting those toys (Pentex, not even once). The priest enacted rites, fever gone and he declared victory over forces of evil.<br /> <br /> Though naysayers may say the kid just got over the loss of toys, the mother insists prayers made wonders and warns about the taint that MLP toys carry. She also namedropped Barbie and Hello Kitty as gateways to spiritual possession. <br /> <br /> Realtalk, it may sound hilarious but I pity any kid with such a parent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T19:00:11-07:00","id":279296,"title":"","content":"Hey guys give me a hand on something. I'm trying to think of a topic for the Premier Professor Penn's Pony Perusal Program Podcast. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T00:12:07-07:00","id":279427,"title":"","content":"I tried to pledge on that Patreon thing, Aeroz, but I don't think it's working. It says you need to confirm the page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:39:13-07:00","id":279667,"title":"","content":"Thanks for letting me know Weimann. I thought the banner thing was for people with lots of subscribers since it mentioned contacting them if you had over 100k. Didn't realize I had to hit it regardless. Should be working now but please let me know if there are any other issues and of course also thanks for the support. Really motivates me to know there are people that want to see more of this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T05:30:18-07:00","id":296988,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anybody else is familiar with the blog My Little Po-Mo (it's a fairly interesting analysis blog that can get into some fairly intricate detail in reviewing the episodes), but they recently featured <a href=\"http://mlpomo.blogspot.ie/2014/10/commissioned-essay-from-feminist.html\" target=\"_blank\">this essay</a> that I found to be quite nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:22:48-07:00","id":297434,"title":"","content":"Pretty short article, and I'm not sure a single show will have so big an impact as to &quot;change the world&quot;, but I agree with the general sentiment. The show absolutely has a strong feminist agenda, and it is admirably subtle about it, too.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree there is any particularly strong &quot;love and tolerate&quot; message in the show, however. And I never bought into the brony community being particularly special in terms of those values either when the chips are down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:06:25-08:00","id":302852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=297434#post297434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree there is any particularly strong &quot;love and tolerate&quot; message in the show, however. And I never bought into the brony community being particularly special in terms of those values either when the chips are down.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fandom, is much like any fandom really so you have intolerance and elitism, but I think the show does have a strong love and tolerance push. Partly because it kind of has to due to some government mandate stuff. It just handles it alot better than most such shows. Such as having the characters not being flawless when it comes to such stuff. The stuff with Maud Pie was a good example about how tolerance and acceptance isn't the same as getting along. Some people you just aren't compatible with and thats ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:45:47-08:00","id":306888,"title":"","content":"ArcaneArts, I finally saw EG2, and pretty much agree with every single thing you wrote about it...except the conclusion. I dunno, while I agree with your analysis of the storyline problems, in the end, they just weren't bad enough to throw me out of the narrative. I have no problem with saying that I enjoyed this one more than the first, in fact!<br /> <br /> The music was certainly better, thanks largely to the Dazzlings. I also noticed that there were fewer impromptu musical numbers, most of the singing was actual in-setting performances (it always kinda bothered me that the first story in the series lampshaded how shocked the Mane Six were that Pinkie would suddenly break out into song...only for them all to start doing it throughout the rest of the series!). And I think I LOL more at the comedy than at any other story, esp Snips and Snails' rap and Celestia's deadpan reaction (&quot;Please do not drop the microphones!&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'm actually sad that I didn't get to see it theatrically, as it would have been amusing to hear the audience's reaction to a lot of the shout outs and references...half of the audience, anyway, although seeing the non-Brony kids and their parents' reaction to jokes they were getting (like Maud's cameo and Octavia suddenly speaking) would also have been interesting.<br /> <br /> In fact, I was really surprised how, aside from the opening credits pantomime and a couple of quick lines here and there, the movie explained very little about what had happened before and who was who, to a degree I'm usually used to from anime film adaptations! You didn't need to have seen the series to get the first movie, but if you were walking into this one by itself, I suspect you'd be pretty lost...<br /> <br /> And yeah, I am sold on reformed Sunset now, esp seeing her having to deal with the consequences of her actions. Interestingly, the Dazzlings aren't even given as much as she was in the prior movie. What happened to them? I half expected to see them handcuffed in the back of a police van or something, but...nothing! Certainly no indication that they've been &quot;reformed&quot;, so apparently they're still evil, just powerless? Hmm...<br /> <br /> As a Trixie fan, it was nice to see her get much more screen time, effectively becoming the secondary villain! And apparently her act was good enough to make it to the finals on its own; didn't really like her song, but it's annoyingly catchy! Anywho, hopefully this will inspire a return for Pony Trixie in the new season, or the upcoming Pony-Only movie they just announced...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:49:06-08:00","id":306889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QsuRJ6RvrOw\" target=\"_blank\">10 Best MLP Songs</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tXpghSK7u7s\" target=\"_blank\">10 Worst MLP Songs</a><br /> <br /> Agree? Disagree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T19:34:08-08:00","id":307098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=306888#post306888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Trixie fan, it was nice to see her get much more screen time, effectively becoming the secondary villain! And apparently her act was good enough to make it to the finals on its own; didn't really like her song, but it's annoyingly catchy! Anywho, hopefully this will inspire a return for Pony Trixie in the new season, or the upcoming Pony-Only movie they just announced...</div> </div> </div> </div>Tertiary, Rainbow Dash was more of an antagonist than Trixie.<br /> <br /> I keep getting the feel I would like Rainbow Rocks better if I watched it a second time, but I haven't gotten the chance to yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:00:52-08:00","id":307794,"title":"","content":"Saw it when it showed on the Hub(or whatever they're calling it nowadays), and Omega sums up my thoughts perfectly. The ending was especially awesome, though I wish Sunset might have gotten more focus. Oh well. If this &quot;Equestrian Academy&quot; spin-off I've heard vague rumors about actually pulls through, we'll see a lot more of her. <br /> <br /> As for a new topic, any news on S5? I'm wondering if there might be more adventure-y episodes this season, considering the one bit of episode we've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:24:24-08:00","id":308327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=307098#post307098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tertiary, Rainbow Dash was more of an antagonist than Trixie.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, while she certainly had *antagonistic* aspects to her role, RD still wasn't actually a *villain*, which is the word I used. Trixie needed little prompting (not even the supernatural type!) to inspire her to &quot;Pizzazz and the Misfits&quot; levels of mischief...which really makes her far more sinister than her Pony counterpart, who never did anything &quot;wrong&quot; without being supernaturally compelled first!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:29:46-08:00","id":308342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=307794#post307794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a new topic, any news on S5? I'm wondering if there might be more adventure-y episodes this season, considering the one bit of episode we've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Whatchu talking `bout, ZC24?<br /> <br /> EDIT: The only thing I've heard, and I must stress this is a RUMOR, is that the 100th episode will be a love-letter to the Brony community, centering around the background ponies that the fans have adopted and named (hopefully using the fan names, otherwise, why bother?). Presumably, they will also be voiced, and scuttlebutt has it that David Tennant is voicing Doctor Whooves/Time Turner! <br /> <br /> All sounds too good to be true, but keeping my hooves crossed...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edit