lding in a show. Hopefully there might be some sort of overarching frame plot like in season 4 with the rainbow items. That's what really raised the season, and while I'm not sure it's good to just keep on applying the same formula from now on, some sort of intraseasonal connection between episodes would be awesome.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Do we know if season 5 will be a full 26 episode deal? IF they're going to make a 13-part season, that'd be season 6, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:14:15-08:00","id":408555,"title":"","content":"Not sure. I hope it's a longer one. Also, got some more info:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fimfiction.net/group/197119/worldbuilding-alliance/thread/156008/season-5-concept-art-spoilers-duh\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fimfiction.net/group/197...t-spoilers-duh</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:09:57-08:00","id":424749,"title":"","content":"What do you do when you're procrastinating, like, <i>really</i> hard on exams?<br /> <br /> Watch ponies.<br /> <br /> I finally decided to watch Rainbow Rocks on the internet. I'll have to find a way to pay for it at a later date. Rainbow Rocks is old news by now, but I still wanted to post some thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adagio, Aria and Sonata, huh? Pretty obvious siren influences. I'm liking the premise. I wonder why they were banished.<br /> <br /> Well, the intro is very prettily animated. It's pretty catchy music too, but the lyrics are so-so. That is about the expectation I have on the pieces in the movie as a whole, so yeah. Decent start, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I like that Sunset Shimmer is hanging with the Mane 5 in true Defeat Means Friendship fashion. Not only because it fits with their theme, but also because she forms a parallel to Twilight without actually being very derivative of Twilight.<br /> <br /> <s>Like, Celestia? Maybe listen to the people who literally defeated a deamon last year? They might have some sort of say when it comes to supernatural stuff?</s> Oh, okay, charmed by the siren song. Fine. Speaking of which, though...<br /> <br /> [nerdy nitpick] &quot;They even sang a little song to vice principle Luna and <b><u>I</u></b>.&quot; Oh my god, Celestia. If you're going to try to sound classy by using the subject form of the pronoun instead of the heavily overused object form, would it <i>kill</i> you to do it in a place where it's not <i>actually supposed to be the object form?</i> [/nerdy nitpick]<br /> <br /> Ooh, the crystal palace. nice continuity.<br /> <br /> ...the sirens in Twilight's story have fish tails. Is this whole movie really just a joke on sea ponies? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iakTl9SZTTY\" target=\"_blank\">Sho-be-do, sho-sho-be-do?</a> Aria and Sonata are even the right colours!<br /> <br /> Starswirl the Bearded is like the go-to proxy for &quot;someone who did something impressively magical long ago&quot;. Then again, I suppose Twilight isn't one to talk...<br /> <br /> MLP technobabble. I approve.<br /> <br /> Yes, Twilight. Because a couple people looking the same is sure to be the <i>most</i> confusing thing that's going to happen here.<br /> <br /> Twilight doesn't understand that she can only activate her powers in the last 20 minutes of the movie.<br /> <br /> LOL Maud.<br /> <br /> So... many... references in the competition part. O.o<br /> <br /> You victim blaming, AJ? :S<br /> <br /> Sunset: &quot;You're never going to get away with this.&quot;<br /> Adagio: &quot;Why? Because you didn't?&quot;<br /> The burns are real.<br /> <br /> Got to admit. the Dazzlers have had the strongest songs so far.<br /> <br /> They're gonna put Twilight against Trixie in the semifinals? I kind of have to love that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh my god, is AJ ever feisty today. Lay off the hatin', sistah.<br /> <br /> [nerdy nitpic] Thank you, Trixie, for showing us when to really use a pronoun in subject form. [/nerdy nitpick]<br /> <br /> Wow, Trixie's song is actually pretty good. Is there a full version of it? *googles* There is. The fact that I didn't know this is the ultimate proof of how far outside the fandom I've fallen.<br /> <br /> OH HAY YOU GUISE TURNS OUT WE CAN JUST PLAY WHATEVS HAHA TOO BAD WE WAITED SO LONG KK LETS GO<br /> <br /> Is... this the closest we have gotten to a villain actually managing to fight back against a Magical Friendship Laser? In the sequel to a spinoff movie? Really?<br /> <br /> The sirens were autotuned? That's brilliant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And now Sunset will write to Twilight. Here's wondering if THAT'll ever show up in the main series (spoiler: it won't, for if so, a great roar shall rise from the fandom and they shall trample all under their hooves until it is retconned).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That spoiler above is a couple of as-I-go reactions, but overall... well, what can I say? I like Friendship is Magic, and that was certainly Friendship is Magic. Great animation, quite good songs, funny moments in the character interaction (though I think I somehow managed to catch a version that had some minor scenes cut; great excuse to rewatch it). While this movie was better than the first one in a way, in that it developed known characters such as Sunset Shimmer and had room for more nods and winks than the first one necessarily had as it had to establish the premise, it also felt like a sequel in that it's essentially the same damn thing but with justification for the songs. In the end, they're both Quite Okay.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And now when I've successfully spent two hours doing absolutely no work, I need to return to my exam in order to... or, y'know, there was that Trixie song...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-01-2015, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T23:22:28-08:00","id":427483,"title":"","content":"Well, since I inadvertently actualized ponies for myself again, I saw <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=txIWhTCyS_A\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a> posted on EQD. It discusses whether FiM got worse or better after Faust left, and while I'm sure it's been talked about before, it made me kind of curious to see where the opinions lie. Do you think the show got better or worse, or did it stay roughly the same quality level?<br /> <br /> My opinion:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">S1 was the only season that Faust was fully in charge of, but she was still a consulting producer in S2. That makes S3 the first season without Faust's involvement at all, and frankly... it wasn't all that. There's no reason to think that this was all due to Faust's non-involvement, but neither did it inspire confidence. Luckily, S4 was my favourite so far, and I feel like one of the best things it did was to conclusively prove that we do not need Faust to produce quality FiM.<br /> <br /> However, it's not fair to compare a first season to a fourth season and say &quot;good luck they fired her&quot;. The production team is just that: a team, and as a team they now have more practice and a better understanding of the show than they had at the start. Faust might well have made a splendid S4 if she had still been on. It would have been a different season, I'm sure, but that's not to say it wouldn't have worked in the context she would have built up for it beforehand.<br /> <br /> So, do I think Faust leaving had a direct impact on the quality level of the show? No. Do I think it has gotten better since? Yes, and I also think it has not peaked yet. In fact, depending on what they chose to do with the premise set up at the end of S4, it might well be that Faust's intentions of world building and adventure will play a bigger part in S5, which in a way makes her legacy live on through another lens.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T02:15:46-08:00","id":429961,"title":"","content":"Also, in case you didn't see it yet, <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/03/season-5-of-my-little-pony-friendship.html\" target=\"_blank\">S5 premier on 4 April</a>. GET HYPE.<br /> <br /> (Heavy spoilers in the bottom part of the link, but the first screen should be safe.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:01:18-08:00","id":430001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=429961#post429961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in case you didn't see it yet, <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/03/season-5-of-my-little-pony-friendship.html\" target=\"_blank\">S5 premier on 4 April</a>. GET HYPE.<br /> <br /> (Heavy spoilers in the bottom part of the link, but the first screen should be safe.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I AM HYPE.<br /> <br /> No Spoilers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:21:09-08:00","id":430085,"title":"","content":"MY BODY IS NOW READY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:29:38-07:00","id":444500,"title":"","content":"Ugh, just found out that apparently Hasbro couldn't come to an agreement with Netflix or something, so MLP is getting kicked off after today.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Marathoning my favorite episodes before they're lost to time forever (hm, Twilight's a LOT more sarcastic in the early episodes)...<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, did you hear about the 100th episode? Apparently, it's going to be a love letter to Bronydom, being a complete story for background ponies, some of whom will have names and personalities that were determined by the fandom, and apparently even Dr. Whooves will be confirmed to be pretty close to the actual Doctor! Can't wait!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 03-16-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:30:35-07:00","id":445580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=444500#post444500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, just found out that apparently Hasbro couldn't come to an agreement with Netflix or something, so MLP is getting kicked off after today.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Marathoning my favorite episodes before they're lost to time forever (hm, Twilight's a LOT more sarcastic in the early episodes)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, man. I was just going to get Netflix too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=444500#post444500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more positive note, did you hear about the 100th episode? Apparently, it's going to be a love letter to Bronydom, being a complete story for background ponies, some of whom will have names and personalities that were determined by the fandom, and apparently even Dr. Whooves will be confirmed to be pretty close to the actual Doctor! Can't wait!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am looking forward to it, but I do wonder how it'll work out. I remember in S3 when I said that the one thing I really hoped for was a rematch between Twilight and Trixie. And then we got it. And it was one of the worst episodes in the season for me right then. Looking back at it, it's probably not that bad, but the problem was that I had this great idea of how it would look and the episode wasn't <i>that</i> idea.<br /> <br /> I do believe they'll do something cool with it; it's not like they didn't choose to do it themselves, and the bronies can't be the only ones to recognize background characters. I am looking forward to it, but I'm trying not to get too excited over a single episode. It'll be cool to see what they make of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:24:54-07:00","id":451244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=445580#post445580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, man. I was just going to get Netflix too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's still up, actually. For now, anyway. Maybe they worked out a deal, after all, or gave another extension?<br /> <br /> Either way, NF is WELL worth it, even without Ponies! To quote Ferris, it's so choice...If you have the means, I highly recommend it!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am looking forward to it, but I do wonder how it'll work out. I remember in S3 when I said that the one thing I really hoped for was a rematch between Twilight and Trixie. And then we got it. And it was one of the worst episodes in the season for me right then. Looking back at it, it's probably not that bad, but the problem was that I had this great idea of how it would look and the episode wasn't <i>that</i> idea. </div> </div> </div>In that it didn't end with the two of them making out? Yeah, I feel ya...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do believe they'll do something cool with it; it's not like they didn't choose to do it themselves, and the bronies can't be the only ones to recognize background characters. I am looking forward to it, but I'm trying not to get too excited over a single episode. It'll be cool to see what they make of it. </div> </div> </div>Anypony in particular you think should be highlighted?<br /> <br /> On another note, the comics are doing something VERY interesting with <a href=\"http://www.idwpublishing.com/first-little-pony-mini-series-event-little-pony-fiendship-magic/\" target=\"_blank\">Fiendship is Magic</a> (not a typo)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T00:28:31-07:00","id":451355,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd like to see some focus on Octavia. I think her relationship with Vinyl Scratch would make a good show foundation. By that I don't necessarily mean their relationship as the bronies have defined it, either, but it's hard to deny the possibility of a creative episode with a friendship lesson at the end stemming from those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:53:24-07:00","id":451997,"title":"","content":"It's weird, considering how I felt the last season started turning into a significant improvement, but I feel very ambivalent towards the next season. I'm not saying I want it to end, but considering it looks like it might be wrapping up some arcs, I'm not sure I'd object to this being the last season.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just have a much cooler relationship with the series now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T15:32:32-07:00","id":452057,"title":"","content":"I would say that I wouldn't have minded it ending last season. It was strong enough to argue a &quot;quit while you're ahead&quot; situation. Of course, Hasbro would never let that happen. I don't think this show will die a graceful death, unfortunately: it's way too successful to not milk, and doesn't have enough cultural clout to make it an outrage if it overstays its welcome a few seasons.<br /> <br /> I'm personally less into the brony community than I was for a while, but I'm still rather hype for the new season. Barring the S1 finale, each finale has properly managed to introduce something new into the series for the next season to feel fresh, and (importantly) always managed to tie back to that real early on. Given the trailer, it looks like I will be giving the producers my trust once more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:10:18-07:00","id":453233,"title":"","content":"I've never been into the community, my only contact with it is through peripheral threads on forums. I basically pay attention to the new fanart, videos, etc. during a season but once the season ends I drift away until the next rolls round again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:56:56-07:00","id":463755,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/03/season-6-of-mlp-confirmed-in-new.html\" target=\"_blank\">So, as it turns out, MLP is continuing onward. Unless it's a typo.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:14:21-07:00","id":463775,"title":"","content":"Iiiiinteresting. It is a big show, no doubt, but confirming the next season even before the current one has begun seems like, if nothing else, poorly planned timing. Everyone who cares about that will already be hyped for S5 and that lessens the impact. But, I mean, sure, I ain't complainin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:31:23-07:00","id":463883,"title":"","content":"I already did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T02:29:38-07:00","id":468255,"title":"","content":"5.5 hours to pony. I won't catch it live due to work, but I'm pretty excited!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:20:01-07:00","id":468299,"title":"","content":"&quot;This day is going to be just perfect. The kind of day of which I've dreamed since I was small....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:09:33-07:00","id":468450,"title":"","content":"So, This is the best opening arc ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T13:46:05-07:00","id":468731,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E1-2 - The Cutie Map</b> (It seems to be called Cutie Markless on some sites, but The Cutie Map is the name in the videos and on Wikipedia, so I'm going with that.)<br /> <br /> In my comments on the conclusion of the season four finale, I predicted glory days ahead for bronies. Season four had, in my opinion, shown that the post-Faust FiM was not only able to match but in some cases outdo what had come before. Going into this season five premier, I was a little bit worried. Would I have to eat my words?<br /> <br /> The answer is, not yet, that's for damn sure.<br /> <br /> The Cutie Map is a very interesting episode. Compared to many of the previous openers, it's very low-key. Forget about saving the world from eternal night, or primordial chaos, or a whole kingdom's enslavement to a shade-form master of mind magic (and stairs). This time, the stakes are a one-street town, literally on the end of the tracks, with a population of, what, 100 ponies, maybe? The villain they face is no world-ending monstrosity, but simply a pony who use her magic for no other (stated) purpose than wanting to feel like the biggest kid in the school yard.<br /> <br /> The setting is decidedly unconventional, and not only that, but also the mane six's role in it. In all the aforementioned openers, the Elements have been the focus of the show. They (and sometimes Spike) have been the heroes that save the day, the ones to be lauded and honoured with stained glass windows and crystal statues. This time, there is no such grandeur. Half-way through the episode, they are reduced to the same level as everyone else, and they even get their powers back significantly later than every other no-name pony in the village did. Instead, their effects are much more abstract. The mane six represents an alternative to a societal norm, which doesn't have much at all to do with shooting rainbow lasers. Their influence manifests through providing perspectives, and it lets the themes of the episode be so much stronger than it would have been if said rainbow laser had been in commission.<br /> <br /> And what themes we are talking about, too. Equality, uniformity and individuality and the ordering, liberating and disrupting effects of both all to some extent are discussed in the episode. Sure, it's evident that one side is clearly represented by a villain, but on the other hand, through Fluttershy, one of the protagonists shows that parts of the doctrine of uniformity exists in her as well, which I found absolutely fascinating (not to mention super clean character writing). If they will indeed spend a few more episodes in the village, as the ending scene kind of implied, I would <i>love</i> to see an aftermath scenario where the village ponies learn to embrace their re-won talents once more, and possibly incorporate any beneficial parts of Starlight Shimmer's doctrine that they may have learned, to show that people grow through their experiences and come out stronger through plurality and diversity. If I dare dream, that is.<br /> <br /> This episode doesn't overload my senses with awesome like Twilight's Kingdom. It's hard to say it's perfect, full points, tenouttaten. Instead, and that's much more interesting, it rather demands other points of comparison. If this is a taste of the direction the show is going in, then I can see a super interesting, but probably also polarising, time as we move ahead in season five.<br /> <br /> For now, though, I stand by my assessment from last year. Glory days, bronies. Glory days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spoiler: some running thoughts I kept during the viewing, included just for fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">E1<br /> <br /> New season! Yay! I can't wait to see how OH WOW isn't that a convenient magical map plot device that was just summoned now for no apparent reason and is immediately accepted without question?<br /> <br /> In this scene: Spike is a boy.<br /> <br /> MY LITTLE PONY *sings* New shot of the castle in the background. Product placement never fails to deliver.<br /> <br /> Anyone else getting a slightly familiar feeling about this episode? The heroes are given a quest through convenient means, they go where they are told and, upon arriving, expect danger and decide to investigate by chatting with the locals? Is this actually just a session log from McCarthy's D&amp;D game?<br /> <br /> Twilight Sparkle, Sunset Shimmer, Starlight Glimmer... they like that theme, huh.<br /> <br /> Speaking of theme, In Our Town is a really effective song for getting the theme of the episode across. It's actually a pretty interesting way of contrasting equality and uniformity, which are important concepts in society today. I like where this is going.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's slightly lost on account of Starlight Glimmer obviously being a villain. But still.<br /> <br /> &quot;No wonder nopony's wearing anything!&quot; - Rarity 2015<br /> <br /> Sugar Belle is cute and confused. Unfortunate when your ideology doesn't line up with observed facts, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Poor Pinkie. The baker's worst torture.<br /> <br /> The Cutie Mark Vault: the world's biggest iPhone.<br /> <br /> When Starlight Glimmer is talking about the great mage Metalbrook (is that right?), there's a second when Twilight looks away and her eyes dart a little bit. I love those frames. It's evident that she's searching her memory for something, but they could have done that with her just looking away. The eye flicker is such a beautiful detail.<br /> <br /> Wait, it just struck me. Didn't Tirek remove the Cutie Marks when he stole all the magic? Twilight should have known that, right?<br /> <br /> E2<br /> <br /> So Fluttershy is a pretty interesting border case. The non-confrontationalism that the town represents kind of plays into her personality, and it ultimately does represent a form of kindness. I like that one of the mane six seems to gravitate slightly towards it, as it gives it a bit more ambiguity. Here's wondering is Flutters can take the heat of being undercover, though.<br /> <br /> Apathy Pinkie is awesome. That is all.<br /> <br /> Bottled Cutie Marks. Buy 'em in six-packs. It'll be the new coke.<br /> <br /> Wow, Starlight. One pony with a Cutie Mark would destroy your entire philosophy? That's not a very rigid ideological framework you got there.<br /> <br /> Woah. Action Fluttershy there. Damn, girl.<br /> <br /> Starlight is so in for it. Good lord.<br /> <br /> The last part of the episode is frankly great. I love that they're putting in the villagers as the active parties. By keeping the mane six's influence on the ideological plane, they don't come off as the big saviours as much. It also relates that the only ones who can break a societal norm are ultimately the people of the society.<br /> <br /> &quot;My butt is glowing! My mission is accomplished!&quot;<br /> <br /> Wait, does that ending mean that they will stay in the village for a few episodes? That would be great! I would love to see Pinkie and that balloon pony together. :3</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-04-2015, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T13:51:54-07:00","id":468734,"title":"","content":"I know, right?<br /> <br /> It's like the show is about showing the power of friendship for once, instead of just using friendship as an empty glass case for action.<br /> <br /> Oh hey, metaphors extend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:55:30-07:00","id":468830,"title":"","content":"Did...did I just watch a cartoon in which pink and purple ponies play around within a communist conformist nightmare state against their express will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:16:35-07:00","id":468839,"title":"","content":"Not sure where you're getting communist from, really. Communism is tied closely to socioeconomics, and in this episode we saw no evidence of the economic system (other than that everyone must be equally bad at their jobs and make crappy stuff, which is rather on collision course with the Marxist ideas that communism often builds on). Not to mention that a &quot;communist state&quot; is a bit of a contradiction as communism dictates statelessness (fun fact: none of the states commonly referred to as &quot;communist&quot; actually achieved communism as a direct result).<br /> <br /> I think it's more aptly read as a comment on the nationalist and fascist tendencies growing in Europe.<br /> <br /> Edit: But yeah, I agree that it's a pretty impressive subject matter for a pink and purple pony show, no matter how you read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-04-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:18:07-07:00","id":468840,"title":"","content":"Certain parts of America too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:29:09-07:00","id":468869,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a big problem. Which is why it's double cool that a kids show introduces it to a younger audience implicitly through an awesome television show, in my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T00:28:15-07:00","id":469235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=468839#post468839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure where you're getting communist from, really. Communism is tied closely to socioeconomics, and in this episode we saw no evidence of the economic system (other than that everyone must be equally bad at their jobs and make crappy stuff, which is rather on collision course with the Marxist ideas that communism often builds on). Not to mention that a &quot;communist state&quot; is a bit of a contradiction as communism dictates statelessness (fun fact: none of the states commonly referred to as &quot;communist&quot; actually achieved communism as a direct result).<br /> <br /> I think it's more aptly read as a comment on the nationalist and fascist tendencies growing in Europe.<br /> <br /> Edit: But yeah, I agree that it's a pretty impressive subject matter for a pink and purple pony show, no matter how you read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing the connection to Animal Farm? We're all equal, except some are more equal than others. With Animal Farm being allegorical for the Stalinist revolution in Russia.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Stalinism would have been better a word than Communism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T11:55:30-07:00","id":469492,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rexburg,_Idaho\" target=\"_blank\">I just know that they showed the town I'm currently living in.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:57:26-07:00","id":472665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=469492#post469492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rexburg,_Idaho\" target=\"_blank\">I just know that they showed the town I'm currently living in.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't associate that when we were watching it, but too true. Too true....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:35:43-07:00","id":473021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=472665#post472665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't associate that when we were watching it, but too true. Too true....</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, the episode had more in common with cult camps than anything else. I mean, come on, did you notice the hair styles at work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T17:51:03-07:00","id":477395,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E3 - Castle Sweet Castle</b><br /> <br /> Meh, it was okay.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, this episode dealt with something that couldn't really go unaddressed in a well-written show. Changes, particularly traumatic changes, leave marks and it will take time to work through it. Twilight's sense of loss was relatable and the moment when she and Spike stood in front of the ruined Golden Oaks was actually very touching. The moral of the episode, that it's not the material place that makes a home but the memories associated with it, was a good one too. This was an episode that was entirely justified, probably even needed in order for the show to support the fandom's claims that it's more sophisticated than other shows aimed at children.<br /> <br /> But it was also pretty dull. Predictable (doesn't <i>have</i> to be a problem, but it kind of was this time), not super sharp writing on the script nor the song, and the mane six didn't get to play their personalities up properly: with all of them having strong opinions on interior design, Rarity's schtick was kind of invaded, and it's a pretty narrow one to begin with. The possible exception was Pinkie Pie, and she was the one who was responsible for the few times I chuckled. Speaking of them, I was rather confused as to why the character with the most relevance to the subject matter was shipped off at the start and kept out, as a plot point even, until the last few minutes again. The idea of the episode wasn't bad as such, but it would have benefited from Twilight and Spike getting a bigger part of it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, good to see this episode, but it's not a rewatch. Average at best for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-11-2015, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T00:07:10-07:00","id":477623,"title":"","content":"I basically agree with Weimann. I was, however, pleasantly surprised by the fact that the five of them realised they had made a mistake <i>and</i> what their mistake was <i>and</i> how to fix it without the need for Twilight to come back home and essentially tell them they'd done it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:19:33-07:00","id":484631,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E4 - Bloom and Gloom</b><br /> <br /> I caught a stream of this today. Reminder to self: don't do that again. On top of the channel commercials, the stream commercials block out up to half a minute at times.<br /> <br /> In a way, I thought this episode was kind of the reverse of the previous one. The subject matter was rather inconsequential to the show at large, it felt like kind of a stock moral to me and well, I just don't get as hype over Luna as some others do (which doesn't mean I appreciate a stream ad kicking off JUST as she revealed herself...). On the other hand, it was really pretty funny. The dream cycle thing worked for me; I've had those a couple of times and they're scary as shit. Some of the scenes were also pretty funny, like the different Cutie Marks Apple Bloom got towards the end of the cycle. Notice how she got come McDonald's fries? To go with Big Mac? Ehehe... shipping.<br /> <br /> It started out a bit boring, but once they didn't have to hide the premise it picked up speed and in the end I'll have to rate it <i>slightly</i> higher than Castle Sweet Castle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-18-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T10:24:54-07:00","id":484721,"title":"","content":"Well, that episode was a terrible cash in on the &quot;Oh, I hope all the CMC have episodes with Luna&quot; thing of the fandom.<br /> <br /> I place odds on this being the worst episode of the season. This episode was seriously lacking imagination and relevance, and unlike the venerable Wei, I was not moved by the humor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T19:29:41-07:00","id":485020,"title":"","content":"One thing the episode did make me think about was the function and place of cutie marks in the world of Equestria.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, in the first dream, Apple Bloom is shown suddenly getting really good at something she's never even heard of before because she happened to get a cutie mark about it. That's clearly just a representation of a child's fears, as it's shown on multiple occasions, not least in Magical Mystery Cure, that the cute mark isn't a talent lottery that makes you good at some random crap, but instead a representation of the talent you already got. Luna also speaks (somewhat) to that effect towards the end. In fact, it seems like cutie marks can often be quite broad, almost thematic in their application. Cheerilee, for example, has flowers as her cutie mark, which represents her affinity for cultivation, but she applies that affinity to cultivating young minds as a teacher instead of, y'know, flowers. One can even look towards the mane six for this. Rarity's cutie mark isn't about making dresses, it is in fact about finding gems in the ground. However, it can be argued that her talent is as broad as bringing out hidden beauty, which would connect her dress design with her cutie mark.<br /> <br /> It is, however, pretty obvious that the cutie mark has a social dimension as well. The third dream, where Apple Bloom is afraid she won't get an apple-related cutie mark, I could imagine being reality in some cases (not with the Apples, of course, since they are Good Guys, but elsewhere). This could be said to be the case in reality as well, but in Equestria it will be tattooed on your butt, making it very explicit. I can imagine some talents not being super fun to advertise like that. Someone with talents like theft, prostitution or other socially questioned traits would probably wish they'd at least not have to wave it around everywhere. Like, even if you're not <i>actually</i> a thief or prostitute, it's still what you're leaning towards and that open for all to see. I can see families cutting ties with someone because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-18-2015, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:19:17-07:00","id":488709,"title":"","content":"Finally got some free time this week to do more than work, sleep and eat so (after a shower...) I watched the episode (next up, Game of Thrones).<br /> <br /> Errummmuuhhh...meh?<br /> <br /> It was apparent almost immediately it was nothing but a dream sequence so it wasn't going to have any actual relevance to real world events and I will admit I was basically watching it in the hope of seeing Luna do something cool with her 'use darkness and similar negative motifs for good' schtick but aside from just turning up and being wisdomous it was a bit of a dud.<br /> <br /> They may simply be dream creatures but the electrobugs of doom could be some more indication of just how hardcore Equestria is. A swarm of bugs is one pretty terrible thing but a swarm with lightning attacks that can blast a house apart in a single strike is another thing entirely.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that I <b>never</b> remember my dreams (I assume I have them, as everyone supposedly does, I just never remember them) so dream sequence stuff always falls flat for me (which is why I like Luna's current role as she is obviously physically manifest, doing physical tangible things in the real world but also somehow able to be present in dreams as a manifest entity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 04-22-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T03:41:27-07:00","id":489205,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think thd CMCs cutie mark search has orn thin, nd the need to uyst have them get theirs already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T04:32:08-07:00","id":489284,"title":"","content":"The CMC has their moments, but they're certainly one trick ponies (I am just the funniest person alive) in the plot point regard. Fluttershy is also kind of monotone, but when she's not the main focus she can at least be nuanced. The CMC, unlike Fluttershy, rarely show up when it's not primarily about them, but when they do, it's often their best performances. Example: Sleepless in Ponyville, Pinkie Apple Pie.<br /> <br /> Giving them cutie marks would give them a new basis to work with, so that might shake it up for a bit, but I feel like the monofocus would shift from getting them to whatever task they seem to represent. Development needs to come from something else than ditching one all-overshadowing schtick for another. That said, it does just seem to be about time soon, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:20:21-07:00","id":489439,"title":"","content":"I've been watching the new season approximately as it comes out. I've not had much to say so far; I like it well enough, the opening two-parter was pretty good as these things go (the premise it sets up looks like it might be interesting, and the plot had a nice ring to it) and I thought it was nice to address how Twilight's home was destroyed.<br /> <br /> This latest episode though... I just have to have a word about how dull it is.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not the worst episode in the series, but at least those ones left an impression of some sort. This one just meanders around for the first half going through the motions of its obvious dream set-up (so obvious that it feels weird that they try to play up some things for tension when it's clear that they're not real). It doesn't even really manage to do anything interesting with it; the whole Apple family rejection scene is kind of surreal, but is really so disconnected that it's not very provocative. And its surreality isn't even very interesting when it comes down to it, just basic &quot;switch around voices and have them state Apple Bloom's already clearly stated fears&quot;. The whole shadow thing wasn't very interesting for similar reasons; it's barely there and barely does anything (and the acting for it is honestly pretty wooden) so the payoff doesn't really mean much.<br /> <br /> I see Luna show up in the episode, and I get the feeling she's less there to guide a troubled soul through a nightmare and more that she's about as ready for the episode to end as I am.<br /> <br /> And the parts with Sweetie Belle and Scootaloo... they've got some interesting implications in the idea that, deep down, those two actually recognise what their talents are, and fear the possibility of them being taken away from them, things that seem as though they could make a more substantive plot to this kind of episode, but it's kind of revealed a weakness in the character of Apple Bloom as a whole.<br /> <br /> I tend to like Apple Bloom a fair bit, and at worst I don't usually mind Cutie Mark Crusader episodes, but this episode has made it fairly apparent that Apple Bloom has basically nothing else besides Cutie Mark anxiety going on when she's not part of a group. I mean, not just in terms of hinting at what her talent might actually be (the show having never really followed up on the carpentry and construction stuff suggested in The Show Stoppers the way it has for Sweetie Belle's singing and Scootaloo's athleticism), but also an apparent lack of traits with which to give her stories on her own, the way Sweetie Belle has tensions with her sister or Scootaloo has a desire for an idol or problems with her wings. When she's not an ensemble or satellite character, it's always just some variation of &quot;is more sad about Cutie Mark issues than her friends, has some unpleasant encounter as a result, learns a valuable lesson&quot;, and it's been going on so long now that it's becoming hard to get past the marked lack of other traits.<br /> <br /> I mean, no wonder she's worried about her Cutie Mark; <i>I</i> sure as hell can't tell what her traits or talents are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> If they're going to keep coming back to this well, I really think some adjustments need to be made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:54:30-07:00","id":489531,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure Apple Bloom built the CMC's treehouse so I think carpentry is her talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:26:53-07:00","id":489777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=489531#post489531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure Apple Bloom built the CMC's treehouse so I think carpentry is her talent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to belong to Applejack, but when she handed it over to the CMC, Apple Bloom had to fix it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:56:17-07:00","id":490063,"title":"","content":"@Levi: Yeah, I feel like the biggest problem is how much it highlighted how little character Applebloom has.<br /> <br /> Well, no-rather how with Applebloom, much like with Applejack in a majority of her episodes, they don't have a proper understanding of her character. She does not have a lot, but she does have some, and those aspects of her character can lead to rich exploration and character expansion, but the writers don't seem to grasp these ideas and so just keep pushing the cutie mark issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:34:50-07:00","id":490084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure Apple Bloom built the CMC's treehouse so I think carpentry is her talent.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have some thoughts on that... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the show having never really followed up on the carpentry and construction stuff suggested in The Show Stoppers</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:05:44-07:00","id":490275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=490084#post490084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have some thoughts on that...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did they follow up on Sweetie Belle or Scootaloo? I don't remember them really getting much more on the CMark front development either? Unless I supose the brief dream sequences this episode, but that's not so much development as reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:14:56-07:00","id":492278,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E5 - Tanks For Everything</b><br /> <br /> Wow, what a pick-up in an otherwise pretty mellow season start.<br /> <br /> To begin with, the overarching storyline is cute as hell. I love how they show the softer side of Rainbow Dash, which isn't really on display too much, and even then isn't particularly... soft. Casting any other pony in this role would have been much worse, which is perfect as she just happens to be the one with the newest pet as well and it's totally in character for her not to read up about the fiddly details in advance. Then, when she's confronted with this problem, she's just all action, all the time, as usual. Naturally, a plan like stopping winter will fail, but the sequence in Cloudsdale is dynamic and fast-paced and entertaining despite the outcome being known in advance. And in the end, it's Fluttershy who has to step up and give Dashie a reality check, kind of turning around the roles for them from for example Hurricane Fluttershy and also showing continuity form the lesson learned in It Ain't Easy Being Breezies. The characterization of them both in this episode is super well done. The &quot;moral&quot; of the episode isn't so much a moral in its own right, or at least it isn't pointed out as such, which makes it stronger in my opinion. The message is that reality won't change to your fancy, and denying the unavoidable is not a long-term solution. The fact that they show that it's okay to be devastated about something and still accept it's necessity, that crying doesn't show you're weak but that you actually <i>give a damn</i> about something, that's a rock solid message, not only for kids. And the ending is a right heart warmer, too.<br /> <br /> That's all good and all, but beyond that, there are some great minor moments that complements the big story line. The return of the Running of the Leaves, for example, and in general the pony-controlled environment which I've been nagging about not seeing again since season 1. That was a requirement for the plot of the episode, and I'm glad they remember to work with it when they can.<br /> <br /> There's a little problem here, though, because it seems like the show is trying to create some kind of chronological continuity, and that just won't work. Going by Rainbow's comment that this is her and Tank's &quot;first winter together&quot;, it's been less than a year since she got Tank in S2E7 May the Best Pet Win!. Not only would that imply that there's been a whole hell of a lot going on in Ponyville this last summer, but it also flies in the face of S2E11 Hearth's Warming Eve, just four episodes later, which clearly takes place during winter! Now, the episode needed a reason for Rainbow not to know about a turtle's behaviour during winter, so it might just be that. I just hope they're not trying to create chronological continuity in MLP, because that'd be much more jarring than just not caring about it.<br /> <br /> Wow, got sidetracked there. Anyway, the moments like the pegasi doing their &quot;my name is also a descriptor for something else&quot; routine, Twilight pointing out that &quot;winter is coming&quot;, the mutually matching Rainbow and Tank slippers on Tank and Rainbow respectively, and Applejack crying on the inside were, among other things, great ways to enhance the episode.<br /> <br /> This episode was good in the way that I feel has made FiM what it is. Sure, it's great to have big monsters and DBZ combat and other gimmicks at times, but the meat of the show comes from the character-influenced episodes that one by one builds up the image we have of our heroines. I'm very happy with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-26-2015, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:16:22-07:00","id":492280,"title":"","content":"Today was not only one of the most unfunny and contrived episodes I've ever seen, but it is also the single most gutless episode of My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic ever.<br /> <br /> I hate this one more than I hate Mysterious Mare-Do-Well, Spike At Your Service, Magical Mystery Cure, Power Ponies, and Daring Don't. I apologize to Bloom and Gloom, cause this has just taken all the cake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T00:42:40-07:00","id":492407,"title":"","content":"I quite liked it, it was cute (the matching slippers were particularly good) and I think it was trying to get at a difficult topic.<br /> <br /> However I do feel it rather...pulled the punches on a serious topic - namely, what happens when someone important to you leaves your life. From friends moving away at school or you heading out to some new stage in your life. They could have done more with that but cushioned the effect with the knowledge Tank would come back in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T01:06:36-07:00","id":492414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=492280#post492280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today was not only one of the most unfunny and contrived episodes I've ever seen, but it is also the single most gutless episode of My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic ever.<br /> <br /> I hate this one more than I hate Mysterious Mare-Do-Well, Spike At Your Service, Magical Mystery Cure, Power Ponies, and Daring Don't. I apologize to Bloom and Gloom, cause this has just taken all the cake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you really have to develop that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T15:01:46-07:00","id":492939,"title":"","content":"Okie dokey.<br /> <br /> There are Four Factors that make this episode ultimately intolerable, for me anyways. Still, I think it might be more fair to say it hinges on two particular factors, which leads into the third. The fourth one is all me, but we'll get to that(though I imagine it'll become apparent for anyone who reads the other threads quickly). But the combination of the other factors make this the only episode that left me feeling dead, like the episode had taken something from me rather than given something. So, let's go into those factors.<br /> <br /> <b>1)The Premise of the Episode, or Gutlessness</b><br /> <br /> It has already been brought up that the broad theme of this episode is the struggle to cope with someone you care a lot about having to leave, and I can see how people can take and apply it that way, and I don't object to it. That said, the framing of this episode makes it clear that they were going something much more specific.<br /> <br /> They are very much talking about <i>death</i>.<br /> <br /> In particular, they are talking about pet death, but again it can be broadened outward, and again I don't fault anyone for that, but I can see the original artistic intention fairly clearly. This is a subject many kids deal with, and pet death is easier to go into rather than the death of a parent, sibling, or friend, and I think the MLP team decided they wanted to tackle that in some way. And you know what, good for them, this is not only an interesting premise, but it's an important one, and I'd normally praise the team for going that route.<br /> <br /> However, it doesn't take long to see why they didn't go straight for the goal posts there, and I don't blame them for getting gunshy. I described the episode yesterday to a friend as a &quot;Damned if you do, damned if you don't&quot; kind of episode, because the subject matter has no clear answer to succeed without drawing in backlash. It is a heavy subject that can run counter to the mood of the show and upset children. Even if the artists didn't start feeling uncomfortable, executives very definitely would have, and so it has to get pushed off to a close knit metaphor. It's not even a hard transition from a very high perspective. Rainbow Dash, with her anxiety over being left alone, was always going to be the one crushed the most by a separation from their pet, and hibernation is a handy stand in. Shift the details and you're good, right?<br /> <br /> However, even before we get to the second part of this shit, there's too much too dislike about the shift, and so many problems that comes from this decision.<br /> <br /> The biggest one, for me, is that refusal to be bold and to take the audience seriously. If you remember any of my hardcore reviews, you know I prioritize risk-taking and bold messages over playing it safe, and even if this episode scored every note right, it would perpetually annoy me that they aimed low.<br /> <br /> THe second is that by shifting away from a serious subject to a metaphor, <i>in this instance</i>, they weakened the power of the episode, and in fact they damaged the buy-in. This implicitly becomes Rainbow's problem, and it's not necessarily one that everyone can sympathize with, because not everyone has Rainbow's anxiety or has experience with people like her. I know Lesson Zero all about respecting the problems of another person even if we don't understand it, but that episode highlighted the problem here: Tank's coming back, so Rainbow's panicking strikes us as petty(More on that in the second section). On the one hand, we know Rainbow has these issues, on the other hand it seems like a hard thing for the average viewer to take seriously.<br /> <br /> That conflict of what is happening versus what it stands for creates some serious dissonance throughout the episode, in it's moods, in it's ideas, in it's executions. For once, using a metaphor has not soften the subject, but instead made it a slippy, slidy thing that sometimes runs the risk of not being associated at all. Going back to what I said, the episode can broadly stand in for a lot of things,from death to someone moving away for a while. and that broadness works against it because the thematic and emotional strains don't have anything to grab onto.<br /> <br /> There's also a question of continuance. I am going to go on in my assumption of this being a metaphor for pet death, at the least, but allowing for broadness makes further episodes with Tank an interesting question. Parents and other concerned parties who use this episode to help a child with the fact that their friend is moving away is going to run into issues if the meaning of the metaphor is taken as legit and Tank never appears again. But if they are taking the episode seriously as a Metaphor, it's fair if Tank never shows up again, and people who use it to help prepare their kids for pet death will be validated that way, where as if Tank shows up again, this creates the false notion that pets come back from the dead in our lifetimes. Kids pick up on these things, and they subconsciously connect things together, and so things can go really badly either way.<br /> <br /> There's more I can talk about how the gutlessness of their ideas hurt them, but I want to get onto, particularly since this premise will tie into the other sections. Look forward to the words &quot;This is a Dying Animal&quot; ruining things for you.<br /> <br /> <b>2)The Setup of the Episode, or Contrivance</b><br /> <br /> Why hasn't Rainbow Dash dealt with this already?<br /> <br /> Even if we went with the metaphor, this episode could have worked....back in Season 2 before Hearth's Warming Eve. But this is Season <i>5</i>, with tons of implied time passed <i>several times</i> throughout the entire series. Are we really supposed to believe that over the course of years, Rainbow Dash <i>has never once noticed the hibernation patterns of her pet?</i> THe episode tries to deal with this in the most ludicrous fashion possible by suggesting that is their first time together for winter. Even if we assume that the episode they met was set in spring, <i>THEY HAD HEARTH'S WARMING EVE ALREADY.</i> There is <i>clearly</i> a winter before this one. And on top of that, are we really supposed to believe that <i>everything from the Changeling Invasion to Tirek's Conquest happened over the course of a god damned year?</i><br /> <br /> This is just the first, what, minute and a half? And they have already given me questions that make it impossible for me to invest in this episode. The contrivance in play to make this episode happen is utterly <i>absurd</i>. And it only gets <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> And it all could have been solved by having Tank be <i>dying</i>, just saying. The contrivance of this episode is how I know there's a metaphor at work, because no one bends this far up their ass just to create a semblance of coherence.<br /> <br /> Contrivance is the only way they can make this episode work. Exaggeration is commonly used, and normally I let that slide, but we're dealing with more mature characters now than we were in Season 2, and there are people who have experience on these things. So, without further ado, some things I just don't buy in. Asides from everything I've already brought up.<br /> <br /> A) I buy into Rainbow Dash freaking out over Tank hibernating, and if this were Season 2, and I'd even buy into just about everything else she does from here, but Season 5 Rainbow Dash is more mature, a little calmer, a little more open. Yes, she'd freak out for a time, but the excesses she reacts with are nuts for this girl, such as<br /> <br /> B) Not taking Fluttershy seriously-and further, not taking Spike taking Fluttershy seriously seriously(Not a typo). She knows her friend is the supreme expert on animals, and while denial/anger/bargaining/depression will happen before acceptance, I can't, for a second, believe that her denial takes her as far as it does. I'll allow up to Spike, but at that point, the insanity goes too far<br /> <br /> C) That the ponies didn't do more to stop her and help her. Look, these guys have lassoed her to the ground and made her listen to reason until she finally came in contact with her emotions. They have done it in various ways throughout the entire series, and I know they are more observant than that. Honestly, Fluttershy probably raised the alarm as soon as Rainbow left her cottage. BUT THAT DIDN'T HAPPEN.<br /> <br /> D) That Rainbow thought she could have stopped winter. Look, Rainbow is more capable than most ponies, I admit that. There's a reason they have to wrestle her down. Rainbow Dash is a god-damned superhero, and the only thing that stops her from being such is the fact that some of her superhero traits are more commonly shared, but in the end Rainbow is a tough pony to stop. But I think her anger/bargaining state should have died when she confronted the hell out of the weather team with all of her wiles and power and <i>still failed</i>. Nevermind going to the source, you spend all that time going and you fail, you fucking switch to despair.<br /> <br /> There's a lot more, but these are some of the big movers in the episode, and I think it's easy to see that we're still playing with a Rainbow Dash and other Mane Six we quite frankly don't even have anymore. No one does anything they would, nothing happens the way it should. This episode is shoved out, not carefully weaved together.<br /> <br /> But, uh ,Kubler-Ross Model at work in this episode, so....not worth anything, no, I'm not giving points here.<br /> <br /> <b>3)The Execution of the Episode, or Failed Humor</b><br /> <br /> Let's create a series of thoughts to repeat.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a dying animal.&quot;<br /> &quot;This wouldn't happen.&quot;<br /> &quot;Is this supposed to make me laugh?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, concession-there are images that, completely out of context, are probably fucking hilarious. I know Rainbow made some marvelous faces in this episode, and I imagine I'll enjoy them for a day before the internet overdoes it.<br /> <br /> But in context? I find myself repeating those three statements <i>a lot</i>. And really, that's not what's supposed to happen.<br /> <br /> I don't want to say humor doesn't have a place in this sort of topic. I know for a fact it does. In fact, you <i>need</i> humor to make an episode like this work. So, the problem is not that they went for a laugh, but rather that the things they did were not funny in the context of the larger frame. THey might have been fine on their own-in fact, I know a lot of them <i>are</i> fine on their own, but the Premise and the Setup is so damn terrible that it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Two stand out points for me? One is a moment where Rainbow is racing off to save Tank from hibernation, and Tank gets knocked off of something. Make that <i>any time</i> this moment happens, because it happens a lot. The other is when Rainbow is yelling at the ponies. <br /> <br /> The first one is, actually, really funny, because it really fits with Rainbow's personality. Let's be honest about a pony who got a pet out of resentment towards everyone else having one and a disdain for not being involved, she's probably not the greatest owner. I'm not saying she's a bad owner, but her banging Tank against the door on the way out is totally within character, and it's funny within the cartoon realm of violence.<br /> <br /> But then I suffer the thought &quot;This is a dying animal&quot; and I can't laugh. I just can't. It stops being funny and just emphasizes that Rainbow is a bad owner, which she isn't(not the greatest, but not bad). She is slamming her dying pet around and I'm supposed to laugh. And I can't, because Rainbow, at her most extreme in a situation like this, would be babying that god-damned tortoise worse than out-of-character Applejack ever does Applebloom(AHEM). And you juxtapose this with how much damn work she does to make summer happen, it's jarring. So the entire time, I'm just thinking &quot;This wouldn't happen&quot; and &quot;This is a dying animal&quot; ,and nothing can stand to those thoughts. And it happens a lot.<br /> <br /> The second one? Am I supposed to laugh? I am supposed to find Rainbow's level of denial and frustration and grief funny, that she has to yell at the ponies about how she's not angry? Out of context, it's hilarious, because contradiction is a great source of humor, but the emotion is too real in context for me to laugh. It's too visceral-hell, it's too real.<br /> <br /> THose are the ones where it stands out, but the episode is laden with a multitude of these sorts of scenarios that make it just not work for me. By the time I get to the ending which <i>should</i> be getting me all weepy, even through the metaphor, I feel nothing but dead inside.<br /> <br /> The song also was a fucking mood whiplash. I realize that humor and lightheartedness goes far in this sort of discussion, but given how damn desperate Rainbow is, the song is too happy and cheerful to satisfy, and it's lyrics are perhaps the dullest put in the show yet, which is weird how sharp this show can get with its' music at times. I was probably supposed to get swept up in Rainbows' misguided but noble struggle to stop winter, but that didn't happen because the emotion was utterly false.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the ending is the best part of this episode, and if I divorced it from the rest of the episode, the little fun touches added to the somber scenes would make for a nice, warm, bittersweet experience, which are my favorite kind of experiences, but as I mentioned, by the time I got there the elements of the show have shorn off my ability to care, because nothing is connected to anything meaningful.<br /> <br /> <b>0)The Audience of the Episode, or My Personal Issues</b><br /> <br /> Despite indulging in some flavor, I have tried to keep this within an appropriate realm of academic criticism, because I think this episode is bad as a piece of artwork. However, I'm fairly sure that if you've read this, you'll notice a certain gravity towards a particular interpretation. A large part of that is because it is the thing that makes the most sense in terms of critical analysis and production speculation, but I would be lying if I said I wasn't also biased towards this particular reading because my experiences as of late is probably filtering my experience.<br /> <br /> At the end of February of this year, my dog Tyris passed away. It may seem cliche to say, but for those of you who have not had pets be a big part of your life, let me clarify that I have no problems regarding Tyris as an adopted daughter, and I have taken her death about as hard. I am moving on with my life, but I am very mindful of these sorts of subjects and the emotions that go with them because the experience is still fresh with me. And it's not like this is the first death I've dealt with, my father having died in the late 90s and completely changing my life forever-I would not be who I am today if my father was still alive. Despite my considering this to be a predominantly good thing, the reflection on my father's death in the wake of my daughter's death has made me aware of just how much these sort of things affect a person.<br /> <br /> So when I reached the end of the episode, I did have to ask a question, not just &quot;Would this help a person cope with loss?&quot; but &quot;If I had gotten this episode the Saturday I had to put my daughter down, would it have helped, done nothing for, or hurt what was happening?&quot; There is no clear answer to that question. I don't think there can be for me now. But as it stands now, I felt like the episode spent most of it's time stumbling and inadvertently making light of something that mattered to me, and I have the suspicion that it would have evoked a more violent reaction from me then. Then again, I might have forgiven it's flaws in its' attempt to reach out for me, I can concede that. All I know is that I feel talked down to now.<br /> <br /> I bring this up as a concession, an admittance of bias. But the point of this allowance is to explain why I personally hate it, not to admit that it might be good. I still, as objectively as I can, think that this episode is at least <i>bad</i>, that it should be on people's bad list. I think it really badly of this episode, but I am conceding that some of it might be because of the experience. This is why it's point zero. It is only a valid point for me, where as the other three, in concert, still make the case.<br /> <br /> <b>In Conclusion, or This Episode is Really Bad You Guys</b><br /> <br /> So despite the concession, I still think the episode is apparently bad. It all feels forced and fabricated, which wouldn't be half the case if the subject matter shifted over to a highly prominent and likely interpretation-so likely it was probably the original intended message. THe entire delivery of the episode on the whole is just incompetent, an oil slick sliding all over the place on top of an ocean of good ideas.<br /> <br /> The worst part is that this episode could have been so good. This could have been <i>the episode of the season</i>, the one where critics all over talk about it busting ground and delivering a thoroughly satisfying and gutsy message. But they went and played it so safe that it became less than bland and actual becoming uncaring of the audience's emotions. <i>It talked down to the audience</i>.<br /> <br /> If you think this episode was good, I dunno what to say. I suppose if you turn off a lot and just let it go, it works. But as an academic, it has poor structure and a dead heart, and all that's left is an atrophied husk of a script. Heaven forbid what happens when I think about is as someone who went through the experience.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, I don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T01:41:38-07:00","id":493377,"title":"","content":"That was an interesting read, Arcane. I can respect that criticism. I want to make a little point about what you say towards the end in your post, but in doing so, I will also reply to the fullness of it.<br /> <br /> I think the big difference between my and your interpretation is your &quot;point 0&quot;. I personally don't have any kids nor pets, the latter of which I'm never looking to acquire either, so my impressions of the episode didn't focus as much on Tank in his own right, as a living, feeling entity. I objectified Tank while you subjectified him; I saw him as an important but ultimately interchangeable &quot;thing that Rainbow Dash really loves&quot; and you saw him as a character. This made me focus more on Rainbow Dash's reaction than on Tank's situation, and the point of the episode became about dealing with the things in life you can't change and not being afraid to show emotions about them, rather than pet loss, or more specifically death, in particular.<br /> <br /> This means that for me, point 1 wasn't a problem, because the episode wasn't about the death of a pet. It was about Rainbow Dash dealing with wanting something she can't have. For me, hibernation was just that, and Tank will be back in a couple months.<br /> <br /> Point 2 I will give you. The idea that it's been no winter since Rainbow Dash got Tank is a stretch, and that particular issue could have been solved if the episode was explicitly about death instead of hibernation. For me, though, it's more an issue of inter-seasonal continuity rather than something that affects this particular episode. It's been long established that the timelines in FiM is handwavey at best. However, yeah, there is in fact explicit evidence that Hearth Warming Eve must occur before Tanks for the Memories because the evidence is right on Twilight's back - she does not have her wings in Hearth Warming Eve. Hearth Warming Eve might admittedly have taken place before May the Best Pet Win!, however.<br /> <br /> Point 3, I feel, again comes from the assumption that it's a metaphor for death, so for me, the mood whiplash wasn't as bad. I'm also easy to entertain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The point of going through all that, though, is to reply to a few lines you have in your point 0 at the end, where you divulge your own background in relation to your interpretation.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I bring this up as a concession, an admittance of bias. [...] I still, as objectively as I can, think that this episode is at least <i>bad</i>, that it should be on people's bad list. [...] I am conceding that some of it might be because of the experience. This is why it's point zero. It is only a valid point for me, where as the other three, in concert, still make the case.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the order in which I replied to your points, you will note that point 0, which you put last, is first in my list. That is because all the differences in our interpretation and evaluation of the episode stems from that point. You say it's an admittance to bias, a concession that you're letting your mind be influenced by unrelated things. I say that the only way to make value judgements about art is to base those judgements in a context. In this case, it's your personal context, and that context is an entirely valid one. Sure, the more closely we tie our interpretations to the material we're critiquing, the more we build up our argument with causal links between events and characters and don't just go &quot;well, I think that...&quot;, the easier it will be for people to accept our interpretation. But it will still be a subjective piece, based in a context that some people might not have and which they will therefore challenge with their own interpretation. There can be no objectivity. And that's okay.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this to try and undermine your interpretation. I just wanted to say that your experience is a worthwhile foundation for your opinions, and that our differing opinion doesn't inherently invalidate either of our perspectives. In fact, the whole point of criticism could be said to find those differences, so that we can mine the work for more meaning. And I think we have done a good job of that here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-27-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T01:56:40-07:00","id":493383,"title":"","content":"I think that above crystallizes something I felt uncomfortable with but couldn't really place.<br /> <br /> The way Tank is treated throughout.<br /> <br /> Now, he's (?) a tortoise so fairly damn tough (it's in the name!) but he gets bashed around and forced to do everything that RD wants without even a concession to asking him if he's alright with doing the things that he's forced into doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T08:12:14-07:00","id":493642,"title":"","content":"The thing of the matter is that there is a difference between content and craft, though some can be related quite thoroughly, such as theme. When we make an assertion about the <i>quality</i> of an episode, we have a limitation of what we're talking about before we enter into a realm of subjective taste and it literally being a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> I believe the episode is bad on a craft level, that the presentation does not fulfill the goals and in fact confuses and potentially mocks the ideas that begin the project. I wanted to keep my argument on that and not how I felt like the episode made light of my own experience, which is a very subjective experience. That said, knowing I have those experiences, I couldn't, in good conscience, tear the episode apart without admitting &quot;Yes, I might be taking this really badly because it deals with a sore subject for me.&quot; I have had a lot of emotionally volatile reaction to my experience with my daughter's death and a lot of thought has gone into it, and all of that means I could just hate the episode for reasons that actually don't actually reflect on the quality of it. When you're taking a driving test, you should admit to potential tiredness influencing your driving, same difference.<br /> <br /> It <i>is </i>part of the experience. It's valuable for analysis, perspective, and interpretation-but it's not so great for quality assessment in a subject that's already subject to, well, subjectivity. I had to acknowledge that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:23:07-07:00","id":493729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=493642#post493642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing of the matter is that there is a difference between content and craft, though some can be related quite thoroughly, such as theme. When we make an assertion about the <i>quality</i> of an episode, we have a limitation of what we're talking about before we enter into a realm of subjective taste and it literally being a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> I believe the episode is bad on a craft level, that the presentation does not fulfill the goals and in fact confuses and potentially mocks the ideas that begin the project. I wanted to keep my argument on that and not how I felt like the episode made light of my own experience, which is a very subjective experience. That said, knowing I have those experiences, I couldn't, in good conscience, tear the episode apart without admitting &quot;Yes, I might be taking this really badly because it deals with a sore subject for me.&quot; I have had a lot of emotionally volatile reaction to my experience with my daughter's death and a lot of thought has gone into it, and all of that means I could just hate the episode for reasons that actually don't actually reflect on the quality of it. When you're taking a driving test, you should admit to potential tiredness influencing your driving, same difference.<br /> <br /> It <i>is </i>part of the experience. It's valuable for analysis, perspective, and interpretation-but it's not so great for quality assessment in a subject that's already subject to, well, subjectivity. I had to acknowledge that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, it's absolutely correct of you to acknowledge your basis of perspective. I also agree that your critique of the &quot;craft&quot; of the episode might not be (fully) based in that same perspective.<br /> <br /> However, I disagree that it's therefore objective. When you make a value judgement about anything, you're always already in a subjective realm. If you call the craft of the episode &quot;bad&quot; (or &quot;good&quot;, for that matter), then there you go: that is a subjective statement. Why? Because you can only call something good or bad in relation to a context. You say that you think the &quot;craft&quot; of the episode is &quot;bad&quot; because it &quot;does not fulfill the goals and in fact confuses and potentially mocks the ideas that begin the project&quot;. So the value judgement that the craft is bad is related to how well it managed to express the ideas behind the episode. And those ideas are... what? Hard to answer, because they are open to interpretation, which is a subjective activity. You fill them in based on your personal experience, and others might fill them in based on theirs, and so the evaluation of the &quot;craft&quot; is based on different foundations and must also therefore have the potential for different outcomes.<br /> <br /> And to reiterate, that's okay. We don't need objectivity. It's not about finding a right answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-27-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:18:37-07:00","id":493757,"title":"","content":"I didn't much care for the episode either. I only saw an implication of the pet dying thing as a bait-and-switch myself, and was fairly willing to take the animal hibernation thing as unadorned text myself (particularly when I recalled during the credits that hibernation is a thing tortoises do). I was even all ready to take on board a cute story of facing the disappointment of big plans with a friend not really being feasible because the circumstances don't line up, since I've been there.<br /> <br /> My problem with it was the fact that the whole thing felt terribly dragged out and badly paced. Rainbow Dash outlandishly trying to stop winter seemed funny at the start, but it goes on for far too long, and by the point that it escalates to the point where she wants to try going home and smashing a load of equipment it feels like a rehash even apart from how it's such an extreme and selfish action that it greatly saps my sympathy (and then there's a crazy-rushing-around-blasting action set piece that I feel goes back into bad pacing, at the opposite extreme).<br /> <br /> Their &quot;Who's on First&quot; joke was cute enough, at least as something to put in the foreground while Rainbow is stealing clouds, but it still feels like it amounts to a lot of filler.<br /> <br /> And I found the ending (as distinct from the epilogue) to be weird and stilted; even disregarding my lack of sympathy for Rainbow's plight at that point, it all came off as stuttered and unnatural, particularly in terms of which characters were suddenly breaking down in tears with little rhyme or reason (which, again, is something that felt like it was being dragged on to fill time when Rainbow Dash needs to catch a third wind or whatever). Which is a shame, because I actually liked the initial image and framing of her lying dejected in bed and cuddling her tortoise to her (as well as the visual gag of Pinky Pie walking through the wall).<br /> <br /> I guess that last image (as well as my basic good will towards the epilogue, which is past the point of saving the episode for me) summarises my problem with the episode; I feel as though it would have been better served by being more focused on some introversion with the interactions between Rainbow Dash and Tank, a bit of nice expansion on the introduction and all of the subsequent cute little shows of affection between them, a nice little opening of her shell, but instead it goes for extroversion in a form that is loud and escalating and obnoxious. I don't find somebody destructively flailing about in futility over an undesirable circumstance to be particularly funny or compelling.<br /> <br /> I also found that &quot;winter is coming&quot; line to be distracting and pandering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:16:28-07:00","id":494289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=493757#post493757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also found that &quot;winter is coming&quot; line to be distracting and pandering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very nearly stopped watching at that line. Ironically, it's one of the least of things for this episode, not even related to what I brought up, but god damn I just-man, that joke was just phoned in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T22:13:21-07:00","id":494409,"title":"","content":"Man, I thought it was cute. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:42:30-07:00","id":500495,"title":"","content":"If the CMC are ever going to get their cutie marks, I predict it will be near the end of this season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:02:25-07:00","id":502148,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E6 - Appleoosa's Most Wanted</b><br /> <br /> Headache. Will keep it brief.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I think we spotted the arc of this season. I can get behind a storyline developing the CMC with a possible culmination in cutie mark acquisition.<br /> <br /> This episode felt like fresh air for the CMC. Most often, they tend to solve problems relating to themselves, or even problems they have themselves caused. This time, they actually did something for someone else. I'm not saying the one is better than the other, but one is certainly rarer, which does lend it more weight. I also like the implication that there will be some discussion regarding cutie marks throughout the season, and if they tie that the CMC, I can see that working.<br /> <br /> Most of the enjoyment came from seeing the CMC doing something different, but I also thought Applejack was written really tightly here. All of her actions were right in character, and she had some really nice animation too. All of Appleloosa was a pretty neat background as well, kind of looking like what we foreigners think Texas is like, I guess. I liked it.<br /> <br /> Troubleshoes... I can take or leave. He served his purpose.<br /> <br /> No real complaints, no super highlights. Good show. While the previous episode obviously had some range in its reception, I persoanlly feel like the season is picking up after an initial lull.<br /> <br /> No pony next week, though. Sadface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:53:06-07:00","id":502983,"title":"","content":"I thought CMarks weren't an absolute statement of what you could do? His CMark seems to make him essentially a danger to himself and everyone around him leaving him with only options for...well...slapstick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:19:00-07:00","id":502993,"title":"","content":"Cutie marks are certainly not absolute statements. If they were, Troubleshoe's mark would say &quot;rodeo clown&quot; straight up.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not the mark that made him clumsy; it was his clumsiness that gave him the mark. He'd still be clumsy even if he got another cutie mark. See Derpy (who <i>is</i> canon as being clumsy) for example.<br /> <br /> That said, having that clumsiness as your <i>special talent</i> does have to suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:30:15-07:00","id":514772,"title":"","content":"Since there was no new ep this week, I went and finally got the final issue of the &quot;Reflections&quot; storyline in the comic (pages of which I posted in this thread a couple pages back). <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-FD8_CEhOeO4/U5Z4cYqIutI/AAAAAAABzr0/ogrsNf53Xs4/s1600/unnamed.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">After checking in on a cute scene with Celestia and Luna,</a> we get to see what Evil Celestia and Evil Luna have been up to:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://41.media.tumblr.com/554983f77634b6c287bb1370f7789bea/tumblr_n5s22uYvSy1tbieaco1_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> They have a meeting with our heroes...<br /> <img src=\"http://fdzeta.com/subir/images/QCwl8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Oh Snap! Evil Celestia makes her move!<br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-morGrL-SxNM/U6MWO9kKibI/AAAAAAAB0LA/Iw3XyPx9We8/s1600/6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Gotta love Princess Celestia's Battle Form!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-IMzk-W0QeFA/U6MWNrPK3qI/AAAAAAAB0K0/kSudD0ZiScU/s1600/3.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> is anyone else here still keeping up with the comic and its spin-offs?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:55:23-07:00","id":514788,"title":"","content":"Quick question: what's the usual lag time between Hub Network and Netflix? I have access to the latter (on a free trial that ends in a little under a month), but I don't have access to the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T23:52:57-07:00","id":514857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=514772#post514772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is anyone else here still keeping up with the comic and its spin-offs?</div> </div> </div> </div>No...but apparently I should be. (kind of a lie, I used to but when they did a big time skip in an X-Men series I was reading so the characters were essentially different people I got annoyed and stopped buying comics)<br /> <br /> To Comixology...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T03:34:01-07:00","id":514931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=514772#post514772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is anyone else here still keeping up with the comic and its spin-offs?</div> </div> </div> </div> I haven't had a chance to read the comics, but I've been reading up on Fiendship is Magic recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T04:05:18-07:00","id":514949,"title":"","content":"The comics are something I've always thought might be cool, and I've heard good things about them. For some reason I've never actually gotten around to acquiring them however. I suppose I'm saving up a backlog for a binge at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:50:01-07:00","id":516250,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E7 - Make New Friends but Keep Discord</b><br /> <br /> I mean, it's Discord, right? I've never seen a brony who actually dislikes Discord as a character. Sure, some may dislike how he's been handled, but I've never seen his basic idea or personality complained about. So this episode already has that going for it.<br /> <br /> The other thing the episode has going for it right from the start? It was written by Natasha Levinger, who also wrote Pinkie Apple Pie, one of my absolute top episodes in terms of comedy quality.<br /> <br /> And good heavens, does she deliver.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the episode is hilarious. I was laughing to myself almost the whole time, which admittedly is standard when Discord is around, and he was all the time this episode. But the rest of the cast kept up; Maud's dead-pan joke in particular slayed me.<br /> <br /> Secondly, do you see how many <i>seeds</i> are in this episode? We have the second Grand Galloping Gala (continuity!). We have the CMC going to the GGG for the first time with their new outfits. We have Discord's home realm. We have two entirely new characters, Tree Hugger and the Smooze. I was sceptical about Tree Hugger at first, because she seemed like a stereotype hippie (and I mean, she blatantly is, her name is <i>Tree Hugger</i>), but she was actually pleasant and entertaining and it wasn't like she was going to get much room for character development either way, so a strong personality statement from the start was probably needed. Better that than a shapeless blob of a background pony. And through that <i>INCREDIBLE</i> segway, the Smooze. I was legitimately surprised they introduced him in this way. From what I heard, in G1, he was a big villain. That said, I had no expectations either and I don't hate him here, even if I felt he had less of a presence than Tree Hugger. Bottom line, though, there is a wealth of material for the fandom to work with here, and that means that new and exciting shit happened, and I'm happy about that.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, beyond all the comedy and such, doesn't the story feel very, very real? I've sometimes joined the chorus of people complaining that Discord's redemption was very quick and easy for a centuries old spirit of chaos, and while we have seen him relapse a few times and come back around, it has never been seen from his point of view. We have never seen him work with it on his own before, and that is just what we see here: someone discovering a new facet of friendship that they didn't consider before. It lends credibility to the Discord story arc.<br /> <br /> Levinger's writing has a certain style to it. It's snappy and quick and doesn't worry about explicitly recapping the plot quite as much as some other writers do. There's bite in it, and it doesn't pay too much reverence to the characters but dares to push them further; for example, I don't think I've ever seen Celestia laugh as much as in this episode (but she still can't cast spells worth a damn &gt;.&lt;). Basically, she trusts her audience to get on her level, and I think that not only does wonders for their quality but also adheres to Faust's original vision of a show that didn't talk down to an audience that's usually talked down to.<br /> <br /> In my book, this episode nails just about every aspect I can ask for. Tenouttaten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 05-16-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T00:52:49-07:00","id":516851,"title":"","content":"Pinkie and Maud had the best lines throughout. I kind of agree that it's necessary for Discord but...is Discord necessary for us? He keeps on turning up in places but he doesn't seem to be contributing much overall. We've spent quite a lot of time this season <i>not</i> with the main six and I'm starting to feel that we should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:31:44-07:00","id":517240,"title":"","content":"Mmm, I think Discord contributes his part, at least as much as any other main character. He provides a more loose cannon personality than the mane six and you're never really quite sure where you got him. He's a bit of variety.<br /> <br /> At first, I was actually inclined to agree with you about the mane six being curiously absent, but when I went back to check, it turns out that the mane six or someone from it has been the focal character(s) of 4 out of 7 episodes so far. In the other episodes, it's not like they've been absent, either. They have been distinctly more low-key, though, which might contribute to the impression. The only one who really went wild was Rainbow Dash in Tanks for the Memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T15:40:29-07:00","id":517380,"title":"","content":"Having rewatched the episode, I think I can pinpoint why I feel Tree Hugger works despite being so stereotypically hippie. She is unfazed by Discord while he gets more and more frustrated with her, and it's not only over her relationship with Fluttershy, but about her as an individual as well. He is the one calling her out on not making any sense. Think about that for a second. Also, towards the end, she makes him lose it and, in an uncharacteristically straight-forward manner, attempts to simply throw her out of the world. That's a power move, and it comes out as desperate from someone who normally does his business through frustration and confusion. His antics doesn't work on her, and that's what makes he work for the show. She essentially makes Discord play her straight man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:58:10-07:00","id":523981,"title":"","content":"Found some things of great interest: One is the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/TheJournalOfTheTwoSisters\" target=\"_blank\">Journal of the Two Sisters</a>, supposedly the actual journal found in the series, full of fleshing out the history of Equestria (according to this, although written by oneof the show's writers, unfortunately they didn't have the writers in the show who handle most of the world building do it). Still, some of the details, like the price unicorns paid to raise the sun and moon, are *chilling*...<br /> <br /> We're just an ep away from <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Recap/MyLittlePonyFriendshipIsMagicS5E9SliceOfLife\" target=\"_blank\">Slice of Life</a>, the 100th episode, with NONE of the Mane Six, but all background ponies. Looks like it has more of a plot than I thought...I have high hopes for this one, and am expecting it to be a high point of the series! Unless the ep titled &quot;Do Princesses Dream of Magic Sheep&quot; lives up to its source material...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/WesternAnimation/MyLittlePonyEquestriaGirlsFriendshipGames\" target=\"_blank\">A new Equestrian Girls Movie</a>, already?? Yep! Hopefully, this one will have the guts to stand without Princess Twilight...not that they won't be enough Twilight to go around anyway, apparently...And in league with the Shadowbolts??<br /> <br /> Gonna be an interesting year for Pony stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T22:12:32-07:00","id":523999,"title":"","content":"In Equestria Girls, we get to see what happened to the Mane Five in a world where they never met Twilight Sparkle; now, it appears that we'll be seeing what happened to Twilight Sparkle in a world where she never met the Mane Five. I've been looking forward to this one ever since the Rainbow Rocks stinger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:03:56-07:00","id":524157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=523981#post523981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found some things of great interest: One is the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/TheJournalOfTheTwoSisters\" target=\"_blank\">Journal of the Two Sisters</a>, supposedly the actual journal found in the series, full of fleshing out the history of Equestria (according to this, although written by oneof the show's writers, unfortunately they didn't have the writers in the show who handle most of the world building do it). Still, some of the details, like the price unicorns paid to raise the sun and moon, are *chilling*...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've yet to properly consume the texts associated with the main show, such as the comics, and I have about the same feeling about this one as I have about them. It's something I probably should read, and which I might even enjoy, but I'm not sure I'm actually going to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=523981#post523981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're just an ep away from <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Recap/MyLittlePonyFriendshipIsMagicS5E9SliceOfLife\" target=\"_blank\">Slice of Life</a>, the 100th episode, with NONE of the Mane Six, but all background ponies. Looks like it has more of a plot than I thought...I have high hopes for this one, and am expecting it to be a high point of the series! Unless the ep titled &quot;Do Princesses Dream of Magic Sheep&quot; lives up to its source material...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Epiode 100 is a blank slate for me. I've no expectations, really, not even sure if I'd like them to do lots of community-based nods or produce new character hooks for the community to latch on to (probably the latter, come to think of it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=523981#post523981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/WesternAnimation/MyLittlePonyEquestriaGirlsFriendshipGames\" target=\"_blank\">A new Equestrian Girls Movie</a>, already?? Yep! Hopefully, this one will have the guts to stand without Princess Twilight...not that they won't be enough Twilight to go around anyway, apparently...And in league with the Shadowbolts??</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is probably the thing in your post I'm most excited about. The first movie was kind of so-so, but the second was actually rather good, even if most of it came from the songs and the villains. I'm curious if they'll be able to keep the quality up when they don't have such a music-themed premise to base it around.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a contained movie where Twilight doesn't cross over from Equestria. After Rainbow Rocks I kind of started thinking about Sunset Shimmer as the Twilight stand-in in the EqG world, but part of the appeal with her is that she's not a copy of Twilight. I'm hoping they'll let the two worlds' main characters be differentiated and not shoehorn a human!Twilight into the group just for symmetry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:44:25-07:00","id":525058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=524157#post524157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've yet to properly consume the texts associated with the main show, such as the comics, and I have about the same feeling about this one as I have about them. It's something I probably should read, and which I might even enjoy, but I'm not sure I'm actually going to.</div> </div> </div> </div>We got a Sunset Shimmer novel at my job; flipping through it, it's clearly set after the 2nd movie, as it has her communicating with Twilight through the diary. Hopefully,we'll get JotTS, in which case, I'll buy it, but I'm not going to seek it out otherwise...probably.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Epiode 100 is a blank slate for me. I've no expectations, really, not even sure if I'd like them to do lots of community-based nods or produce new character hooks for the community to latch on to (probably the latter, come to think of it). </div> </div> </div>This is really the best attitude to approach it with. Esp as they said they'll be going with some fanon but definitely not with others (well, I never expected to see Lyra and Bon Bon openly making out, but I hope they use those names and reaffirm their friendship!).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, this is probably the thing in your post I'm most excited about. The first movie was kind of so-so, but the second was actually rather good, even if most of it came from the songs and the villains. I'm curious if they'll be able to keep the quality up when they don't have such a music-themed premise to base it around.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a contained movie where Twilight doesn't cross over from Equestria. After Rainbow Rocks I kind of started thinking about Sunset Shimmer as the Twilight stand-in in the EqG world, but part of the appeal with her is that she's not a copy of Twilight. I'm hoping they'll let the two worlds' main characters be differentiated and not shoehorn a human!Twilight into the group just for symmetry. </div> </div> </div>Antagonist-Twilight vs. Protagonist-Sunset OR Twilight vs. Twilight both have so much potential, I can't decide which I'm hoping more for! Also, sorry,but the Dazzlings just *made* that movie's music work...NOT looking forward to a soundtrack of nothing but more bland girl-pop...Hopefully, we'll get a good villain song, maybe from the principal of Crystal Prep--ah, wait,that's gonna be Cadence, isn't it?<br /> <br /> I'll actually be shocked if Earth-EG Twi doesn't end up transferring to Canterlot High by the end, regardless...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:46:12-07:00","id":525059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=523999#post523999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Equestria Girls, we get to see what happened to the Mane Five in a world where they never met Twilight Sparkle; now, it appears that we'll be seeing what happened to Twilight Sparkle in a world where she never met the Mane Five.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://www.idolnotes.net/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/It%E2%80%99s-Not-My-Fault-That-I%E2%80%99m-Not-Popular-41-Read-It%E2%80%99s-Not-My-Fault-That-I%E2%80%99m-Not-Popular-41-Online-Page-1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img1.ak.crunchyroll.com/i/spire2/e7eabcaf4b7932eee01d71e5646356b41369958460_full.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">(For those who don't know who this is)</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T13:38:56-07:00","id":527003,"title":"","content":"Now that episode was much more like it! Pinkie on form - Gilda sounded strange though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:36:46-07:00","id":531831,"title":"","content":"Ok, and now a sign of how weird I am, I just had a discussion on another site arguing over the sexual orientations of the Mane Six. Is that too weird? Or par for course with this fandom?<br /> <br /> Oh, sidenote, thought everyone seems to have varied opinions on all, everyone who chimed in thought Rarity was straight....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:41:07-07:00","id":531832,"title":"","content":"It's never really been a relevant part of the show so it;s not come up much that I've seen.<br /> <br /> Though Rarity is one o the few tat we've seen interested in the opposite gender, in that episode where Rarity and AJ fight over who can be the better farmer/dandy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:58:16-07:00","id":531834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=531831#post531831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, and now a sign of how weird I am, I just had a discussion on another site arguing over the sexual orientations of the Mane Six. Is that too weird? Or par for course with this fandom?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually completely normal. Not sure what is says about us as a fandom, but it is normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T09:03:11-07:00","id":531989,"title":"","content":"Wow, I really need to get down to watching that last episode. On the other hand, since the next one is two weeks away still, maybe it's good that I (involuntarily) paced myself this time.<br /> <br /> As for discussing the sexuality of the mane six, seems harmless enough. It's part of what the fanbase is supposed to do, I think; add and expand on the material provided in the show. Sexulaity is a facet of a character that the show will likely never address in earnest, so it falls on the fandom to do it.<br /> <br /> Rarity is in fact one of the few we've seen semi-romantically interested in someone else, namely Trenderhoof in Simple Ways, and he was male. It's mixed up with the hope that he'll write an article about her as well, of course, but I think it's pretty evident that she wouldn't disapprove of a more intimate relationship either.<br /> <br /> Some would probably argue that there's something going between Rarity and Applejack too, and they do have a very special relationship, but I think that's more about how their friendship shapes itself around their very distinct personalities (but they're also very similar; they are easily the two most hard-working ponies of the mane six and they both have little sister, for example). Do I ship it? Maybe a little. :3<br /> <br /> I've not read many shipfics, but most people seem to agree that Rainbow Dash is bi (&quot;Rainbow Dash ships with everyone&quot; was a meme for a bit) or lesbian, probably due to stereotypes relating to her tomboy personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:14:24-07:00","id":533951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=527003#post527003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that episode was much more like it! Pinkie on form - Gilda sounded strange though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Pinkie can be hard to write for...all too often she gets flanderized as &quot;the wacky one&quot;, a character type I normally hate. She's only really interesting to me when her insecurities come up; she hasthe biggest issues of all the Mane Six, but at least they give her *some* depth. She's still my least favorite, but I'd be lying if I said she didn't crack me up every now and then. And this was one of her better eps...Interesting also, that this is the first ep showing how the &quot;mission format&quot; works, with the Map selecting certain ponies to go to certain places. I wonder if all the missions will relate to something/one intheir pasts? <br /> <br /> And it was hilarious seeing Twilights' reaction to not being selected! I didn't realize how much I missed grumpy, snarky Twilight...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arimaspi\" target=\"_blank\">Some interesting points about the real world mythology referenced inthe episode...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:30:11-07:00","id":533957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=531832#post531832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though Rarity is one o the few tat we've seen interested in the opposite gender, in that episode where Rarity and AJ fight over who can be the better farmer/dandy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, waaay back in,like, the third ep with the Prince, so it can't be said that this is some violation of Faust's Vision! Of course, both of those infatuations had the same base, <i>what associating with those guys could do for Rarity's image and prestiege</i>...once her romantic fantasies were shattered, the ease with which she ditched them both could argue that she never really was *attracted* to either.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/2014/4/22/607267/full.gif\" target=\"_blank\">Meanwhile, she and Applejack are practically bursting with UST!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:41:15-07:00","id":533962,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, what's u-<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> This is a weird conversation to walk in on. I'll catch up soon.<br /> <br /> EDIT!<br /> <br /> 1) Griffonstone is actually my favorite episode so far for the season. Lots of really cool character dynamics, good world building, a resolution where friendship and reason <i>actually mean something</i>, yeah, this was a good episode.<br /> <br /> 2) I know there are lots of theories and speculation about the ponies sexuality, but I just don't think there's enough evidence any particular way. That said, I do think Rainbow Dash is actually largely straight with a few exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-31-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:49:36-07:00","id":533968,"title":"","content":"So after, like, TEN weeks, they've <i>finally</i> stopped showing the premiere promo as though it was coming on next week (this never would have happened if it were still the Hub!)...only to tease us with the 100th ep promo for *two weeks*! Why?? Isn't it bad enough that I have to wait so long for Exalted 3rd Edition?! Like Rainbow said, is this some kind of cruel joke??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anywho, the promos look pretty promising (and hold at least one major surprising spoiler):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ya-iHgt04EU\" data-code=\"Ya-iHgt04EU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ya-iHgt04EU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSW7Ave6tcA\" data-code=\"DSW7Ave6tcA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DSW7Ave6tcA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Can't bloody wait!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T21:09:51-07:00","id":533987,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;We're going to celebrate the 100th episode of My Little Pony by showing all your favorite characters who have been sitting un-importantly in the background all of a sudden doing things..&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In any other fandom, I'd be questioning this so much. It still sounds really backwards.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:52:21-07:00","id":534653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=533987#post533987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;We're going to celebrate the 100th episode of My Little Pony by showing all your favorite characters who have been sitting un-importantly in the background all of a sudden doing things..&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In any other fandom, I'd be questioning this so much. It still sounds really backwards.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>When you put it like that, yeah, it does seem strange. :P<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the fandom has been integral in developing those background characters. Remember that at the start, they were literally just filler to make Ponyville seem populated. Names like Lyra, Bonbon, Octavia, Vinyl Scratch, Carrot Top and (naturally) Derpy all came from the fandom. Only recently have the writers started giving new background ponies their own names. Since the fandom were the ones to develop the background ponies into any kind of charcters, it kind of makes sense that an homage might involve them.<br /> <br /> The question is if the show intends to focus on canonizing fan-made aspects of the characters, or if it'll focus on providing new aspects of the characters for the fandom to relate to. I'm kind of hoping the latter, though surely some of the former will happen as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:29:22-07:00","id":534933,"title":"","content":"Like I said, in any other fandom, I'd be questioning this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom"