com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:25:37-07:00","id":535512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=535259#post535259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as someone who has only ever seen MLP on Netflix: where can I find Season 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>YouTube. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/2lsq9gwR_4A\" target=\"_blank\">Link for season 5 premiere.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:33:03-07:00","id":536272,"title":"","content":"Is that an official source, or is it \u201cpirated\u201d? If the latter, what's the official source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T20:08:08-07:00","id":536423,"title":"","content":"Not available until Discovery Family puts the DVD out, most likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:34:01-07:00","id":545085,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E8 - Lost Treasures of Griffonstone</b><br /> <br /> Really took some time for me to see this episode, and then when I finally did, I didn't have much to say about it.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's really good! I loved it. The adventure formula worked wonders, and I'm inclined to believe it's due to the fact that they have to find out what the problem was when they go there. That added an incentive to interact more meaningfully with the place they were put in. I'm not sure the map as a quest dispenser won't wear thin after a while, but right now, it seem to be working.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Pinkie and Rainbow are colourful and interesting, Gilda is back again, we get more worldbuilding and Twilight being all salty. Sweet!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img11.deviantart.net/56d9/i/2015/143/d/a/the_lost_treasure_of_griffonstone_by_jamesawilliams1996-d8uhewh.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Also this.</a><br /> <br /> There were some things I had a hard time to swallow. Are we really supposed to believe that <i>everyone</i> is a douchebag in Griffonstone? Also, I get that they wanted to visually represent the disarray the place is in, but at least clear the rubble out of the houses, right?<br /> <br /> Disregarding that, I liked the episode, it was refreshing and clever while still being a really solid, narrative-focused staple of a series.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:03:57-07:00","id":546559,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else find it interesting that we're well into the season, and so far, we haven't seen even a *hint* of the &quot;Rainbow Power&quot; that saved the day at the end of last season?<br /> <br /> I suspect it's the animators' subtle way of sweeping a toy design that was forced on them under the rug, at least as much asthey can. They'll probably HAVE to include it somewhere, maybe at the very end of this season, again...But it would be nice to know that they found the designs as ugly as much of the fandom did!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:11:56-07:00","id":546566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=545085#post545085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were some things I had a hard time to swallow. Are we really supposed to believe that <i>everyone</i> is a douchebag in Griffonstone? Also, I get that they wanted to visually represent the disarray the place is in, but at least clear the rubble out of the houses, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-UN-fC5Evxw#t=0m14s\" target=\"_blank\">I think the problem...was Pinkie's song. Pinkie, do you have any, uh, y'know, <i>happier</i> songs about partying?</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 06-09-2015, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T02:17:42-07:00","id":546682,"title":"","content":"Griffonstone felt pretty dark actually. It's a whole community that has basically given up and is just going through the motions. The whole seeking money thing also felt like they were clinging on to <i>something</i> but we never saw anyone with money using it for much, there were no luxurious mansions among the general decay. Pursuit of money because it's something to pursue rather than any real need or desire for it.<br /> <br /> I particularly liked that Rainbow and Pinkie <i>didn't</i> solve the problem. They gave a kickstart to fixing it but the Griffons themselves are going to have to put in the real work to rebuild a sense of community and fix the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T04:02:47-07:00","id":546723,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's true. That's a recurring theme from the Cutie Map premiere. I like the change of pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:06:46-07:00","id":553119,"title":"","content":"<b>E5S9 - Slice of Life</b><br /> <br /> what is life even","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:24:48-07:00","id":553361,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E9 - Slice of Life</b><br /> <br /> Having rewatched the episode, I now hope I can formulate some more coherent thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> Not on the content, though. That'll just have to stand on on its own. You will either like it or not, and I think it's as simple as that in this case. Personally, I liked most of it, but I felt like the parts where they dragged out material that the fandom had already done at length was easily the weakest. I mean, cool to see Octavia and Vinyl living together. Less cool to see them doing the classic/dubstep mix thing, since the fandom has already done that, and much better. Picked up again when they went for a ride through Ponyville, though that stretched my suspension of disbelief juuust shy of breaking. I think Lyra and Bon Bon was really well handled: they incorporated fanon but added their own (crazy) spin on it too. You really kind of do have to take this episode at face value; some things will work for you, others won't, and that's really all there is to say on the matter.<br /> <br /> Is this a &quot;love letter to the bronies&quot;? It certainly strokes our egos, no doubt, see in &quot;this thing that we made&quot; being retold back to us. I can relate to that. On that note, yeah, one episode like this every five seasons sounds about like the right dose. Not only because the fandom is really the best at doing fandom stuff, but also because the best love letter we can get is a continued original, high quality production of the show we love.<br /> <br /> The question that I keep asking myself is how the episode looks to someone who's not in on the jokes. It's really internal. For a single episode, that's okay in my mind, but somewhere a bunch of 10-year-old might sit around wondering what the hell just happened.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm wondering what the hell just happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T18:56:04-07:00","id":553615,"title":"","content":"The second half was better than the first half. I did not hate the episode. I liked all the ways they avoided exactly hitting what the fans did. I would watch it again.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:17:22-07:00","id":554035,"title":"","content":"I got a smile out of just <i>how much</i> they stressed Lyra and BonBon were just friends. I also like Octavia and Vinyl in fanon but they just...weren't any good here, that music was dreadful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:15:15-07:00","id":554065,"title":"","content":"Show says: &quot;It's lucky we are such GOOD FRIENDS that we can overcome this crisis in our FRIENDSHIP, don't you think so, BEST FRIEND?&quot;<br /> <br /> Bronies hear: &quot;Make-up sex tonight.&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked how they played with that too, and also that it really came off as just that: a play, a joke. No way something like that will fanonised when there's such a big foundation for the other interpretation. I really think that was what this episode tried to do, too; not lay down the law, but run with our ideas for a bit.<br /> <br /> Vinyl and Octavia were decent for me, but yeah, the music was really bland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-14-2015, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:18:31-07:00","id":554321,"title":"","content":"It had strains of the Saban/Dic dub of Sailor Moon with Uranus and Neptune. I giggled incessantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:35:15-07:00","id":558835,"title":"","content":"It seems the the Lyra/Bonbon part is the one that stuck the most from the episode. Aside from any shipping, Special Agent Sweetie Drops is showing up in many fanworks on EqD, and I bet she'll remain after season 5 has ended, too.<br /> <br /> It's cool because it's a bit of a turn around from the normal way the Lyra/Bonbon dynamic is portrayed. I've found that typically, Lyra is the energetic and crazy one while Bonbon is down to earth and slightly nervous. With her secret agent identity, she gets to play another role than her usual one, which also provides opportunity for Lyra to be reimagined in accordance. I think this is good for both of them in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:10:46-07:00","id":558872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=558835#post558835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems the the Lyra/Bonbon part is the one that stuck the most from the episode. Aside from any shipping, Special Agent Sweetie Drops is showing up in many fanworks on EqD, and I bet she'll remain after season 5 has ended, too.<br /> <br /> It's cool because it's a bit of a turn around from the normal way the Lyra/Bonbon dynamic is portrayed. I've found that typically, Lyra is the energetic and crazy one while Bonbon is down to earth and slightly nervous. With her secret agent identity, she gets to play another role than her usual one, which also provides opportunity for Lyra to be reimagined in accordance. I think this is good for both of them in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, the way the the show's crew played with expectations and changed dynamics was the best part of the entire show. It was essentially the show doing it's own fanon to balance out the audience's own, and it worked. The consensual awareness(not acceptance, of course) of the collective identities at work is now broadened and deepened and given new life, shaking stagnate conceptions out of their comfort zone and into new angles of narrative.<br /> <br /> You know, the more I think about this episode, the more I love it. It's one of the few times where I can think of a piece of medium actively changing the fanbase on something that has long bothered me for the better, and it does it more or less by being weird and awesome enough to pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:33:50-07:00","id":558884,"title":"","content":"Being new to the Brony community, a lot of this episode flew over my head. That is, I was just aware <i>enough</i> to know that Bronies have adopted various background ponies and fleshed them out in a fanon \u201cexpanded universe\u201d; but aside from Doctor Hooves and Vynil (and not counting \u201csupporting cast\u201d like the Princesses or the CMCs), I didn't recognize anypony featured in the episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:16:00-07:00","id":558914,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was always the risk of it. Br, my roommate, knows shit about the fan's ideas, and so the entire episode was just weird stuff and references that didn't make sense. This is not a causal viewer episode, and that keeps it from being a truly good episode due to exclusivity. But if you're in on the joke, then it's expansive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:33:18-07:00","id":560925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=553361#post553361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S5E9 - Slice of Life</b><br /> <br /> Is this a &quot;love letter to the bronies&quot;? It certainly strokes our egos, no doubt, see in &quot;this thing that we made&quot; being retold back to us. I can relate to that. On that note, yeah, one episode like this every five seasons sounds about like the right dose. Not only because the fandom is really the best at doing fandom stuff, but also because the best love letter we can get is a continued original, high quality production of the show we love.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's generally considered the &quot;correct&quot; pov to have--and I don't disagree with it!--but I'm gonna go out on a limb and say that, ifthe show were to evolve and grow beyond its current form and give us THIS every week, I'd absolutely love it. Hell, give us a spin-off show or webisodes with the same background cast, there's clearly anaudience for it, and it might well prove more popular than the original show!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question that I keep asking myself is how the episode looks to someone who's not in on the jokes. It's really internal. For a single episode, that's okay in my mind, but somewhere a bunch of 10-year-old might sit around wondering what the hell just happened.<br /> . </div> </div> </div>Much as I was wondering after Rainbow Rocks, which was similarly filled with Brony shout-outs. OTOH, kids are a lot more savvy about these things than I was growing up, and we know there are children who identify as Bronies, so it's entirely possible that most of them got all the jokes...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:39:25-07:00","id":560929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=558835#post558835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems the the Lyra/Bonbon part is the one that stuck the most from the episode. Aside from any shipping, Special Agent Sweetie Drops is showing up in many fanworks on EqD, and I bet she'll remain after season 5 has ended, too.<br /> <br /> It's cool because it's a bit of a turn around from the normal way the Lyra/Bonbon dynamic is portrayed. I've found that typically, Lyra is the energetic and crazy one while Bonbon is down to earth and slightly nervous. With her secret agent identity, she gets to play another role than her usual one, which also provides opportunity for Lyra to be reimagined in accordance. I think this is good for both of them in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>They share a similar &quot;odd couple&quot; relationship with Octavia and Vinyl Scratch, so it was interesting to see how that theme was played with. Lyra being the Straight Man was a nice switch! Andfanon often portrays Octavia as being frustrated with VS's antics, so it was nice to see her willingly jamming with her.<br /> <br /> The Princesses were another nice touch, seeing them bicker like actual sisters do. Esp got a kick out of Celestia being so miffed at Luna, when it was apparently Celestia's fault, anyway! I was expecting the fanon nicknames they have for each other (&quot;Tia&quot; and &quot;Lulu&quot;) to pop up, but you can't have everything. <br /> <br /> Was there a particular reason we got Amethyst Star? I'mpretty up on the fanon, but I'd never even heard of her. What's her deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:41:59-07:00","id":560932,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/06/ma-larson-reveals-all-sorts-of-fun.html\" target=\"_blank\">The episode's writer reveals scenes and ideas that didn't make the cut, what Hasbro mandated, etc!</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/06/the-voices-behind-todays-episode-100.html\" target=\"_blank\">The voice cast of the backgrounders, also revealing their official names (including Derpy's)!</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&#91;/URL\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/06/we-love-you-dhx.html]And did anyone catch this hidden frame in the ep?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 06-19-2015, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T17:45:14-07:00","id":561408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=560925#post560925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's generally considered the &quot;correct&quot; pov to have--and I don't disagree with it!--but I'm gonna go out on a limb and say that, ifthe show were to evolve and grow beyond its current form and give us THIS every week, I'd absolutely love it. Hell, give us a spin-off show or webisodes with the same background cast, there's clearly anaudience for it, and it might well prove more popular than the original show!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not watch it. That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T19:37:11-07:00","id":561516,"title":"","content":"Show with the background ponies? Okay. Show based on fan shout outs, like Slice of Life? I don't see it working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:19:32-07:00","id":561884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=561516#post561516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show with the background ponies? Okay. Show based on fan shout outs, like Slice of Life? I don't see it working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I mispoke myself...I didn't really mean a calvacade of fan refs, per se, but just a different approach to storytelling. I've been saying for a while now that, as muchas I enjoy the show, I wish the makers would allow it to change and develop with the acknowledgement of its older audience. Most people seem to think I mean making it &quot;darker and edgier&quot;, but that's not what I'm talking about. <br /> <br /> When I read the comic book (some pages of which I posted earlier in this thread), I practically shouted,&quot;YES! That's it, *that's* the tone I'd like to see it the show!&quot; And the100th was much closer to that. It's still very appropriate for kids, but more of an &quot;all ages&quot; feel; I don't think changing MLP, *if done correctly*, will somehow automatically destroy The Formula and/or alienate kids. <br /> <br /> Part of The Point of the show that Faust wanted to get across was that kids are smarter, tougher and more sophisticated than TV allows for, that TV doesn't have to be simplified and dumbed down for their ages, and that they will not shatter like fragile glass if you <i>challenge them</i> by pushing the boundaries. If anything, most will thrive on that! <br /> <br /> That's what I would like to see more of from FIM, and this ep was really a step in that direction. I don't expect the show to stampede in that direction, no, but I do hope it keeps making baby steps there, at least...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:27:29-07:00","id":563441,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E10 - Princess Spike</b><br /> <br /> Kinda... boring? I don't know, the first half was kind of lackluster to me. The &quot;run around and obsess over your job&quot; is rather overdone, and while it was done pretty well and it did tie back in later, it was still meh for me. It did pick up in the second half, where Spike gets to confront the reality of his newfound power.<br /> <br /> I did like how the episode wrote Spike. Real Spike episodes are few and far between as it is, and this time he came into his role really well. The way he drifts from wanting to help Twilight to using her name for his benefit felt smooth and gradual, and I think it can be used to speculate about his character. For example, how does his dragon nature play into wanting to manifest his power and acquire favours? He never really <i>stops</i> wanting to help Twilight, though, so maybe his dragon birth doesn't play in?<br /> <br /> It's a pretty good episode, no real faults except a sense of having seen it before, but executed well enough that it at least didn't get tedious. The accents were funny too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T00:44:13-07:00","id":563794,"title":"","content":"Meh, a Spike episode. They always feel generally the same: Spike tries to do a thing, he means well but is bumbling, lazy and gets sidetracked with things for his own gain. It all goes wrong in the end and Twilight/etc. step in to save the day. He never grows, never changes, never seems to have self awareness despite all the time he's done this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:42:07-07:00","id":565764,"title":"","content":"I don't know\u2026 the problem seems to be that Spike's role as Twilight's sidekick is all there is to him. Frankly, the most positive \u201cSpike episode\u201d I've ever seen was the one where everyone was sucked into one of his comic books \u2014 and that only worked because the episode threw the Mane Six completely off their game and placed the key to resolving the dilemma smack dab in Spike's claws; all he had to do was to overcome his inferiority complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:37:06-07:00","id":566812,"title":"","content":"If Power Ponies is the most positive Spike episode, the poor kid is more fucked than he has any right to be.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">muthafuckingpowerponiesepisodewasfuckingterrible</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:08:53-07:00","id":566836,"title":"","content":"Am I misremembering Power Ponies...wasn't Spike's special moment thing that he'd basically read comics so knew the tropes? I.e.: he was special for doing something that basically anyone could replicate with little effort or unique skill or talent or anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T00:16:13-07:00","id":567494,"title":"","content":"Best Spike episode was easily Equestria Games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:34:56-07:00","id":568441,"title":"","content":"The issue with Spike episodes is they all undermine him as a character. Spike outside of Spike episodes is helpful and responsible to the point of self destruction. He's a submissive in the best way, he just enjoys helping others. Spike in a Spike focused episode is a self centered greedy jerk that has no concern for the consequences of his actions. This happens pretty much any time he is granted any level of independent control, authority, or rewards for his actions.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind the unfortunate undertone of these stories. &quot;You are a follower, you do as you are told. If you try and decide things for yourself you will always make the wrong call. Expect compensation for your hard work and the temptation will drive you to greed and excess.&quot; As he has been written in these stories Spike can only be happy and a good person as Twilights personal servant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T07:49:18-07:00","id":570255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=563441#post563441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S5E10 - Princess Spike</b><br /> <br /> Kinda... boring?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, felt way too straight forward and linear to me. We all knew right where this was going, and it dutifully took us right there. I was afraid my reaction was due to it coming after the madness that was the 100th, which was always going to be a tough act to follow, but if you compare this to the Equestrian Games ep, it's just far less entertaining than that was.<br /> <br /> I really just think Spike's not well-suited to carrying an ep all by himself. Pair him up with the CMC, or Rarity, like in Inspiration Manifestation, and he works much better, IMO!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T11:24:39-07:00","id":570373,"title":"","content":"Well, today's episode sucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:03:51-07:00","id":571342,"title":"","content":"I thought it was alright actually, Pinkie's reverse slide exit made me smile more than it had any right to. Though her 'party planning' files were creepy as hell...at least she doesn't have a torture dungeon down there.<br /> <br /> The <i>plot</i> however was pretty rubbish. Why do they care about the Yaks? Why is this not being done by Cadance and the Crystal Empire who literally border them? Why was the solution to the 'problem' obvious the moment the Yaks turned up the first time and the episode was spent repeating the same gag?<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm saying is that scene by scene I thought it was pretty good, as a whole episode...less so. Pinkie's been pretty good throughout this season so far and we all know she can be...difficult...to write well at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:58:12-07:00","id":577573,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E11 - Party Pooped</b><br /> <br /> So is this going to be about Pinkie getting bowel problems?<br /> <br /> I know, I am the master of comedy.<br /> <br /> Right, so. Half of this episode is bad. The yak half. That really sucks. No two ways about it.<br /> <br /> The parts with Pinkie and the rest of the gang though? I really liked. Both Pinkie and Twilight are written perfectly to character and the quick cuts and Pinkie's travel journal narration style, mixed with her usual quirkiness, makes the episode stand out and be interesting. The dialogue and writing was good as well.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for the yaks, this would have been a great episode. Now it's merely decent. Can't win 'em all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 07-03-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:49:32-07:00","id":579487,"title":"","content":"I question her need for files on everyone when she has eidetic memory.<br /> My only real complaint is its not up to the standard from season 1. Griffon the Brush Off (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jf_V3VlickA\" target=\"_blank\">can check out my video review here)</a> for example played alot with expectations. I was hoping for a more realistic lesson along the lines of, no they are being unreasonable dicks and there is a point where they have to compromise too. Its not bad just not the revolutionary play on cliche that got me into the series in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T15:47:23-07:00","id":580317,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E12 - Amending Fences</b><br /> <br /> Anyone who has read my semi-regular posts on the different episodes will notice that I often cut the show a lot of slack. If there is something I like in an episode, I often let that colour my opinion of it and the verdict comes out mostly positive. Only rarely do I hate on any single episode (but looking at <i>you</i>, Putting Your Hoof Down). Sometimes I wish I did that more often, though, because it means that when something truly awesome comes around, my praises will ring just a bit more hollow. And Amending Fences really did it for me, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> My first feeling when watching the end credits roll, even before thinking about how great this episode had been, was &quot;this is almost the exact opposite of Party Pooped&quot;. In Party Pooped, the plot was started by visitors from a place we've never heard of before and never got any real information about, coming in and making demands in a (fittingly) cartoonish way that didn't even make them one-dimensional as much as one-functional; they really only existed to perform the action of disapproving with subsequent wrecking of stuff and make empty threats with no credibility (did anyone really think a war threat would ever actually be realised in MLP?). It then prompted a much better journey-section which was funny, but as all Pinkie Pies antics it will never be referenced again. Even the party archives (is that what we're calling them?) will likely not show up again and if they do, they'll only reinforce a characteristic we have already accepted in Pinkie Pie. The whole episode was a parenthesis. It might as well have never happened in the greater scope of the integrity of the show.<br /> <br /> Amending Fences, on the contrary, provides us with a look at, a reaction to and a development of a part of Twilight's life that we have known must be there but which has never really been mentioned before now. The fact that the plot of the episode comes from the character, and not from outside of her, is probably the thing that carries the episode hardest. This is natural, a conflict that has grown out of the character's situation organically, and it feels really important as a result. Yaks, not so much.<br /> <br /> On a more detailed level, what did I like about this episode? Well, as I said, it showed the Princess of Friendship dealing with the consequences of her choices earlier in life. It also puts into sharp focus her own development, what has changed in her and what hasn't. Moondancer becomes a dark reflection of Twilight, an image of a path not taken, but despite that they're more similar than different. That in turn becomes a potent message of how your path is not laid out for you. Moondancer and Twilight are very alike, but they ended up in very different places. It challenges the stereotype of the asocial bookworm by showing a bookworm who has lots of friends, without losing her bookishness or drastically changing her personality. Twilight isn't Pinkie Pie, who is super social and has lots of friends. She's not Applejack, who has a big family and have to stay friends with all of them. She's an introvert, bookish nerd, and yet <i>she</i> is the Princess of Friendship.<br /> <br /> The callback to episode one was of course great as well, and I really loved that they included Minuette as a speaking role. We also got new info that Lyra and Twilight used to be friends. It ties back into the previous point that the Princess of Friendship would forget her friends' names, and I think it was a nice touch which was fortunately not pushed further than it could handle. Overall, the three old friends were very likeable, down to earth and believable, and for a good while, I thought the moral would be &quot;get over yourself, Twilight, you're not the center of the universe&quot;. But when it turned out that Twilight might actually have influenced Moondancer by her not attending her party, it kind of made sense as well. Now, I should say, this here is probably the weakest point in the episode. It's not 100% clear why Twilight in particular was so important to Moondancer, especially when she clearly was better friends with the other three. It could be argued that she would likely have kept hanging out with the other ones at least, even if the grew resentful of Twilight. But as they say, reality has the edge over fiction in that it doesn't have to convince you it's real. I can imagine someone nervously trying her hand at something for the first time, and then breaking down when it fell through; the minds of people are irrational and emotional things. It's also probable that Moondancer felt like Twilight was the most like her, and would have liked the get closer to her more than the others, and when it failed she felt rejected and despaired and grew bitter. I digress, though. The whole dynamic between the characters was splendid.<br /> <br /> And that's really all there was! No need for a contrived plot about pleasing dumb yaks. Just characters interacting, creating intrigue as they clash. This episode was top notch. Best of the season? So far, absolutely. Best of the show? Can't say, but it's certainly up there in the running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 07-05-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:25:40-07:00","id":580551,"title":"","content":"And it adds some materiel for the third Equestria Girls film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:51:10-07:00","id":581113,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I disagree with Weimann and here's why.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think that this is an okay episode. I think that it has implications which the writers did not totally think through and never intended. I think that with minor adjustments, this could be a great episode; one of the best in the series.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Twilight had several friends back in Canterlot. Most of them moved on with their lives and were totally okay with her leaving, even if they thought that the circumstances were a little strange. One of them did not. She was completely and totally broken by Twilight moving away. I think that the startling implication of this is that you are completely responsible for the mental health and well-being of your friends, and since their lives are so totally and completely in your control, you must be ever mindful of what you do. If your friend breaks down, it's your fault and you should have done better. This personally rubs me the wrong way because I have been Moondance. I had a friend on whom I was totally dependant. They disappointed me and I was broken into small, scared little pieces. I have, however, been able to recover and put myself back together. I am the better for it. Moondance had the first part of this happen: she was totally dependant on Twilight and when Twilight disappointed her she was broken. She, however, is lacking the second part. The only way that she was able to recover herself is when Twilight came and put her back together. This is not going to make her a stronger pony. If anything she's going to be worse off for it than she was before. Now she knows that if she ever is completely broken by Twilight again, she doesn't have to worry about it because Twilight will come and make things better eventually.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to the detrimental effect that this will have on Moondance's well-being, this also puts too much of a burden on Twilight. She's now completely responsible for Moondance's well-being. If Moondance is upset, it is Twilight's duty to put her back together. This puts far too much of a burden on her; nopony can be that responsible for the well-being of another. It is exhausting and eventually we all fail, regardless of intentions. We have someone for whom we are totally responsible: ourselves. That's enough responsibility for anypony. Having to be responsible for somepony else is an unbearable burden. (And we could get into being responsible for children, but I don't really think that's necessary to get into.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think that the biggest implication that the writers didn't think fully through is that this episode really says extroversion is good, and introversion is bad. While it is eventually made clear that Moondance is not a healthy introvert, not everypony who just doesn't feel like hanging out is unhealthy. Sometimes for introverts, there can just be too much social interaction. That happened for me this weekend. Since it was a long weekend, we played an extra session of Mouse Guard on Thursday night. Then we played our normal session on Friday. Saturday we had a BBQ for Independence Day. After that, the people hung around and played games. For hours. And hours. It was too much social interaction for me for one weekend. I had to leave. It actually was a little overwhelming and caused me some anxiety later in the evening. I think that, if one of Twilight's old friends was an introvert, but not someone who was unhealthy like Moondance, that the episode would have been increased in quality at least threefold. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's not necessarily a bad episode, not like the Yak one. But it treated a complex situation with perhaps too much simplicity. I know, theoretically it's a TV show directed at prepubescent girls and children are not capable of understanding the same depth of complexity that adults are sometimes, but 1) I think that sometimes we give children too little credit and they understand things better than we give them credit for and, 2) if you think that you have to dumb down the show this much and dilute a complex situation like this to this degree, maybe you shouldn't have tried to address it in the first place. Friendship is magic (bitches) and everybody needs friends. And you should try to be a good friend. Good messages. But the representation here is too simplistic for what they were trying to address.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:52:41-07:00","id":581843,"title":"","content":"Just getting this out of the way, her issue wasn't introversion, I mean she is but her issue is social anxiety. A completely unrelated thing. Introversion has absolutely nothing to do with being a bookworm or disliking social gatherings. Just how mentally taxing it is. Not a huge deal, just a pet peeve of mine. I believe what we saw was co-dependency. You are certainly right she puts far too much stock in just twilight. I mean if the flakiest member of your entire circle of friends missed a party you should focus on those that did not on that one person.<br /> <br /> I do like the continuity established in this show. Also notice it justifies these ponies appearing in Ponyville and Canterlot. My real complaint is it looked like they were going for something deeper but pulled back. Judging by what Moondancer said, this wasn't the first time Twilight did that. Heck earlier they said no one was shocked Twilight up and left because thats just who she was. Let me call back once more to Griffon the Brush-off. Which at the end went, no a party at the end of the doesn't always fix all your problems. Sometimes there are no quick solutions. I'd have liked if this was the start of the healing process. Something small like. &quot;I'm still upset Twilight, but I'm willing to start over.&quot;<br /> <br /> One nice thing they didn't flesh out enough, was the idea of different layers and types of friends. I think even after this those girls don't view twilight as a close friend, nor did they view her like that to begin with. The kinds of friends most of us had in high school. You talked, hung out, but when you lost contact with them it wasn't a huge loss. Not that you had anything against them, and you'd spend time with them again, they were just never a huge part of your life. That seemed to be how they viewed Twilight. She was nice, they care for her, but its not a huge deal if she comes or goes because they knew that from the start. Thats just what they came to expect from her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T04:59:40-07:00","id":586981,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/07/season-five-split-up-season-six-not-at.html\" target=\"_blank\">So it seems S5 will be split up into two parts.</a> The second part will come &quot;later this year&quot;. This means that tonight's episode is the last one for a while. I was... not prepared for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T06:05:28-07:00","id":588051,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E13 - Do Princesses Dream of Magic Sheep</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fluttershy:</b> &quot;Mmmm, it's so nice to be the pet for once.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you hear that? It's the keyboard clatter of a hundred slashfics being born.<br /> <br /> Pet peeve, but could someone explain to me why it's &quot;magic&quot; and not &quot;magical&quot; up there? You have three perfectly useful and distinguishable forms: &quot;magic&quot; is the noun, &quot;magical&quot; is the adjective, &quot;magically&quot; is the adverb. Still Merriam-Webster lists &quot;magical&quot; and &quot;magic&quot; in the adjectival sense as synonyms to each other. Why use the noun form as a second adjective? I'll never get that.<br /> <br /> Right, the episode.<br /> <br /> Luna fans will orgasm over her getting so big a role on her own. I'm personally of the opinion that Celestial is #BestPrincess, but sure, no harm. I had some issues with the presentation of her, though. Not only did I roll my eyes at her having created the Tantibus in order to punish herself, but also that she could apparently have saved herself years of self-imposed nightmares by asking the others if they liked her? She sure came around real fast at the end there, and it all felt pretty plastered on. I'm also worried Luna will get typecast into being the &quot;dream princess&quot; exclusively; the fact that even her own episode was about that is a bit worrying. But maybe she hadn't shown up enough to have to worry about that yet.<br /> <br /> The dream sequences were pretty cool, though. A few references, some callbacks to previous episodes (Flutterbat was neat, but the Power Ponies did not have to return however). I particularly liked the return of their, uh, Rainbow Forms? <a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/powerlisting/images/e/ed/Mane_Six_Rainbow_Power.png/revision/latest?cb=20140606014939\" target=\"_blank\">Y'know, these things?</a> I liked their design and it's nice to see them again. Princess Big Mac and the giant Derpy was maybe a bit on the nose, but I felt like it worked without coming off as super forced.<br /> <br /> All in all, pretty fun episode, but the biggest thing about it was that Luna was in it, and I'm not sure I like where they seem to be taking her. They are making more of a character out of her, however, and that is rewarding to see. Here's wondering if they'll do more with Celestia as well, of if at least one sister needs to stay mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:30:00-07:00","id":588274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=588051#post588051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pet peeve, but could someone explain to me why it's &quot;magic&quot; and not &quot;magical&quot; up there? You have three perfectly useful and distinguishable forms: &quot;magic&quot; is the noun, &quot;magical&quot; is the adjective, &quot;magically&quot; is the adverb. Still Merriam-Webster lists &quot;magical&quot; and &quot;magic&quot; in the adjectival sense as synonyms to each other. Why use the noun form as a second adjective? I'll never get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the title is, like many episode titles, a reference. In this case to the novel <i>Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep? </i>by Philip K. Dick. They're following that form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T13:39:17-07:00","id":588438,"title":"","content":"Ah, I didn't make the connection. Thanks for pointing it out. Since &quot;magic&quot; does seem to be an accepted (if annoying) adjective form, I suppose keeping the -ic ending sound for the reference justifies using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T23:04:29-07:00","id":589926,"title":"","content":"Pinkie and Dash had the best Nightmares. Though it was interesting that Fluttershy used monster-Angel as her weapon of choice in the last dream. Otherwise it was pure Luna fanservice which I enjoyed wholeheartedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:37:54-07:00","id":612568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=586981#post586981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2015/07/season-five-split-up-season-six-not-at.html\" target=\"_blank\">So it seems S5 will be split up into two parts.</a> The second part will come &quot;later this year&quot;. This means that tonight's episode is the last one for a while. I was... not prepared for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw what you did there.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know it's not charitable, but I sometimes wish for a special layer of Malfeas for whoever started this &quot;splitting seasons&quot; nonsense. Whatever the original cause was, and how necessary it may have been, it seems that shows today are simply doing it because &quot;that's just the way it's done now, right?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some people justify this one as meaning that there's less of a wait till the next season now, but I just see it as TWO waits instead of one...and we could have had the entire season to rewatch and debate about during that one wait. Ah well, at least the first part of the current season is now up on Netflix, which I wasn't expecting!<br /> <br /> And it looks like the new Equestian Girls movie is being released straightto video/tv, which probably means that the last one didn't do too well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bofs3nWd_3c\" data-code=\"bofs3nWd_3c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bofs3nWd_3c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7P4S3_vSLU\" data-code=\"l7P4S3_vSLU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/l7P4S3_vSLU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T12:35:38-07:00","id":663391,"title":"","content":"We back? We back. Actually looking forward to the movie coming out next week, and up until then...<br /> <br /> <b>S5E14 - Canterlot Boutique</b><br /> <br /> Rarity was once my favourite character. She had all the opportunity to become the stock antagonist socialite, but it was turned around in a way that really impressed me. She and Twilight was best pony for season 1 and 2, because they both seemed so counter-trope. On the other end of the spectrum was Rainbow Dash, who was an obnoxious douche with a flat portrayal. It's interesting to see that when I assess my 2015 Best Pony list, the top spot is shared by Twilight and... Rainbow Dash, and while Rarity isn't at the bottom (sorry, Flutters, but you're just so boring to me), she shares a split fourth place with Applejack.<br /> <br /> What happened? Well, Rainbow Dash got a lot of episodes that developed and challenged her, and Rarity... didn't. She's not quite as bad as Fluttershy for being a one trick pony, but she's probably the pony which is the most thematically framed-in. Canterlot Boutique suffers a bit from that, because while it's not really a Suited for Success 2: Electric Boogaloo (instead of having to stress to accomodate the wishes of her customers, she is understimulated by all her customers just wanting the same thing), it's also really easy to see the similarities (that song, for example, which for reference was mediocre). It's just always about dresses with her, isn't it? It kind of annoyed me that once she finally got an episode, it's about the same thing she's been doing in the background for the whole run of the show.<br /> <br /> That said, if you get over all that, the episode was good. I liked the dynamic between Sassy Saddles and Rarity, for example. It's clear that they both want for the shop to succeed, and both of them have personal stakes in that, but they have different ideas of what that success looks like, and Rarity gets pulled into Sassy's version before she rediscovers what the core of her craft is. That doesn't make Sassy bad, per se; instead, it makes Rarity an inspiration figure for Sassy, which I think was great since Sassy showed no signs of needing guidance at all, in fact quite the contrary. The characterisation of Sassy was easily the best part of this episode, though that doesn't mean I <i>like</i> her much.<br /> <br /> Solid and really good for many reasons, but not among my personal favourites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-13-2015, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:22:27-07:00","id":664459,"title":"","content":"It didn't feel a particularly strong re-start. No stand out sight gags, no funny turns of phrase and, as an outsider to the fashion industry (I believe I bought a new set of underwear last year, otherwise everything else I own fits...so why would I buy anything else?) it seems Sassy is doing exactly what the fashion industry actually does. Takes the - often absurd, but not always - stuff from the high fashion types, distills it down to something you might actually wear and then mass produces it with close to slave labour. So the resolution with rarity showing how much better personalised, unique clothing is rings really hollow when a clothes shop you might actually walk into will indeed have 20 copies of the same item in different sizes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:55:50-07:00","id":664547,"title":"","content":"It depends on the style of boutique you go into. I've been to some of the really high end places in Vegas, the sorts celebritites shop in, and I'll be damned if I ever saw two of a kind.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure they had them? But the idea sold in those places was a premise of exclusivity in product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:36:41-07:00","id":673438,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E15 - Rarity Investigates!</b><br /> <br /> Short on time, so gonna be blissfully brief. Liked the episode doing new things. The first part was kind of slow, but I also appreciate that they held off a bit on the trenchcoats, so that the detective part didn't overstay its welcome. I also felt that Rarity came off as getting her &quot;fashion thing&quot; plastered on a bit at the beginning of the investigation sequence, but it felt more natural later on. Rarity and Rainbow Dash is a rare combo, but fruitful since they cover so little common ground, provided the writers manage to find some ground to base them both off. That happened here, I felt.<br /> <br /> The episode cast Rarity in a new light, which she sorely needs. On the other hand, it also didn't really dare to not include the same old fashion thing we've seen for ages. I think there are more themes in Rarity than the ones she's stuck in right now, and this episode helped to bring that out. I liked this one more than Canterlot Boutique.<br /> <br /> On a side note, <a href=\"http://www.mane6.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Mane6</a> just launched <a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/them-s-fightin-herds\" target=\"_blank\">an Indiegogo campaign for the new incarnation of Fighting is Magic named Them's Fightin' Herds</a>. Check it out if you're curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T18:28:16-07:00","id":673709,"title":"","content":"So, looked to the end of the week on my tv guide, and the description for Friendship Games calls it a &quot;collection of shorts&quot;. I'm... honestly not sure how to feel about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:52:45-07:00","id":673970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=673709#post673709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looked to the end of the week on my tv guide, and the description for Friendship Games calls it a &quot;collection of shorts&quot;. I'm... honestly not sure how to feel about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just got significantly worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T20:14:17-07:00","id":679579,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E16 - Made in Manehattan</b><br /> <br /> I swear someone on the writing team ships Charity/Applesack OTP. They've had more coupled episodes than anyone else, I think. And they do go well together: as I've said earlier, while they are very different, they're actually in some fashion the mane ponies with the most in common as well. This time, it's their similarities that make the episode work, even if it's not what's focused on. In fact, the episode does good job of making it not be about the focus ponies at all. Both Applejack and Rarity is comparatively in the background, instead letting the problem take the foreground, which is good for the episode since the moral of the story is that everyone can help a little if they take the time. It's also consistent with the theme from the season premiere and other episodes of the mane six stepping back and letting others work with their own problems.<br /> <br /> Lost Treasure of Griffonstone was definitely a more adventure-style map episode but there was a chillness and down-to-earth feeling in this one that I liked. Not exciting, but nice and pleasant. I liked it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Twilight, not that hype to be a princess is it? Maybe while your friends are having adventures you can <i>fly around</i> in your <i>big castle</i> with your <i>wings</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-27-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T00:23:17-07:00","id":679726,"title":"","content":"I imagine she's done the flying thing to death. I do like that the general approach is to have the main cast turn up and catalyse others to action rather than solve everything themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T16:46:51-07:00","id":680519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=679726#post679726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine she's done the flying thing to death. I do like that the general approach is to have the main cast turn up and catalyse others to action rather than solve everything themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's one of the things that make this season interesting, and also kind of hard to compare to the other seasons. I can't really decide if I like season 4 or season 5 better, because they kind of do things sufficiently differently to be hard to compare.<br /> <br /> And speaking of doing different things, there was a new movie premiered yesterday! It's been a pony-filled weekend for sure. I caught the US premiere on stream, but I've been told that it was cut to make room for commercials. I'll have to watch it again once the full version comes up up somewhere. Nonetheless, I think I got the gist of it anyway. So without further ado...<br /> <br /> <b>Equestria Girls 3: Friendship Games</b><br /> <br /> Okay, let's be honest. This is the third time they use this structure: there's a thing at the school, they have to team up to compete in it, there's some complication in the meantime and in the end there's a big boss fight. On the one hand, that can come off as feeling bland and uninspired. On the other, it makes it kind of easy, and interesting, to compare the three and see what they did differently.<br /> <br /> One thing to compare is main character. In EG1, it was clearly about Twilight. She was the one we experienced the world through, and while Sunset Shimmer was the new and interesting one, it was still a very traditional Twilight-and-her-friends-but-mostly-Twilight-saves-the-day affair, complete with friendship rainbow laser at the end. In Rainbow Rocks, Twilight was still kind of in focus, but Sunset was the one who got her story told. It was a redemption arc, where she got to be accepted by the humane six (that's a term now) and in turn again accepted the tutelage she had rejected from Celestia from Twilight instead. Rainbow Rocks probably contained more character development than any other FiM feature has ever done, and it did get a much better reception.<br /> <br /> Friendship Games, in turn, is the story of human!Twilight. In a way, human!Twilight is a Moondancer character, since the comparison between her and pony!Twilight are unavoidable. Even if it's not quite as traumatic as in Amending Fences, and human!Twilight seems to even yearn for something to change in her life while Moondancer was very guarded to that, the progression from seclusion to openness is clear. When human!Twilight unleashes the magic at the end, the transformation shows that even in those with only academic interests, seclusion and ego-focus can corrupt as surely as &quot;evil&quot; intentions, and highlights the importance of friends to ground and check you. This development is is one of the strongest parts of the movie. We get to see human!Twilight in two separate situations in the span of one movie, and the events that brought her from one place to another, and that alone makes her character more useful than pony!Twilight ever was in EG1. Pony!Twilight couldn't develop here, because EG is a spinoff. Human!Twilight is on home turf, however, and her character is stronger for it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there's much good happening for Sunset in this movie. In EG1, she was defeated as a demonic villain (no offence), and in Rainbow Rocks she was redeemed into friendship with the humane six and accepted a position of tutelage. Here, we get to see her become the one to offer redemption and, in a sense, become the tutor for human!Twilight in the ways of friendship (and yeah, I fanboyed when she turned phoenix-alicorn, I fanboyed <i>so hard</i>). At the end of the movie, she has three different kind of relations tied to her, which makes her remarkably complex, not only for FiM or children's animation, but for much of popular entertainment media. When it comes to character writing and development, Friendship Games is some of the best we've had from the franchise yet.<br /> <br /> Which is good, because otherwise it's really kind of bland.<br /> <br /> In terms of the school event that frames the movie, this one was by far the least interesting one. In EG1, there's a tight tie between the real villain Sunset and Fall Formal, and the tropes regarding proms and teen highschool drama lurk in the background. In Rainbow Rocks, the villains were also very tightly tied to the Battle of the Bands, and the music scene in the community provided another touchstone. The Friendship Games... doesn't manage that. There's not a strong enough idea of what the Games are for them to become significant, I found, and they mostly felt like something to drive the plot forward rather than something that was actually important. Hell, not even the <i>characters</i> knew what the Games were actually about before they happened (but they were still expected to train?). The only part that really had any punch was the second one. The first one was only there for a song (which admittedly was among the better ones) and the third was cancelled entirely due to sudden demons. Given that the main story about human!Twilight deals with her everyday life, I think setting it in a more everyday surrounding would have benefited the movie more. Either that, or the Games could have taken a stronger profile, like saying &quot;this is a football game!&quot; or &quot;it's a swimming competition!&quot; and not just been a bunch of events bundled together.<br /> <br /> And speaking of event relevance to the actual threat, let's talk about villains. Sunset was a functional, if very traditional, villain. The Dazzlings stepped it up a notch, not only being threatening but also carrying personalities and... they were just cool, weren't they? Come on, they had style, they had allure. They managed to show the thrilling side of being bad, which was what they were supposed to, naturally. I know many considered them and their music the highlight of Rainbow Rocks. By comparison, Friendship Games has Principal Cinch as main villain. That... just doesn't cut it. Sure, you dislike her, she's actually really horrible, but she's just so bland. Now, there's something to be said for a down-to-earth bad guy without high-flying plans, but the main problem is that she's not a villain so much as an obstacle. You know she's not going to be the one transforming into a demon at the end. The lack of a proper villain doesn't have to be a problem, but when they choose to cast the movie in the same form three times in a row, the comparison becomes obvious, and so does the shortcoming. If they want to go another route, they'll have to change more than the one thing.<br /> <br /> Okay, quick round. The music was pretty cool, but Rainbow Rocks' was better overall. I liked Twilight's song at Crystal Prep (&quot;I know there's more that's out there; another me I haven't met&quot;), but damn did it remind me of Let It Go. Also, Unleash the Magic is a nice villain song, but it reminded me of &quot;Stop the Bats&quot;. Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> The Crystal Prep students that were supposed to be counterparts to the humane six were interesting for a gimmick. I think those will show up in fanworks but probably not get developed more elsewhere. The movie could have pushed their angle harder, made it about individual rivalries to lend relevance to the Games, but alas. Opportunity lost, I think, but then again, some of the gimmicks might not have stood up to closer scrutiny anyway. Also, don't call her Indigo Zap, writers. That should have totally been Lightning Dust and you know it. She even has the earrings!<br /> <br /> The way Shining Armor looked at Dean Cadance, I wonder what happens in her office after hours. In other such news, they really have to decide about Flash Sentry. Either make something of him or just cut him and free up another minute for something useful. I don't hate him as such, and I think he might be a cool romantic interest for human!Twilight, but please make him something more than a human roadblock.<br /> <br /> Final score? Well, I do like it. When I watched it the first time, I thought it was really good, and from some perspectives, it really is. But then I watch it again, with a bit more distance, and I see all the things that Rainbow Rocks did that is just missing here. I would say that Rainbow Rocks is still the best Equestria Girls movie. This one isn't all that far behind, but it is behind. Still totally worth seeing, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-27-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T16:21:32-07:00","id":687613,"title":"","content":"The joke this week got old <i>really</i> fast. The judges should have signed him in and told him to take off the costume after that. It would have had it's amusing moment, gotten a smile or a chuckle and moved us on.<br /> <br /> Otherwise...cliche message but an alright one none the less. I would have been much more interested in them having the message be about people <b>not</b> being able to open up about the things that are worrying them (boys in particular are often pressured to not show 'weakness' and emotional vulnerability, a role Big Mac is rather uniquely placed to fulfill in the series as someone who is demonstrably strong, trusted and reliable but also overshadowed).<br /> <br /> They probably wouldn't have had to change much of the episode at all. Maybe end it on a bit of a downer. Have Apple Bloom walk away after Big Mac says 'Nope,' one time too many and leave him on the hill alone, looking at the sunset and quietly saying something like &quot;I wish you still looked up to me like you used to. Like you look up to Applejack...&quot; then kind of trail the episode off there. Pick it up and resolve it later in the series.<br /> <br /> I felt that he essentially came round and explained what he felt far too quickly.<br /> <br /> Again and again and again we see and know that people will reject help and just asking is often not enough. Perhaps it's 'too dark' but if any series could introduce to younger audiences the idea of friends and family noticing something is wrong with someone, they are behaving oddly, they reject help or rebuff offers, etc. and eventually, over time, working to solve the problem, it's MLP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 10-03-2015, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T15:03:52-07:00","id":696536,"title":"","content":"It's a Final Fantasy 13 inspired twist!<br /> <br /> Branded with a mark, given only some barely comprehensible idea (I believe FF13 says a hazy glimpse) of what you're meant to do with it.<br /> <br /> So confusing in fact that whatever is giving them their marks requires the creation of a custom super squad to try and work out and explain what it actually meant in the first place.<br /> <br /> Which...yeah, is actually better than the Fal'cie managed in FF13, even when they demonstrated they could literally talk to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:32:22-07:00","id":696610,"title":"","content":"Well, shit.<br /> <br /> So I haven't actually watched Brotherhooves Social yet, since I'm a bit busy with stuff and I wasn't all that interested in the episode anyway. Still, when I browsed some random Youtube video, I saw a comment that the newest episode was hype as shit, so I decided to watch it out of order in order to not get accidentally spoiled. I feel I made the correct decision, since this would probably have been hard avoiding for long.<br /> <br /> <b>S5E18 - Crusaders of the Lost Mark</b><br /> <br /> As it turns out, this episode marks the exact five-year anniversary of the first airing of the first episode of Friendship is Magic, unhelpfully titled &quot;Friendship is Magic&quot;. I suppose that might have been a clue that something special might go down if I had known about it. As I didn't, I walked into this completely blind. And well, uh. Development happened.<br /> <br /> Actually, before we get into the details, can we stop to recognise what a <i>huge amount of stuff</i> happens in this one episode? I mean, sure, I'm not complaining that there's an action packed episode that manages to really keep you hooked, but damn, some of that could have been an episode in itself! In fact, it would most likely have been more impactful if there had been a setup for some of this stuff. This is one of the biggest problems with FiM, and it kind of serves to bite this episode in the plot (pun intended). But we'll get there in due time.<br /> <br /> I want to talk about this episode in three parts. They'll all be pretty long, so I'll spoiler them for convenience.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First, the lead-in. Pip's campaign against Diamond Tiara is actually some of the tightest sequences I've seen from the show in a while. The duet flows back and forth at a natural pace, Diamond Tiara's multiple shifts in tactics are characteristic and the CMC are actually doing a pretty dang good job. This part contains some of the funniest little throw-away gags in a long time. For example, the fact that the playground being damaged by Twilight fighting Tirek was somehow hilarious to me due to the sheer incongruity of scales. On the other hand, it makes sense that kids should care about things that are close to their daily lives, so it was actually also a clever way to tie their lives into the continuity of the bigger series. Also, this thing:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/21155142/Pix/Sk%C3%A4rmklipp%202015-10-10%2023.55.37.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, can we talk about this? Please? Because to me, this looks like Tiara is trying to blackmail someone by threatening to reveal a secret that she is <i>clearly</i> using right then and there, in broad sight, thus making it impossible for it to be a secret? And even if it were, she then explicitly reveals it loudly and clearly, <i>in song</i>, in the very next line anyway, thus rendering her blackmail ineffective? Oh, and also, the thing we are talking about here is a <i>school kid </i>with <i>super strength </i>which we have<i> never heard about before in any capacity. Who has a <b>hedgehog cutie mark!</b></i> <b><i>SHOW?! CAN WE PLEASE TALK ABOUT THIS?!</i></b><br /> <br /> Arbitrary super powers aside, there's a crispness to this scene that I think demonstrates the positives of being on a time restraint. Strictly speaking, they could have made an episode about this election alone, but keeping it down to just the first segment of the episode make it feel intense and well paced without losing anything important. This is the equivalent of an action scene, it should be quick and to the point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Segue into the second part, Tiara's redemption. This is clearly the meat of this story, and it unfortunately suffers from the negative side of time restraint. Or rather, it suffers from the aforementioned tendency FiM has to not set things up in advance. One reason season four was such a huge success was the season-long arc of the rainbow connections tying it all together, thus setting up a foundation to base the finale on. Here, everything happens at once.<br /> <br /> First of all, Silver Spoon finally has enough of Diamond Tiara and ditches her (sidenote: FINALLY! You go, girl! You don't need that drama!), which actually makes for a pretty strong moment. After that, we get to know about Tiara's home conditions, which are pretty severe but also rather on the nose, I found. There could be more subtlety there. None the less, we get to see Tiara from another perspective, and even if it's a pretty clich\u00e9d one, it still adds to her character, and I think that might frankly be one of the best effect of this episode. Diamond Tiara and Silver Spoon have been one-dimensional for as long as they've existed, and this together with Silver Spoon taking her stand earlier lends at least some depth to them.<br /> <br /> So after the CMC has found out about this, they invite her into the club house. Now, I must say that this move here is either a display of unprecedented capacity for empathy. or shoddy writing to speed things up. Seriously. Tiara has never been anything but a pest to the CMC. I'm not sure I completely buy the whole &quot;now we know why she does it&quot; thing when they've been the targets all along. I was bullied by someone I later made great friends with, but that was because they stopped bullying me and apologised <i>first</i>. Letting that rest, though, we then get a pretty interesting discussion about the benefits and tradeoffs of being born into a position of privilege but also strong expectations without much room for experimentation with your identity, as opposed to having much freedom but small sense of purpose and the anxiety that brings. The in-world rules of the cutie marks aren't super strong here, but they work as nice enablers of a discussion, which I like.<br /> <br /> The Tiara section closes with a musical chase through Ponyville as the CMC tries to convince Tiara to not expose Pip's predicament to the class (which I'm not sure what effect it would really have, but sure, let's pretend it's important). They manage to make her see that she has a choice to make about her own behaviour and it all ends with her funding the playground repairs and standing up to her mother.<br /> <br /> This part is where I unfortunately really lose the redemption story. I can buy that Tiara would undergo some introspection and come to term with that her behaviour is not only harmful but also not quite her own. But come on! After the end of the song, she's hugging fillies like she was Pinkie Pie, and building fences like she was Applejack. This is a filly who 11 minutes earlier in the episode was in all ways her usual bully self. That's a 180 on a dime if I ever saw one, and I just don't buy it!<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of dislike how the show doesn't take into account the material conditions that Tiara has to abide by. The CMC makes it out like this choice is all hers, they talk about &quot;turning away from the dark&quot; and stuff. But fact is, Tiara still has to live with, and be under the care of, her parents for several years yet. She can't just ignore their wishes for some very practical reasons, many of them including her continued support. No offense, but the whole thing felt very &quot;American&quot;. Individualism, freedom to follow your principles (which, let me remind you, she apparently acquired in 11 minutes after showing no signs of them for five season) and being the sole master of yourself isn't actually a realistic thing. Particularly not for a child, who is so utterly dependent on others.<br /> <br /> They tried to do too much, too fast with Tiara, and it doesn't work the whole way through.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And now for the third part, the CMC getting their cutie marks. Wow, I actually wrote that. This is still a bit of a chock to me, as I honestly did not expect it. Like, at all. The few hype comments I had seen on Youtube could easily have been satisfied with the Diamond Tiara redemption arc, and while I had predicted the CMC getting their cutie marks this season, I thought for sure it'd happen in the finale. Not even Magical Mystery Cure had me so surprised, since the whole thing was kind of public knowledge by the time the episode came around. I feel like I could have made a decent reaction video if I had my webcam running.<br /> <br /> This, of course, is a thing five years in the making, and it feels really good to have the payoff. I've no real further comments about it, just that it could be a nice new start for the CMC, who desperately needed a new formula and which they have admittedly partially gotten this season. From here, I'm curious to see where they go.<br /> <br /> About the marks themselves... time for some speculation.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/21155142/Pix/Sk%C3%A4rmklipp%202015-10-11%2001.15.14.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At first, I was a bit disappointed about the similar design. Not so much that they all got the same backgrounds, but the fact that even the parts that were different were clearly of the same theme. I got over that pretty quickly, though. I suppose it's really hard to deliver perfectly on something you've been building up for five years.<br /> <br /> Now, the background is clearly representative of their friendship, and that they're good at doing things together. I like that part. It fits with the friendship theme.<br /> <br /> The symbol in the middleground seems to represent their heritage. A star to represent Sweetie Belle's unicorn magic, a wing to signify Scootaloo's pegasus wings and an apple to show Apple Bloom's history as an earth pony and part of the Apple family. Except for Apple Bloom, this is kind of strange and a little bit superfluous, I find. most cutie marks in the show does not reference their carrier's race. Apple Bloom needed an apple, of course, but otherwise... but, eh, no big deal I guess.<br /> <br /> The sympol in the foreground, lastly, display their individual talent. Sweetie Belle got a note, which is expected; we've seen her sing often. Scootaloo got a lightning, which is also reasonable; she admires Rainbow Dash and is pretty damn fast on that scooter. The thing that kind of confuses me is Apple Bloom getting... a heart? I'm... kind of stumped there, actually. not sure what that's supposed to mean. But that's part of the thing I like! I think this will provide great episodes for these three, as they try to work with their cutie marks and find more and more applications for their talents! I think it can be great!<br /> <br /> Also, time to modify those vectors drawings.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In conclusion... this is a really hard episode to rate! I mean, there are some pretty big problems with it, but it's also kind of impossible to not like it just because... because of <i>that thing that happened</i>! Summary: not the best one, but certainly very very satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-10-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:05:35-07:00","id":696657,"title":"","content":"I hear you on the reaction video. I yelled a lot at the screen, and ended with a series of non-plussed &quot;Wut&quot;s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T02:45:48-07:00","id":696892,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I had to pause a couple times during their transformations sequence and just kind of contemplate the whole thing (read: talk loudly to myself). Like, in a few seconds, they'll never look the same again. That was big.<br /> <br /> By the way, grats on getting a freelancer gig, Arcane. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-11-2015, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:36:10-07:00","id":706998,"title":"","content":"I...thought I'd find this episode very annoying but throughout it kept coming up with something fun for Pinkie to do. Pleasantly surprised and very much enjoyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:42:24-07:00","id":707010,"title":"","content":"I was so baffled by it I can honestly say I have no idea what my feelings are towards it. I suppose that's better than outright dislike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T10:57:32-07:00","id":707096,"title":"","content":"I think making the in character focus be about <i>Twilight</i> rather than Cadance and Armour was a misstep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T12:20:16-07:00","id":707228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=696892#post696892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I had to pause a couple times during their transformations sequence and just kind of contemplate the whole thing (read: talk loudly to myself). Like, in a few seconds, they'll never look the same again. That was big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, yeah, I did the exact same thing! <br /> <br /> Was this the most number of songs in any single episode?<br /> <br /> The one thing I disliked was DT's face turn, which was a bit too quick and complete. Suddenly, she's a great person to be around and everyone likes her? Sunset Shimmer needs to take some lessons from her!<br /> <br /> RE: The Pinkie ep, it annoyed me a bit, what with how everyone suddenly is offhandedly mentioning babies so much around PP, but then I realized that this is just your basic sitcom set-up, and accepted it as such. It was nice to see Ms. Pie get a dose of her own medicine, being hounded by constant reminders to keep a secret from Twilight! Not so easy when the horseshoe is on the other hoof, is it, Pinkie?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T18:18:56-07:00","id":707865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=707228#post707228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hehe, yeah, I did the exact same thing!<br /> <br /> Was this the most number of songs in any single episode?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how you count (is the first and last song the same song?), I think Magical Mystery Cure might have it beat, but I've not counted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=707228#post707228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I disliked was DT's face turn, which was a bit too quick and complete. Suddenly, she's a great person to be around and everyone likes her? Sunset Shimmer needs to take some lessons from her!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, absolutely. That was my biggest gripe with the episode by far. Kind of interesting how they put the 11-minute miracle side by side with the climax of a development that's been (close to) five years in the making. I mean, hard for Tiara to win that comparison. :P<br /> <br /> One thing I've noticed is that while many people rag on Tiara's redeption, not many people seem willing to &quot;analyse&quot; the CMC's ascension. Not that I've seen all reviewers or anything, but most people reacted emotionally; whether with joy or indifference, they let it lie. Few seems to want to argue about it. But I'm not going to claim it's universal.<br /> <br /> Oh, and also:<br /> <br /> <b>S5E19 - The One Where Pinkie Pie Knows</b><br /> <br /> Woah. That was a right one-two punch after last week, wasn't it? Are they trying to break the fandom? I don't think it can bear so much upheaval at once. This is clearly a much smaller deal than the CMC's marks, but I can't help but wonder if the rather low-key season 5 is being used to set up a new status quo, where the mane six is less the immediate focus and some new focus characters are introduced? I mean, the CMC will have to get completely reconceptualised. And this new little addition will grow up eventually too, won't it? Maybe a playmate for Pound and Pumpkin?<br /> <br /> Also, five bit says it's a girl. Because ponies.<br /> <br /> I liked how the reveal was the premise for the episode, and not the end of it this time. I also liked that despite what could have easily been made emotional and dramatic, they chose to make it fast and funny. We've been missing a solidly written pure enjoyment episode for a while (but I hear Scare Master is written by Levinger, so I'm banking on that one as well), and this one is just the right kind of pacing and snappy dialogue for it's type of humour. Also, seriously, <i>awe-inspiring</i> animation in this one, not to mention the voice work from Andrea.<br /> <br /> Yeah, just, yeah. Exciting reveal, awesome episode, no complaints.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=707228#post707228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: The Pinkie ep, it annoyed me a bit, what with how everyone suddenly is offhandedly mentioning babies so much around PP, but then I realized that this is just your basic sitcom set-up, and accepted it as such. It was nice to see Ms. Pie get a dose of her own medicine, being hounded by constant reminders to keep a secret from Twilight! Not so easy when the horseshoe is on the other hoof, is it, Pinkie?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was kind of cool, yeah. I didn't think about that when I watched it, but it's true that there was a reversal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T21:34:12-07:00","id":711753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=707228#post707228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RE: The Pinkie ep, it annoyed me a bit, what with how everyone suddenly is offhandedly mentioning babies so much around PP, but then I realized that this is just your basic sitcom set-up, and accepted it as such. It was nice to see Ms. Pie get a dose of her own medicine, being hounded by constant reminders to keep a secret from Twilight! Not so easy when the horseshoe is on the other hoof, is it, Pinkie?</div> </div> </div> </div>One might think she's pushed the Pattern Spiders around one time too many.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:09:43-07:00","id":713789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=680519#post680519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Equestria Girls 3: Friendship Games</b><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rare that I agree with virtually every word of a review, but this is one of those cases. <br /> <br /> Don't have much to add, except that I'm a little disappointed to hear that there will probably be a fourth EG movie. Not that I dislike the franchise, but I really felt that Sunset Shimmer's journey has pretty much come full circle and resolved itself; she has become the guide to friendship for another version ofthe one who helped her. I was really on-the-fence about Sunset before, but I've come to see her as pretty much THE most developed character inthe entire tv/movie franchise! Having said that, I don't really see any need to go back to her, unless they come up with a really good story to tell, instead of just pushing out another one to sell more dolls...<br /> <br /> Also agree about the music. I really disliked the &quot;girl-pop&quot; of Rainbow Rocks, but thought that the Dazzling's songs were among the best in the franchise. This movie's songs were midway between that range, with the more traditional &quot;musical&quot; style songs sounding better than the &quot;pop&quot; stuff, but still not as catchy asthe Dazzlings'. While I did like Twilights' song, I kinda felt that that took away from Sunset, as though the movie still couldn't quite commit to Sunset being the main character of the series. <br /> <br /> And while the CP students clearly seem like fanfic-fuel, I'd expect to see much more attention given to Shining Armor and esp Dean Cadence, who was just adorable (what's the diff between a dean and principal, anyway)!<br /> <br /> If I had any real complaint, it's that there was not enough fanservice, which RR was chock-full of, almost as much asthe 100th! But I can see where others may not be into that so much. Maybe the full cut had more fandom refs? Will have to wait till it shows up on Netflix to find out, I guess.<br /> <br /> But yeah...needed more Trixie!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T01:29:50-07:00","id":713988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=713789#post713789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have much to add, except that I'm a little disappointed to hear that there will probably be a fourth EG movie. Not that I dislike the franchise, but I really felt that Sunset Shimmer's journey has pretty much come full circle and resolved itself; she has become the guide to friendship for another version ofthe one who helped her. I was really on-the-fence about Sunset before, but I've come to see her as pretty much THE most developed character inthe entire tv/movie franchise! Having said that, I don't really see any need to go back to her, unless they come up with a really good story to tell, instead of just pushing out another one to sell more dolls...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have long accepted that everything MLP will end on a whimper, not a bang. There's no way Hasbro will allow something as profitable to not overstay its welcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also agree about the music. I really disliked the &amp;quot;girl-pop&amp;quot; of Rainbow Rocks </div> </div> </div>Not sure if it's descriptive to call it &quot;girl&quot;-pop. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:18:06-07:00","id":714603,"title":"","content":"Friendship Games barely even pings in my brain anymore.<br /> <br /> Given the timeframe, that's really bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:01:05-07:00","id":714656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=713988#post713988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have long accepted that everything MLP will end on a whimper, not a bang. There's no way Hasbro will allow something as profitable to not overstay its welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Esp the Transformers...at least their new show is a continuation of TF Prime, instead of a reboot. Honestly, TFP pretty much did everything you can DO with the franchise, there'd be no point to starting a brand new show after it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\