"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=714693#post714693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do that time from time. But I tend to go back to the old favorite, in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The masked one? What is that, if I may ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:04:07-07:00","id":719733,"title":"","content":"Moppet from Return to Labyrinth. I call it my Grace avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:46:31-07:00","id":724219,"title":"","content":"&quot;We have a lot in common when it comes to thinking about turning into things,&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The first one is about rocks. They're all about rocks,&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/mlp/images/1/10/Maud_Pie_ID_S4E18.png/revision/latest?cb=20140317163136\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Episode was a lot of fun, Maud remains great, somehow, not sure why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 10-24-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:05:39-07:00","id":724882,"title":"","content":"I still do not like Maud, but my opinion of her has softened this time around.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I'm super pleased they gave Applejack a problem that would actually be a problem for Applejack <i>for once.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T08:42:15-07:00","id":732341,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E20 - Hearthbreakers</b><br /> <br /> Look at that! Twilight got a little pre-intro scene to remind us she exists!<br /> <br /> Nah, she's pretty visible still. But compared to her season 1 and 2 ubiquity she's really taken the back seat lately. Which I like since it lets focus fall on other ponies, and also makes her feel more busy as a princess.<br /> <br /> This episode was really good! Some episodes I liked because of lever messages and implications, some because something awesome happens, but this was just nice development of earlier established things. So much CONTINUITY! The rapport that grows between Applejack and Pinkie Pie, the introduction of the wider Pie family and the way they interact with the wider Apple family are all really nice (also, MarbleMac, anypony?). I also like that the show avoids falling into the &quot;everything is horrible at the rock farm but WE LIKE IT THAT WAY&quot; trap. I think it comes across that the traditions are just different, not worse.<br /> <br /> I think season 5 has picked up towards the end. There's been a series of really great episodes lately. I hope it'll keep up on the home stretch.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'll get around to watching Brotherhooves Social, I promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:35:14-07:00","id":732573,"title":"","content":"I disagree that it's great. Season 4 did a job of picking up from a terrible opening into a stream of great episodes. Since we've come back from the break in the middle of Season 5, we've had okay, good episodes, but very few that actually make me explode with joy.<br /> <br /> I might be losing the train of Pony, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:38:29-07:00","id":732583,"title":"","content":"Did you check out Steven Universe yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:51:22-07:00","id":732635,"title":"","content":"The first two episodes. It's on my list, but since I'm losing Netflix at the end of the year(unless someone at home has it), I switched over to watching Leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:46:00-08:00","id":747406,"title":"","content":"Apparently everyone has seen this episode already?<br /> <br /> Ummm, it was alright I guess. Call back to Stare Master, I liked that she had a spider in her house helping her out right at the start...otherwise I find Fluttershy's schtick uninteresting and her being surprise amazing at stuff that seems incongruous with her character eye rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:40:16-08:00","id":747784,"title":"","content":"I liked it's message. Jury's out on the actual episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:33:59-08:00","id":752283,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E21 - Scare Master</b><br /> <br /> This episode is best described in a single word, a word that in my opinion captures the bottom line perfectly all on its own. That word... is cute.<br /> <br /> I mean, look at <a href=\"http://pre07.deviantart.net/59bf/th/pre/i/2015/271/6/1/applejack_in_a_lion_costume_by_yetioner-d9aj7sp.png\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> <a href=\"http://fdzeta.com/subir/images/a357y.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">shit</a>. It's unbearable adorable. The whole tea party scene was actually the height of the episode for me, because just <i>listen to Fluttershy</i>. I don't think I've ever heard her so pleased with herself. It gives me diabeetuz.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it's otherwise kind of a downer for me. I've been on about Levinger before, and her trademark deadpan deliveries and quirky gags are present, but so are they in many other epsiodes and I've come to expect more of her. The beginning is repetitive, and the end feels like filler. I mean, of course it's predictable, but there's no interesting thing happening there at all. I kind of did like how everyone but the mane six was buying into the &quot;add-your-own-panic&quot; thing, because that's not a turn you see often, but yeah. You can't win them all.<br /> <br /> Okay episode, expected better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:24:24-08:00","id":752362,"title":"","content":"I actually was amazed with the tea party scene for two different reasons.<br /> <br /> 1)ZOMG Anime ponies including Utena.<br /> <br /> 2) Holy shit, Fluttershy, you're actually being a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:02:30-08:00","id":753090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=752362#post752362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually was amazed with the tea party scene for two different reasons.<br /> <br /> 1)ZOMG Anime ponies including Utena.<br /> <br /> 2) Holy shit, Fluttershy, you're actually being a dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The anime references were neat, but I only recognised Bulma and Ranma at the first glance. I'm so bad at anime these days!<br /> <br /> 2) I know! A very moderate, on-demand dick, but a dick none the less. It's quite refreshing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:19:14-08:00","id":754397,"title":"","content":"Point 2 was not refreshing for me, but it also was not problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:26:34-08:00","id":760783,"title":"","content":"Twilight Sparkle was stupid.<br /> <br /> Discord is probably another one of my spirit animals.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T04:12:22-08:00","id":761359,"title":"","content":"Don't you <b><i>EVER</i></b> spend time away from your friends. Fuck the things you think are fun or important to you but but not other people. Fuck you for being introverted and finding continuous social interaction tiring and undesirable. Spend time with your friends constantly or <b><i>ELSE!</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:32:08-08:00","id":762400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=761359#post761359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fuck you for being introverted</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's not very nice to Maud Pie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T22:59:07-08:00","id":765367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=761359#post761359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you <b><i>EVER</i></b> spend time away from your friends. Fuck the things you think are fun or important to you but but not other people. Fuck you for being introverted and finding continuous social interaction tiring and undesirable. Spend time with your friends constantly or <b><i>ELSE!</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see how the message could be interpreted this way, but I don't think that's what was meant. At least, I choose not to see it that way, if only for consistency's sake, as that would be in complete contradiction with the previous (very strong) moral, where Fluttershy realizes that it's ok to keep up her pattern of skipping out on her friend's annual get together in favor of doing her own thing.<br /> <br /> Like with Amending Fences, parts of this one were a little hard to watch, as I've been exactly where Twilight was...hell, given that this forum is a hive of geekery, I'd bet that many, if not most, of us have! So I can see where some of these issues are sore spots, but I still praise the series for Going There, and for depicting genuine Emotion in its characters, probably more than in any previous season! Seeing Twilight finally break down like that, much like Moondancer did (and Luna in Magic Sheep) really brings home why this show is head-and-hooves above other shows of its kind. <br /> <br /> That said, it's still not *perfect*, by any means: All of those above examples spent so much time on the comedic filler, that the actual climax and aftermath felt really rushed; unfortunately, the makers are still playing it safe when it comes to their demographic and what they feel they can safely handle. <br /> <br /> As for the rest of the ep, my main problem was with Discord: He is normally Funny, to the point that his eps tend to be the funniest of the season. However, in order to get the audience to empathize with Twilights' not getting his running gags, he was given incredibly lame humor here, specifically so that we wouldn't laugh either. Which makes for boring watching, but...well, I guess that's the only way to really make this sort of thing work, maybe?<br /> <br /> Also, the ending, attempting to vindicate Twilight or something, by putting Discord in her position, felt really weak and labored. Also, I didn't mind the reveal that he had deliberately caused it all, but it seems like it might have been more in character for him to leave in a huff rather than just shrug and Hugs All Around like he did...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T10:47:49-08:00","id":765649,"title":"","content":"Much like other problematic episodes, the problem is not that the lesson isn't worthwhile, it's the execution.<br /> <br /> Granted, I didn't think the episode came off as a giant &quot;Fuck You&quot; like Scutarii implies, but Twilight's smart and self-aware now that her constant denial of jealousy and just not accepting that it's okay for friends to have experiences that you don't share is annoying.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Twilight becoming dumber, Wow does that come out in today's episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T23:23:25-08:00","id":766084,"title":"","content":"What came out in today's episode is that Twilight is letting the \u201cPrincess of Friendship\u201d title go to her head: she's not so much being \u201cdumb\u201d as she's being cocky and overconfident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T07:55:14-08:00","id":770732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=765649#post765649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like other problematic episodes, the problem is not that the lesson isn't worthwhile, it's the execution.<br /> <br /> Granted, I didn't think the episode came off as a giant &quot;Fuck You&quot; like Scutarii implies, but Twilight's smart and self-aware now that her constant denial of jealousy and just not accepting that it's okay for friends to have experiences that you don't share is annoying.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be annoying, but I can absolutely buy it.<br /> <br /> Intelligent people can still be unbalanced in other ways, and I don't think Twi is anywhere near as self-aware as you imply...although she is getting better. In fact, most all of the Twilight eps this season have had a common theme, of her chafing under the responsibility of being responsible for something that she really doesn't know a lot about, and her resulting insecurity. This last ep was a classic case of *overcompensating* because of it, which makes sense as she has always gone to extremes.<br /> <br /> Now that we've seen some of the original concept art that LF had put together, and we have seen her idea of Twi's graduation, becoming somesort of scholar/mage like her hero Starswirl, I would dearly love to see an ep that confronts this directly. One she shares with Celestia where the climax is her finally blowing up at her mentor, along the lines of &quot;YOU made me into this, <i>and you never even asked me if this was what I wanted!&quot;</i> (of course, this would also be a not-so-subtle jibe from the writers to the execs who mandated the change in Twilight's Destiny,as well!).<br /> <br /> I don't expect the show would ever do such a thing, but then I didn't think it would give usthe emotional stories it has this season, either!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I switched over to watching Leverage.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://orig04.deviantart.net/0006/f/2010/358/7/8/my_leverage_pony_by_scavgraphics-d35m267.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Or alternatively:<br /> <img src=\"http://img11.deviantart.net/f4d6/i/2012/091/2/a/my_little_con_artists___leverage_by_miasma_evanesce-d4umprc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 11-21-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:32:41-08:00","id":774282,"title":"","content":"Wow, I swear. While I've never felt that my education has been more useful than this last month, I've also never felt it's been this <i>tiring</i>. Which means I've slipped behind on pony. Since the S5 finale is apparently coming up this weekend, I'll just do a blitzthrough to make sure I'm not missing anything.<br /> <br /> <b>S5E17 - Brotherhoof Social</b><br /> <br /> I finally watched it. Why did it take so long? For some reason I had gotten into my head that it would be awful. It wasn't. At all. Big Mac's act was a <i>bit</i> grating at times, but it was mostly really funny and quite touching at the end. Damn, I can be stubborn at times.<br /> <br /> <b>S5E22 - What About Discord?</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, what about him? This episode just fell flat for the first 2/3. It wasn't even bad, it just failed to engage me at all. Discord managed to be <i>bland</i>, how about that? True, it did pick up towards the end when Twilight started jumping to conclusions, and Discord being devious is pretty satisfying, but they could have made it at least <i>not dull</i> for the other part.<br /> <br /> <b>S5E23 - The Hooffields and McColts</b><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, this is more like it. Twilight's princesshood has been a recurring thing in the background this whole season, and I love how they play with her insecurities and bookishness at once in this episode. Twilight as the theoretical diplomat and Fluttershy as the ground-level humanitarian (or... animalist, I suppose?) makes a nice contrast between them, and I think there's a relevant comparison to the current refugee crisis (even if that's not connected <i>just</i> to the war in Syria). Overall, the map episodes have been at worst good and often outstanding, and I think the gimmick can last another season at least.<br /> <br /> <b>S5E24 - The Mane Attraction</b><br /> <br /> So this is the final piece from Amy Keating-Rogers, huh? Maybe I'm wrong about that and she's writing the finale as well. If it's true, however, I can see no fault in this episode being her topping off her time on pony. This was strong and emotional. Lena Hall did a great job as Ra-Ra, and while I wasn't too impressed with the song when it was spoiled at ComicCon half a year ago, it benefited from having the context of the plot around it. Also, hey, it's Applejack!<br /> <br /> Very well. I am now all caught up, and ready for the finale. Bring it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T15:11:51-08:00","id":775650,"title":"","content":"Finally got round to seeing last weeks episode. Not bad, good in fact. The first song sounded so horribly wrong with that voice coming from a child and at times I really cringe when you get all the pony and equestria references in a song that is sung sounding so earnest but I liked it a lot as a whole piece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T14:55:37-08:00","id":777380,"title":"","content":"I did not think we'd start a season with twisted Stalinism via Animal Farm and end with time traveling World War Pony with conscription and wartime economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T16:18:22-08:00","id":777414,"title":"","content":"<b>S5E25-26 - The Cutie Re-Mark</b><br /> <br /> Sorry, just a moment. I'm looking for something. Won't be a minute.<br /> <br /> Ah, right, here it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=580317#post580317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">did anyone really think a war threat would ever actually be realised in MLP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Would you look at that. It's funny how I'm made to eat my words on <i>this</i>, of all things. I thought <i>this</i> at least would be a safe bet.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I'm still not sure the scenes in the season finale can be called a &quot;realised&quot; war scenario, since it's only a few clips in an alternate timeline. But for that short clip, they did manage to show not only the combat but also the structural consequences on Equestrian life. This isn't a &quot;good guys win in decisive battle&quot; thing. For about a minute, we saw a drawn-out conflict between nations, and how that affected society at large. I can honestly say there's not much I would have expected less from My Little Pony.<br /> <br /> Since it seems I've started on the different alternate timelines, I might as well finish them. The Sombra timeline was easily the best one to me. It carried so much potential, and I'm sure it will be explored extensively in fanfics. Likewise, the Queen Chrysalis (they managed to say her name this time) timeline was similarly evocative, but we weren't told much of the bigger picture. Is this the last remaining resistance to Chrysalis' offensive? Or is it one of many rogue cells that fight a guerilla war against a still stabilizing new queen? This is all open to interpretation, which is a good thing in this case, but it doesn't mean I would have liked to know a bit more about the context.<br /> <br /> And from there to Nightmare Moon's timeline, which is... actually kind of lazy in comparison. My problem here is that we're not really told anything we didn't already know (except for her taking up residence in the old castle and imprisoning Celestia in the moon for revenge, though I'm sure someone had already imagined that as well). We only got to see her and seven guard ponies, with no new information about the world at all. They trusted her character to carry the whole timeline, and it didn't really do that. It felt unsatisfying in comparison.<br /> <br /> Of course, the last three ones were only there so they could say those characters had been included. The Flim-Flam one was a pure joke. Nevertheless, it made the episode stand out like few others in terms of sheer spectacle, only really rivalled by the other season endings. And all of it is fanservice. Awesome, awesome fanservice that I'm still somewhat reeling from (I've seen the episode at least five times, it's that good), but still just something to stroke our sensationalist desires. What about the actual conflict?<br /> <br /> What about Starlight Glimmer?<br /> <br /> One thing that makes this episode stand out even among the premiers and finales is that Twilight is alone. Every other time, the mane six have tackled any problem as a unit (or, well, at least all been involved). This time, it's Twilight vs Starlight. And that is because Starlight is smaller scale, so one against six wouldn't make sense. Yes, she has tremendous power and is a schemer second to none. She's still small scale; she's not after world domination, like most other villains have been. Her problem with Twilight is that Twilight wrecked her gig out in the desert where literally no one knew there were even ponies. This is all about her personal revenge. That's what I love about her. She's petty and prideful, and she doesn't even know about the consequences of her actions. This gives Twilight the possibility to be the Big Damn Hero without necessarily turning Starlight into a monster. I can honestly relate to her (note, not <i>support</i> her: she was clearly doing some messed up shit in that village, but I can put myself in her shoes and imagine how I would feel).<br /> <br /> The fact that we get to see Starlight's past is also a contributing factor. How many other villains do we know the history of, by which I mean their personal experience rather than a record of their actions. The scene between Sunburst and Starlight might seems menial and perfunctory (and not saying it isn't, this really could have used a minute more), but it's eminently important none the less as it establishes a personal reason for Starlight's behaviour other than &quot;for teh evulz, lol&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sidenote here: it wasn't my idea, I picked it up from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCjdwNs9CRNtald-Lc2pLw2Q/feed\" target=\"_blank\">a reactor I like to watch</a>, but wouldn't it be <i>perfect</i> if Sunburst had been Sunset Shimmer instead? We know she was sent to Celestia's school as a prodigy, and it's totally a plausible turn of events given her previous personality. Of course, the moment they even hinted that EqG might even resemble canon is the day when they have to hire bodyguards. But just imagine! It would be so sweet tho!<br /> <br /> The situation is resolved into redemption, which given the establishment of Starlight's character is surprisingly credible. Once again, not friendship rainbow laser. I am happy about this.<br /> <br /> Speculations have been going around about Starlight's place in the show next season. Will she be Twilight's &quot;faithful student&quot; and be a new member of the mane cast? Will she be a sometimes character that get an episode a season? I'm open for a closer relationship with her, and I think there are some plot seeds already sown (the aforementioned Sunburst, for example).<br /> <br /> In light of all this, I hereby dub Starlight Glimmer Best Villain. Because she managed to make me actually care what became of her without that making her any less threatening.<br /> <br /> Alright, just a few more shoutouts, then I'm done. Kelly Sheridan, Starlight's voice work was excellent. Animation team, you consistently blow me away; particularly the scene where Twilight is trapped in a crystal while Starlight is monologuing is super, because while so much straight-up talk could get boring to watch, the fact that the crystal is slipping sloooowly through the clouds makes the tension remain. Such a simple move, such a great effect. (All they had to do was suddenly and drastically change how clouds work, but, y'know, magic.)<br /> <br /> The song was meh.<br /> <br /> In the end, I think the thing I liked the best about this episode was that it still, after five years, managed to surprise me. Not only be good and meet my expectations, but actually throw a curve all out of left field. That is my beacon of hope for the next season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 12-01-2015, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T20:10:28-08:00","id":777514,"title":"","content":"I've got to say, it was interesting watching Twilight <i>oppose</i> an effort to stop a foal from being bullied. I know; context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T00:03:38-08:00","id":777602,"title":"","content":"Shame we didn't get a Trixie rules the world snippet though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T01:08:55-08:00","id":777615,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if they had Flim and Flam, they might as well have had Trixie. <br /> <br /> According to writers, she's visible in the extreme background of the Chrysalis future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T02:17:54-08:00","id":777634,"title":"","content":"Question about the changelings. What do they eat? It seemed like they fed on Love and/or happiness. Was that a dietary requirement or just something like a luxury good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T07:30:20-08:00","id":777753,"title":"","content":"I don't have the episode handy, but many sources say that they feed particularly on love. You'd think that they be better served hiding in society than conquering it, but I suppose love surges cleanest in dire circumstances, and they might be able to harvest it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T21:07:14-08:00","id":778095,"title":"","content":"I made a decision, somewhere in the middle of this season, to put pony down. I'm done with the show.<br /> <br /> So I'm pleased to say that with this last finale, I can do so with a smile at least. There's some flaws with the ending, as it happens, but I do think it's an amazing delivery on the series premise, and a solid mark of maturation from the days that Twilight made friends and then blasted the enemy to high hell. It was good. Not enough to change my mind about being done, but good enough to leave me with probably warmer feelings than I otherwise would have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:56:15-08:00","id":779499,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2015/4/4/864457__safe_twilight+sparkle_princess+twilight_equestria+girls_trixie_rainbow+rocks_sunset+shimmer_spoiler-colon-s05_starlight+glimmer_my+past+is+not+today.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:44:11-08:00","id":779801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=778095#post778095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a decision, somewhere in the middle of this season, to put pony down. I'm done with the show.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, you'll be back. Once part of The Herd, they ALL come trotting back!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, sorry to hear that, always enjoyed your comments here. Hope you still stick with this thread from time to time, at least! And just because you drop the show, doesn't mean that you can't enjoy the movies and tell us what you thought of them...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:08:27-08:00","id":779820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=777414#post777414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S5E25-26 - The Cutie Re-Mark</b><br /> Since it seems I've started on the different alternate timelines, I might as well finish them. The Sombra timeline was easily the best one to me. It carried so much potential, and I'm sure it will be explored extensively in fanfics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I disliked there was that we got even *less* dialog from Sombra! This could have been a great opportunity to flesh him out unlike the wasted original appearance, but a missed one...at least the comic did so, which is apparently alluded to in this ep (his lack of a cutie mark) so it may well be canon. <br /> <br /> Also, it would have been nice seeing Celestia fighting him directly...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, the Queen Chrysalis (they managed to say her name this time) timeline was similarly evocative, but we weren't told much of the bigger picture. Is this the last remaining resistance to Chrysalis' offensive? Or is it one of many rogue cells that fight a guerilla war against a still stabilizing new queen? This is all open to interpretation, which is a good thing in this case, but it doesn't mean I would have liked to know a bit more about the context. </div> </div> </div>Did they actually say where Celestia was, in this one? Or Cadence and Shining Armor? For that matter, those two were missing in all the timelines, weren't they?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> And all of it is fanservice. Awesome, awesome fanservice that I'm still somewhat reeling from (I've seen the episode at least five times, it's that good), but still just something to stroke our sensationalist desires. </div> </div> </div>As much as people, for some reason, give the show guff for pandaring to the bronies, IMO doing so gives us some of the Best Episodes! Frankly, at this point, they couldn't go wrong with creating a spin-off show directly targeting the Brony Demographic, most likely featuring the Alternate Mane Six, that would probably do at least as well, if not better!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about Starlight Glimmer?<br /> <br /> The situation is resolved into redemption, which given the establishment of Starlight's character is surprisingly credible. Once again, not friendship rainbow laser. I am happy about this.<br /> <br /> Speculations have been going around about Starlight's place in the show next season. Will she be Twilight's &quot;faithful student&quot; and be a new member of the mane cast? Will she be a sometimes character that get an episode a season? I'm open for a closer relationship with her, and I think there are some plot seeds already sown (the aforementioned Sunburst, for example). </div> </div> </div>I was actually hoping she wouldn't be reformed, as it would be more interesting to have a recurring pony villain popping up from time-to-time, and hadn't we already done that dance with Sunset Shimmer? Still, it was setup and done pretty well, I must admit, and I also applaud the use of reason instead of Friendship Blaster (which smacks a bit of Mind Control and was the reason I didn't initially buy SS's sudden Face Turn).<br /> <br /> Dunno if I want to see her back next season, as, again, we're getting pretty much the same story as the movie. Well, we might have, if the end of this ep hadn't condensed all that into a montage. Seeing Starlight win back the trust of the Our Towners might have been a great ep, but uh, guess not now. A bit similar to Diamond Tiara suddenly winning friends all over the place, now I think about it. Sunset must be wondering how all these formerly horrible ponies are doing so much better than she has! Maybe ponies are just quicker to forgive than humans?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In light of all this, I hereby dub Starlight Glimmer Best Villain. Because she managed to make me actually care what became of her without that making her any less threatening. </div> </div> </div>Wonder where she'd rank in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vGCZTX361bM\" target=\"_blank\">this list?</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, I think the thing I liked the best about this episode was that it still, after five years, managed to surprise me. Not only be good and meet my expectations, but actually throw a curve all out of left field. That is my beacon of hope for the next season. </div> </div> </div>No mention of that final shot? It still gives me shivers (the good kind!), and many people have noted that it seems suited to a *series* finale...Or imagine if the actual upcoming Pony Movie ended that way!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:27:51-08:00","id":779833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779820#post779820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I disliked there was that we got even *less* dialog from Sombra! This could have been a great opportunity to flesh him out unlike the wasted original appearance, but a missed one...at least the comic did so, which is apparently alluded to in this ep (his lack of a cutie mark) so it may well be canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I really need to read those comics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779820#post779820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they actually say where Celestia was, in this one? Or Cadence and Shining Armor? For that matter, those two were missing in all the timelines, weren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, no sign of Celestia in that one, nor Cadance and Shining in any.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779820#post779820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as people, for some reason, give the show guff for pandaring to the bronies, IMO doing so gives us some of the Best Episodes! Frankly, at this point, they couldn't go wrong with creating a spin-off show directly targeting the Brony Demographic, most likely featuring the Alternate Mane Six, that would probably do at least as well, if not better!</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I want to make clear I'm eating this shit up. It's aimed directly at me, and surprise, it works. I also do think it supports a show to try to be qualitative on several different wavelengths, as FiM does.<br /> <br /> However, I don't agree with a Brony Extravaganza Show. We've talked about this before, and I just can't see it working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779820#post779820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually hoping she wouldn't be reformed, as it would be more interesting to have a recurring pony villain popping up from time-to-time, and hadn't we already done that dance with Sunset Shimmer? Still, it was setup and done pretty well, I must admit, and I also applaud the use of reason instead of Friendship Blaster (which smacks a bit of Mind Control and was the reason I didn't initially buy SS's sudden Face Turn).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends. As I will point out when I write my reflection on the season as a whole, there's a lot of setup going on in S5. If it can lead to progression of the status quo, then I'm more interested in that than in a new villain who shows up just to be thwarted in half an hour or so. FiM was always protagonist-driven anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779820#post779820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mention of that final shot? It still gives me shivers (the good kind!), and many people have noted that it seems suited to a *series* finale...Or imagine if the actual upcoming Pony Movie ended that way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was powerful. I didn't mention it as I had nothing to really say about it, not that I didn't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T09:49:52-08:00","id":783490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779833#post779833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I want to make clear I'm eating this shit up. It's aimed directly at me, and surprise, it works. I also do think it supports a show to try to be qualitative on several different wavelengths, as FiM does.<br /> <br /> However, I don't agree with a Brony Extravaganza Show. We've talked about this before, and I just can't see it working.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't see it working for the community, or is it more that you personally wouldn't be into it? There IS a difference! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And, really, if they DID make such a thing, are you really so certain that you wouldn't find yourself sitting in front of the tube, watching--and enjoying--it, after all (assuming it was done well)? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that was powerful. I didn't mention it as I had nothing to really say about it, not that I didn't like it. </div> </div> </div>I was like, &quot;...Why are all the little ponies staring at me? Are *they* watching *me*, now? Are they trying to tell me something?? What do they *want* from me?!&quot; And then I turned on Moonbeam City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T10:09:19-08:00","id":783500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=779833#post779833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I really need to read those comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great stuff! It's obviously not intentional, but there's some interesting foreshadowing with the Moondancer ep...<br /> <img src=\"http://img4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140328215214/mlp/images/2/29/Lyra_and_lemon_Hearts_comic_annual_.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> And I love most of the background humor!<br /> <img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2013/7/24/382667.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The story of how Starswirl the Bearded exiled the Sirens *must* be seen to be believed:<br /> <img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/2015/4/15/874240/medium.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There's some bits of continuity I could possibly do without, however...<br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-CY6NRvrP4xo/U7yusx9lRBI/AAAAAAAB11Q/ltYlA3_c1l0/s1600/670772__safe_princess+luna_princess+celestia_lyra_lyra+heartstrings_bon+bon_nightmare+moon_idw_sweetie+drops_royal+guard.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I'm sure this will end *very* well, Spike!^_~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-10-2015, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T10:53:12-08:00","id":783520,"title":"","content":"There was also a fantastic issue recently that featured a &quot;team-up&quot; between Discord and Luna in an attempt to get to the bottom of his reality-warping nightmares...Some highlights:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/view/2015/9/5/973321__safe_fluttershy_princess+luna_magic_discord_sleeping_idw_spoiler-colon-comic_preview_artist-colon-brendahickey.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/87/45/79/8745799f0e30b9c379f252017f4893d4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/8d/f9/7f/8df97f496e0909365130cfe0f854d9ff.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/93/dc/7e/93dc7ee3e535ab43b00f8e8e2396fc68.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Of course, it's not all so heavy...There are plenty of hilarious pop culture refs and <a href=\"https://derpicdn.net/img/2015/9/9/975818/thumb.png\" target=\"_blank\">a particularly funny shout out in how Discord sees Celestia in his nightmares!</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://31.media.tumblr.com/89a97e0d60e8a8ad3ed46d546e8a61eb/tumblr_inline_nd4uxyndnS1rbfi89.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">A previous issue also gave us an interesting look into Discord's past love-life...and an interesting implication of his current one...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-10-2015, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:38:28-07:00","id":847340,"title":"","content":"Friends! Ponies! Gather under your banners! Defend your houses from the approaching tide of technicoloured Flash animation! (Or, alternatively, invite it inside. It seems like a nice fellow.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ewqjZo7zcSA\" target=\"_blank\">Season 6 is coming!</a> (Don't worry, it's spoiler-free.)<br /> <br /> Two-part premiere 26th of March. That's less than two weeks away.<br /> <br /> Get. Hype.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-14-2016, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:33:24-07:00","id":847423,"title":"","content":"Edit: Actually, on second thought, I don't like this post. It just felt self-indulgent and detracted from season 6. It shall be PURGED!!!<br /> <br /> What's everyone's predictions/wishes/hopes and dreams for season 6? I'm personally very curious about what will happen with Starlight Glimmer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-15-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:17:00-07:00","id":847666,"title":"","content":"I don't mind &quot;Bronies&quot; being part of any community, as long as they are not intrusive and obnoxious about their Pony show. For example, it becomes intrusive when they make an over-abundance of MLP threads and fill the board with pony Avatars and Signature Banners, for example, which just meets the stereotype that Bronies terra-form other communities into more MLP communities, to the detriment of the &quot;natives&quot; of that community.<br /> <br /> I myself don't watch Friendship is Magic but I do watch Equestria Girls. Having had the characters translated into a form and medium I appreciate, I began to see why Bronies could become so attached to their Pony characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T17:48:25-07:00","id":848505,"title":"","content":"I was flipping through EqD, which I've not done for quite some time, and so only noticed this just now: apparently, neither <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2016/03/natasha-levinger-not-writing-for-season.html\" target=\"_blank\">Natasha Levinger</a> nor <a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2016/03/ma-larson-not-involved-in-season-6.html\" target=\"_blank\">M. A. Larson</a> will return as writers for season 6. Given that we also know that Amy Keating-Rogers quit last season, there's been quite some shift in the writing squad indeed as we approach the new premiere.<br /> <br /> I'm not really worried, but it kind of brings a new thrill for me, to see what authors will be added and if it's noticeable on the show. Particularly Larson gave us some of the best (Amending Fences) and most controversial (you know what) episodes of the whole show, and while season 4 did great without him, I don't think he's that easily replaceable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T01:40:37-07:00","id":850056,"title":"","content":"Official MLP RPG is coming. From a company that makes wargames rules. Huh?<br /> <br /> But Alessio seems to at least be enthusiastic about it, has a track record as good at games design (though not RPG design, it's his first) and name drops enough MLP references in the interview in a 'natural' sounding way that I think he at least knows his stuff.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://riverhorse.eu/wp-content/uploads/2013/04/2297e6bc-9e5f-4fb4-8f92-e21cbd48532e-1030x320.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Interview here (at 41:53 in)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hdLf27704FQ?t=12\" data-code=\"hdLf27704FQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hdLf27704FQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T02:34:51-07:00","id":850459,"title":"","content":"Pretty interesting. I wonder how the system will have to be designed to deal with the highly disparate audience, however. Maybe they'll choose to focus more heavily on one side, but it'd be so interesting if they could figure out a way to bridge an age gap like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:15:57-07:00","id":850561,"title":"","content":"So basically Tri-Stat (Body, Mind, and Charm; and Talents instead of Attrubites) with a Cortex+-style dice mechanic (that is, ratings are how many sides your die has)? To be honest, this strikes me as a bit worrying. <br /> <br /> Given the subject matter, I really hope they get away from the \u201c<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Combat</span> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and everything else</span>\u201d trap that most games fall into. Frankly, I'd rather have something like Hopes and Fears rather than Stats and Talents as the centerpiece, and a focus on cooperative play where there are tangible rewards for working in harmony \u2014 a \u201cwhole is greater than the sum of its parts\u201d sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:23:50-07:00","id":850703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=850561#post850561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically Tri-Stat (Body, Mind, and Charm; and Talents instead of Attrubites) with a Cortex+-style dice mechanic (that is, ratings are how many sides your die has)? To be honest, this strikes me as a bit worrying.<br /> <br /> Given the subject matter, I really hope they get away from the \u201c<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Combat</span> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and everything else</span>\u201d trap that most games fall into. Frankly, I'd rather have something like Hopes and Fears rather than Stats and Talents as the centerpiece, and a focus on cooperative play where there are tangible rewards for working in harmony \u2014 a \u201cwhole is greater than the sum of its parts\u201d sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not super sure that I think more freeform stats like Hopes and Fears (which I assume are meant to be filled in individually) would work great from a mechanical point of view when it comes to younger kids. After all, with Body, Mind and Charm you at least have some die to roll whatever you're trying to do. I you get to pick fully on your own, there's a risk you'd not have any dice to do something with. The solution would be for the parent to let them do that anyway, and then you remove the point of just not having an all-covering base system.<br /> <br /> I do agree with you that I'd love a Harmony mechanic that incentivises team play, though. That feels like a mechanic you could absolutely build an RPG around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:03:39-07:00","id":853976,"title":"","content":"Slight spoilers for new episode kinda...<br /> <br /> <br /> So what did everyone think of the beginning of this season? I was a bit underwhelmed but it was a cute little arc. I thought Sunburst was cute and I'm happy Starlight grew a little. Spike was MVP this episode too, glad to see him take that initiative. I always like when Spike it appreciated and not treated as strictly comic relief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:15:47-07:00","id":854045,"title":"","content":"It was ok. I wonder if Starlight Glimmer is going to take over as much of the narrative as this seems to imply. Not fully sold on her, as she's kinda a Sunset Shimmer knock-off, but then Sunset grew on me over time, so I'll give her a shot. She works well with Spike, so that's something!<br /> <br /> Flurry Heart? <i>Flurry Heart?!</i> Man, I thought that was the worst name evar when I thought it was just cutely meaninglessness, but they<i> actually named her to memorialize the time she almost destroyed the Crystal Empire?? </i>Good luck explaining that one when she grows up, jackasses...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...I feel like I'm missing something regarding Sunburst. He seemed to show plenty of magical ability in SG's flashbacks, and she was *there*, not recounting something second-hand...and Celestia said he was a former student of hers, sooo...why isn't he actually a wizard? This could have done with a bit of explaining, but since they didn't bother, I think I'm missing something obvious...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Was this the first season opening without an actual villain (unless one counts FH!)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T09:10:24-07:00","id":854073,"title":"","content":"Well the thing with the Sunburst flashbacks it showed him doing some cool stuff but it seems Starlight always kinda picked up on it quickly because of her innate ability. I think 'wizard' in the show is some sort of profession, so although he has magical ability it's not enough to be a 'professional' wizard. Not sure what he actually did before becoming the 'Crystaler' which seems is going to be a glorified babysitter/tutor/servant to the new Princess but he seems good with the filly, at least. <br /> <br /> I do hope we get an episode to explain Starlight's cutiemark and how she earned it. But otherwise I don't want too many Starlight-centric episodes. I'd like her and Sunset to meet, if I'm honest though, since they're so alike...Like almost literally the same pony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:22:42-07:00","id":854114,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E1 - The Crystalling</b><br /> <br /> Aaand we're back! Back in <s>black</s> pink!<br /> <br /> Or rather, kind of beige, I guess? Real talk, this episode was bland as all hell. It seemed to simultaneously try too hard and be afraid to commit. Reeling in three hooks from last season (Starlight's position in the show, Starlight's old friend Sunburst and the new royal baby) in the first episode, while not horribly handled, made all of them comparatively smaller deals than they could have been. This criticism is of course rendered moot if the show decides to actually put extended focus on them rather than giving them a big flashy episode and then forgetting about them, but the latter has unfortunately been the standard so far.<br /> <br /> And the baby was just totally a repeat of Baby Cakes, which was way cuter anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, Flurry Heart? Really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854045#post854045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was ok. I wonder if Starlight Glimmer is going to take over as much of the narrative as this seems to imply. Not fully sold on her, as she's kinda a Sunset Shimmer knock-off, but then Sunset grew on me over time, so I'll give her a shot. She works well with Spike, so that's something!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she's in the group shot in the intro, a grace that even Discord hasn't received, so I think we'd better get used to her.<br /> <br /> I was disappointed with her this episode. She was totally lacking her defiant and egotistical demeanor here, which was essential to her role as a villain. Unfortunately, it seems that removing her villainhood also removed any trace of character she had. Since we seem to be getting more episodes with her, there's a chance she'll grow, but they're really not giving her much to work with here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854045#post854045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flurry Heart? <i>Flurry Heart?!</i> Man, I thought that was the worst name evar when I thought it was just cutely meaninglessness, but they<i> actually named her to memorialize the time she almost destroyed the Crystal Empire?? </i>Good luck explaining that one when she grows up, jackasses...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, dude. At least it didn't actually do anything, so people might not even remember it. Maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854045#post854045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I feel like I'm missing something regarding Sunburst. He seemed to show plenty of magical ability in SG's flashbacks, and she was *there*, not recounting something second-hand...and Celestia said he was a former student of hers, sooo...why isn't he actually a wizard? This could have done with a bit of explaining, but since they didn't bother, I think I'm missing something obvious...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I too felt like they were keeping something back from Sunburst. I really hope they'll return to him later. They clearly didn't spill the beans on him yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was this the first season opening without an actual villain (unless one counts FH!)? </div> </div> </div>I think so. Honestly, much as I rag on adventure-type episodes in this show, I totally felt the lack of edge. I'd go as far as to say it's my least favourite premiere yet, at least without knowing how (or even if) the material from it gets handled in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854073#post854073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the thing with the Sunburst flashbacks it showed him doing some cool stuff but it seems Starlight always kinda picked up on it quickly because of her innate ability. I think 'wizard' in the show is some sort of profession, so although he has magical ability it's not enough to be a 'professional' wizard. Not sure what he actually did before becoming the 'Crystaler' which seems is going to be a glorified babysitter/tutor/servant to the new Princess but he seems good with the filly, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd say Starlight has come off as someone with great innate ability to so far. The two times we've seen her, she's been using pretty much one big spell each time, making me view her more of a prodigy than a genius. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854073#post854073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope we get an episode to explain Starlight's cutiemark and how she earned it. But otherwise I don't want too many Starlight-centric episodes. I'd like her and Sunset to meet, if I'm honest though, since they're so alike...Like almost literally the same pony.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're similar to an extent.Then comes the part where Sunset has been given excellent character building over three movies and is now essentially the star of EqG, while Starlight seems to have had her personality wiped between season (or, to be fair, in this one episode).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:49:09-07:00","id":854122,"title":"","content":"I agree it was bland but it's also the first bland season beginning in six seasons, in my opinion, so I can forgive them for that. I just not hope it's not foretelling what the rest of the season will be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:51:38-07:00","id":854195,"title":"","content":"Did we ever actually see Sunburst's Cutie Mark? I'm wondering if the fancy robe covers his flank to hide his cutie mark which might give him away as not a wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T02:40:00-07:00","id":854397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854045#post854045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I feel like I'm missing something regarding Sunburst. He seemed to show plenty of magical ability in SG's flashbacks, and she was *there*, not recounting something second-hand...and Celestia said he was a former student of hers, sooo...why isn't he actually a wizard? This could have done with a bit of explaining, but since they didn't bother, I think I'm missing something obvious...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>From the flashback scenes, and his own statements as to why he left magic school, he has the knowledge needed, but doesn't have the raw power to cast most of the spells he knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=854195#post854195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever actually see Sunburst's Cutie Mark? I'm wondering if the fancy robe covers his flank to hide his cutie mark which might give him away as not a wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, rewatch the scene where he gets his mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T08:06:09-07:00","id":858344,"title":"","content":"A good episode. Maud had the best lines, as normal. The wink at the end was...expertly executed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:17:59-07:00","id":858588,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E3 - The Gift of Maud Pie</b><br /> <br /> This episode felt much more accomplished than the opener. Some of the scenes felt very true to character, and you could see how the episode dealt with the themes associated with both Pinkie (laughter/celebration) and Rarity (generosity/care about others), united by a common point that touches them both (gifts), but didn't actually play them &quot;straight&quot;. The episode was about it, but didn't typecast the roles. I thought it was very well produced. The script was also significantly better than the premiere. FiM really is at its peak when the characters are the focus, and here, they got to take some space and their personalities could shine through.<br /> <br /> Maud is a very effective foil to Pinkie Pie, and yes, she does have some killer lines, but I'm frankly more impressed with Rarity's performance. Tabitha st. Germain routinely kills it, and this is no exception.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of continuity happening right now. It's good, but it also kind of annoys me that it doesn't matter more. It's like there are things happening in the background but it won't really affect that show on a character level, which I wish it would since (again) the characters drive the show. Then again, I guess not every series can be Game of Thrones.<br /> <br /> Like, this episode was just good. I'm much more hyped for season 6 now than I was last week!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:41:46-07:00","id":862764,"title":"","content":"On Your Marks\u2026 (\u201clook at my flank; look at my flank!\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:21:08-07:00","id":863329,"title":"","content":"Episode was fairly meh, the CMC looking for their new purpose. Message that just because stuff changes you don't need to lose your friends. Problem was there wasn't much that was <i>fun</i> going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T21:39:48-07:00","id":868168,"title":"","content":"Gauntlet of Fire: Ember sure <i>is</i> different from the others; I wonder why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T05:00:51-07:00","id":868325,"title":"","content":"I really liked Ember's design. I still wonder where Spike's wings are...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T03:53:13-07:00","id":869212,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E4 - On Your Marks</b><br /> <br /> I dislike when life gets in the way of ponies. I don't seem to have missed much here though. Tree Hugger was painted like one of your French girls, and we got the exciting reveal of Scootaloo's long lost brother. Otherwise... it just didn't feel like they tried enough. It's nice that they're focusing in their individuality a bit more, but bleh. No fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:24:54-07:00","id":871351,"title":"","content":"Amazing. A Spike-centric episode that I can stand to watch again!<br /> <br /> I mean, it's still Spike-centric so there's limits but he was actually good at doing a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:35:42-07:00","id":871437,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems the newest one has made waves. I need to get around to watching it.<br /> <br /> I'm usually more inclined to a Spike episode than a CMC episode, myself, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T13:37:46-07:00","id":871677,"title":"","content":"The thing is, it was <i>so</i> Spike-centric that the ponies were part of the scenery. Figuratively <i>and</i> literally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:15:40-07:00","id":872834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=871437#post871437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it seems the newest one has made waves. I need to get around to watching it.<br /> <br /> I'm usually more inclined to a Spike episode than a CMC episode, myself, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno...it seems that even in his own ep, Princess Ember (I went the whole episode thinking it was &quot;Amber&quot;!) stole the show. The fandom seems to be going crazy over her, not without good reason! <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm pretty bummed they skipped a week for some reason, esp given the spoileriffic teaser they gave us:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jw_OtvTZSUc\" data-code=\"Jw_OtvTZSUc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Jw_OtvTZSUc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Oh snap! Can't wait to see how this plays out...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T03:11:24-07:00","id":879411,"title":"","content":"Best thing to do when you're hung over: catch up on ponies.<br /> <br /> <b>S6E5 - Gauntlet of Fire</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=872834#post872834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno...it seems that even in his own ep, Princess Ember (I went the whole episode thinking it was &quot;Amber&quot;!) stole the show. The fandom seems to be going crazy over her, not without good reason!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing though, Omega. Spike episodes don't work like mane six episodes. Yeah, he's not the <i>star</i> of the show; that's not his role. Not everyone has to be a hero to be a protagonist. In this episode, he had an important role despite Ember being the focus character. And it works! It was a great episode where the world was expanded and we got meet new characters and follow up on others.<br /> <br /> On that note, Ember is cool. No, wait... hot? Eh, none of those sound appropriate. I hope she'll come back later seasons. However, I wonder why they insist on calling her &quot;princess&quot; when there's clearly no hereditary power structure in this society? Is it just an MLP thing that everyone is a princess? Maybe it just means &quot;daughter of the current dragon lord&quot; and she'll lose the title when a new one comes into power? Also, props for having a female authority figure who <i>actually assumes the highest ranking title when she ascends to it</i>. Dragon Lord Ember, long may she reign.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I like how Spike is worried about hearing the other dragons' plans for foreign policies, but he completely forgets to ask Ember what <i>her</i> tendencies towards pony-controlled areas are. Yeah, she's his friend now, but he's a dragon. She'll make sure to save him during the invasion. Not saying that's what will happen (her father was apparently, despite his brutish demeanor, on non-aggression terms with Celestia and she might have inherited his views), but Spike doesn't even ask about the one thing that made him worried in the first place.<br /> <br /> Oh well, Friendship is Magic.<br /> <br /> <b>S6E6 - No Second Prances</b><br /> <br /> That title is stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=872834#post872834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh snap! Can't wait to see how this plays out...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But, well, it turns out it played out great. I really liked this episode. The last time Trixie returned, I was far from pleased with the outcome. This time, we actually got some development for her character, and gave us more ground to stand on with Starlight as well. Not only that, but it actually displayed a different image of one of the most explored characters in the show, namely Twilight herself.<br /> <br /> I've seen some comments complaining about how Twilight (and Celestia, for some reason?) was out of character this episode. I would strongly disagree. It's been well established that Twilight can be rather neurotic when she feels she is being judged and evaluated. This character trait is then explored through the lens of those who are not entirely sympathetic to her, and guess what? It might paint a different picture. And who's to say there's not some truth to that picture?<br /> <br /> The whole episode is actually rather complex. There's the image of Twilight as we the viewers know it, and as experienced by Trixie, and how Starlight fits in between those poles. There's Trixie's lasting &quot;rivalry&quot; with Twilight (and that can't be a fun comparison for her) contrasting with the budding friendship with her student, which actually came across as one of the most motivated developments I've seen in this show. There's also, of course, Twilight's position as both student and teacher (middle management is rough), and the balance she has to walk between being having an guiding role and letting Starlight go her own way. I super enjoyed the whole mess, because to me, it felt genuine, and certainly not out of character. Just... seen from a new perspective.<br /> <br /> How anyone could say Celestia is out of character from her one sigh of dialogue is beyond me.<br /> <br /> The fandom winks fell pretty flat. But hey, I'll take them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 05-08-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T20:35:58-07:00","id":880706,"title":"","content":"Woo-Hoo, 500th response!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E4 - No Second Prances</b><br /> <br /> That title is stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than &quot;Griffon the Brush-Off&quot;?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, well, it turns out it played out great. I really liked this episode. The last time Trixie returned, I was far from pleased with the outcome. This time, we actually got some development for her character, and gave us more ground to stand on with Starlight as well. Not only that, but it actually displayed a different image of one of the most explored characters in the show, namely Twilight herself.<br /> <br /> I've seen some comments complaining about how Twilight (and Celestia, for some reason?) was out of character this episode. I would strongly disagree. It's been well established that Twilight can be rather neurotic when she feels she is being judged and evaluated. This character trait is then explored through the lens of those who are not entirely sympathetic to her, and guess what? It might paint a different picture. And who's to say there's not some truth to that picture?<br /> <br /> The whole episode is actually rather complex. There's the image of Twilight as we the viewers know it, and as experienced by Trixie, and how Starlight fits in between those poles. There's Trixie's lasting &quot;rivalry&quot; with Twilight (and that can't be a fun comparison for her) contrasting with the budding friendship with her student, which actually came across as one of the most motivated developments I've seen in this show. There's also, of course, Twilight's position as both student and teacher (middle management is rough), and the balance she has to walk between being having an guiding role and letting Starlight go her own way. I super enjoyed the whole mess, because to me, it felt genuine, and certainly not out of character. Just... seen from a new perspective. </div> </div> </div>I'm a pretty big Trixie fan, so I was hoping we'd get to see the &quot;real&quot; Trixie this time around, as opposed to her stage persona/being possessed...and the ep delivered! In addition, it nicely balanced her portrayal between someone who was truly reformed, but still had a bit of an &quot;edge&quot; to her, and wasn't entirely resolved on her issues with Twilight, which was much more plausible than Sunset Shimmer's (and Diamond Tiara, for that matter) instant conversion. So, she was both the antagonist AND the one in need of help! Frankly, watching those three sort out their issues was one of the best pieces of writing the show has done, imo...now if only Sunset and Moondancer could get involved, somehow...<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since a major criticism of Starlight is that she's essentially a Sunset Shimmer clone, I mentally spliced SS into the ep instead as a mental exercise just to see if it played any different. How do you think she would have reacted to these same events?<br /> <br /> Starlight becoming Trixie's assistant and traveling with her could be a good way to write her off for a few eps while the Mane Six take center stage again, and add continuity when she comes back with greetings from Trixie. Don't think they'll do that, but it's an idea...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How anyone could say Celestia is out of character from her one sigh of dialogue is beyond me. </div> </div> </div>I'd guess it's because she appeared pretty annoyed and impatient for someone who has always been depicted as composed and friendly at such gatherings (compare to when she was having dinner with the Cakes in S1). Of course, she is also wise to Twilights' ways, and it's blatantly obvious that she's *lying* to her in this case, so the cross expressions and overall exasperation is warrented, imo.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fandom winks fell pretty flat. But hey, I'll take them. </div> </div> </div>You'd think Trixie alone would be enough...<br /> <br /> BTW, was I the only thrown by the fact that the ending featured what appeared to be a genuine, despair-driven *suicide attempt* by Trixie?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:00:29-07:00","id":880979,"title":"","content":"No; it seemed raher bizarre to me, too. Not \u201cStarlight's abandoning me; I'd better call off the stunt\u201d. No, it was \u201cStarlight's abandoning me; I'm going to go ahead and fire myself into the <i>literal</i> jaws of death, with my one way out now gone\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:38:34-07:00","id":885652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=880706#post880706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse than &quot;Griffon the Brush-Off&quot;?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for me, yeah. Come on, &quot;prances&quot; isn't even a noun! It could never be modified by &quot;second&quot;. Unless &quot;second&quot; is the noun, but that clause is entirely nonsensical in this context. Gah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=880706#post880706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, since a major criticism of Starlight is that she's essentially a Sunset Shimmer clone, I mentally spliced SS into the ep instead as a mental exercise just to see if it played any different. How do you think she would have reacted to these same events?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't see Starlight as a Sunset clone. Particularly not now, when Sunset is one os the best developed characters in the gen 4 lineup, including the mane six. Sunset would not get as close to Trixie as Starlight did, because Sunset has dealt with her shit. She's a villain who has gone through her redemption, become a student and, if I guess correctly at the end of Friendship Games, has now also become a teacher for human!Twilight. Starlight is still just done with the redemption thing (and even that could be seen as volatile yet) and is only just starting her role as a student. Sunset would have been much more confident, and probably not met Trixie at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=880706#post880706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd guess it's because she appeared pretty annoyed and impatient for someone who has always been depicted as composed and friendly at such gatherings (compare to when she was having dinner with the Cakes in S1). Of course, she is also wise to Twilights' ways, and it's blatantly obvious that she's *lying* to her in this case, so the cross expressions and overall exasperation is warrented, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's a difference between being composed when someone is trying their best and literally having her time wasted. Twilight could easily have said &quot;I'm sorry, Starlight isn't here, I'll talk to her later&quot; and let the damn god-queen have some dinner. It's not like they don't know each other. The fact that she's still there at all is composed enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=880706#post880706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, was I the only thrown by the fact that the ending featured what appeared to be a genuine, despair-driven *suicide attempt* by Trixie?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=880979#post880979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No; it seemed raher bizarre to me, too. Not \u201cStarlight's abandoning me; I'd better call off the stunt\u201d. No, it was \u201cStarlight's abandoning me; I'm going to go ahead and fire myself into the <i>literal</i> jaws of death, with my one way out now gone\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I... don't know about that, myself. I didn't really see it as a suicide attempt, but it sure is unexplained and pretty damn silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:00:46-07:00","id":885671,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E7 - Newbie Dash</b><br /> <br /> AKA, the episode that made me remember why I despise the military. Not that I had forgotten. I realise this isn't an accurate depiction of a military compound, but I do believe that the attitude rings true. Hey, we're going make you part of our culture of casual derogatory treatment. It's okay because everyone does it. Now you belong!<br /> <br /> I want to like Wonderbolt episodes. Rainbow Dash's journey towards her goal of becoming a real member, which I think officially happened in this episode, has been well paced. We had time to get invested in it, and now the payoff is all the greater. I really love seeing Rainbow Dash so excited and genuinely moved. But I just can't abide the themes that comes with the territory. Maybe it's an American thing, because I just can't see the point of it.<br /> <br /> The Rainbow Crash thing is an excellent example. It should be easy as pie to tell your co-workers &quot;hey, I got bullied like that in school, I'd really appreciate if you didn't call me that&quot;. I recognise Rainbow does not have the most stable of egos, but this is something that's followed her from her childhood. She should not be obligated to suck it up. There should have been someone she could have talked to.<br /> <br /> The part where Rainbow imitated the other mane six was legitimately funny. Otherwise, it was an okay episode. The ups kind of cancelled out the downs, almost, and it was a big moment in the show continuity. I much preferred the previous two, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T06:53:37-07:00","id":892461,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E8 - A Hearth's Warming Tail</b><br /> <br /> Man, they've really lowered their title pun game this season. First No Second Prances and now this? It didn't even <i>mention</i> a tail. I mean, I guess they all have tails all the time, but they don't have to name the episode after it. It's the decline of pony, I tell you.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm milking what little critique I can since the rest of the episode was absolute gold.<br /> <br /> The natural focus of this episode is the songs, and I will talk about them. I'd just like to preface with how freaking excited I am that they used the retelling of an old and existing story as a metaphor for mirroring Starlight's history. I'm a big fan of structuralism and post-structuralism as a literary theory, and the idea that stories communicate, quite without the conscious meddling of humans, is a pretty big concept there. I find that this episode utilizes how Starlight's story and A Christmas Carol bleed into each other and help each understand the other, and it's quite moving.<br /> <br /> Now, on with the show. I won't talk about all the songs, but in general, I will say one thing for the songs in general this episode: the god damn lyrics! Oh my god, did they consistently <i>nail</i> the lyrical presentation. I can't describe it better than that they felt genuine. There are some times when a song will contain a turn of phrase that'll feel flat, like &quot;oh, they had that line here because they needed a rhyme with a word that was in character&quot; and sometimes it just doesn't work. Except for the Hearth's Warming Eve Is Here Once Again framing song, I don't think I heard a single line that sat badly with me.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Say Goodbye to the Holiday</b> - When I heard this the first time, I was like &quot;oh my freaking god, did they finally beat This Day Aria?&quot; Having listened to it again and compared, I'm forced to conclude that they probably didn't. I still think the dual voices, the &quot;deceptive cadance&quot; trick and the sheer importance of it in the show at that point still manages to cement This Day Aria's place as the best villain song, and from some perspectives the best song, in Gen 4. That said, Say Goodbye to the Holiday more than challenges it when it comes to sheer execution. Kelly Sheridan is on point here, and the fact that this wasn't even my favourite song in the episode when I had to question if it beat <i>my favourite song in the show ever</i> is something else. I can't get over how good of a villain Starlight makes. I'm almost sad that she's becoming a good girl.<br /> <br /> <b>Pinkie's Present</b> - And when I heard <i>this</i>the first time, I was like &quot;shit, did they beat Smile Smile Smile?&quot; And... I frankly don't know. I could go so far as to say that they might have. This isn't a character statement on Pinkie Pie in the same way Smile is, but it's so <i>in character</i> that it might as well have been. Smile is about Pinkie, but this is about Pinkie and also something more. It's about Pinkie's philosophy, or state of mind if you will. Smile tells you who Pinkie is, but Pinkie's Present tells you why being her is <i>awesome</i>. Combined with the jazzy tune which makes it stand out from the regular feeling of the show's songs, I personally think it's the best song of the episode.<br /> <br /> <b>Luna's Future</b> - Right, I'm not a Luna fanboy. Luna singing is neat because she's legitimately underused, but I wasn't squeeing when she sang in Season 4 finale. This time, though. God, this song was just made for her. The lyrics says she has a new voice actor (for singing, I assume) named Aloma Steele, and what a way to introduce her. The depth of her voice really sells Luna, and I can't wait to hear more of her.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This was Michael Vogel's first episode as a main writer. He's been with the show in different capacities before, but still, this is one hell of a strong start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T21:29:37-07:00","id":893016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=885671#post885671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E7 - Newbie Dash</b><br /> <br /> The Rainbow Crash thing is an excellent example. It should be easy as pie to tell your co-workers &quot;hey, I got bullied like that in school, I'd really appreciate if you didn't call me that&quot;. I recognise Rainbow does not have the most stable of egos, but this is something that's followed her from her childhood. She should not be obligated to suck it up. There should have been someone she could have talked to.<br /> <br /> The part where Rainbow imitated the other mane six was legitimately funny. Otherwise, it was an okay episode. The ups kind of cancelled out the downs, almost, and it was a big moment in the show continuity. I much preferred the previous two, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, while I agree with that <i>in principle</i>...<br /> <br /> Maybe it's because I'm getting older, and watching with fascination as a cultural shift is visibly happening around me, but sometimes I wonder if our modern emphasis on a Culture of Sensitivity is perhaps going just a bit Too Far. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I do still hate bullying, having suffered from it myself, and definitely respect the right of individuals to be treated with respect. Having said that...there is some virtue to the notion that <i>some </i>slights, when not outright <i>traumatic</i>, can be dealt with by growing a thicker skin and/or just getting over it. I'm not saying that will always be easy, but it is <i>worthwhile.</i><br /> <br /> I see many young people today who seem to have this idea that they can censor the world around them to suit their preferences, and...well, NO. The world does NOT stop being hard, or ignorant, or offensive, just to suit one person or even a group/movement of people, however righteous your ideals. It's nice if you actually CAN change the world for the better, sure, but sometimes, you just need to adapt to things and, well, get over them and <i>get on with your life. </i><br /> <br /> So, to that extant, I actually <i>liked </i>that the ep didn't end with them all stopping calling her that, but that she was able to get over her issues and even gain new strength from this. It also helps that they weren't being genuinely malicious about this...hell, maybe if Dash had actually explained her sitch, they might have stopped. And at least she wasn't called &quot;Pussy-Hooves&quot;! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />(Always Sunny in Fillydelphia ref)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T21:41:34-07:00","id":893021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=892461#post892461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E8 - A Hearth's Warming Tail</b><br /> The natural focus of this episode is the songs, and I will talk about them. I'd just like to preface with how freaking excited I am that they used the retelling of an old and existing story as a metaphor for mirroring Starlight's history. I'm a big fan of structuralism and post-structuralism as a literary theory, and the idea that stories communicate, quite without the conscious meddling of humans, is a pretty big concept there. I find that this episode utilizes how Starlight's story and A Christmas Carol bleed into each other and help each understand the other, and it's quite moving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that we can easily see why the tale would be so appealing to both Starlight AND Twilight, as it mirrors both of their pasts in different ways, in one character! I kinda wonder if Twilight was mainly thinking about her own reflection in the story, and maybe only realized how it paralleled Starlight as she was reading it to her...Awkwaaard! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I totally called that Twilight actually was singing the songs to Starlight before that reveal!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm calling it now: The season finale will be The Last Temptation of Starlight, as something happens that drags her dangerously close back to her villainous ways...Of course, her redemption will instead be complete, but it could be very cool if the show actually surprised us by having her run off back to the dark side, or exiled/imprisoned/etc...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Luna's Future</b> - Right, I'm not a Luna fanboy. Luna singing is neat because she's legitimately underused, but I wasn't squeeing when she sang in Season 4 finale. This time, though. God, this song was just made for her. The lyrics says she has a new voice actor (for singing, I assume) named Aloma Steele, and what a way to introduce her. The depth of her voice really sells Luna, and I can't wait to hear more of her.[/spoiler]<br /> . </div> </div> </div>These songs are much more like it! The &quot;girly-pop&quot; style the show and movies sometimes indulge in does nothing for me; like Sweetie Belle, I much prefer the old-school orchestral/musical-style numbers (which was why I enjoyed the last EG movies' music more than the others...well, except for the Sirens!), and these were the best I've heard in some time! I usually go for the darker, villainous songs, but Luna's was the first that grabbed me even more than those...Good show, and gives me hope for the upcoming Pony Movie!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:17:01-07:00","id":893033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=885671#post885671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E7 - Newbie Dash</b><br /> <br /> AKA, the episode that made me remember why I despise the military. Not that I had forgotten. I realise this isn't an accurate depiction of a military compound, but I do believe that the attitude rings true. Hey, we're going make you part of our culture of casual derogatory treatment. It's okay because everyone does it. Now you belong!<br /> <br /> I want to like Wonderbolt episodes. Rainbow Dash's journey towards her goal of becoming a real member, which I think officially happened in this episode, has been well paced. We had time to get invested in it, and now the payoff is all the greater. I really love seeing Rainbow Dash so excited and genuinely moved. But I just can't abide the themes that comes with the territory. Maybe it's an American thing, because I just can't see the point of it.<br /> <br /> The Rainbow Crash thing is an excellent example. It should be easy as pie to tell your co-workers &quot;hey, I got bullied like that in school, I'd really appreciate if you didn't call me that&quot;. I recognise Rainbow does not have the most stable of egos, but this is something that's followed her from her childhood. She should not be obligated to suck it up. There should have been someone she could have talked to.<br /> <br /> The part where Rainbow imitated the other mane six was legitimately funny. Otherwise, it was an okay episode. The ups kind of cancelled out the downs, almost, and it was a big moment in the show continuity. I much preferred the previous two, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I watched the episode, cause I'm more or less done, but again-yeah, this is an American thing. Remember, the Wonderbolts are based off the Blue Angels, which are an American Military promotional team (primarily). With that comes the stigma of everything in the military.<br /> <br /> If this episode takes a step at calling that out, great. Maybe in future we'll see some significant breakdowns on the American Military training systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:14:03-07:00","id":893706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=893016#post893016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, while I agree with that <i>in principle</i>...<br /> <br /> Maybe it's because I'm getting older, and watching with fascination as a cultural shift is visibly happening around me, but sometimes I wonder if our modern emphasis on a Culture of Sensitivity is perhaps going just a bit Too Far.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I do still hate bullying, having suffered from it myself, and definitely respect the right of individuals to be treated with respect. Having said that...there is some virtue to the notion that <i>some </i>slights, when not outright <i>traumatic</i>, can be dealt with by growing a thicker skin and/or just getting over it. I'm not saying that will always be easy, but it is <i>worthwhile.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first of all, I would argue that this <i>is</i> outright traumatic for Rainbow. It's not just a minor annoyance; this is clearly messing her up. See how she reacts? It's interfering with her flying. It's keeping her up at night. It's taking precedence over her attaining her childhood dream. It's clearly a big deal. This isn't her finding it uncomfortable to get called something, this is previous trauma resurfacing. To use a term that's been appropriated by the internet in all the wrong ways, she's getting triggered. That's not the same as being sensitive.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit, Rainbow is that too. For all that ego, it's always been very brittle. This, however, is not that.<br /> <br /> Let me also posit that if we leave the individual perspective and look at the larger implications, there's much evidence that even low-level, non-traumatic exposure to this kind of abuse can create quite real problems over time. Look at any internet personality. They grow thick skins, as you say, because they have to and that's how it works. It also leads to health problems and is a cause for retirement in many cases. Toughing it out is hardly a good solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=893016#post893016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see many young people today who seem to have this idea that they can censor the world around them to suit their preferences, and...well, NO. The world does NOT stop being hard, or ignorant, or offensive, just to suit one person or even a group/movement of people, however righteous your ideals. It's nice if you actually CAN change the world for the better, sure, but sometimes, you just need to adapt to things and, well, get over them and <i>get on with your life.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Rainbow's been trying to do? It's the Wonderbolts that are pulling her back into the past.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I see a big difference in trying to censor out information that doesn't fit with your worldview, and the fully reasonable expectation not to get panic attacks at your job. The fact that you recognise that bullying is a problem (i.e, don't censor it out) does not mean you should have to put up with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=893016#post893016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to that extant, I actually <i>liked </i>that the ep didn't end with them all stopping calling her that, but that she was able to get over her issues and even gain new strength from this. It also helps that they weren't being genuinely malicious about this...<b>hell, maybe if Dash had actually explained her sitch, they might have stopped.</b> And at least she wasn't called &quot;Pussy-Hooves&quot;! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />(Always Sunny in Fillydelphia ref)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly! Why didn't the episode provide that as a solution? That seems like the kind of behaviour you'd want to encourage in kids, and hell, adults as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:01:10-07:00","id":907986,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that nobody has commented on the last two episodes yet: Rarity's Manehattan store opens, and Rarity tries to take an overworked Applejack to the spa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T23:58:02-07:00","id":908183,"title":"","content":"I've just been really preoccupied city end-of-school stuff. Gonna watch them once I get some breathing room! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:27:15-07:00","id":913541,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E9 - The Saddle Row Review</b><br /> <br /> There's something about this episode that reminds me of the Dresden Files. Somehow, the way more shit just keeps piling on is <i>hilarious</i> to me. The individual bits in the episode is pretty funny on their own, but the fact that the characters get to comment on them makes them perfect. And so great timing with many of those little bit scenes, like AJ's and Dashie's hoof bump.<br /> <br /> Really, the episodes when the characters just get to rub against each other like that (and not in <i>any other way</i>) are my favourites, because there are so many developed relationships between each and everyone that it could fill an episode alone. While it's cool that we get continuity in the form of Rarity's boutique (and is it just me, or has season 6 really pushed the long term status quo in a way previously unseen?), it's really just an excuse for the group to do something all together. And that's great! This isn't the most important episode, but it's up there among the funniest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:16:35-07:00","id":939179,"title":"","content":"Well, the mid-season hiatus is soon over, so I should probably wrap up the first half, and since I do just love the sound of my own voice (sight of my own text?)...<br /> <br /> And yes, I did watch them ages ago, I just couldn't be bothered to write anything. :P<br /> <br /> <b>S6E10 - Applejack's &quot;Day&quot; Off</b><br /> <br /> Cute. AJ-Rarity has been an antagonistic pairing a few times, so it's nice to see them get along. It's also useful to point out the value of reflecting on your own behaviour. AJ is a silly pony. Otherwise, not much to say. It worked.<br /> <br /> <b>S6E11 - Flutter Brutter</b><br /> <br /> Fluttershy's parents. yay.<br /> <br /> So... Zephyr Breeze. I kind of like him. It's clear that he's supposed to be an unwitting asshole, and they made that so clear that I kind of have to admire the craftspeople at work on the show. He managed to walk a fine line between being really exasperating and outrageous (I'm ashamed I found his hitting on Rainbow as hilarious as I did), and still making you realize that he was supposed to fill that role and that it actually made his character better. That said, he doesn't need to come back. Ever.<br /> <br /> The lesson kind of hit home for me. I do rely a lot on my family to stay afloat, and while it's not like I crash in their basement, they still fund a lot for me since my education has had a few false starts. It made me realize how ready I am to actually start having a proper job and make an income that I can sustain myself on.<br /> <br /> Since it's a Fluttershy episode, it was about confidence and speaking up. I've resigned myself to her being a one trick pony that way. However, I did think they gave it a twist with her not being the struggling one in this case. It's certainly one of her better ones.<br /> <br /> <b>S6E12 - Spice Up Your Life</b><br /> <br /> Every boy and every girl! Spice up your life! People of the world! Spice up- sorry, I'll stop.<br /> <br /> This was... pretty bad. Really. I don't know the first thing about food criticism, but I'm pretty sure it doesn't work like that. In fact, the idea that Zesty Gourmand was somehow at fault for publishing her opinion is strange indeed to me. That's literally what a critic does. True, those opinions should be based in solid arguments and evidence, but we do get an explanation of Zesty's critical perspective in the episode (she values the subtle and rare tastes, as she sees them as indicative of a high degree of cooking craftmanship). I'd argue that the fault is with the crowd, who blindly followed her ratings instead of reflecting on if those ratings would be a good guiding tool for them. Now, it's true that at some point a critic will have to look at themselves and acknowledge the power they wield, and take that into account when writing their reviews, and that might be where Zesty is at fault. That said, in the end, I find I have to respect her for standing her ground and adhering to her own perspective of culinary criticism.<br /> <br /> Also, since when has Rarity been about conformity? Yes, she's into the whole high society deal, which requires a degree of adjustment to standards, but she's always been a trend setter, not a follower. I don't think she filled her role well.<br /> <br /> Well then, I'm ready. Bring on the next one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 08-21-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T16:13:46-07:00","id":945731,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E13 - Stranger Than Fan Fiction</b><br /> <br /> I was guarded when I found out that this would be a Daring Do episode. I felt that the previous Daring Do episode was divided into two almost wholly separate parts: the one that was about fandom and the one that was an adventure. The first part, that was about Rainbow and Twilight was delightfully meta and reflective of fandoms in general and the brony fandom in particular, and it felt like it was talking about, and to, me. The second part was about Daring Do, and it was... a normal adventure episode. I was less than impressed by the 90 degree swerve in the direction of the dramatic arc there.<br /> <br /> Stranger Than Fan Fiction was what Daring Don't should have been. There's an adventure in the background, but the fandom theme doesn't stop because of it. Daring Do is there, but it's never <i>about</i> her (which is a personal preference, of course; she's not so interesting to me). Instead, the fandom theme is always in the foreground and the message is important, if not original. They're talking about problems that kids and adults alike have in real life, and issues that touch on communication in the internet age and, along that trajectory, political discourse. That is a solid message.<br /> <br /> And, y'know, Quibble Pants. This was his episode. I gather that the voice actor is well known in voice work, and it shows. Sharp delivery, clever lines, dripping with personality in a way that even the mane six doesn't reliably manage.<br /> <br /> Summary: This Daring Do episode was good since it wasn't about Daring Do.<br /> <br /> Edit: I tried to figure out which one of Rainbow Dash and Quibble Pants I was most like myself, but I couldn't really figure out if they represented any kind of dichotomy. If so, it's not very clear. Neither of them seem to hold sustainable positions either way. RD can be seen as &quot;show committed&quot;, loving whatever had the Daring Do logo on it due to her own relationship with the character (in her case personally). QP instead looks at the texts first and thinks about how they play into the external factors that matter to him (like believability and continuity). Those readings are really forced though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 08-21-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:16:01-07:00","id":947745,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E14 - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Cart Before the Ponies</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> Well, that was boring. I don't know, I didn't hate it, but I also didn't get into it at all. The message was kind of nice, but yeah...nothing else about the episode caught me. Eh, can't win them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 08-21-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:41:10-07:00","id":954963,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E15 - 28 Pranks Later</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, this one was solid. The title kind of gave it away, but it was still a pretty drastic turning point when MLP became a zombie movie. It's also didn't pass me by that it hinted at the infamous Cupcakes fanfic at times, but not too heavily. Overall, the callback of Rainbow's prank habit and the sudden turn towards very unorthodox genre territory created a really clever mix of familiar and surprising that made the effect of the contrast that much bigger. I'm no horror expert, but I feel like the invasion of the strange into the familiar is a cornerstone of the horror genre, and they really built that up in this episode.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of shit that would really scare me when I was young, and I wouldn't have liked it then because I was wuss. Other kids would enjoy the sense of thrill and the catharsis that it brought, and I absolutely think this is a good episode for kids and adults alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 08-21-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:32:04-07:00","id":958750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=939179#post939179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>S6E10 - Applejack's &quot;Day&quot; Off</b><br /> <br /> Cute. AJ-Rarity has been an antagonistic pairing a few times, so it's nice to see them get along.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got along *very* well during their last outing to Manehatten...and with this entire ep being driven by Rarity's almost-desperate desire to get some &quot;alone time&quot; with AJ, it's like the animators are actually <i>encouraging </i>the shipping! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>S6E11 - Flutter Brutter</b><br /> <br /> Fluttershy's parents. yay.<br /> <br /> So... Zephyr Breeze. I kind of like him. It's clear that he's supposed to be an unwitting asshole, and they made that so clear that I kind of have to admire the craftspeople at work on the show. He managed to walk a fine line between being really exasperating and outrageous (I'm ashamed I found his hitting on Rainbow as hilarious as I did), and still making you realize that he was supposed to fill that role and that it actually made his character better. That said, he doesn't need to come back. Ever.<br /> <br /> The lesson kind of hit home for me. I do rely a lot on my family to stay afloat, and while it's not like I crash in their basement, they still fund a lot for me since my education has had a few false starts. It made me realize how ready I am to actually start having a proper job and make an income that I can sustain myself on.<br /> <br /> Since it's a Fluttershy episode, it was about confidence and speaking up. I've resigned myself to her being a one trick pony that way. However, I did think they gave it a twist with her not being the struggling one in this case. It's certainly one of her better ones. </div> </div> </div>I didn't like him at all, but I got the point. Looking at a lot of responses in the fandom, it's clear that he reminds a LOT of people of various negative ppl in their lives...so much that they kinda missed his &quot;redemption&quot;. I dunno, could be interesting to see him return if he does really change...maybe he should team up with Cheese Sandwich?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>S6E12 - Spice Up Your Life</b><br /> <br /> This was... pretty bad. Really. I don't know the first thing about food criticism, but I'm pretty sure it doesn't work like that. In fact, the idea that Zesty Gourmand was somehow at fault for publishing her opinion is strange indeed to me. That's literally what a critic does. True, those opinions should be based in solid arguments and evidence, but we do get an explanation of Zesty's critical perspective in the episode (she values the subtle and rare tastes, as she sees them as indicative of a high degree of cooking craftmanship). I'd argue that the fault is with the crowd, who blindly followed her ratings instead of reflecting on if those ratings would be a good guiding tool for them. Now, it's true that at some point a critic will have to look at themselves and acknowledge the power they wield, and take that into account when writing their reviews, and that might be where Zesty is at fault. That said, in the end, I find I have to respect her for standing her ground and adhering to her own perspective of culinary criticism. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, she was clearly set up as &quot;the villain&quot;, so it might have fit that role better if it was established that she'd used her influence to silence contrary critics, or something. Otherwise, if you put your ideas out there, and crowds of people willingly follow, why would you think you're wrong or bad? &lt;glances worriedly at Hoofler&gt;<br /> <br /> I agree with the rest of your seasonal observations; I liked Daring Do attending her own convention because she could hide in cosplaying crowds, and how that backfired, as her enemies could do the same. Also, I never thought this show would throw in a joke/reference to Bondage/Body Pillows!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do wish the show cleared up the whole DD identity thing a little, however...and can't Cabelleron just *sue* her for using his identity without permission??<br /> <br /> 28 Pranks Later was enjoyable, but...I guess the ponies are just resigned to the idea that Rainbow is such an ass, that they regularly have to troll her into being less of one every other season or so? Sometimes this Friendship thing sucks...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Today's ep will be one that strikes close to our collective hearts, being about Role Playing Games! This will be interesting...Mass media has traditionally villified our hobby, making it out to be laughable at best, but as more of us enter Hollywood (&quot;Age of the Geek&quot;, as Hardison would say!) that's been changing...this could go either way, but I'm guessing Discord, as the guy who initially looks down on RPing, comes around in the end...or maybe it'll be like that STTNG ep where Q made the crew into Robin Hood and his Merry Men?<br /> <br /> Anyway, if it's even half as good as Community's take on DnD, I'll be pleased!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:50:07-07:00","id":958758,"title":"","content":"Anyone know how the MLPFIM RPG is coming along? I don't expect much out of it; but they could pleasantly surprise me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:42:43-07:00","id":958795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=958758#post958758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know how the MLPFIM RPG is coming along? I don't expect much out of it; but they could pleasantly surprise me.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.equestriadaily.com/2016/08/cover-and-more-info-revealed-for.html\" target=\"_blank\">This is all I've read about it...</a> Would be interesting to see Onyx Path/WW handle it, wouldn't it?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looking forward to &quot;POV&quot;...I love Rashomon style eps!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:32:53-07:00","id":968236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=958750#post958750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They got along *very* well during their last outing to Manehatten...and with this entire ep being driven by Rarity's almost-desperate desire to get some &quot;alone time&quot; with AJ, it's like the animators are actually <i>encouraging </i>the shipping! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Charity/Applesack OTP. But yeah, it's clear that they don't want to make the contrasts between them the only way they relate to each other. I like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=958750#post958750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't like him at all, but I got the point. Looking at a lot of responses in the fandom, it's clear that he reminds a LOT of people of various negative ppl in their lives...so much that they kinda missed his &quot;redemption&quot;. I dunno, could be interesting to see him return if he does really change...maybe he should team up with Cheese Sandwich?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, that'd be something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=958750#post958750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the rest of your seasonal observations; I liked Daring Do attending her own convention because she could hide in cosplaying crowds, and how that backfired, as her enemies could do the same. Also, I never thought this show would throw in a joke/reference to Bondage/Body Pillows!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do wish the show cleared up the whole DD identity thing a little, however...and can't Cabelleron just *sue* her for using his identity without permission??</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Caballeron might not be too keen on getting in touch with authorities, particularly not if his complaint is that the fictional character comes too close to his real life. Selfincrimination much?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=958750#post958750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today's ep will be one that strikes close to our collective hearts, being about Role Playing Games! This will be interesting...Mass media has traditionally villified our hobby, making it out to be laughable at best, but as more of us enter Hollywood (&quot;Age of the Geek&quot;, as Hardison would say!) that's been changing...this could go either way, but I'm guessing Discord, as the guy who initially looks down on RPing, comes around in the end...or maybe it'll be like that STTNG ep where Q made the crew into Robin Hood and his Merry Men?<br /> <br /> Anyway, if it's even half as good as Community's take on DnD, I'll be pleased!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>God, I've been falling behind like crazy. I need to get watching these recent ones. But it's kind of nice to have a bunch all at once as well.<br /> <br /> Speaking of shows featuring RPGs, I just started watching Stranger Things. Pretty damn cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:27:34-07:00","id":968459,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E16 - The Times They Are A Changeling</b><br /> <br /> Okay, that was a funny title.<br /> <br /> How do I put this... you know that feeling you get sometimes of &quot;is this <i>My Little Pony?!</i>&quot; or &quot;oh my god, only in FiM&quot;? Like when Twilight had a DBZ fight with Tirek or when there was a whole episode devoted to background characters and fandom memes? Those episodes that remind you that there's a show here for everyone?<br /> <br /> This episode was the opposite of that. It called back to a previous setting element (and even to the <a href=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/VSyYiAphX20/maxresdefault.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">season</a> <a href=\"https://2.bp.blogspot.com/-1NsBMTtDGeM/VvayDCO99hI/AAAAAAAACfA/aI0hbC5Et5stm5NsNRl-EWaGXp9o8ZGyA/s1600/Season%2B6%2Bpremiere%2Bmystery.png\" target=\"_blank\">premiere</a>), had a nice song, conveyed an important message and was all <i>super standard</i>. The only time when I felt a little spark of interest was when Spike rejected Thorax the first time, but that was over in a moment. The theme was also a bit confused: most of the episode was focused on prejudice, but then Spike's song was about how a &quot;changeling can change&quot;, which made it sound like Thorax <i>had</i> done something wrong and was seeking redemption. Which he might have done previously, but not towards the Crystal Empire.<br /> <br /> I don't want to say it was a bad episode. The theme was strong and important. But it was also formulaic, lacking that edge that I know MLP has. For once, I felt like I might not be the target audience here. That's bound to happen sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:35:15-07:00","id":972691,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E17 - Dungeons and Discords</b><br /> <br /> God damn it, does Hasbro have to include a commercial for their roleplaying game in the series that's an ad for their plastic toys? I'm not sure if I should be impressed or outraged about the depths of capitalism.<br /> <br /> Y'know what? This was cute. Which I suppose isn't the first adjective that comes to mind in an episode about Spike, Big Mac and Discord, but none the less. The best part was easily the interactions between the three parties; it's clear that Spike and Big Mac doesn't <i>really</i> want to intive Discord, and it's clear that he doesn't <i>really</i> want to accept, but it kind of just turns out that way due to what's not really miscommunication but something rather akin. That felt authentic. I also like that Big Mac didn't seem too uninterested in Discord's night out (here's looking at you, banana mare) despite sticking to Spike's side, showing that not all who play RPGs are monofocused nerds. The reveal at the end, that both parties kind of accepted because they felt sorry for the other, was also nice.<br /> <br /> The RPG part wasnt really what did it. As a huge nerdlord myself, I appreciate it because it's home territory. It could probably have been switched out for some other secluded activity, though.<br /> <br /> I didn't love it. It's okay, though.<br /> <br /> <b>S6E18 - Buckball Season</b><br /> <br /> Fluttershy is cute. Pinkie is cute. RD does her RD thing. AJ works well with RD. Moral: you do you, filly.<br /> <br /> Booooring. Seriously, this was so lightweight. Cute, fluffy, almost filler. You just <i>know</i> this game will <i>never</i> come up again. Is it just me, or has there been a few in a row that are just... not so great now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-19-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:14:54-07:00","id":972709,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E19 - The Fault in Our Cutie Marks</b><br /> <br /> So, I came into this expecting a story about a teenage filly with terminal cancer meeting the colt of her life, also with cancer, and them having a more fulfilling year together than most of the mares and stallions around them because love is infinite no matter how big your infinity is. I'm only slightly disappointed.<br /> <br /> &quot;What the apples&quot; is now the cutest way of not swearing on air.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I really liked this. Gabby was delightful, and I liked that they adressed one of the issues I have with cutie marks; they are often portrayed as something you get when you find the right situation and which then dictates your job, kind of like a lottery where you have to search for the ticket. They're actually supposed to be an external representation of your inclinations, which in fact allows for great flexibility in your life choices. Main example is Rarity: she's all about fashion, craftmanship and beauty, but her actual cutie mark relates to finding precious stones.<br /> <br /> I thought the whole episode was high-energy fun with a subtle theme of cultural inclusivity. Really solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:29:11-07:00","id":975064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=968459#post968459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme was also a bit confused: most of the episode was focused on prejudice, but then Spike's song was about how a &quot;changeling can change&quot;, which made it sound like Thorax <i>had</i> done something wrong and was seeking redemption. Which he might have done previously, but not towards the Crystal Empire..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he HAD been a willing participant in an invasion force against ponies in general, just because it wasn't that exact state is probably splitting hairs. The real issue is the &quot;one good Orc&quot; problem, which we've also seen with Princess Ember and Gabby...that ONE member of a normally unsociable &quot;race&quot; who just doesn't fit in with them because they're &quot;nice&quot;. Handled poorly, that can have definite Unfortunate Implications...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> God damn it, does Hasbro have to include a commercial for their roleplaying game in the series that's an ad for their plastic toys? I'm not sure if I should be impressed or outraged about the depths of capitalism. </div> </div> </div>...Y'know, that never even occurred to me! I suppose if they had actually called it by the RL name, it could be considered such. Did you know that the name they used was actually taken from the MLP comic books? Shining Armor is an old hoof at it! <br /> <br /> At first, it seemed odd that Big Mac would be into it, but then I remembered the glimpse we got of his dreams before...Still, a campaign with just ONE player?? They really should have added some others in, even if they were background ponies (SA is understandably too busy now)...Also, given that we've had at least two long speeches from BM that I can recall, it's a bit frustrating keeping up the &quot;Eyup&quot; gag in an ep that features him so prominently!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At least make it funny, like in Filli Vanilli...<br /> <br /> I'm glad that it ended with some of the girls joining in the game, as it was seriously crossing the old &quot;girls aren't gamers&quot; line otherwise...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Booooring. Seriously, this was so lightweight. Cute, fluffy, almost filler. You just <i>know</i> this game will <i>never</i>come up again. Is it just me, or has there been a few in a row that are just... not so great now? </div> </div> </div>Sadly, it's not just you. I suspect that with the old people leaving and new people coming it, Lauren Faust's original ideas of *pushing the boundaries* of what such a cartoon can do is slowly eroding, hence more standard Slice of Life Childhood Lesson stuff. And for all the people insisting that Pony is best with SoL stories, they seem to have forgotten that LF's original intentions was to have an Action-Adventure show with the ponies as Magical Girls, but Hasbro made her go the SoL/Sitcom route. I think Pony's &quot;edge&quot; as you put it is best shown with either the Adventure eps or the outright Weird ones...<br /> <br /> Of course, this season DID bring us Saddle Row Review, which was the outright funniest the show has been in a while!<br /> <br /> OTOH, a standard ending for the latest ep would have given GAbby a cutie mark despite the fact that she can't have one. That would have been a real Shark-Jumping moment for me. One of my biggest criticisms of children's entertainment is how the protagonists always get what they want (the early Harry Potter movies bending over backwards to give Griffindor the House Cup--even by blatantly cheating on the part of authority figures--really gets me. No wonder Slytherin hates them so much...), so I'm glad to see shows acknowledge that that doesn't happen in real life. This was the closest the show has also come to acknowledging Scootaloos' disability, as well (something LF wanted to do an entire episode about), so that was cool to see, as well.<br /> <br /> Seems the show still has some legs left to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:35:02-07:00","id":975236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, he HAD been a willing participant in an invasion force against ponies in general, just because it wasn't that exact state is probably splitting hairs. The real issue is the &quot;one good Orc&quot; problem, which we've also seen with Princess Ember and Gabby...that ONE member of a normally unsociable &quot;race&quot; who just doesn't fit in with them because they're &quot;nice&quot;. Handled poorly, that can have definite Unfortunate Implications...</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. I can buy that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first, it seemed odd that Big Mac would be into it, but then I remembered the glimpse we got of his dreams before...Still, a campaign with just ONE player?? They really should have added some others in, even if they were background ponies (SA is understandably too busy now)...Also, given that we've had at least two long speeches from BM that I can recall, it's a bit frustrating keeping up the &quot;Eyup&quot; gag in an ep that features him so prominently!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At least make it funny, like in Filli Vanilli...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean, it's not like he delivers a wel-spoken observation to Applejack in, like, his very first appearance in the show or anything. His non-talking does relegate him to the sidelines more than otherwise, unfortunately. They could have made the &quot;eeyup&quot; gag prominent without making it (almost) exclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad that it ended with some of the girls joining in the game, as it was seriously crossing the old &quot;girls aren't gamers&quot; line otherwise...</div> </div> </div> </div>RD was a rogue/assassin and Pinkie a bard, no surprises there. Wonder what the the others would be... Twilight as a wizard, obviously, and Fluttershy as a druid. I've seen AJ as a fighter a lot, but I think that's just because she's hard to pin down beyond &quot;she's strong I guess?&quot; D&amp;D has few mechanics for farming or related to gaining strength from family. Rarity's focus on social skills and crafting also doesn't play well into D&amp;D. She might be a sorcerer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, it's not just you. I suspect that with the old people leaving and new people coming it, Lauren Faust's original ideas of *pushing the boundaries* of what such a cartoon can do is slowly eroding, hence more standard Slice of Life Childhood Lesson stuff. And for all the people insisting that Pony is best with SoL stories, they seem to have forgotten that LF's original intentions was to have an Action-Adventure show with the ponies as Magical Girls, but Hasbro made her go the SoL/Sitcom route. I think Pony's &quot;edge&quot; as you put it is best shown with either the Adventure eps or the outright Weird ones...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been on record expressing that action-adventure episodes seldom fully hit home for me. I'm not sure I'd throw my lot in fully behind the slice of life concept either, but to me, adventures should sprinkle seasoning on a foundation of character work. If Faust had been able to fully realize her vision without meddling, it might have worked just as well, but in the state of the show now, I can't I'd want more of it than we get (but not necessarily less either).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this season DID bring us Saddle Row Review, which was the outright funniest the show has been in a while!</div> </div> </div> </div>No doubt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=975064#post975064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, a standard ending for the latest ep would have given GAbby a cutie mark despite the fact that she can't have one. That would have been a real Shark-Jumping moment for me. One of my biggest criticisms of children's entertainment is how the protagonists always get what they want (the early Harry Potter movies bending over backwards to give Griffindor the House Cup--even by blatantly cheating on the part of authority figures--really gets me. No wonder Slytherin hates them so much...), so I'm glad to see shows acknowledge that that doesn't happen in real life. This was the closest the show has also come to acknowledging Scootaloos' disability, as well (something LF wanted to do an entire episode about), so that was cool to see, as well.<br /> <br /> Seems the show still has some legs left to it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Gabby's solution was a great one, not only because it didn't break a setting assumption that did not benefit from breaking, but also because it showed an innovative and setting-consistent way of dealing with the problems that may plausibly arise in the setting. That's signature tight MLP writing. I've no doubt that there's fuel left in MLP for a while more, it's just that I've recieved these last episodes poorly. That doesn't have to be indicative of a trend.<br /> <br /> That said, we are on the sixth season. There are critically acclaimed adult TV series that hasn't gone strong this long. It wouldn't be a strange thing if it was starting to feel a bit thin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T14:51:42-07:00","id":976737,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E20 - Viva Las Pegasus</b><br /> <br /> Yeah! This is nice! I liked how they used Flim and Flam (to begin with, I thought they were antagonising each other on purpose to play the crowd). It makes them more rounded, if only for a bit, and it kind of makes me feel that the show could never use them again and I'd feel like they'd have had an ending, a redemption of sorts. Furthermore, it lends credence to Gladmane's character as a manipulator that the manipulators got manipulated. Gladmane himself was a credible villain with an understandable motivation, not evil (his artists weren't bad off, just not as well as they could be) but certainly egotistic, which made me antagonise him in an interesting way. AJ and Fluttershy is also a nice combo, but the villains (all three of them) stole the show for me here. Strong episode, if not <i>super</i> interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-26-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:32:07-07:00","id":976764,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E21 - Every Little Thing She Does</b><br /> <br /> The very first thought in my head when I read the title was &quot;that was a cheat code in Warcraft 2&quot;. Is it an established expression? When do you use it? I'm curious.<br /> <br /> God damn it, Starlight just <i>defaults</i> to being a villain. It's not that she's evil, it's the way she thinks. She's the best one in the show, I swear.<br /> <br /> This episode was legitimately funny. All the dead-pan humour, the references and the absolutely-not-hung-over ponies at the end was enough to rival Saddle Row Review in my mind (but not quite beat it). And the best part is that it's not only funny, but quite well written too. I can feel Starlight here. Breaking habits and learning new thing can be hard, even scary. The episode laid a subtle but solid foundation that revealed Starlight's motivation between her actions: she was afraid to face her tasks, and when she couldn't push them before her anymore she wanted to get them over with as quick as possible, because she didn't know how to properly engage them. There are some really short but important bits that lift this episode to a different level.<br /> <br /> Starlight has actually really brought some fresh air to the show. She's useful because through her, we can see the things we already know in a new light, and resting novelty on the foundation of the familiar is a cornerstone of progression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:27:15-07:00","id":978184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=976764#post976764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E21 - Every Little Thing She Does</b><br /> <br /> The very first thought in my head when I read the title was &quot;that was a cheat code in Warcraft 2&quot;. Is it an established expression? When do you use it? I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a line from a rather popular song by <i>The Police;</i> the rest of the line <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aENX1Sf3fgQ\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;is magic&quot;</a> ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 09-29-2016, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:16:03-07:00","id":978491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=976737#post976737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E20 - Viva Las Pegasus</b><br /> <br /> Yeah! This is nice! I liked how they used Flim and Flam (to begin with, I thought they were antagonising each other on purpose to play the crowd). It makes them more rounded, if only for a bit, and it kind of makes me feel that the show could never use them again and I'd feel like they'd have had an ending, a redemption of sorts. Furthermore, it lends credence to Gladmane's character as a manipulator that the manipulators got manipulated. Gladmane himself was a credible villain with an understandable motivation, not evil (his artists weren't bad off, just not as well as they could be) but certainly egotistic, which made me antagonise him in an interesting way. AJ and Fluttershy is also a nice combo, but the villains (all three of them) stole the show for me here. Strong episode, if not <i>super</i> interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda wish Gladmane had been less Elvis, and more Don King...<br /> <br /> Gotta deduct a point for being set in Pony Las Vegas, and not having even ONE reference to the G&amp;PT, but otherwise solid! I actually like that the Bros were NOT redeemed, and proceeding to fleece everyone there! Did you know that this plot had already been done <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Recap/MyLittlePonyFriendsForeverIssue9\" target=\"_blank\">in the comics, but there it was Granny Smith who reunited them?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:24:11-07:00","id":978497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=976764#post976764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E21 - Every Little Thing She Does</b><br /> <br /> The very first thought in my head when I read the title was &quot;that was a cheat code in Warcraft 2&quot;. Is it an established expression? When do you use it? I'm curious.<br /> <br /> God damn it, Starlight just <i>defaults</i> to being a villain. It's not that she's evil, it's the way she thinks. She's the best one in the show, I swear.<br /> <br /> This episode was legitimately funny. All the dead-pan humour, the references and the absolutely-not-hung-over ponies at the end was enough to rival Saddle Row Review in my mind (but not quite beat it). And the best part is that it's not only funny, but quite well written too. I can feel Starlight here. Breaking habits and learning new thing can be hard, even scary. The episode laid a subtle but solid foundation that revealed Starlight's motivation between her actions: she was afraid to face her tasks, and when she couldn't push them before her anymore she wanted to get them over with as quick as possible, because she didn't know how to properly engage them. There are some really short but important bits that lift this episode to a different level.<br /> <br /> Starlight has actually really brought some fresh air to the show. She's useful because through her, we can see the things we already know in a new light, and resting novelty on the foundation of the familiar is a cornerstone of progression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, all around! I questioned earlier how Starlight was different from Sunset Shimmer, and this ep is a good expression of that; I can't Sunset really doing something like this (even IF she had the magic to do so,that is)...of course, we don't get to see her growth between movies, so, maybe...? But I somehow doubt it. <br /> <br /> I was wondering why Twilight didn't just take Starlight along with her and introduce her to Moondancer...imagine the discussions they could have on friendship, magic...and Twilight!<br /> <br /> The plot of the season finale has been revealed. I already mentioned how I'd endthe season, but I'm liking this better, it really brings the story of Starlight full circle, and could easily be used to write her off in a positive way if they want to! Who do you think will be on her &quot;Alternate Mane Six&quot; team? I'm thinking Sunburst and Trixie are almost givens,but the rest might depend on who the &quot;returning&quot; villain is. If it's Queen Crysalis, then Thorax makes a lot of sense. Still, keeping my hooves crossed for a proper look at King Sombra...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:52:59-07:00","id":979805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=978184#post978184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a line from a rather popular song by <i>The Police;</i> the rest of the line <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aENX1Sf3fgQ\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;is magic&quot;</a> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>AH, sweet! Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=978497#post978497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, all around! I questioned earlier how Starlight was different from Sunset Shimmer, and this ep is a good expression of that; I can't Sunset really doing something like this (even IF she had the magic to do so,that is)...of course, we don't get to see her growth between movies, so, maybe...? But I somehow doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not now, certainly. But it was literally her plan A in the first EqG movie, except for that it wouldn't be her friends (since she had none).<br /> <br /> Which reminds me that Equestria Girls: Legend of Everfree was released today! I'm kind of stoked, not going to lie. The only thing I know about it is the base setting, and it's not a competition, so that a nice change of pace. While I realize there will be some kind of conflict, I'm hoping the focus will be on the development of human!Twilight in relation to the humane six in general and Sunset in particular. After Friendship Games, it kind of felt like Sunset's obvious character arc was concluded, and I hope a different focus this movie might re-enrich her potential story going forward. Human!Twilight on the other hand has a lot of potential right now. She's in a new school, she has friends for the first time, oh and she turned into a magic-hungry demon. The strength of the Sunset Shimmer character is that we have seen her deal with all that (except for the &quot;new school&quot; thing), and I'd like to see how human!Twilight comes out through that same struggle.<br /> <br /> Oh, and get her together with Flash. Seriously, just give the poor sod a reason to exist. Armcandy will fit him just fine, but right now he's literally not worth screen time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=978497#post978497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering why Twilight didn't just take Starlight along with her and introduce her to Moondancer...imagine the discussions they could have on friendship, magic...and Twilight!</div> </div> </div> </div>That last part might be why she's not too keen on that. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=978497#post978497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The plot of the season finale has been revealed. I already mentioned how I'd endthe season, but I'm liking this better, it really brings the story of Starlight full circle, and could easily be used to write her off in a positive way if they want to! Who do you think will be on her &quot;Alternate Mane Six&quot; team? I'm thinking Sunburst and Trixie are almost givens,but the rest might depend on who the &quot;returning&quot; villain is. If it's Queen Crysalis, then Thorax makes a lot of sense. Still, keeping my hooves crossed for a proper look at King Sombra...</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well, one alternate configuration I've seen is Lyra, Bonbon, Vinyl Scratch, Octavia, Dr. Hooves and Derpy. That won't be it, of course, since we already had the background pony episode and it has nothing to do with Starlight. I'm thinking Trixie and Sunburst are selfevident as well, but I couldn't guess for the other three.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-01-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:12:07-07:00","id":979818,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E22 - P.P.O.V (Pony Point of View)</b><br /> <br /> A Twilight episode? What is this, season 2?<br /> <br /> This was reference city. I'd make a complete list with time stamps if I thought a Youtube would live more than 24 hours, but off the top of my head: <a href=\"http://ponybot.net/pix/7857.png\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity</a> <a href=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/514/103/64e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">vs</a> <a href=\"http://img09.deviantart.net/e256/i/2013/086/8/f/rarity_vs_crabs_2_by_lilolebob-d5zgaak.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">crab</a> (I've no idea why that was ever a thing), <a href=\"http://mlpforums.com/uploads/post_images/img-316352-1-my_little_pony_friendship_is_magic_2x03_lesson_zero_04_rarity_on_a_fainting_couch.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity's fainting couch</a>, <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/17/de/63/17de631fb19a739677253ce30453c38d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity standing at the very front of the ship while saying &quot;a luxury cruise never sinks&quot;</a>... eh, I guess it was mostly Rarity. Oh, and didn't Pinkie say just last episode that she never burns a cake? Hah! Busted!<br /> <br /> Highlight of the episode might be pirate Applejack. Just... just perfect. Also, did AJ's perspective on Pinkie essentially equate to &quot;mentally challenged&quot;?<br /> <br /> This episode was funny for the same reason both Every Little Thing She Does and Saddle Row Review was: it exaggerated the characteristics and relationships that have been established, causing the comedic effect to be grounded in something we accept. The plot was obvious from he start, but that obviously wasn't the point, even if it did manage to preserve some form of tension in the question of how the boat sank (tangent: it irks me so much that they didn't even try to make the water depth consistent enough for a boat to actually sink *nerdrage*).<br /> <br /> Witty script, funny comedy, a winner in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:28:44-07:00","id":981729,"title":"","content":"Wow, I just watched Legend of Everfree. I'm going to write a review on it later, but I just need to say, right now: this movie at least ties with, possibly exceeds, Rainbow Rocks. My expectations were most righteously crushed. I am so happy about this movie, you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:46:37-07:00","id":981838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=979818#post979818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S6E22 - P.P.O.V (Pony Point of View)</b><br /> <br /> This was reference city. I'd make a complete list with time stamps if I thought a Youtube would live more than 24 hours, but off the top of my head: <a href=\"http://ponybot.net/pix/7857.png\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity</a> <a href=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/514/103/64e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">vs</a> <a href=\"http://img09.deviantart.net/e256/i/2013/086/8/f/rarity_vs_crabs_2_by_lilolebob-d5zgaak.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">crab</a> (I've no idea why that was ever a thing), <a href=\"http://mlpforums.com/uploads/post_images/img-316352-1-my_little_pony_friendship_is_magic_2x03_lesson_zero_04_rarity_on_a_fainting_couch.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity's fainting couch</a>, <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/17/de/63/17de631fb19a739677253ce30453c38d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Rarity standing at the very front of the ship while saying &quot;a luxury cruise never sinks&quot;</a>... eh, I guess it was mostly Rarity. Oh, and didn't Pinkie say just last episode that she never burns a cake? Hah! Busted!<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I...had actually never even heard of the &quot;Rarity vs. Crab&quot; thing before. That's really a thing? And did you notice the changing clothes between the different versions? One of Rarity's was actually the fancy dress from Titanic (completing the prow ref)! And considering that her lover in the movie was (Apple)Jack...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And, of course, she didn't burn cakes this ep, but...what was it, brownies? Either way, it was effective at showing how upset she was...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, did AJ's perspective on Pinkie essentially equate to &quot;mentally challenged&quot;? </div> </div> </div>That's...pretty accurate, actually. That is, that's pretty much how Pinkie *always* comes off, at least to me. Makes sense that &quot;hooves on the ground&quot; Applejack would see it even moreso!...I did smile at her Rarity's overuse of &quot;darling&quot;, tho!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:52:20-07:00","id":981843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=981729#post981729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I just watched Legend of Everfree. I'm going to write a review on it later, but I just need to say, right now: this movie at least ties with, possibly exceeds, Rainbow Rocks. My expectations were most righteously crushed. I am so happy about this movie, you guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was a nice way to break up my Luke Cage binge!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't know if I liked it better than RR, but it was a really solid story, and really advanced the EG setting. Definitely proved that it can stand on its own with NO ponies in sight at all, and I even liked how it dealt with the Flash Sentry issue you alluded to above. Still not sure which of the two villains I'd call the main/actual villain, tho...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:23:25-07:00","id":982704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies?p=981843#post981843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a nice way to break up my Luke Cage binge!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't know if I liked it better than RR, but it was a really solid story, and really advanced the EG setting. Definitely proved that it can stand on its own with NO ponies in sight at all, and I even liked how it dealt with the Flash Sentry issue you alluded to above. Still not sure which of the two villains I'd call the main/actual villain, tho...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly done well for the series to distance itself from pony involvement. EqG has developed into a place that doesn't need the connection to its pregenitor any more. Which isn't to say it doesn't need more development. In fact, let me just launch right into this:<br /> <br /> <b>Equestria Girls 4: Legend of Everfree</b><br /> <br /> Okay, first off. Thank you. Thank you for not making Flash Sentry a literal waste of screen real estate. I mean, sure, he's still a flat, one-dimensional cardboard cutout that only exists in relation to his romantic interests (aaaand I just realized that might make him the world's most clever gender trope subversion, but eh), but at least we get to see him reflecting on his role in the movie and being useful to Sunset there for a minute. I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> You know who else I'm okay with? Timber Spruce. The Flash Sentry 2.0 who had more game in this one movie than Flash has displayed in four. I've seen some reactions that paint him in the same corner as Flash, but I think that's just people being butthurt about his mr. Steal-Yo'-Waifu vibe. Timber has a backstory, a laid-back yet slightly nerdy personality (particularly, it seems in relation to biology and geology, which is excellently reasonable), and displays intimacies towards the camp and his sister that he's not afraid to take action for. He's fun and flirty and only a little bit of a tease. I'm not saying it's the love interest of the ages, I mean literally any of the mane six would make a more compelling love story, but since this is Legend of Everfree and not Legend of Korra that's not going to happen. In the meantime, Twilight, you go get some of that.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Timber, how about his sister? Gloriosa Daisy is one of the best villains we've had in EqG yet, and part of that is, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar681_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"681\" data-vbnamecard=\"681\">Hand-of-Omega</a> pointed out, largely due to the ambivalence about if she is one or not. We can all see her motives, and while she's the one perpetrating actual crimes (violence against the campers), we also know it's her panicked reaction to what she perceives as the end of her family business. I think the Dazzlings are still the best &quot;we're here and we're evil&quot; villains we've had so far, but Gloriosa is certainly the better character (who also happens to be a villain). I hardly consider Filthy Rich to be a proper villain here; he's just a someone to hook the function of a threat on. Even Cinch was more a villain than he.<br /> <br /> So, the humane seven. I must admit, there is one aspect where Equestria Girls fails pretty hard in relation to the original show, and that is in making the humane seven &quot;mane&quot; enough. Since the first movie, five out of seven have become... not background characters, but certainly secondary. Rarity in particularly was very egregious with her &quot;I'm displaying my established character traits and staying in character without making too much of a fuss&quot; writing, but all the humane seven except Twilight and Sunset were very circumstantial to the whole plot. It's like nothing is allowed to happen to one of them that doesn't also have a parallel in the others; they don't get to be singularly focused like they do in the show. Maybe that's a price you pay for having seven characters and 1 h 20 min to work with each year? It was something I noticed very clearly this time around, at any rate.<br /> <br /> Luckily, in order to make up for that, the two actual main characters are <i>killing it</i>. Twilight and Sunset are, without a question, the characters carrying this show. Their writing is impeccable. The similarities, as well as the differences, between them, and how they fit into some of the established role slots utilized in FiM, are so interesting.<br /> <br /> I said above that I think this movie at least ties Rainbow Rocks in terms of overall quality. That is because, in a way, this movie is Rainbow Rocks 2, with another focus character and less music. The struggle we see Twilight go through in Legend of Everfree is the same one we saw Sunset go through in Rainbow Rocks. The similarities are eerie, but there are also distinctions. Compare, for example, the songs <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XqnbYUG6Bn8\" target=\"_blank\">My Past is Not Today</a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MPGHvqge9BY\" target=\"_blank\">The Midnight in Me</a>. Both are very introspective: this isn't about other's accepting them (because the ones that count have already done that), it is about accepting yourself as part of the others, and trusting that you are worthy of their friendship. It's about struggling against your own self-image, and reforging it into one that doesn't have &quot;automatically hurting others&quot; as part of it, but instead letting your friends show you others paths through life to walk. However, in the first one, Sunset is distinctly separate from the image of her demon self in the window, and as she swipes it away with her hand, she rejects her past. In the song, she has gone through the process and dares to meet a new dawn. Twilight, on the other hand, is still at the start of her journey. The image of her inner demon is still fused with her, and the swipe of her hand is meant to hide, not to reject. That part of her journey is what the movie is, and it is handled exquisitely.<br /> <br /> In FiM, there's a tendency for the same kind of roles and relationships to turn up over and over again. I've taken to calling them villain - redeemed and student - teacher. A villain usually becomes redeemed, and a student has a teacher (also, redeemed and student has a tendency to coincide). One of the thing that makes Sunset such a good character is that she has been in all those roles, sometimes simultaneously (student of Celestia, turned villain, redeemed by pony!Twilight who then took her as a student, later to herself redeem human!Twilight and become her teacher). As a result, we know Sunset's history and we can see why she and Twilight falls naturally into this dynamic. Sunset has had this experience already. She is being very perceptive and caring, without that making her character any less badass and active than we are used to. Her magic power is even one that lets her understand others better, which is super useful for guiding in relevant ways. This movie really cemented Sunset's role as a teacher, and in the end, it is what helps Twilight to be redeemed, trust that her friends' has her back and that if Midnight Sparkle shows up, they can deal with her together.<br /> <br /> Note that not once does Midnight Sparkle actually appear. Every time she's on screen, it's Twilight conjuring her image. That was so well done.<br /> <br /> I could rant for twice this long yet about why the camp setting was such a great choice and why (most of) the music rivals any you'd find in Rainbow Rocks except the Dazzlings' songs, but I'm just going to say that I think the thought put into this movie will probably make it coalesce into my favourite EqG piece. Y'know, I don't think many people get the chance to say that about the third sequel!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-06-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:01:02-07:00","id":983706,"title":"","content":"Spot-on about the movie! I agree with pretty much all of your observations. A few of my own:<br /> <br /> I'm glad that they moved on with FS moving on from his Twi-crush. It was never gonna go anywhere with the Alien Princess, and tbh, it comes off a little creepy that his interest in Sci-Twi comes down to her resemblance to someone else. TS *is* FS 2.0 in that he's an improvement given that he has an actual *personality* with interests that Twilight can share! Some fans claim that the movies betrayed LF's intentions by incorporating Romance, but I don't see it that way. I think she was just protesting when girls' shows are *all about* Romance and such...but eliminating it entirely is a unnatural view of life. So I'm ok with Twi (and others) finding love, or at least dating, so long as their lives don't revolve around that.<br /> <br /> I'm ok with none of the Humane Five being featured that much, as that's what the shorts are for (apparently, we're getting more of those); at least these movies avoid the Star Trek problem, where the ensemble cast is largely background for the two or three &quot;main&quot; players. I thought we got to see enoughof the others as they discovered their new powers (which I couldn't help feeling was a metaphor for...something else); btw, that's a pretty huge change for the series! At first, I thought their powers would be relegated to the camp/this movie, but the crystals have made them pretty much permanent. But where did those come from? Could they be the Elements of Harmony...?<br /> <br /> A couple of trivial things: I've heard thatthe animation models are slightly different for this one, but I'm not sure I see it. Still, I'm glad we're away from those awful knee-boots that were supposed to make the girls look more pony-ish or whatever. Hopefully, that's not just because they're wearing camp gear, and they're gone for gone! I'm *really* glad the songs are back to the &quot;showtune&quot; style (except that last, but that made sense in-setting)...but would it kill them to find a singing voice for Sunset that actually sounds at least *a little* like her speaking voice? It's a bit jarring when one leads right into the other...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for the links, btw! I thought I'd seen ALL the Rainbow Rocks shorts, but apparently I missed a couple...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW, if you don't want to wait, apparently the season finale has leaked onto Youtube...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:19:58-07:00","id":986631,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E23 - Where the Apple Lies</b><br /> <br /> Okay, I'm torn. On the one hand, I'm really digging the backstory we're getting, the writing is tight, and Filthy Rich got a whole different vibe to him than he did in EqG4 which I definitely like more. On the other hand, it really makes a point of Big Mac's monosyllabic speech, which I just have problems with in general. True, it tries to explain why he does talk like that, but c'mon, that's not a serious explanation. It makes for a good story, though, and I suppose that's the most important part.<br /> <br /> Overall, the episode was hijinks extravaganza, and yeah, it really flows well. It's rounded and well paced and the script is nice. The flashback creates a slightly new perspective that feels fresh without being unfamiliar. I quite enjoyed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:02:28-07:00","id":988292,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E24 - Top Bolt</b><br /> <br /> They've really saved the best ones for the end of the season. I usually love Rainbow in her &quot;coach&quot; role, and Twilight complemented her splendidly. The interaction between the two of them was very enjoyable. Map episodes are usually strong, and this was no exception.<br /> <br /> The relationship between Vapor Trail and Sky Stinger was a straight up feminist commentary on assumption of roles and inequality in male-female relationships. Not, of course, that they ever said anything like it. The moral was important and, in my mind, makes the episode feel very in line with its creator's preoccupations. It was also very crisply written and had a depth of continuity to it, particularly when Twilight and Rainbow coached individually. They often referred back to their own experiences, and that made them feel very alive.<br /> <br /> Absolutely top notch episode. In top five of the season, easily.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to go ahead and watch the finale now, in fact. Hopefully, the trend keeps up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:33:51-07:00","id":988315,"title":"","content":"<b>S6E25-26 - Where and Back Again</b><br /> <br /> No. No. No no no no no.<br /> <br /> First of all, I don't buy it. The premise of this episode is that changelings have replaced all Equestrian royalty and the essential guardians of the realm. This was done in the time it took for Starlight to go to her village back and forth. Sure, there must have been preparation; the whole operation wasn't perpetrated in that time, of course.But the show just doesn't get to remove all the key players due to plot convenience off screen with literally no discussion of what actually happened. Remember, this is no less than four princess alicorns and another five of the arguably most important defense force Equestria has. No, show, <i>you have to talk about that</i>. At least if you want to keep my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the characters. I'll admit, Trixie and Starlight both carried their weight quite well. Discord was fun, and he had some good moments with Trixie in particular, but he's had much better episodes. And then there's Thorax. It's not so much that he's bad on his own, but like... him turning into some kind of... thing and replacing Chrysalis as the changeling leader felt like Twilight becoming an alicorn in the middle of season one. Much too much, way too fast. Chrysalis herself was threatening and impressive, but also felt slightly tacked on. It was like, she's doing her Chrysalis thing, and I guess that's fine, but it wasn't <i>inspired</i>. It wasn't A Canterlot Wedding. There, she was impressive. Here, it felt like they just went &quot;yeah, all that other shit we said before still goes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, freaking <i>faerie bugs?</i> Fo' real though? We know way to little about changelings to make that in any way significant. Not to mention, how could <i>every changeling</i> suddenly do it when it took Thorax a whole journey of tribulations and, y'know, actually <i>having friends</i> to accomplish it? Also, I must say the whole &quot;good form, bad form&quot; thing kind of took the teeth out of the message in The Times They Are A Changeling (and speaking of, congrats on the Nobel Prize, Bob).<br /> <br /> Now, I do appreciate the attempt to make a parallel between Starlight and Chrysalis at the end. That's a fine FiM tradition that I've been talking about at length in the Equestria Girls rant (and I must admit, I think it's hilarious how much they're importing from the spin off into the main series now). Unfortunately, it doesn't work very well, because the parallel just isn't that strong. Both ruled as sovereigns over their people, true. However, while we know from parallels with the real world why what Starlight did was problematic, there's no way we could have known that this wasn't just how changelings worked. In fact, there's no evidence that Chrysalis had any idea about it either, or that she did anything but the best she could for her hive.<br /> <br /> I've seen people saying this was the best season finale yet. I heartily disagree. In fact, I'd say it's probably the worst. While it does have some nice moments, most of them involving Trixie, it's so uneven and insufficiently underpinned that it just doesn't compare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-16-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:57:21-07:00","id":988377,"title":"","content":"I didn't mind the speed and off-screen nature of the Changeling substitution. It had to be fast to work, as anything short of a blitz would have been detected and stopped by the Mane 6 et al before Starlight got involved. As for showing any of it, that would have had to be done via flashbacks so as not to spoil the reveal, and at that point it would have been moot.<br /> <br /> But Thorax and the New Changelings? Yeah, that bugged me, too. And for all the reasons you mentioned: too much, too fast; and frankly, too easy and too facile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:17:44-08:00","id":1001798,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, sweet Ponies, take me away from this election madness...without you, I'd be driven to drink!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some fans are upset that, just when we're learning more about Changelings, they up and change them completely, when they were fine the way they were. Of course, there are still more that haven't been changed, so the way is open for a Changeling Civil War, which should make for some great fanfic material...<br /> <br /> Speaking of, did it bother anyone else that they didn't deal with the whole threat? Discord was about to take our heroes to Fluttershy's/Ponyville, where *there are still Changelings masquerading as the Mane Six*, but they decided to go to the festival instead! Serves them right if they end their week of partying to find out that Chrysalis got her revenge back heading straight for Ponyville to raze the place with her still-loyal followers...For that matter, aren't there imposters of the Princesses still in power? At the very least, I would have also replaced the Wonderbolts...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:28:08-08:00","id":1001856,"title":"","content":"\u201cAarrrhh!!! There be <i>holes</i> in that there plot!!!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T18:55:31-07:00","id":1148958,"title":"","content":"OK, how come nobody bothered to mention that there's a whole seventh season now, <i>and</i> a theatrical movie? Not to mention a trio of full-length Equestria Girls episodes (Dance Magic, Movie Magic, and Mirror Magic), along with several shorts. Have the bronies lost interest? Is there something wrong with the season? Or the movie? There's a <i>lot</i> to talk about here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-11-2017, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T23:09:36-07:00","id":1149006,"title":"","content":"Good question! Myself, I just got busy, man. I got a new job that took a lot of time to get used to, and I didn't want to spend my severely reduced free time watching little ponies anymore.<br /> <br /> However, I'm right now binge watching season 7, and so far, I'm certainly not seeing any drop in quality. In fact, compared to season 6, which I thought was of middling quality overall, it's been a marked improvement. I'm not sure what I expect from the EqG &quot;episodes&quot;, since they do kind of break the form and style of that universe, but I'm excited to see them. And, of course, the pony movie.<br /> <br /> I'm on episode 10 now, and I'll be posting some form of assessment at the mid-season hiatus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T02:46:30-07:00","id":1149352,"title":"","content":"Okay, I caught up to the mid-season hiatus. Lighting round! As always, spoilers!<br /> <br /> <b>S7E1 - Celestial Advice:</b> Cool. They needed to adress what would happen to Starlight, and it's always nice to see the continuity that lasts. The Starlight character arc is a sort of background storyline for both the previous and this season, and I think it comes into its own much better during this season.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E2 - All Bottled Up:</b> Aaaand more Starlight. It's cool I guess, seeing her with Trixie is fun as always. They have nice chemistry.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E3 - A Flurry of Emotions:</b> Is babby! Cute! I always liked baby ponies, and they're Flurry Heart much more character here than she got previously, and frankly, for example, much more than Pound and Pumpkin got. Twilight is B(est) A(unt) E(ver).<br /> <br /> <b>S7E4 - Rock Solid Friendship:</b> I mean, it's Maud. And more Starlight. Hey, I'm not complaining. If Starlight made Maud move (adjacent) to Ponyville, I absolutely take that.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E5 - Fluttershy Leans In:</b> Fluttershy was never my favourite pony. In fact, she consistently ranked lowest among the mane six, because... well, what is there to her? She's slightly less one-note than Rarity, but none of her notes are as interesting as the others'. For a good while, all her episodes were about her trying to overcome her shyness and stand up to those around her. And this episode, she freaking does that! All on her own, she fights for her vision of a (highly marketable) animal resort and resists all the influences that both professionals and friends have on the project. Fluttershy is expertly written here, taking care to account for her kindness while making her take very collected and considered stands for the things that matter to her. This really makes her kindness come off as her default position, but it has now been tempered by a conscious awareness of when to go against her instincts and fight for her stance. I LOVE this episode, and it might be my favourite among the first batch.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E6 - Forever Filly:</b> And the reason I said &quot;might&quot; up there is this one right here. It, too, displays development, and even if I think Fluttershy's is more narratively anchored, the simple fact of passing time is really enough justification to merit this episode. I don't think there's a big message or moments of character writing here, but it really does resonate with me. What? Yes, I did just turn 30 last month, why are you asking? Anyway, I hope that the CMC will get a growing-up treatment, perhaps even with shifting character models later down the line.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E7 - Parental Glideance:</b> Ehhh, this one was more miss than hit for me. Mkay, RD's parents and all, but nothing big. That said, it IS nice to see just where she gets her confidence from.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E8 - Hard to Say Anything:</b> Fun gags, did laugh. But it does say something that this was the one episode I had to check the synopsis for to remember what it was about. <br /> <br /> <b>S7E9 - Honest Apple:</b> This is probably my third favourite episode of the batch. The issue of the plot is one that is highly relevant in today's society, and I think it's subtly brilliant in its approach. We all know that Applejack isn't a bad person, so having her play the &quot;bad filly&quot; is very effective. We also get to see her being wrong, but not going back on her opinion, which is important. My one gripe is perhaps that in the final scenes, AJ admits that she thought she was being honest, but instead she was hurtful. I would have liked them to say that she was being honest AND hurtful, as there is no contradiction between that, but that's literally (speaking of, did you hate or live Lily Lace?) me picking on a single word. Also, how often do you see Rarity shred guitar?<br /> <br /> <b>S7E10 - A Royal Problem:</b> OOOOHHHH SHHHIIIIT it was decent. No, it was more than decent: we've been wanting an episode about the royal sisters for a while, and this was a good one. But Daybreaker... like, first of all, we must realise that Daybreaker isn't evil Celestia, or even the potential of evil Celestia. It is Starlight's nightmare image of the potential of evil Celestia. I'm not saying Celestia could never lose her shit, but we have no reason to believe that Daybreaker would be the form she would take. Furthermore, while not implausible, there's something kind of gauche about Celestia's evil form being just the inverse of Nightmare Moon. Nightmare Moon had a purpose and a vision; her decision to plunge Equestria into eternal night was in line with her desire. She was forgotten and alone, so she wanted to bring about night so that everyone could see its beauty and adore her. Daybreaker has no such motivation; it's just &quot;POWER!&quot;, mixed with a little &quot;fuck everyone I don't have to do anything anymore&quot;. Yeah, I don't know, she didn't do it for me. But, again, the episode was good.<br /> <br /> <b>S7E11 - Not Asking for Trouble:</b> It's yaks. I don't like it. Not only was it kind of boring, except for a few Pinkie Pie fourth wall breaks, but I'm ideologically opposed to morals that implies &quot;you're just supposed to GET IT&quot;. No. We have to get more comfortable both communicating our our desires explicitly, and listening to what others want. If you need help, ask for it. Particularly if your damn kids are starving.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> said, there's a lot that can be discussed here. I personally think that this season, so far, have been lower on the adventure and is focusing more on the character and dialogue writing. Which is great news for me, because those are my favourite aspects of the show. I didn't point it out above, but I've never really cringed at any line or felt that they were simplified for the child viewer this time around, which I have sometimes before. There's an overall improvement in that aspect. It also feels like the crew is more comfortable progressing the state of the world between seasons, and many of the episodes have taken that to heart, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T09:03:54-07:00","id":1149935,"title":"","content":"<b>S7E12 - Discordant Harmony</b><br /> <br /> Oh wow! Look at that title! Discord and harmony are really important concepts in the world of Equestia, each represented by the princesses, who keep night and day in harmony, and Discord, who throws that harmony into chaos. Perhaps, since Discord no longer serves the chaotic agenda, the harmony in Equestria has begun to oversaturate, creating a sort of meta-discord that is unraveling reality. It might require Discord to-<br /> <br /> Oh? We're doing what? Tea parties?<br /> <br /> <i><b>...fine.</b></i><br /> <br /> Honestly, this is an okay episode, even if the title promises a bit more than it lives up to. In a way, it <i>does</i> kind of go a place where at least Discord, in going against his nature, is put into an interesting situation. It also highlights the difference between adjusting to ones surroundings and going against ones nature. And, y'know, Fluttershy keeps being surprisingly good, and Discord is always a treat. But I found that the dialogue was kind of bland and that the premise, while entertaining, never really took off. Decent, no more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T11:03:08-07:00","id":1149952,"title":"","content":"<b>S7E13 - The Perfect Pear</b><br /> <br /> At some point, hopefully well in the future, when the last season of Friendship is Magic concludes, I will look back, and I will ask myself, &quot;okay, now that this series is a complete thing, which one of the episodes really was <i>the best episode?</i>&quot; That question is a pretty useless one to ask, but I'm going to ask it anyway. And of course, I don't know what will come up in the future, but I do now what would happen if I looked back from this point and tried to find the best one so far.<br /> <br /> For a long time, I would have said &quot;well, they're all so different, and many are good ways others aren't; it's really impossible to say that anyone is the <i>best</i>.&quot; And that would be true, but it would also mean that no one episode managed to move me so hard that I forwent the constraints of logic and <i>felt</i> my way to the answer.<br /> <br /> And then, there really came an episode that I can call my favourite, acknowledging the qualities in all the others but still in the firm belief that this one episode was the best.<br /> <br /> That episode is Amending Fences. But The Perfect Pear might be the second best.<br /> <br /> The Perfect Pear is, in many ways, very similar to Amending Fences. It puts the spotlight on a place in the show that we knew was there, but that had never been developed. It uses that place to create a sense depth and history in the pony world, making it feel three-dimensional and lived in. This is the core of what I loved about Amending Fences as well, that it opened up a whole new venue of discussion in something that has been as well explored as <i>the main characters</i>. Of course, the issue of AJ's and Applebloom's parents have been hinted at several times, but I never really felt that it needed to be talked about; the show could have moved on with us just knowing that they're dead (yes, it is entirely clear that they're dead). But getting to know them was a pleasure.<br /> <br /> Of course, the plot is literally a classic (good to see you hang in there, William), but there's no problem in that from my end. It's entirely possible to mess up Romeo and Juliet, and honestly, this story diverges from the play as well. For example, the characters get to have an actual relationship here before they died, which is more than the originals got.<br /> <br /> Speaking of William, I saw that Grand Pear was voiced by William Shatner. I mean, that alone. Also, Felicia Day played Pear Butter. It's cool that they use guest actors like that.<br /> <br /> This episode was supreme. I believe it's in the top five of the series as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:56:21-08:00","id":1187079,"title":"","content":"Just watched Forgotten Friendship. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Highlights:<br /> 1. Sunset Shimmer reconciles with Princess Celestia.<br /> 2. Princess Twilight's geek-out.<br /> 3. Sunset Shimmer isn't Starlight Glimmer; but they've got similar tastes. Right, Trixie?<br /> 4. [Twilight]: \u201c\u2026the magic of-\u201d [Pinky, interrupting]: \u201cYeah, yeah; light 'em up, girls!\u201d<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pet theory: time runs differently in Equestria than in the human world; arguably, it runs much faster. It's how Starswirl (who lived a thousand years ago in Equestria) banished the Dazzlings to the human world without them appearing in the middle of the 10th century. It's also how whole seasons of development take place in Equestria while at most a few months pass at Canterlot High.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}